&lt;li&gt;Experience in selling Tax solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to sell complex software solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Sales is a team of deep functional and technical specialists who both lead and advise on deals for the most strategically important products in Stripe’s portfolio. Stripe is investing in building out its Fraud &amp;amp; Risk&amp;nbsp; Product Sales team and as an Account Executive you will be a critical part of the team driving the growth of this product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, Product focusing on Fraud &amp;amp; Risk you will use your sales and product expertise to help drive product market fit &amp;amp; growth of Stripe’s risk and fraud fighting products and solutions. You will collaborate with product, engineering and marketing teams to develop deep product and industry knowledge and drive strategic deals. You will be instrumental in leading in depth product discussions with existing and prospect users globally – and building and executing against our go to market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including CEOs, CTOs, and Chief Risk Officers. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding. You’re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives). You’re excited to become an expert and to share your knowledge. You’re an organized self-starter, an excellent communicator who is highly analytical and has a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive new business and revenue growth by selling Radar, Identity, Dispute Prevention and more to a variety of businesses&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex new and expansion deals related to Stripe’s Fraud &amp;amp; Risk product offerings, capabilities, and tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the sales process and what competitors offer in terms of fraud fighting capabilities, with a strong emphasis to overcoming competition to win all deals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize and relay customer feedback and findings to inform Stripe’s product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing and Account teams to help amplify our growth trajectory globally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of customer facing experience at a leading technology or payments company and a track record of top performance, working specifically on enterprise or strategic accounts in Southeast Asia and China markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Mandarin and English, as the role involves working with users within the Greater China region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Display a deep passion for fraud prevention and develop deep expertise&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to deal effectively with ambiguity and thrive in an unstructured, fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building trusted advisor relationships with senior business leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter capable of operating independently to drive meaningful business results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience specifically selling fraud solutions for payments to enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UK Enterprise Retail team supports our users to improve their customers&#39; buying experiences, increase their domestic presence whilst expanding into new territories and unlocking new revenue streams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key member to the UK Enterprise Retail team, you will manage and elevate relationships with a named account list while identifying new growth opportunities and ways Stripe can exceed expectations. If you’re motivated, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive (Existing Business), you will create partnerships between Stripe and the most innovative and fastest-growing companies in the world by helping them to understand how Stripe’s online commerce infrastructure can make payments a competitive advantage for their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and nurture a named account list and develop account plans for winning and expanding business with upper middle market and enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain key relationships with C-level executives, while orchestrating the right executive touch points as well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shaping our Enterprise Retail strategy and building repeatable processes and scaled engagement models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop outbound strategies to create and nurture opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle from lead to close for upper middle market and enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop relationships with executive stakeholders at new and existing clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with company leaders from multiple functions (e.g., Engineering, Product, and Finance) to lead complex product workshops and financial analyses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects to develop and refine our sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to help drive product strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an adept salesperson and relationship manager capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization, including the CTO, COO, and CFO. You have experience working with upper middle market and enterprise companies. You have an in-depth understanding of the buyer journey and can lead a complex, multi-party sale in a highly consultative manner. You are used to building value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require deep product understanding, combined with technical knowledge. You are naturally analytical and enjoy digging into business models and helping customers quantify their investment decisions. You get excited about prospecting, and are capable of independently leading a sales cycle from start to finish. Finally, you enjoy building – you like to actively participate in the development of our sales process, the articulation of our value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re motivated, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a technical product, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience directly selling a technology product or service, preferably at an API-first company, with a record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of moving sales processes forward from inception to close by leading complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner, understanding strategies and applying value proposition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great listening skills and ability to quickly become a trusted resource for decision-makers across technology and finance orgs within software companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to understand complex technical problems and understand how Stripe’s solutions can address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A positive attitude and tireless work ethic when encountering blockers to success, whether external or internal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fastidious approach to CRM hygiene and experience utilizing thorough sales forecasting metrics on a weekly/quarterly basis and communicating them in a succinct manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/Software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech/payments is a plus, but not prerequisite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup SaaS Platform team works with European startups in one of Stripe’s must-win segments. At Stripe, SaaS platforms are companies that use Stripe to embed payments and make financial services a core part of their product. Their partnership with Stripe is vital to their business success. Examples include Shopify, Mindbody, and Lightspeed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SaaS platforms are a global priority for Stripe. Our team identifies and develops Stripe’s future strategic accounts in Europe. We identify and partner with high-potential companies, helping them leverage Stripe’s solutions to better support their users, scale globally, and create new revenue streams through monetisation of payments and financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Grower Account Executive on the Startup SaaS Platforms team, you’ll drive Stripe’s future growth through account expansion and client retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll advise businesses on how to optimise their operations using Stripe solutions. You’ll help users understand how Stripe’s modern financial infrastructure supports their growth ambitions and provides a competitive edge for their business or product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly manage and cultivate a named list of existing user accounts, while crafting account plans to expand business and retain clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand users’ pain points and Stripe’s value for SaaS platform clients, proposing tailored solutions that support their long-term growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide clients through complex evaluations of Stripe solutions for SaaS platforms, working with cross-functional teams across Product, Risk, and Operations to move new projects through activation and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic programs that deepen product adoption and maximise effective utilisation across the current user base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster executive relationships with stakeholders at existing clients to drive retention and identify expansion opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams on shared initiatives that drive internal efficiency and broader business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Stripe’s go-to-market priority to expand the user base and optimise the renewals motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a curious, well-rounded strategic seller who builds strong relationships with Stripe’s clients in this key segment. You’re comfortable owning your territory and balancing a mix of high-value, strategic deals with smaller, high-velocity deal cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re solution-oriented and adaptable, with an interest in developing yourself and getting things done. You enjoy highly technical sales cycles and working with a diverse group of internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in a client-facing or closing sales role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical ecosystems and manage complex sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing projects with input from cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with technical customers, work with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, contribute to team success, and share knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivation to operate in a highly ambiguous and fluid environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a sales or customer-facing role at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort interpreting and discussing API-first solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and open up new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a lot of work ahead. That gives you an unusual opportunity to help put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup SaaS Platform team works with European startups in one of Stripe&#39;s most strategic segments. SaaS platforms are companies that use Stripe to embed payments and make financial services a core part of their own product, such as Shopify, Mindbody and Lightspeed. For these companies, their partnership with Stripe is vital to the success of their business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SaaS platforms are a global priority for Stripe, and our team finds and wins Stripe&#39;s future strategic accounts in Europe. We partner with high-potential companies early and help them use Stripe&#39;s solutions to better support their users, scale globally, and create new revenue streams by monetising payments and financial services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Scaled Hunter Account Executive to win new business with pre-revenue and early-stage SaaS platform startups across the EMEA region.&lt;/strong&gt; This is a new-logo role. Your job is to find the most promising founders building platforms today, win them to Stripe before they choose another provider, and get them live on an integration that fits their needs from day one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside our SaaS Platform Account Executives as the team&#39;s dedicated hunter for the earliest stage of the market. You&#39;ll own the pre-revenue and early-revenue segment end to end, from generating pipeline and handling inbound demand to closing deals and getting each new platform to activation and progressing revenue on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Early-stage platforms make their payments decision early and rarely revisit it, and they often need several products from the start: embedded payments, onboarding connected accounts, payouts, and monetisation. Winning them early, and selling the right solution, gives Stripe a lasting position with the platforms that will scale fastest. This is a high-velocity sales role with short cycles, a high volume of opportunities, and plenty of competitive deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and run your own pipeline. Prospect high-potential pre-revenue and early-stage SaaS platforms across the Nordics, Benelux, DACH CEE and Iberia, and turn inbound interest from early-stage platforms into qualified opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Win new logos. Run fast, consultative sales cycles that move from discovery to close, and win competitive evaluations against other payments providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell the right solution from the start. Understand each founder&#39;s business model and position the right Stripe Connect integration and payments monetisation strategy, so new platforms are set up to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close and activate. Negotiate and close deals, then work with Solutions Architects, Product, Risk, and Operations to get new platforms live quickly. You are measured on new business won and activated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source new business through the ecosystem. Build relationships with founders, VC firms, accelerators, and startup communities across EMEA to create pipeline and grow Stripe&#39;s presence among early-stage founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the SaaS Platform Account Executive team. Share market intelligence on emerging platforms and pass on accounts that are past the early stage, so each seller spends time where they can win the most.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring what you learn from the market back to Product and GTM teams to sharpen how Stripe wins early-stage platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re a self-starting hunter who enjoys finding and winning new business. You like working with founders, you&#39;re comfortable leading technical conversations, and you can run many deals at once without losing quality. You know how to qualify quickly, create urgency, and close. You&#39;re competitive, resilient, and keen to build your skills in a fast-changing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4+ years of experience in a new-business sales role, such as a closing AE, or an SDR/BDR role with a track record of progression and pipeline generation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record of meeting or exceeding new-business targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prospecting skills, with experience building your own pipeline through outbound and inbound&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running high-velocity sales cycles from first conversation to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical products and explain their value clearly to technical and non-technical buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with rejection, competitive deals, and ambiguous, fast-moving environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bias towards team success, collaboration, and sharing knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in written and spoken English alongside at least one other European language for markets listed above&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to early-stage or venture-backed startups, ideally in the EMEA region&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An understanding of the startup ecosystem in EMEA, Venture Capital, Private Equity, and accelerators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling at a high-growth technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with API-first products and technical sales conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments, fintech, or SaaS platform sales experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The French SMB Hunter team is responsible for winning net-new business across the SMB segment for the Benelux region. We focus on bringing Stripe products to high-potential businesses that are not yet Stripe customers. We move with urgency, operate with focus, and pride ourselves on delivering strong commercial results through disciplined outbound execution and high-quality customer engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive on the SMB Hunter team, you will own a portfolio of prospective SMB accounts and be responsible for winning new business for Stripe. This is a true hunting role, with a strong emphasis on outbound prospecting, pipeline generation, and closing new logos. You will partner closely with an SDR to execute targeted outbound strategies, while also building your own pipeline through proactive prospecting and account-based selling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run high-velocity, consultative sales cycles, help prospective users understand the value of the Stripe platform, and guide them from discovery through close and activation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle for net-new SMB prospects, from prospecting and discovery through solutioning, negotiation, close, and activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute outbound strategies across a named account set to create, progress, and close new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with SDRs to identify target accounts, refine messaging, and generate qualified pipeline, while also self-sourcing opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead consultative sales conversations with founders, operators, and functional stakeholders across payments, finance, product, and engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand customer pain points and business objectives, and position Stripe products and solutions to meet their needs, while building trusted relationships with key decision-makers and stakeholders throughout the sales process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations to deliver strong outcomes for both Stripe and prospective users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for pipeline quality, forecast accuracy, and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success in a closing sales role with a strong focus on net-new business acquisition, or in a customer-facing role such as solution engineering, implementation consulting, or strategy consulting with demonstrated experience influencing commercial outcomes and executive decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing outbound sales motions and building pipeline through a combination of SDR partnership and self-generated prospecting, or experience partnering closely with sales teams on account-based strategies that generate and progress new business opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to run high-velocity sales cycles while maintaining strong qualification, deal control, and forecasting discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consultative selling skills and the ability to uncover customer needs, build business cases, and align solutions to buyer priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical concepts and communicate the value of multi-product solutions to both business and technical stakeholders, with strong written and verbal communication skills in English&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling payments, fintech, SaaS, or other technology solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth sales environment with strong outbound expectations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with founders and SMB decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with account-based prospecting and territory planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French or Dutch language is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Based in Dublin, this role is a central piece of our dedicated Irish team focused exclusively on accelerating domestic commerce across Ireland. You will act as a critical growth partner to an incredible portfolio of Irish brands across diverse sectors—helping them navigate scaling challenges, unlock product value, and expand both domestically and globally. If you want to play a pivotal role in strengthening Stripe’s footprint in Ireland while directly empowering the next generation of Irish business success stories, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Account Executive, you’ll manage a portfolio spanning high-profile SMB customers and the broader Commercial segment. You’ll own the full sales cycle—from prospecting and closing new business to managing existing relationships and identifying opportunities to expand Stripe’s footprint.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll execute account and sales strategies, engage internal and external stakeholders, align technical and business requirements with product teams, demonstrate value in competitive situations, lead commercial negotiations, and close deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with existing SMB and Commercial Stripe customers to develop and execute long-term strategies that expand Stripe’s revenue and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full sales cycle, from business-case development, deal structuring, and negotiation through to close and activation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a named account list and develop account plans to win and expand business with high-growth technology companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop targeted outbound strategies to create and nurture new opportunities across your portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deal strategy and commercial negotiations for large or complex new business opportunities, expansions, and renewals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with executive stakeholders across your book of business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map accounts and coordinate effective meetings with the appropriate internal and external stakeholders to deepen and expand customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate opportunities of varying size and complexity, balancing velocity across the broader Commercial segment with a highly consultative approach for high-profile SMB accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams to align customers’ technical and business requirements with Stripe’s products and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and contribute to team projects that develop and refine our sales processes and help shape Stripe’s sales culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of sales experience, preferably selling a highly technical product, with a track record of strong performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a varied portfolio and progressing opportunities with different levels of size, complexity, and sales-cycle length.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop and execute account plans spanning multiple business units within complex organisations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for working effectively with a wide range of people, both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills, particularly for in-person meetings involving multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke commercial agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interest in technology and a deep understanding of the space.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

