&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internationalisation team builds the platform that helps Stripe products work naturally across languages and markets. We create and operate the infrastructure that enables Stripe teams to localize product interfaces, services, and written communications while delivering consistent, high-quality experiences to users around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We work closely with our sister Localization team and its language experts, as well as with product and service engineering teams integrating localized content. Together, we combine engineering, automation, and linguistic expertise to help Stripe build products that feel native to each market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, implement, and maintain Stripe’s internationalisation platform at scale, including the developer and user experiences around it. You’ll help teams continuously localize their products while improving the quality, speed, reliability, and efficiency of Stripe’s localization processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines backend and platform engineering with emerging LLM technology. Depending on the project, you may build end-to-end functionality for internal customers, evolve production LLM systems, develop quality-evaluation capabilities, improve platform reliability and observability, or lead migrations from legacy localization infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build internationalisation infrastructure that supports diverse content surfaces, including backend services, product interfaces, and written communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate localization into Stripe’s software-development and content-production workflows, enabling teams to ship translated experiences continuously and safely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain integrations with translation-management systems, LLM services and external localization providers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve Stripe’s existing production LLM capabilities to improve translation quality, market relevance, turnaround time, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop automated quality checks and human-evaluation workflows that combine LLM-driven automation with expert linguistic judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for reliability through effective testing, monitoring, alerting, and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own ambiguous, high-impact initiatives end to end—from research and experimentation through implementation, launch, measurement, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language (we understand new languages can be learned on the job so our interview process is language agnostic)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing reliable infrastructure, platform, or backend-service solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment and a commitment to building high-quality user and developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own ambiguous work end to end and make progress through research, experimentation, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively in a collaborative, cross-functional environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating production LLM or machine-learning systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating LLM output or combining automated systems with expert human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with internationalisation, localization, translation, or content-management workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD systems, developer platforms, or workflow infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Backend engineering experience building services using programming languages such as Java, Ruby, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building internal platforms that ultimately support customer-facing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;hds-heading careers-listing-details__body-title hds-heading--sm&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Link is a digital wallet designed for effortless and secure online payments and digital transactions. With Link, consumers enjoy convenience and peace of mind—it works on any device or browser, is backed by the highest security mechanisms, offers purchase protections on eligible items, and ensures seamless and quick payments. Across the Link Engineering org, we focus on building delightful payment experiences and allowing our global consumer base to pay with their preferred payment methods. Our team&#39;s work spans the entire stack from front-end experiences, to infrastructure that supports low-latency transactions, to intelligent systems that help protect consumers and merchants from bad actors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Team matching for one of the subteams will begin during final stages. Please note we may also consider you for different orgs based on your experience, location, etc. More information on our team matching process can be found&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zvJkO2c7GzukHG-_oqc5wbOLajpuh5FjbmZPcZPU1o0/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.x8j6mm75yuwr&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;hds-heading careers-listing-details__body-title hds-heading--sm&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for engineers who want to make an impact on payments at a global scale. You&#39;ll play a key role in expanding our product suite and the infrastructure that supports it. Our team collaborates with many cross-functional teams and many other teams across Stripe to deliver innovative solutions that address evolving user needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and design the next generation of Stripe products to meet the high-growth needs of our company and customers for years to come&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug and solve critical production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers to help them grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the company to build new features at large-scale, while improving internal engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a distributed and hybrid team, maintaining open communication and strong connections with colleagues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;careers-listing-details__body&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2 class=&quot;hds-heading careers-listing-details__body-title hds-heading--sm&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;hds-text careers-listing-details__body-content hds-text--md hds-text--soft&quot;&gt;
&lt;article&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–10+ years of industry software engineering experience (does not include internships or co-ops)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong coding skills in any programming language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work across workstreams within your team and contribute to your peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility and an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in working as a backend specialist across varying technologies and stacks to solve problems and delight both internal and external users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale financial tracking systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding and practical knowledge in cloud-based services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience with, or enthusiasm for, building with AI and agentic workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Payments Experiences group is an organization focused on bringing new and novel payment methods to Stripe, and ensuring Stripe’s systems work well for merchants globally. This team works with internal and external partners to expand regional, non-card payment options, and to expand the use of Stripe’s payments processing globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a Sao Paulo-based team, with platform teams in the US and Europe and sister teams worldwide. This team in particular will build and maintain new payment methods for Stripe, with a focus on LATAM and North America. They will manage local market idiosyncrasies, become regional experts that other Stripe teams will rely on, and partner with many non-tech functions at Stripe to expand our global reach and product portfolio.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and reason about integration experiences with a strong focus on end-user simplicity and developer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build back-end services and integrations across solutions across Stripe’s payments product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage and interact with external partners to determine and build technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users to understand their business needs and translate requirements into concrete solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams including product, partnerships, eng platforms, and other engineering teams to deliver these solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to software platforms used across payments at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of backend engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of verbal and written English language&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions that scale to different kinds of user needs, with the ability to empathize with users and advocate for exceptional user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experiences working in payments and on payments technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience using Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The UI Platform team, known as Sail, builds the foundations behind Stripe’s Dashboard and many other user interfaces. Sail Services owns the systems that evaluate feature flags and experiments, ingest frontend analytics, and improve Dashboard load times for Stripe’s largest merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build backend-for-frontend capabilities that connect Stripe’s backend systems to its UI platform. This gives product teams a consistent way to build and operate user experiences without recreating the same infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Backend Engineer on the Sail Services team, you’ll help build and evolve the systems that power Stripe’s user interfaces. You’ll independently drive software projects from problem definition through production, working closely with other UI Platform engineers, product teams, and infrastructure partners. Your work will range from APIs and GraphQL integrations to edge systems, architectural migrations, and the tooling needed to operate them safely at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take end-to-end ownership of software projects, aligning on priorities and then independently scoping problems and carrying solutions through design, implementation, testing, rollout, and operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate reliable, scalable APIs and backend systems that support Stripe’s Dashboard, mobile applications, and other user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help modernize Stripe’s UI architecture through incremental migrations, automated validation, shadow traffic, and carefully controlled production rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, observability, performance, and operability of services on critical user paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with frontend, backend, and infrastructure engineers to understand their needs and turn recurring problems into reusable platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted and agentic development workflows to improve implementation, testing, validation, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute thoughtful code reviews, technical discussions, documentation, and runbooks that improve the quality of the team’s work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in using AI-assisted and agentic development tools as part of day-to-day software engineering, including critically reviewing, validating, and improving generated code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of professional software engineering experience, or equivalent practical experience, building, shipping, and operating production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of backend technologies and infrastructure, including the fundamentals of APIs, data storage, distributed systems, and production operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently scope and deliver open-ended software projects, making practical technical and product tradeoffs with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and debugging skills, with attention to testing, maintainability, reliability, and user impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively with frontend engineers, product engineers, and infrastructure partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building backend-for-frontend systems, UI platform services, developer platforms, or shared infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or integrating APIs, including GraphQL APIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-throughput event ingestion, feature flag or experimentation systems, or other latency-sensitive platform services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with caching, asynchronous systems, configuration systems, or data-consistency tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience executing large migrations using automated validation, shadow traffic, feature flags, or staged rollouts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data, developer feedback, or operational signals to improve a platform or developer-facing product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the gross domestic product of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits team is fundamental to the Stripe experience and directly supports our global workforce. The team ensures that our programs are competitive, clearly understood, and compliant with local regulations across 30 countries. We continually update our benefits strategy to meet the diverse needs of Stripe and Stripes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Benefits Program Manager plays a key role in shaping the strategy, execution, and user experience of our benefits programs. This role focuses primarily on benefits strategy and plan design, financial stewardship, vendor management, communications, the Stripe experience, and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is suited to someone who can think strategically while supporting the successful execution of day-to-day operations and our broader benefits strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full lifecycle of our benefits programs, including market research, benchmarking, plan design, vendor selection and management, annual renewals and negotiations, communications, administration, security reviews, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor industry trends and regulatory changes, and recommend new or updated programs that align with Stripe’s business and Total Rewards strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a subject matter expert and develop clear communication plans that help Stripes understand our programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for benefits vendors, brokers, and third-party administrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and evaluate potential vendors, and manage the request for proposal process in partnership with Procurement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess vendor performance and manage contracts in partnership with Legal, ensuring that vendors meet their contractual commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compile, analyze, and report on key benefits metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with People Partners, People Consultants, Finance, Payroll, Employee Relations, and Legal to support a coordinated approach to our benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance to manage the benefits budget, prepare cost projections, and evaluate the return on investment of new and existing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use Workday and our benefits administration platform to improve workflows and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People Systems to deliver key initiatives and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you’re encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 to 7 years of experience in a benefits role with similar responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and improving employee benefits programs using data, Stripe feedback, and financial analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of government regulations related to employee benefits and time off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing pension and time-off plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using benefits administration platforms, such as Workday.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing stakeholders and negotiating contracts with benefits vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, growing environment, preferably in a technology company or large-scale organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive projects independently, identify and raise issues, and seek feedback when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment, with the ability to make decisions that align with Stripe’s culture and benefits strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing change initiatives related to benefits programs, including vendor or system implementations and transitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced data analysis and financial forecasting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mergers and acquisitions and benefits integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a Security Engineer to build and scale the Bridge security foundation. This is a rare opportunity to design a security program from the ground up, while also leveraging the infrastructure, best practices, and tooling of one of the most mature security organizations in the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement the Bridge security roadmap from first principles to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and tackle the most important Bridge security risks quickly and pragmatically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with Stripe infrastructure where it makes sense, and find custom solutions where it doesn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead threat modeling and hardening efforts for the Bridge money movement systems in collaboration with crypto and infra teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build key security capabilities, including monitoring, secrets management, incident response, access controls, and CI/CD hardening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reinforce engineering best practices around secure development and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Bridge meets compliance and audit expectations as we scale to more regulated markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product, and the Stripe security organization to move fast without compromising safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in Security engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling security programs at a startup or in an embedded role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fast-paced startup environments, building security practices from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Startup mindset—scrappy, pragmatic, and quick to solve the most critical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort writing and debugging backend application code, with Ruby experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with ambiguity and ability to ruthlessly prioritize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance security rigor with speed, especially in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication across technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in the potential of crypto and stablecoins to power global financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Accounting team at Stripe supports products across Stripe by providing guidance on accounting implications and enabling teams to make informed strategic decisions. The team records business transactions accurately and on time in the balance sheet and income statement, and partners with cross-functional and international teams in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an experienced accountant to join our world-class accounting team, focusing on products developed by our Bridge subsidiary. You’ll leverage your technical expertise with U.S. GAAP to identify accounting implications and customer impacts and advise cross-functional partners. You will be responsible for ensuring timely and accurate month-end close results for Bridge products, while also working on initiatives to create scalable accounting solutions..&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly close activities, including journal entries, reconciliations, analytic reviews, and financial reporting deliverables for Bridge products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recommend and implement scalable accounting processes to support global growth at Bridge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our business and finance teams to understand new products, features, and contracts, and advise on accounting implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Internal Systems and Engineering teams to improve financial systems and automate accounting processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the effectiveness of internal controls and design processes and controls for emerging business activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand data and system flows, analyzing financial results to identify and address anomalies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting and/or industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional accountancy qualification, such as CA, CPA, ACA, ACCA, or CIMA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of US GAAP and experience with internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with monthly or quarterly close processes, journal-entry preparation and posting, audits, regulatory reporting, financial-statement preparation, and accounting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills, with the ability to convey financial concepts to both financial and non-financial audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to structure ambiguous work and build systems and automation&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
