&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To avoid the worst effects of climate change, most climate models agree the world will need to dramatically reduce emissions &lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt; remove 5-10 billion tons of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere per year by 2050. The Climate team’s goal is to accelerate Stripe’s path to net zero in parallel with the world’s. We do this by reducing Stripe’s emissions and leading initiatives to increase the likelihood we build sufficient carbon removal capacity to reach global climate goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In 2019, we developed the first measurement of Stripe’s emissions. In 2021 we launched&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/climate&quot;&gt; Stripe Climate&lt;/a&gt;, enabling merchants to direct a fraction of their revenue to help scale emerging carbon removal technologies. In 2022 we launched &lt;a href=&quot;https://frontierclimate.com/&quot;&gt;Frontier&lt;/a&gt;, an advance market commitment to buy $1.8B+ of permanent carbon removal by 2040. In 2024, we entered our first multi-year offtake for clean energy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, Stripe’s corporate net zero program is entering a new phase. We are looking to streamline our emissions measurement, create a template for catalytic emission reductions, and champion buying removals on the path to net zero, all while meeting our expanding global ESG disclosure requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s Climate Program Manager, you will set the strategy and lead the execution and reporting for Stripe’s corporate net zero program. You’ll partner with a wide range of stakeholders within and outside of Stripe – Accounting, Finance, Legal, Procurement, Facilities, Sales, and carbon accounting and assurance providers – to refine our greenhouse gas inventory, deliver a reduction and removal roadmap that meets our climate targets, and provide inputs to global ESG disclosures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires someone with expertise in carbon accounting and reductions strategy, sharp program and process management, a track record of getting big things done fast, and excellent judgement to make the ‘right’ recommendations for Stripe’s program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Net Zero strategy (~15%): &lt;/strong&gt;Own and evolve Stripe’s corporate net zero strategy, including Stripe’s transition plan, priorities, budget, annual goals, emissions forecasts, removal retirements, and progress tracking. Stay current on evolving disclosure requirements, net zero guidance, and industry best practices to ensure Stripe’s program is high impact and best in class&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions measurement (~30%): &lt;/strong&gt;Build Stripe’s annual greenhouse gas inventory. Collect data inputs, evolve methodology, manage Stripe’s footprint vendors, run a rigorous and auditable process with cross-functional stakeholders, and identify opportunities to use AI to improve the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Emissions reporting (~30%):&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Serve as Stripe’s subject-matter expert to deliver inputs to ESG controllership for regulatory disclosures and to customers for RFPs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduction program (~25%):&lt;/strong&gt; Develop and manage emissions reduction initiatives across Stripe. This will include efforts like securing renewable electricity for Stripe’s scope 2 emissions, as well as supporting the creative and high-impact interventions like carbon removal or lower-emission data centers that we need to reach global net zero&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA or BS degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in corporate sustainability, climate strategy, carbon accounting, environmental consulting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent oral and written communication skills – especially adept at translating complexity into clear recommendations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of generating and implementing ambitious emissions reduction initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative skills and expertise in emissions accounting and Greenhouse Gas Protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has led a corporate climate program in a sector with a significant Scope 3 footprint, ideally technology or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is a self-starter, and has a proven track record of producing measurable reductions through clean energy, cloud usage, and other supplier engagement initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has a working knowledge of major emissions accounting and climate reporting standards and requirements (e.g., CSRD, California SB 253, GHG protocol), and experience with Watershed or similar enterprise carbon management&amp;nbsp; platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience partnering with cross functional controllership partners to manage a greenhouse gas inventory process that meets requirements for limited or reasonable assurance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is an exceptionally fast learner. Enjoys (and has experience) quickly ramping on new reduction technologies and sustainability standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe powers businesses all over the world. We process payments, run marketplaces, detect fraud, help entrepreneurs start a business from anywhere in the world, build world-class developer-friendly APIs, and more. Nearly every system we operate interacts with sensitive financial or personal data—making security a top priority for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe will succeed at our mission of increasing the GDP of the internet only if we prove ourselves worthy of our users&#39; trust. As an engineer on the Security team, you&#39;ll design and develop frameworks, systems, and solutions to ensure the security of Stripe&#39;s engineering infrastructure and, most importantly, privacy of our users&#39; data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Cloud Security team accelerates Stripe&#39;s business priorities by building core security controls and services that empower teams to build quickly and securely on top of a well-governed cloud platform and partnering with infrastructure teams to advance select critical business priorities using novel infrastructure or integrations as that platform expands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and operate the core security infrastructure used by all of Stripe&#39;s engineering teams in close collaboration with other stakeholders and our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold our high engineering standards and bring consistency to the many codebases and processes you&#39;ll encounter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to team learning by improving engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build durable solutions that will advance Stripe&#39;s security beyond the state of the art&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help expand Stripe&#39;s cloud footprint on top of secure, paved roads and guardrails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize for security controls that have delightful user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with infrastructure and engineering teams building integrations with our cloud infrastructure or adopting new cloud managed services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make impactful decisions about systems and security—their edge cases, failure modes, and life cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to determine appropriate baselines against which to measure security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define infrastructure that reliably feeds signals to threat teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and prototype new security tools and practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You may work on&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and implementing controls that support security invariants and enforce our security principles while providing a surprisingly great user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing a migration path for newly acquired companies onto the Stripe Secure Platform, embedding with their engineers and biasing for action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI tooling for platform-related configuration, including IAM roles, SCPs, and associated components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guardrails and security controls for both commonly used and newer cloud technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding our cloud identity infrastructure to provide paved paths for AI and agentic access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation tooling for continually driving down permissions and access across our cloud services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, strong communication skills, and a deep respect for the power of collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A learning mindset, regardless of level or experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to drive clear next steps when encountering ambiguous spaces without clear lines of ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High standards for code quality and a constructive attitude to help others raise the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering experience in a high-stakes production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for considering how systems can fail and how to fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with security on one or more of AWS, Azure, or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting threat modeling of software or infrastructure in cloud-native environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Linux systems, Kubernetes, and container-based platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior usage of security monitoring tools (e.g., CSPM, CNAAP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a multi-cloud or complex cloud environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A knack for considering how systems can fail and how to fix them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ability to think creatively and holistically about reducing risk in a complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Commercial Sales team is responsible for the acquisition, growth, retention, and expansion of mid-market customers. As a Grower Commercial Account Executive, you’ll set strategy for your territory, identify opportunities for existing customers to get the most out of Stripe, execute scaled sales strategies to grow revenue and drive end-to-end campaigns to nurture relationships and increase adoption of Stripe products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will play an instrumental role in fueling Stripe’s growth and expanding revenue from Stripe’s existing mid-market customers. In this role, you will also help build out a new team touching more of our install base and GTM motion at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate upsell opportunities to drive revenue growth in your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement sales strategies to grow revenue per user, adopt new products and ensure retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and understand users’ pain points to propose Stripe solutions and own the full sales cycle, from business case development to close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own contract renewals and lead commercial negotiations to increase and retain existing customer revenue and increase Stripe share of wallet&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to solve user pain points and improve Stripe’s product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 5+ years full sales cycle/closing experience with existing business accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple technology&amp;nbsp; products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform quantitative analysis and independently manage pricing negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong operational acumen and ability to manage and prioritize a book of 100 accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability and motivation to operate in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a sales and/or customer-facing role at a high growth payments company&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position details&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employer:&lt;/strong&gt; Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employment type:&lt;/strong&gt; Full-time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; 383 Kent Street, Sydney, NSW 2000, Australia&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications open:&lt;/strong&gt; 30th October 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applications close:&lt;/strong&gt; 30 November 2026&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a global technology company that builds infrastructure for online commerce with a mission to increase the GDP of the internet. Through Bridge, Stripe is building stablecoin infrastructure that helps businesses move, store, and use money globally. This role will support Bridge as it develops and scales products for companies operating across markets.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for an exceptional transactional lawyer to join our commercial legal team supporting Bridge and Stripe’s fast-growing stablecoin business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Support Bridge’s commercial team, leading negotiations for complex and strategic user and partner agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on commercial and legal issues arising from stablecoin products, new product launches, and international expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product Legal and Bridge’s product and engineering teams to bring new products and features to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build Bridge’s commercial legal infrastructure so the business can scale efficiently, including drafting and maintaining agreements and playbooks, improving internal processes, and using AI tooling to optimize how we work with clients, partners, and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams across Bridge and Stripe globally, including commercial, operations, product, engineering, tax, compliance, and risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team provide practical, scalable legal support while working collaboratively across a global Commercial Legal team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver training and resources to help Bridge’s commercial team sell and support its products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a point of escalation for outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectually curious and a creative problem solver - Bridge’s products and the stablecoin industry are complex and fast evolving - you should relish learning new products and finding practical solutions to challenging problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a bias for action - you are proactive and have a strong sense of ownership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A clear and concise communicator (in written and verbal forms), who can distill the key risks and explain complex, nuanced issues in plain and simple terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural collaborator, able to guide cross-functional teams and drive to a win-win solution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with the legal issues and commercial risks arising from fintech, stablecoin, hosted data, and technology services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A team player who is willing to do what it takes to contribute to the collective success.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified with good standing membership in at least one US state bar with a JD degree or foreign equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience in-house or in a technology practice group in a top law firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;E&lt;/span&gt;xperience working in payments, fintech, crypto, or stablecoin businesses and knowledge of associated regulatory issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience advising high-growth companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of LLM tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in improving legal processes with AI technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A working knowledge of data protection laws such as CCPA, GDPR, and HIPAA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company that builds financial infrastructure for the internet. Millions of businesses, from startups to global enterprises, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and expand into new markets. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our products support a broad range of business needs, from payments and software services to emerging areas such as stablecoins and agentic commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;about-the-role&quot;&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced transactional lawyer to join our Commercial Legal team supporting Stripe’s business in the Americas. You’ll lead complex commercial negotiations, advise on new products and international expansion, and help build the legal processes and tools that support Stripe’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work closely with Sales, Product Legal, and teams across Stripe to solve challenging problems and provide practical advice. You’ll also help improve how the Commercial Legal team works, including through the use of AI tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the Americas Sales team and lead negotiations for complex and strategic commercial agreements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise on commercial and legal issues related to new product launches and international expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Legal to bring new products and features to market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft and maintain agreements and playbooks, improve internal processes, and use AI tools to help the team work more effectively with colleagues, partners, and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams globally, including Sales, Operations, Product, Tax, and Risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the global Commercial Legal team deliver consistent, efficient support as Stripe grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and deliver training and resources that help the Sales team understand and sell Stripe’s products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of escalation for outside counsel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you do, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Juris Doctor (JD) degree or foreign equivalent, and membership in good standing in at least one U.S. state bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5+ years of relevant legal experience, either in-house or in the technology practice of a leading law firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the legal issues and commercial risks associated with hosted data and technology services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intellectual curiosity and creative problem-solving skills, with an interest in learning complex, evolving products and finding practical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach and a strong sense of ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex issues and key risks in plain language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to guide cross-functional teams toward solutions that address business needs and legal risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach and a willingness to contribute to the team’s shared success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments or financial technology, including familiarity with related regulatory issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-house experience advising high-growth companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of large language model (LLM) tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI technology to improve legal processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of data protection laws such as the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), and the Health Insurance Portability and Accountability Act (HIPAA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk team helps maintain a healthy financial ecosystem for businesses around the world. Credit Operations conducts credit risk assessments, underwrites small and mid-sized users, and develops mitigation strategies that enable Stripe to take smart risks while supporting growth. The globally distributed team partners with stakeholders across regions to support new and existing users and products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Credit Operations Manager, you will lead and develop a team of credit operations analysts while setting a strategic vision for scalable, high-quality operations. You will help enable new and existing Stripe products by translating product strategies into operational capabilities and appropriate credit controls. In partnership with Credit Strategy, Product, Engineering, and Data Science, you will launch new programs and advance AI-enabled automation across Credit Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, motivate, and develop a high-performing Credit Operations team by setting clear goals, providing regular coaching and feedback, and supporting professional growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess the team’s current and future capability needs and partner on hiring, workforce planning, and development strategies to close material gaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set priorities for the team in alignment with Credit’s broader strategy and translate them into clear goals, work plans, and operating mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve Credit Operations’ systems, processes, and operating model to improve decision quality, mitigate emerging risks, and scale efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new and existing Stripe products by assessing credit and operational impacts, defining requirements and controls, and preparing Credit Operations for launch and ongoing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Risk leadership and cross-functional stakeholders to prioritize investments in risk mitigation, operational efficiency, and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-enabled tools and partner with technical and operational stakeholders to test and implement automation, with appropriate quality controls and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage operating metrics and service-level agreements, using performance insights and root-cause analysis to drive improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee credit-related vendor performance and ensure work meets applicable quality and compliance standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10-15 years of work experience in commercial credit underwriting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience leading credit risk or underwriting teams in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial risk modeling or cash-flow forecasting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building, leading, and developing high-performing teams, including setting goals, managing performance, and coaching team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic thinking and problem-solving skills with the ability to translate complex challenges into actionable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to influence across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing, launching, and scaling programs, products, or operational capabilities from planning through implementation and measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-enabled tools and partnering with technical and operational stakeholders to implement automation, including quality controls, change management, and team adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to delivering a user-centered experience while effectively managing risk&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting credit-related product launches or translating product capabilities into operational requirements, workflows, controls, and launch-readiness plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of accounting principles and experience evaluating financial statements and business models across industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience analyzing data and creating dashboards using SQL&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering teams to develop or improve investigative and decisioning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field; advanced degree or certification is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s comms organization does more than the traditional: we produce films that get shown at festivals, sell over 300,000 books annually, run some of the fastest growing social media channels in tech, write talks and skits for external and internal events attended by thousands of people, build physical machines that track commerce in real-time, create podcasts in pubs, and much more besides. We believe in small, elite, high-taste teams and aim to run a tight operation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Comms Operations is a small, nimble team serving as the connective tissue between strategy and execution. Our mission is simple: we build and redefine the operating foundations that enable the most creative and ambitious storytelling in the world possible. This is not a traditional operations role, and we’re not looking to introduce heavy processes or to eliminate the unpredictability inherent in comms work. Instead, you’ll have a front-row seat in how the Communications team builds and protects Stripe’s brand and influence across the world – and play a pivotal part in designing the flywheel that compounds that impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an exceptional and ambidextrous early-career operator to help us build and scale this infrastructure. You will work across every altitude, from co-designing high-level team planning mechanisms to managing the granular details of a complex project to ensure that it lands successfully. Some weeks, that might mean redesigning processes and building custom AI agents to handle repetitive workflows. Other weeks, it’s gaveling on the best lightning talks to feature during our onsite and pitching a mandatory jingle jam.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team systems &amp;amp; infrastructure: &lt;/strong&gt;Create processes, onboarding resources, and shared playbooks that help the team prioritize, track, and execute work effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workflow automation:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead the transformation of the team’s critical administrative engines such as inbound media requests, speaking inquiries, and team communication channels and aliases. You’ll identify recurring patterns and build AI-enabled workflows and automations that make these processes faster, more reliable, and easier to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project and program management: &lt;/strong&gt;Act as the embedded PgM for complex comms programs (e.g., Stripe Sessions, the Annual Letter) from planning through execution. Translate fast-moving initiatives into clear objectives, plans, milestones, and reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Budget and resource management: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage the team’s resourcing and budget management process including contracting, POs, payments, tracking and budget reporting.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measurement and reporting: &lt;/strong&gt;Build and maintain reporting systems and data dashboards that track communications impact, media coverage, and operational efficiency. Turn the data into clear insights that help the team make decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of experience in strategy, operations, program management, or an operating role supporting a senior leader or complex, cross-functional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven systems thinker who can bring clarity to messy workflows or chaotic projects. You naturally look for the root causes behind problems and build long-lasting solutions rather than one-off fixes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable navigating ambiguity in a fast-paced environment and are able to swiftly adapt as priorities shift alongside the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized and able to manage several workstreams without losing attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively use AI in your daily work and experience building automations to eliminate manual drag for yourself and your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with data and are willing to learn new tools to answer operational questions (e.g. writing basic SQL queries or building custom dashboards from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior operations or program management experience specifically within communications, public relations, marketing, public affairs or experience in an adjacent fast-paced, high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable operational processes or&amp;nbsp; programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets and financial operations, including vendor contracting, purchase orders, payments, and budget tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with communications-specific metrics, media-monitoring platforms, and methods for tracking brand sentiment or impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with SQL, data pipelines, dashboards, workflow-automation tools, or AI agents.&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/en-sg/customers&quot;&gt;enterprises&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.stripeeconomics.com/p/the-age-of-the-solopreneur&quot;&gt;solopreneurs&lt;/a&gt; to the &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/en-sg/sessions/2026/inside-the-ai-economy&quot;&gt;most ambitious startups&lt;/a&gt;—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s comms organisation does more than the traditional: we produce films that get shown at festivals, sell over 300,000 books annually, run some of the fastest growing social media channels in tech, write talks and skits for external and internal events attended by thousands of people, build physical machines that track commerce in real-time, create podcasts in pubs, and much more besides. We believe in small, elite, high-taste teams and aim to run a tight operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an entrepreneurial and creative communications professional to help tell Stripe’s story across Greater China and Southeast Asia. Someone who can position Stripe as a partner to the region’s most ambitious businesses and entrepreneurs; who has a long-term mindset when it comes to building reputation and trust; and who is obsessed with the craft and beauty of communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is both strategic and hands-on. They’re creative, curious, pragmatic—and able to develop and execute Stripe’s communications strategy across our region. They understand the local media and influencer landscape and can turn complex products and technical ideas into clear, compelling stories about what Stripe is building and why it matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape Stripe’s narrative and tell compelling stories about Stripe’s infrastructure, the businesses we’re proud to serve, and how Asian entrepreneurs and companies are contributing to greater economic prosperity—both regionally and globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside Stripe users and partners, bringing their voices, ambitions, and experiences into campaigns, announcements, and other communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with business and technology reporters, influential thinkers, and other important stakeholders across the region, find creative, ever-changing tactics to underscore how Stripe drives economic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply excellent judgment and calm, clear communication to complex, high-profile corporate issues when they arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach each opportunity from first principles rather than relying on familiar playbooks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant experience in communications, public relations, journalism, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly entrepreneurial. You must be highly adaptable, fast to learn, and possess a track record of building creative campaigns from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with an ability to understand, synthesise, and explain complex or technically sophisticated topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Southeast Asia and Greater China, including their business, technology, and media landscapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building relationships with business and technology reporters and other influential stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to manage multiple markets, projects, and collaborate effectively with internal and external stakeholders simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, intellectual curiosity, creativity, and exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to move between strategy and execution—from shaping a regional narrative to drafting social copies and coordinating launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in written and verbal Mandarin Chinese is preferred for this role, as it involves crafting communication content for the Greater China Region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting communications in both Southeast Asia and Greater China, as well as working with global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments, fintech, enterprise technology, cross-border commerce, or the broader internet economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing communications agencies across multiple markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You should include these in your application&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resume or LinkedIn profile.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Writing samples are always welcome.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any other information that would help us understand your background and accomplishments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Singapore (currently residing, or willing to relocate).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Community Operations manages Stripe’s support presence across public developer and merchant communities. The team responds across channels including X, Reddit, LinkedIn, Facebook, YouTube, and app-store reviews. Because these interactions are public and one-to-many, each response can influence user trust, Stripe’s brand, and the experience of people beyond the original poster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team combines responsive community support with proactive signal detection. We identify recurring questions, emerging risk, product friction, documentation gaps, and opportunities to improve how Stripe supports its community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Community Operations Specialist, you will represent Stripe across public developer and merchant communities. You will independently assess and coordinate complex or high-visibility community cases, including situations involving influential users, executive tags, rapid amplification, privacy concerns, and incomplete information. You will guide less-experienced teammates, support incident and escalation response, surface recurring user and product signals, and contribute to defined operational-improvement projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will maintain strong queue performance while building experience in higher-impact Specialist work. For novel, highly sensitive, or incident-level decisions, you will work with senior Specialists and cross-functional partners to determine the safest path forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage community interactions across supported platforms while consistently meeting quality, productivity, and responsiveness expectations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Act as an escalation point for complex, sensitive, ambiguous, or high-visibility community cases, including influential users, executive tags, media-adjacent attention, rapid amplification, cross-platform misinformation, and privacy or brand concerns.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Support teammates as they navigate complex cases by providing actionable feedback and explaining the reasoning behind recommended responses and escalation decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Recognize potential social-media incidents or high-risk situations and engage a senior Specialist or incident lead before making a novel or material-risk public commitment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Participate in incident response under senior Specialist guidance, maintaining clear ownership and communication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gather relevant facts, identify stakeholders and risks, consider response options, and recommend a safe path forward for escalated cases.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Use dashboards, queue reviews, social-listening reports, and basic operational data to identify patterns and support decisions; develop familiarity with basic queries where helpful.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Communicate clear product, user, and risk signals to cross-functional partners such as Product, Risk, Comms, and Docs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Contribute to trend summaries, incident retrospectives, product-signal reports, playbooks, and internal knowledge resources.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Own defined components of pre-scoped improvement projects, maintaining a plan and communicating progress, dependencies, blockers, and risks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Capture reusable lessons from escalations and share them through team documentation and knowledge-sharing forums.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. Preferred qualifications are helpful but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience in public-facing support, community operations, technical support, or a comparable user-facing operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Exceptional written judgment, with the ability to communicate complex or unfavorable information clearly, empathetically, and safely in public forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Sound judgment when handling ambiguity, sensitive user situations, incomplete information, and potential reputational risk, with the ability to prioritize competing cases using user impact, urgency, sensitivity, privacy risk, and public amplification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ownership and the ability to organize work, follow through on commitments, and communicate blockers early.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to guide or support less-experienced teammates using clear, actionable feedback and sound reasoning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfort using dashboards, queue reviews, and basic operational data to identify patterns and support decisions; willingness to develop basic query skills where helpful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to collaborate effectively with teammates and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Receptiveness to feedback and evidence of applying feedback to improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with Stripe products, payments, financial technology, APIs, or developer-facing support.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting users through public or social channels.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with incident response, social escalation, moderation, or brand-risk workflows.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience contributing to operational-improvement projects, root-cause investigations, or knowledge-management initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with operational reporting, social-listening data, SQL, or other data-analysis tools.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, our Mexico City office is a vibrant hub at the forefront of our mission to reshape the financial landscape for businesses worldwide. Our team prioritizes collaboration, innovation, and excellence. As a member of the Mexico City team, you&#39;ll be part of a mission-driven community dedicated to enhancing the global economy and increasing the GDP of the internet. We strive for excellence by creating with craft and beauty, while having fun and celebrating our successes together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;We cultivate a culture of collaboration, inclusivity, and support where every team member’s voice matters. Our commitment shines through as we handle over a million support cases each year, empowering our users not just to solve problems but to achieve their goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Troubleshoot and solve external user issues&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Analyze our processes and instigate changes to help scale our operations and improve user experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work closely with other Stripe teams to improve our product offerings and messaging around new products and features&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gain unique insights into how thousands of businesses on Stripe scale and operate&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Have an opportunity to learn how Stripe operates from the ground up and make a real impact on the future of the organization&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Be a part of building a brand-new team and operational culture for Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Partner with global operations specialists or business process owners to run a critical workflow&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You have a user-first mindset and are energized by the challenge of solving difficult problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You have excellent communication skills, both written and verbal&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You excel in critical thinking and problem solving&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You have prior experience in customer service or internal and external user-facing operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You enjoy learning about technical products and processes, you&#39;re an organized, self-starter with passion for finding solutions to our user’s challenges&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You have a process-oriented mindset and the ability to get things done&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You enjoy working in an in-office environment with strong cross-team collaboration and support&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You prioritize well and enjoy working in a quick-moving environment&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You are humble and have a proven track record for working well across teams and with external partners&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re willing to periodically work a weekend day for which you&#39;ll receive a weekday off. The SDC operates during daytime hours with shifts from the morning through early evening&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior experience or knowledge in user support&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior experience working on projects or process improvement initiatives&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the teams&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Controllership organization is responsible for the accurate and timely recording of Stripe’s business activities, the integrity of our financial reporting, and the scalable processes and controls that support our growth. We partner across Finance, Product, Engineering, Operations, Sales, Legal, Tax, Treasury, and Internal Audit to understand Stripe’s products and operations, resolve complex financial issues, and maintain a strong control environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring four Controllership Interns, with one role on each of the following teams: Accounts Receivable (AR), Controls, Product Accounting, and Corporate Accounting. In any placement, you’ll work with experienced teammates and cross-functional partners on meaningful accounting, data, systems, controls, or process-improvement work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounts Receivable (AR)&lt;/strong&gt; supports invoicing, collections, cash application, and related financial operations through scalable, accurate, and auditable processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controls&lt;/strong&gt; supports Stripe’s internal-control environment by documenting and assessing processes, identifying risks, supporting control testing, and helping teams design sustainable improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Accounting&lt;/strong&gt; supports Stripe’s products by understanding their financial-data flows, evaluating accounting implications, and developing scalable processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Accounting&lt;/strong&gt; supports Stripe’s close, financial reporting, corporate accounting processes, and control environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for graduate students who want to deliver outsized impact while accelerating their growth in a fast-paced, dynamic environment. You’ll apply classroom learning to important accounting and financial-data problems at an industry leader in fintech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll support meaningful work with an impact on Stripe and its users, and collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders. Depending on your placement, you may:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support core Controllership activities based on your placement, including accounts receivable operations, monthly and quarterly close, financial reporting, product accounting, or internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare or support journal entries, account reconciliations, supporting schedules, variance analysis, and other accounting deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze large financial and operational datasets using Google Sheets, SQL, AI tools, or other systems to identify unusual activity, data-quality issues, reconciliation breaks, control gaps, or operational trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support invoicing, collections, cash application, or related order-to-cash processes, where relevant to your placement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research accounting questions and prepare clear supporting documentation under the guidance of experienced accountants&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the design, documentation, testing, and improvement of accounting processes and internal controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support financial reporting, management analysis, and internal or external audit requests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with stakeholders across Accounting, Finance, Product, Operations, Engineering, Sales, Legal, Tax, Treasury, and Internal Audit to understand business activities and resolve issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous process improvement, standardization, simplification, automation, and reporting enhancements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete and present a case study or scoped project to your team and the broader Controllership organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently enrolled at an accredited university pursuing a master’s degree in Accounting, Finance, Economics, Information Systems, Business, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework, a project, or practical experience demonstrating a foundational understanding of accounting principles and financial statements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Google Workspace or Microsoft Office tools, including experience analyzing large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using SQL to query, analyze, and validate data through coursework, projects, or practical work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving and analytical skills, with the ability to bring structure to ambiguous opportunities in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who can drive results, manage multiple priorities, and meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A solution-oriented mindset and enthusiasm for establishing best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build strong, collaborative working relationships with business partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coursework or experience in Intermediate Accounting, audit, technical accounting, information systems, or data analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python, data visualization, or dashboarding tools such as Power BI or Tableau&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with an ERP, financial-reporting, or workflow-automation tool&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI for financial analysis or process improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in payments, fintech, financial infrastructure, digital assets, or technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience documenting a process or presenting analytical findings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Recruiting team builds Stripe’s culture by connecting exceptional talent with our highest-impact business needs. We bring Stripe’s operating principles to life through thoughtful, consistent hiring practices, a high-quality candidate experience, and data-informed partnership with the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for a consultative, creative recruiter to support critical Core Business functions. You will partner with senior leaders who shape Stripe’s financial strategy, external narrative, long-term growth, and company-wide decision-making.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact portfolio with varied talent markets, senior stakeholders, and roles where the quality of each hire can influence how Stripe operates and grows. You will own full-cycle recruiting, advise leaders on hiring strategy and market conditions, and build trusted relationships with candidates and hiring teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This is a 12 month fixed term contract and you are employed directly through Stripe.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders to understand business priorities, define hiring plans, and develop recruiting strategies that support headcount goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full recruiting lifecycle, from intake and sourcing through offer acceptance and onboarding handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise hiring teams on talent-market conditions, candidate availability, competitive dynamics, and hiring approaches for specialized and senior roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute sourcing strategies that build broad, qualified candidate pipelines for current and future hiring needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong candidate relationships and deliver a thoughtful, timely candidate experience throughout the process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use recruiting data to track progress, identify risks and opportunities, and provide clear updates to business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve recruiting processes where needed, testing practical changes that help hiring teams move with clarity and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with cross-functional teams, including Finance, People Operations, Benefits, Onboarding, and Legal, to support a smooth offer and onboarding experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold structured, competency-based hiring practices and help hiring teams assess candidates against the requirements of each role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, including in-house recruiting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with senior leaders on hiring strategy, talent-market insights, and complex searches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trust with senior stakeholders and influence decisions through sound judgment, data, and market knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sourcing strategies and engaging candidates for specialized or senior roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use recruiting data to identify trends, communicate progress, and improve recruiting outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple searches and shifting priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach and comfort working across functions to solve problems and improve the hiring experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about emerging AI tools and a practical approach to testing and adopting new ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting for business, corporate, finance, communications, strategy, legal, or other specialized professional functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting senior-level hiring or roles with complex stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across multiple geographies or advising on location strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with recruiting systems and sourcing tools, including applicant tracking systems, candidate relationship management tools, and LinkedIn Recruiter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we&#39;re building our Accounting team in Bangalore Finance and are looking for someone to help us scale for the future in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly detail-oriented and tech-forward Corporate Accounting Analyst to join our fast-paced corporate accounting team. In this role, you will play a critical part in managing General Ledger (GL) activities, ensuring accurate close processes, and driving accounting precision across specialized technical areas, including debt, prepaids, intercompany transactions, and lease accounting .&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate holds a &lt;strong&gt;Chartered Accountant (CA)&lt;/strong&gt; qualification, possesses &lt;strong&gt;4–6 years of progressive accounting experience&lt;/strong&gt;, and brings a modern, tech-enabled mindset—specifically the ability to leverage AI tools, automation, and advanced analytics to streamline workflows and solve complex accounting problems in a rapidly evolving environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end accounting schedules, journal entries, and balance sheet reconciliations for corporate accounting areas .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage month-end, quarter-end, and year-end closing activities within prescribed timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct variance analyses on P&amp;amp;L and Balance Sheet line items, investigating unexpected fluctuations and providing actionable commentary to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal and external audit requests by preparing audit schedules, supporting documentation, and clear accounting workpapers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams (F&amp;amp;S, FinOps, Tax, Operations) to ensure accurate accounting treatment for complex transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage&lt;strong&gt; ERP automation, analytical capabilities&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;AI-driven tools &lt;/strong&gt;(e.g., prompt engineering, automated reconciliation workflows, intelligent data extraction) to enhance accuracy and timeliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify bottlenecks in the financial close cycle and implement automated solutions or streamlined workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize advanced data tools to process large volumes of financial data accurately under tight deadliness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Certification:&lt;/strong&gt; Chartered Accountant (CA) or equivalent professional accounting designation is &lt;strong&gt;mandatory&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;4 to 6 years&lt;/strong&gt; of post-qualification core corporate accounting experience, with strong hands-on expertise in General Ledger operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI &amp;amp; Tech Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to adopt and operate AI tools (e.g., generative AI for documentation/analysis, workflow automation software, advanced ERP modules) to optimize accounting tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Competencies &amp;amp; Soft Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Paced Adaptability:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to prioritize effectively, meet tight monthly/quarterly closing deadlines, and thrive in an agile, dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical &amp;amp; Detail-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; Exceptional problem-solving skills with a high degree of precision in numerical and technical accounting work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt; Clear verbal and written communication skills to effectively collaborate with remote teams, management, and external auditors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Self-Starter:&lt;/strong&gt; Strong ownership mindset, able to work independently as a contractor with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of (or experience in) the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Big4 working experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oracle suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hubble and SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Communications team builds our brand and influence across the world. We&#39;re looking for someone to join our small—but high-leverage—Corporate Communications team, which shapes and protects our reputation across the financial, policy, and global business communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced communicator to build and lead a proactive corporate storytelling program. You&#39;ll be the connective tissue across the business and policy audiences—building the campaigns, relationships, and moments that shape how the companies that rely on our products the most, and those who write the rules of the economy Stripe is helping to build, understand Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll lead our most influential reputational programs globally—high-profile events, executive media and speaking opportunities, and proactive campaigns that demonstrate our economic impact. At the same time, you&#39;ll work closely with our policy team—advocating for improvements in financial policy and regulation, while also shaping our response to complex policy issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate our economic impact. Build proactive corporate campaigns around our role creating economic opportunity. Lead communications for high-profile events, executive interviews, and public appearances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own our reputational storytelling globally. Design and execute programs that build our profile—and trust—among the core business audience as well as policymakers and the Washington press corps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the next chapter of our policy communications function. Partner closely with our policy team to develop a clear point of view on industry, regulatory, and policy-related topics, and amplify it through the right channels. Establish relationships with the right journalists and influencers in policy and tech, thought leaders in AI, crypto, and tech policy, rapid response capabilities, and a well-tuned approach for navigating the full range of political and regulatory moments that arise in D.C.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive counsel. Serve as a trusted advisor to senior executives on communications strategy. Bring clear judgment to ambiguous situations, help Stripe navigate the moments it didn&#39;t anticipate, and help it seize the ones it did&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional experience in strategic communications, tech PR, policy communications, or an equivalent high-growth operator role (e.g., as a former founder)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A superlative writer with a proven ability to create clear, compelling narratives around complex, high-stakes topics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment in ambiguous, high-pressure situations, with the ability to operate with significant autonomy and make consequential decisions quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in the tech media landscape—including an existing network of relationships with reporters, editors, and influencers in tech policy and business press&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with policy, legal, and senior executive stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative flair and an aversion to the hackneyed and obvious, and a high bar for what a communications program achieves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial streak—someone who is energized by the opportunity to build, not just manage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to design and execute proactive communications campaigns—not just respond to incoming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building something from scratch—whether a comms function, a narrative program, or a public-facing campaign—and iterating on it over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A feel for independent media—Substack, podcasts, YouTube, influencers on X—and how to use these channels to reach and shape conversations among policymakers and thought leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Security Systems and Infrastructure (CSI) team safeguards Stripe’s people, offices, and operations by designing, delivering, and maintaining secure infrastructure across our global workplace portfolio. We take an intelligence-led, risk-based approach and partner closely with Workplace, IT, Security Operations, Legal, and external vendors to build reliable, scalable physical security systems and transition them to our Global Security Operations Center (GSOC) for ongoing monitoring and support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Corporate Security Infrastructure Project Manager, you will lead the security infrastructure workstream for new offices, expansions, relocations, and major workplace upgrades, with an initial focus on Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA) and support for global projects as needed. You will manage projects from early site assessment and design through installation, testing, commissioning, and operational handover.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be accountable for scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, and stakeholder alignment across a portfolio of concurrent projects. In addition to delivering individual projects, you will strengthen the CSI program by improving standards, documentation, vendor performance, reporting, and repeatable project management processes. You will work through ambiguity, surface decisions early, and communicate clearly with technical teams, business partners, vendors, and senior leaders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end delivery of security infrastructure for office construction and expansion projects, from site assessment and requirements definition through design, procurement, installation, testing, commissioning, and closeout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead requests for proposals (RFPs) for security installations, including defining scope and requirements, coordinating bidders, reviewing submissions, evaluating proposals with relevant stakeholders, and supporting vendor selection recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project scope, schedule, budget, risks, dependencies, decisions, and change control; provide clear, outcome-focused reporting to stakeholders and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate security designs and technical requirements with Workplace, IT, Security Operations, Legal, architects, general contractors, landlords, and other project partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review design drawings, specifications, bills of materials, and implementation plans to ensure alignment with CSI standards and local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage security integrators, consultants, and contractors, including statements of work, delivery milestones, quality expectations, service levels, and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee system installation, acceptance testing, commissioning, punch-list resolution, documentation, and first-day-of-business readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure completed projects are smoothly handed over to the GSOC and support teams, with accurate system records, operating procedures, training, and ownership established.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve global construction standards, technical specifications, project templates, runbooks, and closeout documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and track project health metrics, vendor KPIs, budget forecasts, and lessons learned; use insights to improve delivery quality, predictability, and cost efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support new market and site evaluations by identifying security risks, infrastructure constraints, integration needs, and mitigation options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the security repair and maintenance program, with a focus on the EMEA region, collaborating with regional teams to triage, track, and resolve security system and hardware issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CSI engineers and program leadership to prioritize work, resolve cross-project dependencies, and scale consistent processes across the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 25%, including international travel, to support site assessments, project milestones, commissioning, and handover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of project management experience delivering complex physical security, workplace technology, low-voltage, construction, or similarly technical infrastructure projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing multiple concurrent projects across the full lifecycle, with ownership of scope, schedule, budget, risk, quality, and stakeholder communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coordinating cross-functional delivery among technical teams, business partners, design and construction teams, vendors, and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong vendor and contractor management skills, including defining requirements, managing contracts or statements of work, tracking delivery, and addressing performance issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication, with the ability to translate technical details into clear decisions, risks, tradeoffs, and next steps for different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment and structured problem-solving skills; able to operate independently, navigate ambiguity, anticipate issues, and drive timely decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meticulous attention to detail and a demonstrated commitment to accurate documentation, standards, and operational handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing project management processes, tracking performance metrics, and applying lessons learned to improve future delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of physical security systems such as access control, video management, intrusion detection, intercoms, low-voltage infrastructure, and door hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel internationally up to 25%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering security infrastructure for offices in multiple countries or regions, particularly in EMEA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Genetec Security Center, including Synergis, Omnicast, Security Center SaaS, or Stratocast; active Genetec certification is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with system integrations, networking fundamentals, APIs, webhooks, or cloud-managed security technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets, forecasts, vendor KPIs, SLAs, and portfolio-level reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using project management and workflow tools such as Jira and Smartsheet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reviewing and marking up construction and security design documentation using Bluebeam Revu or a similar PDF design-review tool, along with knowledge of commissioning practices and relevant local codes or regulatory requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in project management, construction management, security management, information technology, engineering, or a related field; or a relevant professional certification such as PMP, PRINCE2, ASIS PSP/CPP, or SIA CSPM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to select and use appropriate AI tools to improve work, while critically evaluating and refining outputs for accuracy and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;About the team&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio team works on a variety of brand-centric projects for Stripe, from our brand standards to campaigns, events, IRL experiences, packaging, digital products, and even printed publications. The brand designers on this team are multidisciplinary in nature, able to design robust visual systems, art direction, and craft surfaces that focus on brand and product storytelling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborating with other teams at Stripe, as well as external partners, we raise the quality and consistency of experiences with the Stripe brand IRL, virtually, and everywhere in between. We craft the creative vision and strategy for different types of projects and audiences, and amplify them across various mediums, channels, objects to environments, and digital and physical experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe Creative Lab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Creative Lab aims to create breakthrough, culturally resonant, and exquisitely crafted projects that reveal Stripe’s magic in surprising ways. We dedicate ourselves to meticulously crafting the work to ensure the highest possible creative quality. The work is experimental, often starts with ambiguous briefs and requires finding a way where others might deem it impossible. We are making it up as we go, and that’s the way we love to work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining a highly creative team working across digital experiences, interactive projects, physical installations, experimental technology, and whatever else an idea might require. The work often begins without an obvious technical solution and sometimes without knowing exactly what form the final project should take.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Design Engineer, you’ll work closely with designers, art directors, and producers to figure out what’s possible, prototype ideas quickly, and turn ambitious creative concepts into working experiences. You’ll bring deep technical expertise in at least one area of creative engineering, alongside the curiosity and technical range to work confidently beyond it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A significant amount of our work lives on the internet, so you should be comfortable independently building and shipping highly crafted digital experiences. Other projects may involve hardware, physical computing, unusual displays, installations, or technical systems we haven’t encountered before. You won’t be expected to be an expert in everything, but you should be excited to learn, experiment, and know when to bring in specialists.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype and build highly crafted, experimental digital experiences, interactive projects, and creative tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with designers and art directors to translate ambitious creative direction into technically excellent experiences, while contributing your own judgment to make the work better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore emerging technologies and unfamiliar technical approaches, quickly determining what is possible and how best to build it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently navigate ambiguous technical problems, moving pragmatically from early experiments to finished work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and publish standalone web experiences when appropriate, while identifying and communicating the additional engineering support required for more complex projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment with hardware, physical computing, displays, sensors, embedded systems, and other technologies when projects call for them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with external engineers, fabricators, technical studios, and other specialists, contributing enough technical fluency to be an effective creative and engineering partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a high bar for performance, reliability, usability, and craft without allowing conventional technical approaches to unnecessarily constrain an idea&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant software engineering, creative technology, or creative development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in at least one area of creative engineering, with demonstrated curiosity and competence across adjacent technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio of technically ambitious, highly crafted work such as experimental websites, interactive experiences, realtime graphics, games, installations, creative tools, or other unusual applications of technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong frontend engineering fundamentals and experience independently building and shipping public-facing web experiences&lt;/li&gt;
