&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/billing&quot;&gt; Billing organization&lt;/a&gt; at Stripe builds and operates Stripe Billing, a growing product vertical inside of Stripe. Hundreds of thousands of businesses of all sizes and types use Stripe Billing to collect revenue for recurring and one-time payments across a variety of different pricing models—from selling SaaS subscriptions, to orchestrating multi-stage contracts, delivering business analytics, and providing recovery and retention tools to prevent customer churn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To support even the most unique and complex business models, our technology and products must be configurable and programmable. This requires our team to innovate in how we model different types of businesses, and how we use technology to enable customers to piece together Stripe’s Billing’s platform primitives into holistic solutions that support any type of business. Through this work, Stripe Billing allows worry-free innovation and evolution of any customer’s business model. Stripe is defining the industry’s approach to Billing solutions; we’re looking for innovators to join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced Engineering Manager to lead a team within the Stripe Billing organization. In this role, you will manage a high-performing team of engineers and partner closely with product managers and other cross-functional leaders to shape the team’s strategy and roadmap. You will excel in this role if you’re a product-focused engineering manager who can collaborate effectively across multiple teams and functions to deliver results. If you enjoy building and nurturing high-performing engineering teams, helping guide the direction of product development, and engaging directly with users of the platform, this will be a great opportunity for your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering leaders, product managers, and designers to shape the team’s strategy and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate strong first principles thinking when approaching complex problems and system design&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a healthy team culture with a high level of trust and psychological safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define processes that enable the team do its best work in a fast-paced, dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor engineers on the team to help them advance in their careers and develop new skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Stripe’s recruiting team to hire strong engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full time software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a consistent track record of hiring and leading productive engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve nurtured healthy work environments that are supportive, challenging, diverse and inclusive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re motivated to work in highly cross-functional organizations, with a strong ability to lead and measure product outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve leveraged your strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large scale and difficult technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions that scale to different kinds of user needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the ability to thrive while operating with a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a strong product and design sense, and enjoy finding elegant solutions to complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve built strong cross-team relationships that span organizational boundaries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building and leading a distributed team that works across multiple locations and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Checkout Optimization team is the growth team for Stripe’s checkout UIs. They build high-converting, personalized checkout experiences for buyers and agents, as well as the data platform that powers it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team identifies opportunities to improve checkout through rapid product experimentation and delivers optimization at scale through our ML-powered engine. The team also builds the reliable data foundations that enable this work, including experimentation, optimization, and data-informed product decisions across Stripe’s checkout suite.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over the next 6 to 12 months, the team will focus on:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building personalized checkout experiences powered by the ML-based Optimization Engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic commerce through optimizing OCS experiences for agent buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Checkout optimization for rapidly growing AI companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving our data platform, which is critical to leveraging data internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers at Stripe are responsible for the success of their team. You’ll be deeply involved in the engineering and design processes as well as coaching, mentoring, and leading the team. You’ll have a deep understanding of how to drive efficient engineering teams and you’ll have a strong user focus. You&#39;ll work with engineers on creating technical solutions and communicating effectively across teams and senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of talented full-stack product and data engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand buyer and agent needs and pain points to prioritize workstreams and deliver high-quality checkout experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Data Science, Data Engineering, and engineering teams across Stripe to deliver these solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead experimentation and optimization work that improves checkout conversion and buyer experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the data platform that enables reliable, self-serve analysis, experimentation, and product decisions across OCS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high standards for the quality, reliability, and usability of the data products and pipelines that support OCS decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit top engineering talent in partnership with Stripe’s recruiting team to build a diverse and high-performing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership, including architecture and design, vision, direction, requirements setting, and incident response processes for your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s direction, from north star vision to goals, OKRs, and roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers focused on building and shipping products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of full-time software development experience, with a strong background in backend development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across geographies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading growth or product teams that have used experimentation to drive product usage and other metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building extensible, leveraged software solutions that scale to different kinds of user needs, with the ability to empathize with users and advocate for excellent user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience working in payments and on payments technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading a growth team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience leading a data engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The StripeOS engineering team builds the tools Stripe uses to plan and run its work: setting goals, making and recording decisions, and tracking projects from kickoff to launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These tools sit at the center of how Stripe operates. Every team relies on them to stay aligned, make sound decisions, and move quickly, so every improvement we make compounds across the company. Recent advances in AI give us an opportunity to rethink what these tools can do.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re an AI-native team reimagining how Stripe plans, decides, and executes. We build polished web and mobile experiences alongside AI agents and assistants that do real work on behalf of Stripe employees. We experiment quickly, put ideas in front of real users, and scale the ones that work. As we do, our scope keeps growing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are Stripe employees in every function and at every level, from engineers and product managers to company leadership. We partner closely with the teams that build Stripe’s internal AI platform and developer tooling, and with groups across the company, from engineering to marketing to senior leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a product-minded engineering leader who’s excited to transform how a company plans and executes its work. You’ll lead the StripeOS engineering team as it builds the next generation of Stripe’s planning and execution tools. You’ll set the team’s direction, grow and support its engineers, and stay close to the technical work: shaping architecture, prototyping new ideas alongside your team, putting them in the hands of real users, and turning the strongest experiments into products used across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This leadership role combines technical depth with broad product scope. You’ll work hand in hand with product managers and designers to define what we build, turning ambitious ideas into the right technical solutions. You’ll combine full-stack engineering with emerging AI capabilities and guide your team through open-ended problems where the right product, interface, and architecture emerge together. The potential impact of this role is enormous, and it will keep growing across the entire company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the team’s vision for AI-native workflows: rethink how Stripe employees plan, decide, and execute with AI at the core, and build agents and assistants that synthesize context, automate repetitive work, and help people make better decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers and designers to set the team’s direction and roadmap, turn ambitious ideas into well-scoped technical plans, and guide the delivery of full-stack products, including web and mobile experiences, AI-powered features, and integrations with internal tools and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay deeply engaged in the technical work: review designs, weigh in on architecture, and prototype new approaches with your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, grow, and support your engineers through coaching, mentoring, and clear feedback, and partner with Stripe’s recruiting team to recruit top engineering talent and build a diverse, high-performing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how the team operates, from engineering practices and standards for experimentation to AI-native development that helps the team prototype faster and ship with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users across Stripe to understand how they work, turn what you learn into products they love, and measure the impact of what the team ships to double down on what makes Stripe employees more productive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high bar for quality, reliability, security, and privacy, especially when building on sensitive internal context&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience, leading and growing teams that build and ship products at scale, with a track record of taking critical user-facing products from prototype to production and keeping them reliable as they scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of software development experience, with a strong background in full-stack development, technical depth in modern web technologies, performance, and user experience, and the ability to guide engineers on architecture and the design of extensible systems that serve many kinds of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with modern AI tools and a clear point of view on how AI agents and AI-native workflows can transform the way people work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort leading through ambiguity: framing the right problems, experimenting and iterating, making pragmatic technical decisions, and charting a clear path forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional collaboration skills, with experience partnering closely with product managers and designers to define and build products, and a product-minded approach to building delightful experiences that solve real problems and deliver meaningful outcomes for users and the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for enabling people to do their best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI agents or products powered by large language models to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building productivity, collaboration, or internal tools used across a large organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking new products from initial concept through launch and iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in and with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with modern web and backend technologies, such as Go, Ruby, TypeScript, and React&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive work forward autonomously while bringing your team and partners along toward shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous thinking and comfort making hard decisions and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a platform company powering businesses all over the world, Stripe processes payments, runs marketplaces, and detects fraud, helping entrepreneurs start an internet business from anywhere in the world. Commerce Systems provides a central entry point for Stripe teams to monetize products in global markets. We build platforms and services to define and manage pricing, calculate and collect Stripe’s revenue, and empower Stripe and our users to understand and manage revenue and costs. We work on customer-facing experiences, internal platforms, and data pipelines to empower Accounting, Finance, Strategy, Sales, and Stripe’s Products to drive business value across the entire user and product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a seasoned technical leader to lead a team within the Commerce Systems organization. As the leader in Commerce Systems, your goals will include increasing the self-serve capabilities of the billing platform to accelerate product development across Stripe’s product suite; launching new pricing and monetization capabilities for our product and sales teams; ensuring the rigor, accuracy, and predictability of billing outcomes; and enabling our partners in finance, strategy, and accounting to deeply understand Stripe’s business performance. You’ll work with leaders across product, engineering, sales, and many of our back office functions - finance and strategy, accounting, tax, and compliance - to influence strategy across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Commerce Systems is a core engine powering many of Stripe’s biggest bets, from shipping new products faster to redefining our commercial strategy. The right engineering leadership will enable Stripe to scale more quickly and more reliably as our business accelerates. If that sounds exciting, we’d love to speak with you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the core mission and responsibilities of your team. Set strategies and priorities to balance improvements across multiple dimensions including monetizing new products, enabling greater self-service and improved developer experience, and improving technical foundations and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering and design processes, coaching, mentoring, and supporting your team as they build innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong relationships with other leaders and orgs to ensure efficient collaboration and close alignment on objectives and outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a healthy team with a strong bench of leaders by supporting team members’ growth and hiring both internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ total years of engineering experience with a minimal 4 years of management experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully led high-complexity teams of 8+ engineers, working in parallel on multiple high-impact areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in cross-functional environments, demonstrating rigorous thinking and effective decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited, mentored, and built high-performing teams, creating an inclusive environment that attracts diverse talent and empowers individuals to thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with a high level of autonomy and responsibility, taking ownership of projects and driving initiatives that contribute to the overall success of the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work effectively with partners in a geographically distributed org, promoting clear communication and collaboration across time zones to ensure alignment and shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, enabling clear and persuasive interactions with colleagues and stakeholders, ensuring understanding of technical concepts and fostering collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving platforms that empower other developers, optimizing for self-service and extensibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain knowledge in payments, billing, or other financial technology is beneficial but not essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering at Privy is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High urgency—Shipping very small iterations, very fast, to learn very quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product taste—Our customers &lt;em&gt;are&lt;/em&gt; developers, and to build effective products for them requires technical knowledge —you will often be &quot;the PM&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security mindset—A great portion of our product is trust. While we have a dedicated security team, every engineer brings security to their designs from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, we use &lt;a href=&quot;https://mcfunley.com/choose-boring-technology&quot;&gt;boring technology&lt;/a&gt; like Node, React, and AWS so we can focus our engineering energy entirely on pushing the boundaries of Privy&#39;s core product, e.g. through hardware enclaves, multi-region low-latency APIs, and blockchain abstractions that are accessible to mainstream developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Privy, our Forward Deployed Engineers work on the company’s most important customer problems. They partner closely with customers to architect our most complex integrations and build new product features that close the gap to win deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Engineering Manager to lead this team as it continues to grow. You’ll be responsible for helping an outstanding group of Forward Deployed Engineers do the best work of their careers while staying laser-focused on helping Privy and its customers win.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage role at the intersection of customers, product development, and engineering. You’ll help the team stay focused on the highest-value work, raise the bar on execution, and help turn customer signal into new products and features.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the manager of this team, you own its overall impact. Great management is a core part of how Privy wins: our managers are force multipliers, performance coaches, and culture carriers who help exceptional people do exceptional work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team outcomes and business impact for Forward Deployed Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop engineers across technical depth, customer empathy, and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the team accountable to excellence in quality, throughput, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team is focused on the right problems and highest-leverage opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Solutions Engineering, and GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay close to the work—review PRs, help scope technical work, review design docs, and jump in on complex problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a strong team culture grounded in trust, rigor, and urgency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the feedback loop between customer signal and product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership and a track record of driving outstanding business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent people management skills and experience growing high-performing engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and the ability to evaluate architecture and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset and comfort translating ambiguous needs into clear technical direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional maturity and strong communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing in a fast-moving, high-expectation environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Infrastructure organization builds and operates the shared platforms that make it possible for engineering teams to build, deploy, run, and scale reliable products. The organization owns foundational capabilities across service networking and discovery, safe feature and configuration changes, data storage and orchestration, and batch computing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our platforms support a global engineering audience and power systems at significant scale. This includes the control plane for secure service-to-service communication across tens of thousands of microservices, service and feature deployment infrastructure that helps teams introduce and recover from changes safely, infrastructure for running Stripe&#39;s containerized services, and data platforms for storage, pipeline orchestration, and large-scale processing. Our batch compute platforms support technologies including Apache Airflow, Apache Spark, Apache Iceberg, Apache Hadoop, and Apache Celeborn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, you will lead or strongly influence teams working on business-critical infrastructure with broad internal adoption. You will balance reliability, scalability, security, developer experience, and operational rigor while helping Stripe move quickly with confidence. You will partner closely with product, security, data, support, and adjacent infrastructure leaders to set direction, resolve cross-team dependencies, and turn recurring needs into durable platform capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Stripe, you will operate with full autonomy across a complex, high-impact area of our infrastructure. Your scope extends beyond a single team. You lead or strongly influence multiple engineering teams, execute parallel high-priority workstreams, and develop senior engineering talent. You set direction, align stakeholders, make decisions that hold up over time, and deliver results without close direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with scope and autonomy by driving impact across multiple teams or a significant infrastructure area independently, translating organizational goals into concrete execution plans, and delivering results across parallel workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define strategy and roadmap for your area, anticipating internal user needs, technical challenges, reliability risks, and business priorities, then communicating a clear plan to your team and senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop senior talent by coaching senior engineers and emerging leaders, creating meaningful stretch opportunities, and giving candid feedback that improves individual and team performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional alignment with product, security, data, support, and adjacent engineering teams, resolving ambiguity at team boundaries and aligning stakeholders around shared priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and scale the team by attracting, developing, and retaining senior engineering talent while maintaining a high hiring bar and building an inclusive, high-performing organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate with rigor by setting high standards for reliability, availability, scalability, incident response, and engineering craft, and by addressing systemic issues that affect internal users across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Staff engineers on architecture decisions involving distributed systems, service discovery, configuration propagation, production change management, data processing, and internal platform design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience with 10+ years of software development experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience with a demonstrated track record of autonomous impact as an engineering manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading high-complexity engineering teams that deliver multiple difficult, high-impact workstreams in parallel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence and align cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority, communicating a clear direction that others follow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful recruiting experience, including a track record of attracting and developing senior engineering talent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth sufficient to guide architecture decisions and hold teams to a high standard for product quality, reliability, and engineering craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating high-availability distributed systems, internal platforms, or developer infrastructure used by a broad engineering audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with service networking, service discovery, service mesh, feature flags, configuration management, progressive delivery, deployment tooling, or production change governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data infrastructure, including large-scale storage, data orchestration, batch compute, or processing frameworks such as Apache Airflow, Apache Spark, Apache Iceberg, Apache Hadoop, or Apache Celeborn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving reliability through observability, health checks, incident response, automated recovery, capacity planning, or reducing the impact of production changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing secure access controls, audit systems, approval workflows, or governance mechanisms for production infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud infrastructure and distributed systems technologies such as Amazon Web Services, DynamoDB, Aurora, S3, Ruby, Go, Java, or Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product mindset for internal platforms, including empathy for internal users, a focus on self-service, and a commitment to making safe workflows straightforward to adopt&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;in-office-expectations&quot;&gt;In-office expectations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Office-assigned Stripes in most locations are expected to spend at least 50% of their time in a given month in their local office or with users. This expectation may vary by role, team, and location. The hiring manager will discuss the expectations for this role during the process.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Privy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission is to make privacy and user ownership the default online. To do so, we build simple, flexible APIs and tools for developers that make it easy to build new products on crypto rails.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Privy owns the abstractions and infrastructure layer above wallets, integrating across chains, third-party providers, and Stripe products like Treasury and Link. We get to solve hard technical problems while leveraging Stripe&#39;s distribution to reach customers like Ramp, Klarna, Deel, Kraken, Hyperliquid, and Fomo — powering experiences for both mainstream users and crypto natives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering at Privy is distinguished by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High urgency—Shipping very small iterations, very fast, to learn very quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product taste—Our customers &lt;em&gt;are&lt;/em&gt; developers, and to build effective products for them requires technical knowledge —you will often be &quot;the PM&quot;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security mindset—A great portion of our product is trust. While we have a dedicated security team, every engineer brings security to their designs from the start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In practice, we use &lt;a href=&quot;https://mcfunley.com/choose-boring-technology&quot;&gt;boring technology&lt;/a&gt; like Node, React, and AWS so we can focus our engineering energy entirely on pushing the boundaries of Privy&#39;s core product, e.g. through hardware enclaves, multi-region low-latency APIs, and blockchain abstractions that are accessible to mainstream developers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Privy, you will lead, grow, and shape high-performing engineering teams that make a massive impact on our product and industry. Your North Star is to enable and drive towards the success of Privy’s business overall.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager of your team, the buck stops with you: you are the owner of your team’s ultimate impact on Privy’s product and business. We believe that excellence in management is why our team loves working at Privy. Incredible managers are the core driver behind Privy’s long-term success: they are force multipliers, performance coaches, culture-carriers. They build the scaffolding that supports the team and each individual’s greatest impact. They shape Privy to be the place where each person gets to do the very best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We wake up every day driven to show up for our team. We shape roles around the unique strengths of every person and we are deeply grateful for the time we spend together building something greater than ourselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Infrastructure at Privy is fundamentally a product. With both internal engineers (and increasingly non-engineers) as direct consumers of infra platforms, as well as external product offerings, it is essential that the infra team creates powerful abstractions, educates and grows the Privy team on shipping ever-better software, and operates deeply efficient tooling to be the lever arm for which Privy moves the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own long-term team outcomes and success of Privy’s product and business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the future vision of infrastructure of Privy alongside talented infrastructure engineers, across complex, cutting edge technology like secure enclaves (TEEs) and one-click Bring Your Own Cloud deployments, with performance and high scale as a default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the team accountable to excellence in quality, throughput, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading active infrastructure work across the breadth of the company, from service definition, to reliability engineering, to developer tooling, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team is working on the right scope of work and projects, align decisions with business impact, and build interfaces with other parts of the org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fill gaps as a player-coach; review PRs, write and review design docs, investigate incidents – stay close to the metal and reinforce our builder culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach engineers towards growth and their career goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a supportive, fun, motivating, celebratory team culture so that the team wins every week&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep ownership and a high-level perspective on driving overall business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performance-oriented mindset, with a high bar for quality and excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical excellence to be able to independently evaluate quality and technical feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High emotional maturity, insightfulness, and care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong past experience as a manager and leader – excellent management takes reps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with any of the following a plus:
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and operating systems supporting hundreds of millions of users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Secure enclave platforms, like AWS Nitro Enclaves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observability, incident response, capacity planning, performance tuning, and infrastructure automation (IaC, CI/CD for infra)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in building low-latency, high-throughput systems for trading or payment processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Any blend of public cloud/BYOC architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Internal Systems Automations Platform team’s mission is to unlock productivity across all of Stripe’s internal systems. We build solutions to transform core processes for Finance, Accounting, People, Legal, Sales, Marketing, and more. We orchestrate the full automation lifecycle, using artificial intelligence (AI) for planning, analysis, and reasoning, and deterministic scripts, code, and pipelines for reliable and trustworthy execution. We enable technical and nontechnical users to build hybrid code and no-code automations while working with central Operations, Developer Productivity, Infrastructure, and machine learning (ML) teams on behalf of all Internal Systems customers to build powerful platforms together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced engineering manager with a passion for simplifying complex systems and driving operational efficiency. In this role, you’ll analyze existing processes across Stripe’s internal systems, use automation platforms where possible, and design new solutions when needed. You will implement cutting-edge automation solutions, including AI agents, robotic process automation (RPA), and data pipelines, and build best-in-class platforms. You’ll be responsible for continuously improving workflows to maximize efficiency and deliver meaningful business impact across a broad set of internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead your team of talented engineers to design and deploy data pipelines and intelligent workflows that simplify operations for internal customers, including Finance, Accounting, Legal, People, Sales, Marketing, and Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product managers and talk directly with users to drive a high-impact, prioritized roadmap for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, mentor, develop, and grow engineers on your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be deeply involved in launching new product features and capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers and product managers across Stripe to ensure your features are integrated into the Stripe suite.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of engineering management experience and 10+ years of overall experience in the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working on high-scale systems with a strong technical foundation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works very well cross-functionally and is able to think rigorously and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both supportive and challenging and enables engineers to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background and hands-on experience in solving large-scale and difficult technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with diverse internal teams and stakeholders across Finance, Legal, Operations, and other business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI, large language model (LLM), or ML technologies is highly valuable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of context-driven AI agents that can autonomously figure out solutions when given business problems and context.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About The Team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The payments landscape is changing rapidly and our team is at the forefront of this change. Depending on where you live, you may be used to paying with a credit card (United States), iDeal (Netherlands) or UPI (India), amongst hundreds of other global payment methods. It turns out how you pay is increasingly dependent on where you are and what business you&#39;re buying from. The Local Payment Methods team is responsible for Stripe&#39;s fastest growing payments business. We build payment methods that help businesses drastically increase their revenues and grow their business. Undergirding all of this we also build the platform that allows us to build and distribute payment methods at scale&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineering Managers at Stripe are responsible for the success of their team. You’ll be deeply involved in the engineering and design processes as well as coaching, mentoring, and leading the team. You’ll have a deep understanding of how to drive efficient engineering teams and you’ll have a strong user-focus. You’ll be working with engineers on creating technical solutions and communicating effectively across teams and senior leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of talented engineers on the team, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize engineering work and deliver high quality solutions that meet user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects, overseeing the entire development lifecycle from planning to delivery, while maintaining high standards of quality and timely completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture/design, vision/direction/requirements setting, and incident response processes) for your reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s direction, from north star vision, to goals/OKRs, and roadmap. Align with the broader MaaS organization, and our customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive execution on the roadmap, making sure we deliver big bets, but stay noble to an ever-changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative and inclusive work environment, promoting innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent, and define the overall hiring strategies for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of management experience with a total of 12+ years of software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has built products before, and wants to be involved in product development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a team with multiple workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical enough to drive clarity with staff engineers about architecture and technical strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works effectively cross-functionally and is able to think rigorously, communicate effectively, and make or coordinate hard decisions and tradeoffs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing rigorous incident response processes and on call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both challenging and supportive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experiences working on banking products, if not payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The payments landscape is changing rapidly, with businesses and their customers relying on a growing mix of local payment methods, cards, wallets, bank payments, buy now, pay later, and digital currencies. Stripe’s Local Payment Methods (LPM) business is one of our fastest-growing payments businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;LPM Foundations builds and operates the core platform that enables Stripe’s Local Payment Method teams—and their first- and third-party developers—to build, integrate, and run high-quality payment methods at scale. We turn complex product integrations into reusable, self-service platform capabilities so teams can launch new LPMs faster and reduce the long-term cost of operating them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a payments role with a platform and AI focus. We are building the foundations, interfaces, and workflows that let product and engineering teams use AI effectively to accelerate development, improve decisions, and scale reliable payments experiences globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager, you will lead the LPM Foundations team at the center of Stripe’s long-term payments growth strategy. You will translate regional and strategic priorities into a focused platform roadmap, shape technical direction with your team, and drive execution across the systems behind critical payment flows. You will be deeply involved in engineering and design, while coaching, mentoring, and creating the conditions for an effective, inclusive team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision and roadmap for platform capabilities that help LPM teams build, integrate, and operate payment methods at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineers in designing and delivering reliable, self-service foundations that simplify complex integrations and speed up launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build an AI-first engineering organization: develop the platform hooks and working practices that enable agentic development and help teams use AI to improve execution and product-engineering decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with customers, engineering, product, partnerships, legal, operations, and other stakeholders to align priorities and deliver end-to-end outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clear technical and architectural decisions with staff engineers, balancing reliability, extensibility, velocity, and regional payments complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and improve the team’s operating processes so it can execute effectively and engage well with the rest of Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and retain great engineers; support their growth and help build a challenging, supportive, and inclusive team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience managing teams that shipped high-quality products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An entrepreneurial mindset and comfort operating with a high degree of autonomy and responsibility in an ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of recruiting, developing, and building great engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work effectively across functions, think rigorously, communicate clearly, and make or coordinate hard decisions and trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen to partner with staff engineers on architecture and technical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating a healthy and inclusive work environment that is both challenging and supportive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platforms, developer products, or large-scale distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI to software development, engineering workflows, or product delivery, with strong judgment about where it creates durable value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for leadership, users, and company-wide audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong quantitative and analytical background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading fully remote or distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1 id=&quot;engineering-manager-machine-learning-credit-risk&quot;&gt;Engineering Manager, Machine Learning Credit Risk&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Credit Risk team develops intelligent systems that help Stripe identify high-risk accounts, minimize credit losses, and improve profitability. Credit risk is a complex machine learning problem that requires us to distinguish emerging risk from healthy business activity while giving legitimate users a clear and reliable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team consists of machine learning engineers who build models and systems used across Stripe’s credit-risk products. We work closely with partners in Product, Data Science, Credit Strategy, Operations, and other engineering teams. Together, we help stakeholders make informed decisions and support sustainable growth wherever credit risk affects Stripe’s products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an engineering manager to lead the Credit Risk team and shape how Stripe uses machine learning to manage credit risk at scale. You’ll set the team’s technical and product direction, connect advances in machine learning to measurable business outcomes, and help engineers deliver reliable systems that balance loss prevention with the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across engineering, product, data science, and risk to identify the highest-impact opportunities and turn them into a focused roadmap. You’ll also hire and develop engineers, strengthen the team’s technical practices, and contribute to machine learning and engineering leadership across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the strategy for detecting and mitigating credit risk through machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes related to credit losses, profitability, detection quality, and the user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design and delivery of reliable machine learning models, services, and decision systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate advances in machine learning into practical capabilities that support the team’s business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Data Science, Credit Strategy, Operations, and engineering teams to define priorities and deliver cross-functional programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, hire, and develop machine learning engineers while building an inclusive and effective team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to broader engineering and machine learning initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing engineers who build and operate production machine learning systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying machine learning to complex, real-world problems and leading the technical delivery of models and supporting systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting strategy and working across engineering, product, data science, operations, and business teams to deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience recruiting, managing, and developing engineers in a fast-moving environment with significant autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with credit risk, fraud detection, financial risk, trust and safety, or another domain involving decisions under uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience balancing risk reduction with customer or user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building machine learning systems that support high-stakes, time-sensitive decisions at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting a multi-year technical direction while delivering progress through quarterly plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk Detection is focused on providing a delightful experience for our merchants and minimizing friction, while ensuring the safety of our users in the financial ecosystem. Whenever the Risk team takes action on an account, we work to notify Merchants and provide clear status on what’s happening, enable guided workflows for resolving their issues, and redefine our overall Risk processes to make them as smooth as possible for good merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an engineering leader to lead and grow a strong team of engineers, build relationships with customers internally and externally, and champion our vision of making Stripe’s risk management a feature that attracts and retains merchants, and becomes a product differentiator. This is an exciting opportunity to partner with teams across Stripe to build the best merchant experience, and contribute directly to Stripe’s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Support the team in delivering a high level of technical quality and impact via APIs, user-facing experiences, services, and systems&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Recruit, hire, scale, and develop an amazing team of engineers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Executing cross-functionally with leadership, product teams, infra teams &amp;amp; risk strategists&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Be actively involved in strategic direction and platform decisions that impact all of Stripe and Stripe customers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;At least 3 years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience as a Machine Learning Engineer or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have managed teams that can collaborate with product teams, respond rapidly to customer needs along with building technology and capabilities that are strategic and foundational in nature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy designing, measuring &amp;amp; improving user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable planning in quarters, and can set a vision for several years&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams and remote workers&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Mobile Development Productivity team makes building, testing, and releasing Stripe’s mobile applications and device-integrated software fast, reliable, and secure. The team owns the mobile development platform end to end, including development environments, simulators and emulators, continuous integration, automated testing, builds, and releases. We support engineers working across iOS, Android, React Native, Kotlin Multiplatform, mobile SDKs, and device-integrated software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include engineers working on Stripe Dashboard Mobile, Link, Stripe’s mobile SDKs, and Terminal. We enable mobile engineers to use AI agents throughout the development process, including writing code, running tests, and validating changes across mobile platforms. Our work reduces manual release effort, improves test coverage, and makes mobile development faster and more reliable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the Mobile Development Productivity engineering team and set the technical strategy for the platform Stripe engineers use to build mobile applications and device-integrated software. You will work with engineers and leaders across mobile product and infrastructure teams to identify shared development challenges, align priorities, and translate a long-term technical vision into focused plans for your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will grow and support a team that builds development environments, continuous integration systems, test infrastructure, and secure build and release workflows. You will also guide the team’s work to make AI agents effective participants in mobile development by giving them realistic environments, tools, and feedback for validating changes across mobile platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, support, and grow a team of engineers by hiring, coaching, mentoring, and creating opportunities for development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the team’s technical strategy, goals, and roadmap, translating organizational priorities and internal user needs into clear execution plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with mobile product teams, infrastructure teams, and technical leaders to identify shared development challenges and align stakeholders around reusable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with staff engineers on architecture and strategic technical decisions across development environments, continuous integration, automated testing, and secure build and release systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish high standards for reliability, security, engineering craft, and operational rigor across the systems the team owns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the experience of mobile engineers and AI agents by using measures of developer productivity, build and test performance, and release health to guide investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work effectively with geographically distributed colleagues to maintain alignment, visibility, and clear ownership across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software development experience, including 3+ years of engineering management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading teams that build platforms, frameworks, infrastructure, or tools used by other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define technical strategy, guide architecture decisions, and translate ambiguous goals into a clear roadmap and execution plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success hiring, coaching, and developing engineers while fostering an inclusive, challenging, and supportive work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to align and influence cross-functional stakeholders without direct authority, communicate clearly across varied audiences, and coordinate difficult decisions and tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a developer productivity, developer platform, mobile infrastructure, or internal tools team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or operating development environments, continuous integration systems, automated testing frameworks, or build and release infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with iOS, Android, React Native, Kotlin Multiplatform, mobile SDKs, or device-integrated software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Money Management products (Financial Accounts, Treasury, Global Payouts, Issuing, and Capital) let businesses and platforms hold, move, spend, and earn on their money using the same infrastructure they already use for payments. Asia-Pacific (APAC) Money as a Service (MaaS) is a newly formed team based in Singapore. The team is responsible for bringing this product suite to Asia-Pacific markets, enabling global businesses and platforms to use these capabilities directly or offer them to their APAC users, and building the local rails, compliance, and partner integrations that make it all work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll make some of the most significant strategic, product, and technical decisions for money management in Asia-Pacific at Stripe. The systems this team builds let businesses and platforms integrate with Stripe once, then open accounts, move money, and issue cards across an expanding set of APAC markets and currencies. Businesses and platforms can grow across the region without rebuilding their stack for each country.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multiple pods and grow the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for the team’s output: what ships, when, and how well it works for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the engineering side of a zero-to-one charter, turn an ambiguous regional strategy into a sequenced roadmap that reduces risk, make decisions about whether to build, integrate, or partner, and coordinate launches across licensing, bank and network partners, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the business outcome alongside peers in product, go-to-market, legal, compliance, and partnerships, bring a product point of view, and push back when the plan is wrong&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay hands-on and in the details: read the code, review designs, use the product the way our users do, and understand how Stripe’s money movement stack works end to end so you can make sound technical calls under uncertainty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the operating system for a newly formed team: hiring, rituals, quality standards, on-call practices, and the processes that let the team move fast while keeping money movement safe and reliable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire great engineers, develop them, and give direct, timely feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone with a founder’s mindset: high agency, comfortable with ambiguity, and biased toward shipping. You’ve built something from nothing, you know what it takes to launch a product in a new market, and you don’t wait for a perfect specification or for permission. You care about users and the product as much as about the code, and you’d rather own an outcome than a process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of engineering management experience and 8+ years of software engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a product or team from zero to one: a new market, a new product line, or a team you built and scaled&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring, developing, and retaining strong engineers and building a high-performing, inclusive team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth to engage credibly on architecture, reliability, and tradeoffs in complex distributed systems, along with strong product judgment and the ability to translate user and market needs into engineering priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication with technical and non-technical audiences, including senior stakeholders across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, banking, or money movement, especially launching regulated financial products (accounts, payouts, cards, or lending) in new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in APAC markets, including working with local banks, networks, or regulators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founder, founding engineer, or early-stage startup experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with distributed partner teams across United States, European, and APAC time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence (AI) tools to improve execution, quality, and team effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Service Infrastructure enables Stripe’s engineers to build and ship products using efficient, reliable, service oriented architectures. This organization sits at the boundary between Infrastructure and Product where they engineer Stripe’s service frameworks, standard user-facing API semantics, async orchestration platforms, developer tooling, and mission critical product infrastructure (e.g. webhook fulfillment). Key priorities for this group include delivering an amazing internal developer experience, enabling Stripes to effectively leverage Infrastructure platforms, and driving systemic improvements to Stripe’s API availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager of Managers within the Service Infrastructure organization, you will lead multiple teams, collaborate with infrastructure and product engineering leaders, and advance Stripe’s architecture. You will operate some of the company’s most critical services and you will collaborate with Stripe’s product engineering teams to develop frameworks and abstractions that accelerate the company’s most important product launches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with high-visibility teams and their stakeholders to support key engineering initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical leadership (architecture/design, vision/direction/requirements setting, and incident response processes) for your reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user needs and pain points to prioritize the right engineering work at the right time to enable product engineers to ship new features quickly and reliably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with leaders across the company to drive improvements to Stripe’s architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage processes to help infra teams do their best work and interface effectively with the rest of Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and grow a team of engineers and engineering leaders, including line managers, to deliver high business impact projects on schedule with high-quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with our recruiting team to attract and hire top talent, and define the overall hiring strategies for your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience being a manager of managers (leading managers and senior ICs) of teams of at least 25 people.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing teams that ship and operate critical distributed system infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led staff or principal engineers with a track record of driving alignment between highly technical collaborators on architectural or strategic decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed effective incident response processes and on-call rotations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managed engineering teams working on API design, abstractions, frameworks, or client libraries (e.g. building internal or external developer products).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively managed demanding/conflicting stakeholder and partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving business and product success in a highly cross-functional organization with a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully built a team, defined its mission, and executed on its goals. Experience recruiting, mentoring, and retaining great people that fulfill this mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked effectively cross-functionally and are able to think rigorously, communicate effectively, and make or coordinate hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading partially remote teams and colocated teams in distant geos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourages a healthy work environment that’s both challenging and supportive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of management experience, including 5+ years of being a manager of managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills for different audiences (leadership, users, company-wide).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience changing culture across large organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of common infrastructure platforms (databases, logging, event streams, metrics, caching, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products using static (Java) and dynamically (Ruby) typed programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing with and contributing to open source framework ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing sustainable, in-house framework and abstraction ecosystems in large engineering organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building with cloud primitives from AWS or other cloud providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

