&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments Engineering team powers the processing of hundreds of billions of dollars in card payments annually, enabling users to accept card payments across Asia Pacific, Europe, and the Middle East. As the Engineering Manager for the team, you’ll be responsible for expanding the reach of Stripe’s global payments network and delivering a best-in-class card payments experience in these regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll make some of the most significant strategic, product, and technical decisions for card payments at Stripe. The systems this team builds enable our users to integrate with Stripe once, accept payments across an ever-expanding set of card networks, and grow their businesses globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with other Stripe leaders to shape Stripe’s card payments strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop engineers on the team and help them advance in their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the engineering team achieve high levels of technical productivity, reliability, and simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage processes that help the team do its best work and collaborate effectively with the rest of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to engineering-wide initiatives as a member of Stripe’s engineering management team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit exceptional engineers in collaboration with Stripe’s recruiting team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;you-may-be-a-fit-for-this-role-if&quot;&gt;You may be a fit for this role if:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You build a healthy work environment that is both supportive and challenging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited to help engineers develop new skills and advance in their careers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You communicate clearly and persuasively in writing and in person.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You lead by example, set the right context, and help teammates do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have the technical depth to ask engineers thoughtful questions about architecture and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in an engineering management role, with a demonstrated track record of successfully hiring, developing, and mentoring engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full-time software development experience, including experience building extensible software solutions that scale with business growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to lead by example in fast-paced, high-impact, and ambiguous environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to high operational rigor when working with production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive in a collaborative, cross-functional, and cross-time-zone environment while building a positive team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments-related products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in global and cross-regional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using artificial intelligence (AI) tools to improve team execution, quality, and overall effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building new teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing product platforms that serve other product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of collaborating with partners across multiple regions and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and comfort in a user-facing role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue and Financial Automation (RFA) teams create solutions that empower businesses to optimize their revenue operations. A significant component of RFA is the Revenue team, which is one of our fastest-growing product areas and helps businesses manage and scale their revenue effectively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Orchestration team builds the foundational execution engines, background job processing frameworks, and asynchronous event platforms that power Stripe’s global billing infrastructure. We own the core execution primitives and platform systems that orchestrate the end-to-end financial lifecycle for millions of businesses worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe’s scale, the Orchestration team sits at the intersection of high-throughput distributed systems and mission-critical financial reliability. Our job processing and event scheduling platforms execute millions of scheduled workloads and asynchronous tasks daily with extreme precision, handling everything from global recurring billing cycles to complex time-dependent execution workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe expands to support complex monetization models and enterprise scale, our team is architecting the next generation of core platform infrastructure. We build highly leveraged primitives and foundational frameworks that enable product teams across Stripe to innovate rapidly while operating on an uncompromising foundation of reliability, fault tolerance, and global scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Engineering Manager at Stripe, you will play a pivotal role in driving the success of your team and the broader organization. Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading engineering and design processes, coaching, mentoring, and supporting your team as they build innovative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with stakeholders across product, design, infrastructure, and operations to ensure alignment on projects and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning problems from end-to-end by managing diverse systems, processes, and technologies, while continuously seeking opportunities to optimize efficiency and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Upholding high engineering standards, ensuring consistency across codebases, and implementing best practices throughout your team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiting top engineering talent in partnership with Stripe’s recruiting team to build a diverse and high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting your team members&#39; career growth by providing insights and development opportunities tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications below, with preferred qualifications that would be advantageous but are not required. If you meet the minimum requirement, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing and growing teams of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record managing a team of 5+ software engineers focused on building and shipping products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills, with a history of creatively tackling complex challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience thriving in cross-functional environments, demonstrating rigorous thinking and effective decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in dealing with ambiguity and executing on multiple high-impact work streams simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to fostering a supportive, feedback-driven, and challenging work environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency to engage thoughtfully with engineers about architecture and product design, offering valuable insights when necessary.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mindset of autonomy and entrepreneurship, where you&#39;re excited to take responsibility and drive initiatives forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Alignment with Stripe’s Operating Principles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will embody our &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/jobs/culture&quot;&gt;operating principles&lt;/a&gt; by maintaining a focus on user outcomes, fostering open communication and cross-team collaboration, and embracing an iterative approach to both product development and team management. You will make decisions that reflect our commitment to integrity, excellence, and the long-term success of our users and the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are passionate about empowering engineers and driving impactful projects in a dynamic environment, we would love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testability has long been a priority for Stripe. Before users trust code with their money, they need to verify that it’s safe and correct. This need drove Stripe to build test mode and, more recently, Sandboxes, which enables safe, isolated, and scalable testing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As businesses build with AI and agents, their testing needs are evolving. Stripe customers use claimable sandboxes to add Stripe capabilities to prototypes before business registration. Once onboarded, they provision isolated test environments to support agents’ exploration. These capabilities help developers and agents build and test their integrations with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sandboxes team defines, builds, and operates these testing capabilities. We work across Stripe to make our products testable, helping businesses develop with confidence and shaping the future of Stripe’s developer platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead and grow the Sandboxes engineering team, setting technical direction and operating critical systems. You’ll build a culture of operational excellence and thoughtful product development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work directly with users to understand their needs and partner with Product, Design, and Data Science to shape and deliver the team’s strategy. The role combines building reusable testing capabilities across Stripe with attention to the details that make developer tools effective and easy to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering planning and execution, partnering with Design to build clear, useful testing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the team’s strategy and roadmap, aligning partners across Product, Design, Infrastructure, Marketing, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery from problem definition through rollout and ongoing operation, improving both system performance and the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold high engineering standards across the team’s codebases and development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
