&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Self Serve Direct Onboarding helps businesses start using Stripe’s products quickly and confidently. The team builds self-service experiences that guide users through providing business information and completing required checks. We turn complex financial, regulatory, and verification requirements into clear steps, shaping both how quickly businesses can get started and the trust they place in Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of this work is a shared product activation experience: a consistent way for businesses to start using new financial capabilities as they grow. This foundation helps users avoid repeating information and makes it simpler for product teams to integrate onboarding into their offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI creates an opportunity to rethink how businesses get started on Stripe. The team is designing onboarding journeys for users who interact directly through a user interface, work with AI agents, or delegate onboarding to agents entirely. We’re improving today’s experience while building the foundations for agent-led onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll set engineering direction in partnership with Product and Design and develop the team delivering it. The role combines improving activation today with shaping how onboarding works for people and AI agents.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll use strong product judgment to decide where to experiment, where to build reusable foundations, and how to measure progress through faster activation, fewer repeated steps, and reliable outcomes. You’ll work across Stripe to align teams and resolve dependencies, while coaching engineers and giving them meaningful ownership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead engineering planning and execution, partnering closely with Product and Design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the team’s strategy and roadmap, aligning partners across product engineering, Risk, Compliance, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own delivery from problem definition through rollout and ongoing operation, using experimentation to improve activation while maintaining risk controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold high engineering standards across the team’s codebases and development practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguous goals into focused plans, resolve dependencies, and balance new capabilities with operational health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor engineers, provide candid feedback, and support career development tailored to their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Recruiting to hire engineers and build a diverse, high-performing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of engineering management experience, directly managing and growing teams of 5+ engineers building and shipping products at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of full-time software development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user-facing products, with strong user empathy and product judgment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning ambiguous goals into clear priorities and delivering work that depends on multiple teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of coaching engineers, supporting their growth, and building an environment of candid feedback, inclusion, and shared ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical depth to guide architecture and make pragmatic tradeoffs across user interfaces, APIs, backend workflows, and production reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, including the ability to align technical and nontechnical partners with different priorities and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience simplifying complex customer journeys and using data, user feedback, and experimentation to evaluate outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience modernizing an established product or architecture while continuing to ship improvements and maintain production reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping AI-assisted workflows or agent-facing APIs, with clear approaches to evaluating quality and correctness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Premium Support Experience team builds products to enable, support, and grow businesses in their usage of Stripe. Our Dublin-based team is a startup within Stripe, building a greenfield product to provide a high-quality, differentiated support experience for our largest, most complex, and most engaged users. Besides building directly for Stripe&#39;s users, we&#39;re responsible for improving internal tooling and processes that set the foundations for their end-to-end experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is part of the Support Experience engineering organization, which builds and improves Stripe&#39;s user support from end to end: how users get help within our products, how they get in touch with us when they have questions, and how our teams use internal tools to answer those questions. Providing great support to users of all sizes is culturally important to everyone at Stripe. We partner closely with Stripe&#39;s design, product, and operational teams, and we&#39;re using the latest generative AI technologies to re-imagine support experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leader of a new engineering team, your role is closer to a founding engineering manager at a startup within Stripe. You&#39;ll build and grow the team, set its technical direction, and establish a culture of technical excellence and fast, sustained product delivery. You&#39;ll partner with Product and other cross-functional leaders across the company to define and drive the long-term vision for how Stripe serves its users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your team will design, build, and operate production systems with an emphasis on extensibility, reliability, and usability. It will deliver high-quality end-to-end product experiences built around a deep understanding of user needs. You&#39;ll lead your team to use the best tools for each job, whether that means AI-enabled product experiences or proven techniques for building scalable distributed systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, lead, and manage a team of talented engineers, providing mentorship, guidance, and support to ensure their success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the team&#39;s culture from the ground up, fostering a collaborative and inclusive environment that promotes innovation, knowledge sharing, and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product Management, Design, and key leaders across the company to understand user needs and translate them into a technical vision and roadmap aligned with business objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the execution of projects across the full development lifecycle, from planning to delivery, while upholding high standards of quality and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make effective tradeoffs across short- and long-term roadmaps, balancing business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable technical foundation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders to integrate internal tooling and processes into differentiated workflows, navigating organizational complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with stakeholders, providing regular updates on progress, risks, and challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience managing teams that build and operate full-stack web applications at scale, and 10+ years of overall industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully recruited and built great teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prioritize competing requirements and stakeholders to iteratively ship new product features&lt;/li&gt;
