&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Accounting Team is responsible for understanding and telling Stripe’s financial story and shaping our collective understanding of how Stripe is performing as a business. Our primary focus is maintaining a well-controlled environment that effectively supports corporate governance, financial reporting and disclosure requirements. We advise and enable Stripe to grow. We operate in a fast-paced environment and collaborate significantly with cross-functional and international teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is seeking an Accounting leader to join its world class Accounting team and help us scale for the future, in a fast-paced environment that’s growing rapidly. In this role you will support all aspects of our equity programs, leveraging your technical expertise with US GAAP, to quickly identify accounting implications and impacts to our cross-functional stakeholders. In addition, you will support our financial, regulatory and internal reporting processes, financial systems, and related internal controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable accounting processes to support global growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recommend, and implement process and automation improvements, including use of artificial intelligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and perform monthly and quarterly close activities, including journal entries, balance sheet reconciliations, variance analyses, financial reporting deliverables, and analytical reviews with a focus on Equity and Stock Based Compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce internal management analyses and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support external audit processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with teams such as Internal Systems, Finance and Strategy, Treasury, Global Equity Management, Tax, and Legal to determine and operationalize the accounting implications of new business initiatives and transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and prepare technical accounting documentation with a focus on Equity (ASC 505) &amp;amp; Stock Based Compensation (ASC 718)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and execute efficient internal control procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain accounting policies and procedural documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of relevant public accounting and/or industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;B.A. or B.S degree in Accounting or Finance (CPA strongly preferred)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in U.S. GAAP and ability to research complex accounting issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and organizational skills, both written and verbal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal controls (design, implementation and execution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history of taking on various types of challenging projects and producing results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solution-oriented mindset with enthusiasm for establishing best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and have a high degree of accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of (or experience in) the technology or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Oracle, Shareworks, and/or Workiva&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team represents Stripe to governments, regulators, industry partners, and broader stakeholder audiences. We help policymakers understand the businesses building on Stripe, and help Stripe understand the policy decisions that affect them. Our EU work sits at the intersection of financial services, technology and economic policy. The team works closely with Policy Strategy, Legal, Communications and regional product and go-to-market teams to translate Stripe’s experience and our users’ needs into effective policy engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an EU Government Relations Manager to advance Stripe’s priorities in Brussels through effective advocacy and strong relationships with policymakers. You will bring deep expertise in either payments and financial services policy or technology policy, and use that expertise to influence EU legislative and regulatory debates that matter to Stripe and the businesses we serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an advocacy-led role: you will develop and execute engagement strategies, build relationships across the EU institutions, and make persuasive arguments for policies that help European businesses start, grow and compete. Working closely with Policy Strategy, Legal and business colleagues, you will turn Stripe’s policy positions into practical advocacy, exercising judgment about where, when and how to engage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position is based in Brussels and reports to the Head of EU Government Relations. Its primary focus is the EU, working closely with colleagues across EMEA and globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop and execute EU advocacy strategies for an agreed portfolio of issues, setting clear objectives, identifying opportunities to shape the policy making process.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build and maintain relationships across the EU institutions, developing a strong network of policymakers, officials and advisers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Represent Stripe directly in policy discussions, making clear, persuasive arguments grounded in our business, our users’ experiences and the needs of Europe’s digital economy. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bring deep subject expertise to Stripe’s advocacy in either payments and financial services or technology policy, while building the knowledge needed to engage effectively across a broad waterfront of issues.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work closely with Policy Strategy, Legal, Product and Go-To-Market colleagues to develop and refine advocacy positions, drawing on their expertise and ensuring our engagement reflects commercial and technical realities, and the needs of our users. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build support for shared policy objectives through trade associations, industry coalitions and engagement with other companies and stakeholders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Gather political and regulatory intelligence to guide advocacy decisions, keeping colleagues informed of material developments and recommending when and how Stripe should act.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of relevant experience in government relations, advocacy, public affairs or public policy, including direct experience of EU policymaking and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in either payments and financial services policy or technology policy. Expertise in both is not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A demonstrated track record of developing and delivering advocacy strategies and influencing legislative or regulatory debates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of EU institutions, political dynamics and legislative processes, with experience building productive relationships with policymakers and officials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound political judgment: the ability to identify what matters, assess opportunities to influence outcomes, and recommend a practical course of action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about unfamiliar products and policy issues, and the ability to build working knowledge beyond your area of specialism.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and spoken English, including the ability to turn complex issues into clear, persuasive arguments and adapt them to different audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven collaborator who is resourceful, detail-oriented, and able to work both independently and as part of a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for meetings and events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about Stripe’s mission of helping ambitious businesses grow and thrive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, humility, and some comedy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a high-growth, rapidly scaling environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience working in technology, payments, merchant or financial services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to work with a diverse group of policy, regulatory, and product nerds who embrace Stripe’s policy issues, our users and each other.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the other policy domain: technology policy for a payments and financial services specialist, or payments and financial services policy for a technology specialist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the business landscape and experience with relevant business associations in the EU.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Globally-minded and interested: while the focus will be on the EU and the wider EMEA region, given Stripe’s global presence, projects will inevitably become broader than that and the person will have to translate and explain what’s happening in the region to a global audience within Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Events Marketing team is part of Stripe&#39;s broader Americas Marketing organization and builds high-impact event experiences across key industry, product, and segment priorities. The Product and Financial Services portfolio supports programs that drive pipeline, deepen customer relationships, and accelerate adoption of Stripe&#39;s revenue and financial infrastructure products. In this role, you&#39;d join a team that values precision, creativity, sound judgment, and strong operational partnership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an experienced events professional to own the planning and execution of a focused portfolio of Product and Financial Services events within AMER Events Marketing. You&#39;ll lead end-to-end delivery of event programs aligned to Stripe&#39;s Financial Services and product go-to-market priorities, spanning third-party industry conferences and Stripe-hosted experiences. Your portfolio will include Financial Services programs such as Money20/20 and product-focused industry events. Day to day, you&#39;ll manage multiple concurrent programs while partnering closely with field marketing, product marketing, partner marketing, and external agencies to deliver experiences that support pipeline, account engagement, and relationship depth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end planning, coordination, and onsite execution for a portfolio of Financial Services and product-focused third-party and first-party events, including Money20/20.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate event objectives into clear program plans, audience experiences, workbacks, staffing plans, and success measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with field marketing, demand generation, product marketing, partner marketing and industry go-to-market teams to align programs with business priorities and audience needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, manage, and track event budgets, surfacing variances, timeline risks, and scope tradeoffs early with recommended paths forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary event point of contact for agencies, vendors, venues, and other external partners supporting the portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage logistics end to end, including venue sourcing, vendor coordination, contracts, catering, audio/visual, staffing, run-of-show, and onsite execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage day-to-day planning and delivery across assigned programs, coordinating stakeholders and keeping workbacks on track.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate event data in relevant event-management and CRM systems to support registration, lead capture, pipeline attribution, and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead post-event reporting across pipeline influence, lead generation, engagement, and budget performance, and turn findings into practical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present post-event findings, learnings, and recommendations to the Head of AMER Events and relevant GTM stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4–6 years of event-management experience, preferably in B2B technology, fintech, financial services, payments, or product marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience delivering third-party sponsorships and company-hosted events from planning through onsite execution and post-event reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and project-management skills, with the ability to manage multiple high-stakes events concurrently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills across marketing, sales, product, and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing event budgets, vendors, agencies, and operational details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced environment with evolving priorities and cross-functional dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience producing Financial Services, fintech, payments, or product-marketing events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with product and industry events such as Money20/20, MRC, and MAG.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Revenue, Money Management, or related Stripe product narratives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Salesforce and event-management platforms such as Splash, Cvent, or comparable tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting executive-level programs, including roundtables, hosted dinners, and invitation-only summits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset and experience using event data to inform decisions and report pipeline attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build impactful experiences that drive awareness of Stripe, educate users and prospects on Stripe solutions, foster community, and deliver high quality leads to our sales team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is responsible for leading the event registration strategy for the Corporate Events team, developing streamlined processes and tailored experiences for diverse attendee types. You will collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure efficient execution of registration from planning through post-event analysis while maintaining compliance and aligning strategies across global markets. By analyzing data and preparing insights, you will inform decisions that maximize attendance and enhance the overall attendee experience. Additionally, you will manage the development of the event mobile app, ensuring it integrates seamlessly with the registration process and enhances attendee engagement. You will also contribute to compelling promotional materials and ensure communication consistency across all registration touchpoints. Reporting to the Stripe Sessions event lead, this position requires you to work autonomously and present well-prepared recommendations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy and concept development:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead event registration for all events the Corporate Events team works on, including pricing models, simple and elegant attendee flows, and promotional tactics to maximize attendance and revenue where applicable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and document distinct registration experiences tailored to different attendee types, outlining flows, content requirements, email communications, calendar invites, nurture campaigns, and post-event follow-ups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and document registration policies for each event based on historical data and event goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Demand Generation, Marketing Operations, and Product Marketing teams to analyze large data sets, identifying trends and insights to guide future event strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Web Presence and Platform team to define the annual events web roadmap, assess available design and engineering resources, break down web projects into phases as needed, and create timelines that prioritize key deliverables.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Copywriting and the Event lead to craft landing page copy for all promotional pages, ensuring that event themes, value propositions, and key information are prominently highlighted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the Stripe writing style guide to craft clear communications for all transactional registration journeys. Collaborate with the Copywriting and Demand Generation teams to support additional messaging and reviews for event marketing emails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand the internal and vendor systems involved in the registration process to facilitate seamless data movement between each and support registration workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Legal team to maintain compliance in registration forms, regularly reviewing and updating practices as regulations evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Web Funnel teams to ensure registration form fields are consistent with the contact sales form and Salesforce data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with security teams to adhere to established procedures for screening event registrants, and establish communication protocols to be utilized as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement a registration strategy for the event mobile app, ensuring a user-friendly interface and seamless integration with the overall registration process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze user engagement and feedback from the mobile app to identify opportunities for improvement and incorporate insights into future app development and event strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning and execution:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to define clear roles and responsibilities, ensuring efficient coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with global teams to align registration strategies and ensure effective execution across diverse markets and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the entire registration project lifecycle for all events within the Corporate Events team, ensuring seamless execution from the planning phase to onsite management and post-event analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure consistency across all registration materials, including forms, email communications, and event websites, in alignment with brand guidelines to create a cohesive attendee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and distribute weekly registration reports to executives and leadership, offering insights on progress toward goals, attendance trends, and recommendations for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate weekly planning meetings with internal and external teams to ensure alignment and effective collaboration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the quality control process for promotional landing pages and registration forms, ensuring they launch on time and meet Stripe’s quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct quality control and audits on registration data to identify discrepancies and maintain accurate records for reporting and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare onsite registration and check-in processes, contingency plans, and escalation procedures, ensuring their execution as planned during the event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Event Lead and Brand team to develop a comprehensive strategy for attendee badging, ensuring that all attendee types are effectively considered and included in the plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of onsite attendee scanning plans and data upload initiatives, while closely collaborating with the Demand Generation team to develop an effective attendee follow-up plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary point of contact for onsite registration escalations, collaborating with agency partners and security to ensure that pre-event attendee screening protocols are maintained throughout the onsite experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with cross-functional teams to align the mobile app experience with overall event branding, messaging, and promotional strategies, creating a cohesive and engaging attendee journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the development and execution of the event mobile app, ensuring that it is functional, user-friendly, and compatible with all event-related activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate mobile app testing and quality control processes to ensure a smooth launch and operation, addressing any technical issues before and during the event.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel required to support onsite execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Slack, Salesforce, Marketo, Google drive, Figma, and Asana.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in international environments with an understanding of regional differences that may impact registration strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with digital marketing principles and tools, including SEO, email marketing, and social media promotion, to boost event visibility and engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in event registration management for both paid external and internal events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with event registration software and technical tools, leveraging technology to streamline processes and enhance attendee experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills, capable of interpreting data to provide actionable insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management expertise with a proven track record of managing multiple concurrent projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal skills for building relationships across departments and with external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and organized, committed to maintaining quality and consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership abilities and adaptability to navigate changing environments while prioritizing effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and creative mindset, thriving in dynamic, fast-paced work environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in influencing, problem-solving, and consensus-building with experience in managing complex projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in developing scalable processes and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple competing priorities and handle unforeseen challenges with quick solutions in high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Executive Programs team builds relationships and experiences that connect senior customer leaders with Stripe’s leadership, products, and strategy. We create forums where executives can exchange ideas, explore the forces shaping their businesses, and give Stripe direct, substantive feedback.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our executive advisory programs are an important part of how Stripe captures the perspectives of executive buyers. The portfolio includes our global Customer Advisory Board as well as regional, segment, and emerging advisory programs. Our goal is to connect these programs into a coherent system that brings the right customer perspectives into Stripe and helps product, marketing, and go-to-market teams act on what we learn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Executive Advisory Programs, you will define and build Stripe’s approach to executive advisory forums. You will own our existing global Customer Advisory Board and create the framework for launching and scaling complementary regional and segment councils. You will also identify and incubate new advisory programs as Stripe’s priorities and customer base evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will connect program strategy with execution: recruiting influential members, shaping agendas with internal partners, delivering white-glove executive experiences, and building a reliable process for capturing and activating customer feedback. You will work closely with leaders across Product, Product Marketing, Events, Sales, and Customer Success to ensure that Stripe’s advisory programs have clear remits, operate as an interconnected portfolio, and inform relevant product and go-to-market decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Stripe’s global executive advisory strategy, including the purpose, audience, operating model, and relationship between global, regional, segment, and emerging programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Stripe’s global Customer Advisory Board, including member strategy and recruitment, executive engagement, agenda development, meeting delivery, and year-round programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a repeatable playbook that enables regional and segment teams to build effective advisory councils while maintaining a consistent quality bar and connection to Stripe’s broader program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, launch, and incubate new executive advisory programs that address emerging customer needs and Stripe priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Product Marketing leaders to select strategic topics, translate customer priorities into productive discussions, and route resulting insights to the teams that can act on them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional planning across Product, Product Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, and external agencies, establishing clear responsibilities and resolving areas of overlapping ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and measure program impact, including member engagement, the quality and activation of feedback, executive relationship development, and evidence that customer insights are informing Stripe’s decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience building and leading executive advisory boards, councils, or comparable programs for a global business, including setting program strategy and operating the program from recruitment through follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build trusted relationships with C-suite and other senior executives and to represent an organization credibly in executive settings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, cross-functional programs and defining clear responsibilities among teams with adjacent or overlapping remits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand technical products and concepts, identify the implications for customers, and connect executive feedback with product and business priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering high-touch executive events with careful attention to the member experience, content, logistics, and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a portfolio of interconnected global, regional, or segment-based advisory programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing systems for synthesizing qualitative customer feedback, routing it to relevant teams, and measuring whether it influenced decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with product, marketing, sales, customer success, solutions, and events teams in a global technology organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with financial infrastructure, payments, software platforms, or another technically complex industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic infrastructure that makes it easier for entrepreneurs and companies across the globe to grow their businesses. To support those efforts, Stripe is seeking a seasoned Government Relations professional to join our Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team in the US. Stripes on the Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team operate in a fast-paced internal and external environment that requires collaborating with teams across our organization and with outside stakeholders. The culture is thoughtful, transparent, academically rigorous, and kind. In this role you will have the opportunity to impact the trajectory of Stripe in the US and enhance financial innovation and inclusion. This role is focused on US federal legislative and regulatory advocacy and will sit alongside Stripe&#39;s existing federal team in Washington, DC.&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;We are not open to remote or travel candidates for this role.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will deal with a diverse set of issues that straddle financial services, technology, internet regulation, tax and economic policy. You will define, shape, and advocate for initiatives that increase the GDP of the Internet. You will maintain deep relationships with Members of Congress, committee staff, key federal regulators, and the Executive Branch — building and executing legislative and regulatory strategies on issues central to Stripe&#39;s mission, including payments modernization, financial regulation, artificial intelligence, and the future of agentic commerce. If you are a team player who wants to represent millions of businesses around the world growing on Stripe, we look forward to hearing from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a senior member of our Government Relations &amp;amp; Public Affairs team, which works across the globe to strategically develop, pursue, and execute policy objectives as part of Stripe&#39;s global policy priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute federal legislative advocacy — managing Stripe&#39;s engagement with Congress on key legislative priorities including stablecoins, digital assets, open banking, AI governance, and payments regulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with Members of Congress, committee and personal staff, and serve as Stripe&#39;s frontline representative on federal legislation affecting the payments and technology industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage federal regulatory agencies — including the Treasury Department, OCC, FDIC, Federal Reserve, CFPB, and others — to educate them about Stripe&#39;s business, advocate for sound policy outcomes, and navigate regulatory proceedings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, develop, and execute political, policy and advocacy initiatives and campaigns that advance Stripe&#39;s policy goals and those of our users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help colleagues across Stripe understand federal legislative and regulatory developments, identify policy opportunities to grow our business, and translate complex policy dynamics into actionable guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe on trade groups, coalitions, and industry bodies engaged on federal policy issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own internal budget management and reporting, including quarterly business reviews (QBRs) and regular performance reporting to leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate with clarity and precision — producing internal and external written work that reflects Stripe&#39;s high bar for writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 12+ years of experience in a policymaking, government, or senior advocacy role — ideally a mix of time on Capitol Hill, in a federal regulatory agency, or in a world-class organization as an in-house government relations expert or other business-related role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A background working for a Member of Congress, a committee or leadership office, or in a senior policy role at the US Treasury, OCC, FDIC, White House, or comparable federal institution — with a track record of navigating bipartisan legislative environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in financial services regulation and payments policy, with a strong understanding of the legislative and regulatory landscape across banking, money transmission, and digital assets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with, and ideally direct experience on, emerging technology policy — including artificial intelligence, agentic commerce, and the regulatory questions that arise at the intersection of AI and financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationships with policymakers and staff on both sides of the aisle and a reputation for credibility, reliability, and good judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of managing complex, technical policy issues — capable of managing major initiatives independently, driving coalitions, or project managing a cross-functional team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment — capable of making smart decisions in the face of ambiguity and imperfect information and learning from them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A terrific communicator and writer, adept at working with lawyers, regulators, engineers, business teams, and colleagues to make complex concepts clear and understandable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for Stripe&#39;s mission of helping businesses grow and thrive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, curious team-first mindset with experience thriving in ambiguous, high-growth or startup environments across global offices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empathy, humility, and a respect for those who have views that are different from yours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to work with a diverse group of policy, regulatory, and product professionals who care deeply about Stripe&#39;s policy issues, our users, and each other&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel 25% for meetings and events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building an elite team to drive financial insight and strategy at Stripe. The Corporate Finance &amp;amp; Strategy team brings understanding and predictability to Stripe’s financials, and we work together with our key business partners to accelerate long term growth for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with F&amp;amp;S and the Business to drive the long-term success of Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure month close processes get done efficiently, accurately, and on time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Finance, eg. Strategic Sourcing&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally to identify important strategy questions and answer them with data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build financial forecasts and targets, track performance, and understand deviations from actuals to drive strategy and operational rigor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain deep knowledge and understanding of Stripe&#39;s business performance across geographies and user segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automating away recurring work by utilizing AI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in month end close processes and have demonstrated experience working closely and successfully across the other functions of the Finance Org (eg., Accounting, Tax, Treasury)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience running recurring processes and organizing cross-functional partners and stakeholders to deliver materials on time (e.g. enabling, tracking, monitoring status, problem solving the month end close process; driving successful continuous improvement initiatives as it relates to domain of expertise)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of accounting, accruals, and opex management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with financial analysis, financial forecasting, BvA (variance analysis), and other financial concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on ambiguous problems and driving solutions/projects independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to automate and use AI to streamline recurring tasks/analyses, in order to free up time to work on more strategic and higher impact work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building dashboards and data visualization tools from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to build strong collaborative working relationships with business partners and department leads. You are seen as a trusted and objective advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to be a self-starter capable of driving business results without significant supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global capacity (this team will work will all regions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a strategic finance function at a high-growth tech company, preferably in the payments/fintech space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

