&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Collaboration team helps Stripe employees work smarter and more efficiently, get to know each other, and request and receive help from one another. The team is nimble and creative. We work across a wide stack; on any given day, we discuss user interface design, data models, API design, infrastructure maintenance, agentic integrations, or all of the above. We’re excited to innovate in a space that traditionally isn’t thought of as in the forefront of innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being a small team, we carefully choose what we work on to have the highest leverage. This is not always easy—we work very cross-functionally, partnering with groups from engineering to Communications to senior leadership. But one of our greatest rewards is getting to sit next to and see the impact our work has on our users: our fellow Stripe employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an engineer on Stripe’s Collaboration team, you will be a key member of a team that acts as a force multiplier on the internal tools that Stripe uses. You will focus on building innovative AI-native experiences that help Stripe employees be more productive across various tasks and activities. You’ll collaborate with other teams across Stripe, combine traditional hands-on engineering with emerging AI capabilities, and experiment with different ideas and approaches to empower and delight your users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a team of smart, motivated engineers who put their users first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own solutions from end to end, managing complexity and engaging directly with stakeholders to think through everything from success metrics to MCP tooling to the nitty-gritty implementation details of the products you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage the latest AI tooling to refine and optimize both your users’ workflows and your own.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use both qualitative and quantitative metrics to determine priorities and measure effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold Stripe’s high standards for engineering and product quality and mentor newer team members to do the same.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 6+ years of professional software engineering experience, including 2+ years of industry experience building rich web experiences using modern frameworks such as React, Vue, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You work well across a full stack, from user experience to workflow automations to reliability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working directly with users and cross-functional partners to build creative solutions that address their problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are able to think rigorously, navigate ambiguity, and make hard decisions and tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working together with your team toward common goals, but are also able to drive your work forward autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a passion for enabling people to do their best work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have an interest in partnering with creative, non-technical teams, such as those responsible for Stripe’s creative communications and publishing efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a track record of shipping LLM-powered experiences with a strong understanding of how underlying technologies work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have industry experience working with Ruby, TypeScript, and React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are experienced with using AI tools to maximize your technical throughput while maintaining a high bar for quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You never lose sight of the end user, and you enjoy the quick feedback loops made possible by working (sometimes literally) next to your users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At its core, Stripe is a treasury company, and the Treasury Finance team (TFIN) is key to building the Global Payments and Treasury Network (GPTN).&amp;nbsp; Within TFIN, the FX team collaborates closely with product, engineering, sales, and finance teams to manage Stripe’s Corporate and User related FX risk. This includes creating pricing models to keep pace with product expansion and developing hedging strategies to mitigate the risks to Stripe’s profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe supports global commerce across 135+ currencies including digital assets.As a result, Stripe needs to build and maintain platform systems capable of pricing, estimating and hedging the resulting&amp;nbsp; FX exposures. Grounded in an understanding of FX market conventions and dynamics, you will partner with Engineering, Data Science, Product, and Finance to maintain operational rigor today while shaping long-term pricing and hedging strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor FX risks, execute trades , reconcile position, and attribute costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build automated risk monitors, alerting tools, and analytical models using SQL and quantitative coding to enable observability and minimize operational toil&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Engineering to guide the design and scaling of core FX infrastructure, trade execution flows, and liquidity provider integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop risk-based FX pricing methodologies across products and currency pairs, factoring in volatility, transaction costs, netting efficiency, and embedded optionality like rate guarantees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design hedging strategies to mitigate FX risks on financial statements while maintaining robust policies, controls, and operational runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in FX, market risk, trading, quantitative research, or treasury operations, with working knowledge of FX market structure and instruments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and SQL to build analytics and tools, backed by a strong foundation in statistics, time series, and risk measurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail and a proven ability to turn complex, imperfect datasets into clear insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience using AI tools to streamline analysis and automation, paired with a critical eye for model validation and verification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to turn complex data into clear narratives and escalate issues concisely under time pressure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Economics, Finance, Statistics, Engineering, Computer Science, Math, or Physics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated trading and familiarity with option theory and greeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building data pipelines and systems working alongside technical teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Members of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team are responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe’s key strategic partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education, and enablement with our partner organization. PSAs are critical technical liaisons to Stripe Partner Development Managers and partners. This involves creating comprehensive technical business plans for partners, including identifying, incubating, and bringing to market service and solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solutions Architect is someone who is intellectually curious, motivated to win, open, and entrepreneurial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a dynamic and experienced Global Lead of Partner Solutions Architecture, you will lead our growing team of talented solutions architects, working closely with our Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team. This role will focus on building robust alliances with independent software vendors (ISVs) such as Salesforce, Commercetools, and AWS, as well as global system integrators (GSIs) like Accenture and PwC, on top of other strategic regional partnerships. The ideal candidate will possess a blend of technical leadership and managerial prowess, driving the development and execution of strategic initiatives that foster collaboration and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also build and lead a new technical industry function focused on Stripe’s top-priority industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a global team of Partner Solutions Architects (PSAs) and managers of PSAs, providing guidance on best practices for engaging with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and lead a technical industry function for Stripe’s top-priority industries, defining the strategy, operating model, and talent needed to build deep industry expertise. Partner with sales, product, engineering, and industry go-to-market leaders to develop industry-specific solutions, reference architectures, and technical enablement that can scale across customer and partner engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic plans to enhance the capability of the PSA team in supporting ISV and systems integrator (SI) partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic plans for the incubation of the Alliances &amp;amp; Channels (A&amp;amp;C) AI ecosystem (B2B AI and developer platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the executive sponsor and owner of the Stripe Partner Advocate Program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal stakeholders, including sales, product, and engineering teams, to ensure alignment in partner strategies and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with key partner accounts, understanding their needs and translating them into action for the PSA team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze market trends and partner feedback to identify opportunities for improvement and direct the team in addressing these areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement, innovation, and knowledge sharing within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow talent on a global scale across AMER, EMEA, and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and lead efforts to develop Centers of Excellence within partners, driving solutions-oriented go-to-market services, products, and strategies with Stripe as a key pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in technical presales or solutions architecture, including 10+ years in a presales leadership position. The ideal candidate will have experience in a similar role leading a Partner Solutions Architecture organization globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years of experience building and developing teams across multiple regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of cloud computing, APIs, software architecture, and integration technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership skills with the ability to inspire and develop high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to liaise effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven project management skills with the ability to lead multiple initiatives simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A results-oriented mindset with strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an environment that featured Billing, Payments, fraud solutions, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSAs) are domain experts aligned to Stripe’s solutions and the customer buying centers they serve. We combine deep product and industry expertise with an understanding of our customers’ most complex business and technical challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SSA team partners with specialist sellers and the broader pre-sales organization to shape strategic opportunities, develop pipeline, improve revenue attainment, and turn Stripe’s product capabilities into measurable customer outcomes. We also bring field insights to Product and Engineering, helping influence Stripe’s roadmap and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Revenue Suite helps businesses monetize however their customers want to buy: subscription, usage-based, or hybrid pricing. As monetization models get more complex and pricing becomes something companies iterate on continuously rather than set once, this team sits at the center of how Stripe helps businesses price, bill, recognize, and report on revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Global Head of Specialist Solutions Architecture for Revenue, you will lead the global strategy, execution, and growth of the SSA organization supporting Stripe&#39;s full Revenue Suite: Stripe Billing and Metronome together. You will define how Stripe engages customers across the entire monetization-to-revenue-reporting lifecycle, including subscription management, usage-based and hybrid billing, invoicing, tax, revenue recognition, and analytics, from initial business and technical discovery through solution design, adoption, value realization, and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a second line leadership role. You will manage a mix of regional managers, each leading their own team of specialist architects, along with a small number of senior individual contributors reporting to you directly. You will build and develop this multi-layered organization and create the operating model, playbooks, and cross-functional partnerships needed to scale it worldwide. Working closely with Sales, Marketing, Alliances, Professional Services, Support, Product, and Engineering, you will help customers modernize their revenue infrastructure while accelerating adoption and growth for Stripe&#39;s Revenue Suite across every region we operate in.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape a global function at an important point in Stripe&#39;s expansion beyond payments. You will connect deep technical expertise to customer value and commercial outcomes while ensuring that customer needs from every region influence Stripe&#39;s global product and go-to-market direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute the global technical sales strategy for Stripe&#39;s Revenue Suite, aligning specialist coverage, priorities, and investments with growth opportunities across AMER, EMEA, and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, lead, and develop a high-performing organization of regional managers and senior individual contributors, establishing clear expectations for technical excellence, customer impact, and commercial contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and develop your managers directly, building their leadership capability so they can in turn grow strong specialist architects on their own teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales leadership to prioritize resources, shape account strategies, and improve the progression and conversion of complex opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable engagement models, playbooks, reference architectures, and execution standards across the monetization-to-revenue-reporting lifecycle, including subscription management, usage-based and hybrid billing, invoicing, tax, revenue recognition, and analytics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise executives, developers, architects, finance leaders, and other decision-makers on modernizing their monetization and revenue-management architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide strategic customers from business and technical discovery through solution design, validation, adoption, value realization, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate recurring customer needs, market signals, and deal friction into actionable insights that influence Product and Engineering priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Revenue SSA organization in global leadership forums, providing clear perspectives on performance, capacity, risks, customer needs, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the Revenue Suite go-to-market approach across every region, accounting for regional regulatory requirements, business models, and market-specific billing practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong collaboration and knowledge-sharing mechanisms across regional and global teams to improve consistency, reuse, and execution quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance Stripe&#39;s external thought leadership through executive briefings, industry events, white papers, and reference architectures focused on billing, monetization, tax automation, and revenue management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in technical sales, solutions architecture, solution consulting, or another customer-facing technical role in enterprise technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience building and scaling pre-sales or solutions architecture teams, including hiring, managing, coaching, and developing senior individual contributors&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing managers, with a track record of developing people leaders and running a multi-layered organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering with sales leaders on complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise opportunities and connecting technical strategy to commercial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of modern monetization models, including subscription, usage-based, and hybrid pricing, and how businesses increasingly treat pricing as something to iterate on continuously rather than set once, and how that shapes billing, invoicing, and revenue-management requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical background with a solid understanding of APIs, distributed systems, and modern software development practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across global markets, with an ability to adapt leadership and go-to-market approaches across different regions and cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication, relationship-building, and cross-functional leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex business and technical concepts clearly to audiences ranging from developers and architects to finance leaders and C-level executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of the full revenue management lifecycle: recurring and usage-based billing, subscription management, invoicing, tax automation (sales tax and VAT), revenue recognition, financial/custom reporting, and the data pipelines that feed them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or advising on complex enterprise architectures and integrations involving financial or revenue-management systems, including configure-price-quote, order-to-cash, revenue recognition, and ERP systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with usage-based or consumption billing platforms and the metering, pricing, and invoicing architectures they require&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling a global technical go-to-market function during a period of rapid product or organizational growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of translating field insights into meaningful product, engineering, or go-to-market changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing executive-facing thought leadership, reference architectures, or industry-specific solution strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the regulatory and commercial considerations that affect billing, tax, and revenue management across AMER, EMEA, and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Who we are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Creating long-term value for our users is central to Stripe’s mission. The Go-to-Market (GTM) Industries team helps enterprise users and Stripe grow by understanding the challenges businesses face in specific industries and identifying how Stripe can help solve them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build Stripe’s expertise across key business verticals and develop the credibility and thought leadership needed to form relationships with industry leaders. In partnership with our GTM and Product teams, Industry Leads define relevant, value-focused solutions, support our users, and identify new sources of value for users and Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team provides industry expertise across Stripe and supports enterprise business development. We partner with enterprise users and large software-as-a-service (SaaS) platforms to address business challenges and help them grow with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Global GTM Industries team, the Global Industry Lead for Healthcare will shape Stripe’s growth strategy across the healthcare ecosystem, including providers, payers, digital health companies, pharmacies, and healthcare platforms. You’ll use your industry expertise to define and communicate the value of Stripe’s solutions in a healthcare context and build credibility with senior executives and leaders across the industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll partner with Sales, Marketing, Product Marketing, Partnerships, and Product teams to embed healthcare expertise across Stripe, support strategic deals, and develop our GTM strategy. You’ll also lead detailed product and business discussions with existing and prospective users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Stripe’s GTM strategy for the next phase of growth in healthcare&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account teams throughout the sales cycle, from identifying prospective enterprise users and developing pipeline through deal signing and activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with regional sales leaders and contribute to strategic account planning and user engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-level narratives and presentations, lead detailed product discussions, and communicate Stripe’s value to senior decision-makers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe at industry events, community forums, and online events, offering a differentiated perspective on healthcare, regulatory, and technology trends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create industry playbooks and lead enablement that helps sales teams understand the healthcare industry and engage users effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Partnerships teams to share industry insights, shape relevant solutions, and build relationships with healthcare technology, implementation, and strategic partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You have experience developing business strategy, supporting business development, and building GTM models. You understand the healthcare ecosystem and the challenges facing providers, payers, digital health companies, pharmacies, and healthcare platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can define solutions, communicate strategy and tactics, and work across functions and organizational levels. You’re comfortable engaging in business and technical conversations with users, internal stakeholders, and executives. You can build value in competitive situations, develop a detailed understanding of Stripe’s products, and share your expertise with others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of relevant experience in healthcare, healthcare technology, enterprise software, payments, consulting, or GTM roles, including substantial experience working with healthcare organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying user needs and translating them into solutions and GTM strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and develop solutions that address the needs of multiple stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written, verbal, and presentation skills, including experience communicating complex ideas to executives and building collaborative relationships across functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel approximately 25% of the time for industry events, Stripe events, and key user meetings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments or enterprise software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct or indirect sales experience, including closing new business or expanding existing relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising enterprise organizations on growth, strategy, or GTM challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or growing an industry-focused team or program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an industry strategy or industry leadership role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Partnerships team develops and manages the strategic relationships that enable Stripe’s payments, financial-services, and geographic-expansion ambitions. We work with local payment methods, financial institutions, card networks, banks, and other ecosystem partners to build the infrastructure, commercial models, and market access Stripe needs to serve users globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead&lt;/strong&gt; based in Singapore to own Stripe’s Global Partnerships strategy and execution across Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the regional Global Partnerships Lead, you will own Stripe’s most important in-market relationships across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners. You will set the partnership strategy for the region; identify, prioritize, and develop new opportunities; lead complex negotiations; and ensure partnerships deliver durable commercial, product, and expansion outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role at the intersection of product strategy, market expansion, and commercial execution. You will serve as Stripe’s senior partnership representative for the region, build trusted executive relationships with ecosystem partners, and lead alignment across Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, Legal, Risk, Compliance, Finance, Treasury, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Stripe’s &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead for Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore&lt;/strong&gt;, with end-to-end accountability for the regional partnership portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the regional strategy across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Stripe’s senior external relationships in the region, building alignment and representing Stripe’s strategic priorities with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partnership opportunities from market assessment and strategy through negotiation, contracting, onboarding, launch, governance, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional expansion-partnership strategy and execution, coordinating the partnerships required to establish, operate, and scale Stripe in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market intelligence, partner priorities, and ecosystem developments into clear recommendations for Stripe’s product and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional decision-making on commercial, product, operational, regulatory, and technical dependencies related to regional partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage partner-performance metrics, including commercial outcomes, product adoption, operational health, and strategic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and manage partnership risks, escalations, and trade-offs, ensuring sustained executive alignment internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercially rigorous, strategically minded partnerships leader who is deeply familiar with the payments ecosystem in Greater China, Hong Kong, and Singapore. You are comfortable navigating complex stakeholder environments, structuring ambiguous opportunities, and independently driving high-impact outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategy, financial services, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in payments, fintech, ecommerce, banking, card networks, local payment methods, or adjacent financial-services sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex, strategic commercial negotiations with senior external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the payments and financial-partnership landscape in Greater China, Hong Kong, and/or Singapore, including relevant market dynamics and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and English executive communication skills and business-level Mandarin proficiency, written and spoken as this role would require working closely with our users and partners in the Greater China region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to develop a clear point of view amid ambiguity, influence without authority, and drive decisions across complex internal and external stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with product and engineering organizations on partnerships with meaningful technical, operational, and regulatory dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate autonomously while balancing multiple high-priority initiatives and long-term strategic relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a regional or multi-market portfolio of payments or financial-infrastructure partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting market-entry, expansion, licensing, or ecosystem-development initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing senior relationships across banks, networks, payment-method providers, fintechs, or other relevant ecosystem partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, global technology company with cross-functional product, commercial, and regulatory stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team and the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The People Systems Operations Administrator supports the day-to-day work that keeps Stripe’s People technology running accurately and reliably. The role sits in the Service Delivery Center and works as part of the wider People Solutions team, with a close dotted-line partnership to People Solutions Systems Management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own a defined set of routine tier 1 and tier 2 operational work across Workday and related People Systems. This includes monitoring support channels and system inboxes, triaging requests, completing repeatable administrative tasks, maintaining documentation, and routing complex issues to the right People Systems owner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on operations role. It creates clearer separation between routine support work and the configuration, architecture, governance, and project delivery owned by the People Systems team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support queue and request triage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Monitor the Salesforce case management queue and Jira requests for People Systems work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage incoming requests by urgency, business impact, data sensitivity, and defined support process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resolve standard requests using documented procedures, and route exceptions or higher-complexity work to the appropriate People Systems owner.&lt;br&gt;Keep request records accurate and complete, including status updates, required approvals, supporting documentation, and clear handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring request patterns and flag opportunities to improve documentation, self-service, or system processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workday operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the Workday inbox for business process errors, stuck transactions, alerts, and other operational issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete routine Workday support tasks, including standard access requests, account maintenance, and operational follow-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Salesforce and JIRA run work and respond to common People Systems questions using approved guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help with recurring operational tasks such as account monitoring, account resets, and quarterly account reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support year-end activity, including schedule extensions, alert configuration, audit requests, and tracking follow-up items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with release readiness by reviewing assigned Workday updates, completing test steps, documenting results, and escalating issues found during testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support recurring People programs, such as performance-cycle launches, using established runbooks and checklists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting, documentation, and Jira support &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intake and triage Workday reporting and data requests. Confirm required information, route requests to the right owner, and provide status updates to requesters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete standard reporting tasks and access-related requests where there is a documented process and appropriate approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain runbooks, Trailhead content, standard operating procedures, and request templates so guidance stays current and easy to find.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support data-quality checks and follow established processes to correct or escalate issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partnership with People Systems &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with People Systems analysts and engineers to understand support priorities, upcoming releases, recurring work, and escalation paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear handoffs for work that requires configuration changes, advanced reporting, integrations, security decisions, or policy interpretation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in regular reviews of queue trends, service levels, documentation gaps, and operational risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build platform knowledge over time, with opportunities to take on more complex administration and configuration work as skills develop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in People operations, HR administration, systems support, service delivery, or another operations role involving high-volume, process-driven work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, particularly where accuracy affects People records, access, payroll, compliance, or reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work through a queue independently, prioritize requests, follow defined processes, and escalate issues at the right time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and comfort giving requesters concise status updates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Jira, Salesforce, or a similar case-management or ticketing tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort learning enterprise systems and following structured procedures across multiple tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization skills and a consistent approach to documenting work and following requests through to resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good judgment when working with confidential information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting Workday, including Core HCM, business processes, security administration, reporting, or Workday inbox monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling reporting requests, data access requests, and standard user provisioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting cyclical People programs, compliance activities, audit requests, or system-release testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first six months, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the defined tier 1 and routine tier 2 People Systems queue work with accurate, timely resolution and clear escalation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish dependable monitoring for People Systems tickets in Salesforce, JIRA, the Workday inbox, and recurring operational tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce avoidable handoffs and ensure complex work reaches the right People Systems owner with the context needed to act.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep core runbooks and self-service guidance current based on recurring request patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give People Systems analysts and engineers more capacity for configuration, governance, architecture, and strategic delivery work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the job&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Who are we?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About Stripe&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. Stripe’s People &amp;amp; Places Operations team will sit within the SDC and is a highly collaborative, cross-functional team that drives key support for the People and Places function. We work with many different teams at Stripe. We are nimble and flexible individuals that can wear many different hats. We don’t mind working through ambiguity and love adding organization to chaos. We believe that success is not defined by any one individual, but rather by the collective work of the entire team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Provide strategic HR leadership to HR Operations. Effectively manage, develop and engage the global team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure an exceptional employee experience by simplifying key processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and implement HR initiatives and projects which are aligned within HR and Centers of Expertise (COE)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and lead key projects for improvement across HR&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify best practices that can be applied to improve work tasks and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver service improvement activity across HR through employing process improvement methodologies and the application of innovative thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote and lead change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supports the administration and maintenance of HR systems while driving process and data integrity across the HR landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and/or lead projects aimed at expanding centralization, leverage technology to improve the employee experience, and discover actionable insights and recommend solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for driving process consistency, data integrity and compliance to HR policies, procedures, data privacy, audit controls and regulatory requirements in all HR Service Center activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serves as the escalation point for HR Operations guiding the root cause analysis, resolution and communication protocol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the case management system (Ops ticketing system) and team to establish service level agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the HRIS team supporting HR technology upgrades&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain team standard operating procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversees relevant employee data management to ensure that data is secure and maintained consistent with company policies and privacy regulations and that required reporting and filings are delivered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track HR metrics to identify areas for improvement. Develop and implement counter-measures to correct identified misses to goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in verbal &amp;amp; written communication in English&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good working knowledge of MS Office, MS Outlook; MS Excel. Proficiency is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to details.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze and identify patterns in large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decision making aptitudes based on given guidelines and in ambiguous contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be comfortable working with large data sets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Very good knowledge and experience in internet navigation and research – finding specific information about products in a timely manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 7+ years of people and operations management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education - Grad/Post Grad in human resources or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desired 12+ years of overall experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with HR systems such as Workday, Greenhouse, Confluence and Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership skills, data analytical &amp;amp; presentation skills, Written &amp;amp; Communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of overall HR lifecycle – &lt;strong&gt;Core HR&lt;/strong&gt;, Benefits, Talent Mobility, Equity, Compensation, Exits etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Alliances and Channels team drives growth by building and scaling go-to-market (GTM) partnerships with world-class professional services firms, including global systems integrators (GSIs) and consultancies, alongside strategic technology leaders like AWS, Salesforce, and Adobe. Our mission is to provide users with a comprehensive ecosystem of technology and industry expertise, ensuring Stripe and our partners build high-growth, mutually beneficial businesses. We bridge the gap between Stripe’s platform and the specialized solutions our users need to scale globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Global Lead for PwC, you will drive the success of Stripe’s global alliance with these GSI’s by setting global strategy and enabling strong local execution of joint go-to-market and co-sell motions across all active regions. You will own the business plan, driving mutual revenue growth and strategic alignment across the GSI’s Payments, Industry, and AI practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner with Partner Development Managers and Partner Sales Managers globally to generate net-new demand, expand the partnership, and support Partner Development Manager activities across priority GEO’s. In this highly visible, fast-paced role, you will advance our strategic relationship through joint sales execution, solution development, and delivery alignment while maintaining a global view of partner performance and accelerating partner-driven revenue across Stripe’s sales segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate cross-functionally with Partner Sales leadership, Partner Development, Account Executives, and other Stripe teams to identify high-impact opportunities, support complex deals, and maintain strong operational rigor. Success requires deep knowledge of the Stripe partner ecosystem, strong stakeholder leadership, and a partner-first mindset that drives measurable customer value and shared growth for both the GSI’s and Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, enable, and operate the global PwC strategy and business, owning the global business plan and associated KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set partnership objectives, goals, and strategic direction while acting as the senior counterpart to PwC executive sponsors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on joint GTM strategy, including strategic priorities, target markets, and industry focus areas&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global, regional, and local teams (Stripe PDMs, A&amp;amp;C leadership, and GSI&amp;nbsp; counterparts) to drive strategy, solution development, partner enablement, pipeline growth, and deal closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable joint sales success by activating teams on the combined value proposition, leading account mapping, executing blitz activities, and co-creating opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrate cross-functional resources to support co-sell and GTM motions while building and maintaining a scalable long-term joint GTM model that drives partner and customer success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate key partner deals through pre- and post-sales support and lead pipeline reviews to uncover growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broker internal resources, tools, references, and investments required to achieve quarterly business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred experience is a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in GSI Partner Sales and GTM, business development, strategic alliances, or platform sales, with a focus on global partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building successful joint GTM partnerships and solutions with GSIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience working with PwC, including established executive relationships and a strong understanding of the GSI partner’s internal structure and decision-making processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership experience across strategy, sales, and solution development, collaborating closely with consulting partners and/or ISVs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the Managed Services Provider (MSP) landscape and how enterprises outsource functions like fraud and billing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process-oriented mindset with a drive to solve individual challenges while building for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and presentation skills, with the ability to engage diverse functional and technical leadership internally and externally&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of exceeding revenue goals, specifically in partner-sourced or sell-through revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to define and implement new business models (e.g., transforming a professional services relationship into a recurring revenue model through a platform partnership)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a Product or Platform partnership role at a top-tier Enterprise Cloud Software firm or within a GSI’s product arm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to payments and commerce landscape&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of how Stripe’s stack differentiates and compliments other technology solutions in different integration models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is a team of performance-driven marketers and channel specialists. We partner closely with growth, creative, analytics and regional marketing to drive revenue through self-serve and sales motions. We work globally, across all Stripe offerings and with all company segments — from startups to the largest enterprises.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a China Growth Marketer, you will own launching, proving out, and scaling paid media and growth marketing channels for the Chinese market. This is a 0-to-1 role: you&#39;ll identify the right channels, build the playbooks, and demonstrate what works before scaling investment. You&#39;ll work across paid channels native to China (WeChat, Baidu, Douyin, Xiaohongshu, Zhihu, Bilibili, and others), as well as broader growth marketing levers like web optimization, content distribution, and landing page localization for Chinese users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the in-house expert on how to reach Chinese developers, founders, and business operators through digital channels, bringing deep knowledge of the local ecosystem, platform mechanics, regulatory environment, and user behavior. You&#39;ll partner cross-functionally with regional marketing, analytics, creative, product marketing, and sales to ensure paid media supports Stripe&#39;s growth objectives in China.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch and scale paid media channels specific to the China market — including WeChat Ads, Baidu SEM, Douyin/Ocean Engine, Xiaohongshu, Zhihu, Bilibili, and programmatic platforms (e.g., Tencent Guangdiantong, ByteDance Pangolin)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a testing roadmap to prove channel viability: define hypotheses, run experiments, measure incrementality, and make go/no-go recommendations on scaling investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own web optimization and landing page localization for Chinese audiences — ensuring Stripe&#39;s web presence converts effectively for local users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build measurement frameworks for China-specific channels, partnering with analytics to attribute performance through to signups, activations, and revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage campaign budgets, pacing, and performance reporting — communicating results clearly to stakeholders across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the skills and experience to unblock, set up and navigate media platforms and partnerships in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current on China&#39;s digital marketing landscape: platform algorithm changes, content regulations, privacy laws (PIPL), and emerging channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional marketing, sales, and product marketing to align paid media with broader China go-to-market strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write concise performance updates and strategic recommendations for a global audience that ranges from paid media specialists to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of digital marketing experience with significant hands-on experience running paid campaigns on China-native platforms (WeChat, Baidu, Douyin, Xiaohongshu, or similar)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High professional fluency in Mandarin Chinese and English — able to write ad copy, review creative, and communicate strategy in both languages as this role will be heavily involved in the businesses in the Greater China region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the China digital marketing ecosystem: platform mechanics, ad formats, targeting capabilities, content regulations, and user behavior patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching new channels from scratch — demonstrated ability to take a channel from 0 to 1, prove its value, and scale it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills — ability to analyze campaign data, identify trends, and make data-driven optimization decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in B2B marketing, SaaS, developer tools, fintech, or high-growth technology companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter mentality — ability to drive strategic and tactical work forward with minimal oversight in a fast-moving environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication skills — can write concise, clear updates for a global audience with varying levels of paid media expertise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of digital marketing experience with deep China market specialization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to developers or technical audiences in China&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with China-specific analytics and attribution tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with web optimization, CRO, or landing page testing for Chinese audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of China&#39;s regulatory environment as it relates to digital advertising (PIPL, CAC content regulations, industry-specific ad restrictions)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a global company with cross-timezone collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiting team seeks to build the culture of Stripe by aligning the strongest global talent to our highest impact business needs. They focus on bringing Stripe’s operating principles to life in their recruiting processes, providing the highest-quality candidate experience, and leveraging data driven storytelling to influence the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are looking for consultative and creative recruiters to grow and scale our Go-to-Market (GTM) team. The GTM organization at Stripe encompasses our Sales team, Marketing and Sales Development, GTM and Product Operations, and Professional Services. These teams are expanding in the region, focusing on bringing new users onto the Stripe platform, supporting our existing users&#39; scale, and growing their businesses. You can expect high impact and wide-ranging responsibilities: owning full-cycle recruiting, driving hiring strategy, and delivering best-in-class candidate experience. This person must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment—unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic sourcing plans to identify and engage top talent, ensuring a robust and inclusive candidate pool for current and future hiring needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular market research and analysis to stay informed about talent trends, using insights to inform recruiting strategies and address potential challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across the organization to understand their hiring objectives and develop recruiting strategies aimed at achieving headcount goals, with an emphasis on expanding our GTM teams across the US, LatAM and Canada&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze recruiting metrics, providing regular reports on hiring progress to business leadership to ensure transparency and alignment with goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose and implement creative and scalable changes to the existing recruiting strategy to enhance efficacy and reach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams—including Finance, People Ops, Benefits, Onboarding, and Legal—to deliver a seamless and high-quality candidate experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-7 years of full-cycle Recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment including in house experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to build relationships with senior leaders and effectively influence decision-making processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong drive to identify and engage top talent, fostering relationships with candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to utilize data insights to identify trends and refine recruiting processes, enhancing efficiency and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility, adept at shifting tasks and priorities in response to changing circumstances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Applicant Tracking Systems (ATS), such as Greenhouse, Lever, or similar platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging sourcing and CRM tools (e.g., Gem, LinkedIn Recruiter) to build and manage talent pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of recruiting analytics and reporting tools to drive data-informed hiring strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with scheduling, communication, and collaboration tools (e.g., GoodTime, Slack, G Suite)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly adopt new recruiting technologies and optimize workflows for scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build, improve, diagnose, fix, and measure things. Have outsized impact in your role supporting a rapidly scaling sales organization! The GTM sales team at Stripe works with new and existing businesses of all shapes and sizes. As a member of the Central Sales Strategy and Operations team, you’ll be responsible for overall productivity and effectiveness of the sales organization, partnering closely with senior sales leadership and the broader sales team to provide insights and analysis on core business performance metrics and drive key strategic sales initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partnering closely with the GTM leadership team, regional sales leaders to support sales teams, owning the in-depth monitoring and tracking of the business metrics, creation of key intelligence and insights to accelerate growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with key cross-functional stakeholders, including but not limited to Marketing, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, Data Science, Seller Systems, and Strategic Operations to streamline and optimize our internal processes and run-the-business and planning deliverables (Stripe Rhythm of Business: Weekly Business Reviews, Monthly Business Reviews, Quarterly Business Reviews). Shape the processes and go-to-market support model for a rapidly growing company, and make a tangible impact on sales and operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the GTM leadership with intelligence and insight to accelerate growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Sales Strategy and Operations colleagues by standardizing global and regional common process that is currently decentralized&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep dive into key performance metrics and drive deep understanding of business performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem solve and structure analysis outcomes for complex sales operations challenges through data, analytics and insight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify new opportunities and areas of productivity efficiency gains for Regional sales leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in projects defining go-to-market approaches, as well as in regular business and resource planning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run analysis on key performance metrics, providing relevant insights for managing the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee implementation of enabling systems and tools, working closely with internal systems teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare weekly senior leader forecast materials and provide ongoing updates on key business growth/metrics to leadership teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage bespoke projects and effectively manage stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has 7+ years of sales, strategy and operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, or operational experience in investment banking or management consulting or private equity or venture capital, or business insights / analytics roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in SQL and other advanced analytics tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in BI visualization tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging AI to analyze data / derive insights, automate processes, or create reports / dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has strong analytical skills and a structured approach to solving unique business problems. Has experience working with data and large data sets to identify trends and create insights to make recommendations to senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has an enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves” mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, often ambiguous, and rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Growth Marketing is a team of performance-driven marketers and channel specialists. We partner closely with growth product, regional and demand marketing, and sales to drive revenue through self-serve and sales motions. The SEO &amp;amp; AEO function specifically drives organic discovery ensuring Stripe is found, cited, and recommended when developers, founders, and finance leaders are searching for or asking about payments, financial infrastructure, and related topics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role owns one of the most strategically important and evolving acquisition channels at Stripe. Organic search is already one of our largest and most efficient growth channels and the emergence of AI-powered answer engines represents a once-in-a-generation shift in how businesses discover software.&amp;nbsp;The role requires someone who can operate at the intersection of content, product, engineering, and data and who can credibly engage with Stripe&#39;s executive team on the strategic importance of organic visibility.&amp;nbsp;This is a rare opportunity to define what AEO means for a company like Stripe and to build the playbook that others will follow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the organic growth strategy end-to-end across SEO and AEO (Answer Engine Optimization), including technical optimizations, content strategy, on-site experience, and visibility in general purpose assistants (ChatGPT, Google AI Overviews, Gemini, Perplexity, etc.) and coding assistants (e.g. Claude, Codex, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, develop, and retain a high-performing team of SEO and AEO specialists, fostering a culture of experimentation, operational excellence, and continuous learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable improvements in organic visibility, rankings, citations, traffic, signups, sales inbound and downstream activations across both AEO and SEO&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable improvements in how well AI tools are able to understand how Stripe’s products work and how to properly integrate them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with product, engineering, content, growth, data science, and marketing to embed SEO/AEO best practices across Stripe&#39;s web properties, documentation, and product surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve the measurement framework for SEO and AEO: develop attribution models, define leading/lagging indicators, and quantify the revenue impact of organic channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own strategic roadmap for AEO: establish Stripe&#39;s point of view on how AI-generated answers reshape discovery, and position Stripe to win&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements across content quality, website architecture, and structured data to maximize discoverability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent organic growth performance and strategy across Stripe: translating complex technical SEO/AEO concepts into clear business impact narratives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in SEO, with at least 3 years leading a team and 2+ years at a senior/leadership level engaging with executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in both technical SEO and content strategy, with a track record of driving significant organic growth at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of how AI-powered search and answer engines work (LLM-based retrieval, citation behavior, entity recognition) and a clear point of view on how to optimize for them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive improvements across multiple levers: content, website architecture, product surfaces, structured data, measurement, and cross-functional influence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical foundation: comfortable with data, attribution challenges, and building measurement frameworks that quantify the business impact of organic channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to communicate complex technical concepts to executive audiences and build strategic alignment around organic growth investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working cross-functionally with engineering, product, content, and data science teams to implement SEO/AEO improvements at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building, developing, and retaining high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer-focused or technical B2B products where documentation, API references, and technical content are significant organic surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in international SEO strategy, including managing organic growth across multiple markets and languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building programmatic or product-led SEO at scale (e.g., template pages, user-generated content, dynamic landing pages)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated early-mover advantage in AEO evidence of monitoring, optimizing for, or measuring visibility in AI-generated answers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating in a fast-paced, metrics-driven culture where you must build the case for investment through data and strategic narrative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic engine for AI – and it’s working. Today, 88% of the Forbes AI 50 are building on Stripe (and most of the remaining 12% are pre-monetization).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AI GTM team is focused on helping AI-native businesses monetize and scale. We&#39;re in a unique position—partnering with the world&#39;s most ambitious AI companies (like OpenAI, Anthropic, ElevenLabs, and NVIDIA) to help them grow. This is one of the fastest growing parts of the business, and we need more great people to help us continue to accelerate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Sales Manager on the EMEA Startup team at Stripe, you will leverage your sales leadership and product expertise to drive growth through existing strategic AI customers. Reporting to the Regional Sales Lead for Startups, you will lead a team of Account Executives responsible for expanding Stripe&#39;s relationship with some of the most important European AI companies in the world—across payments, billing, and beyond.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be instrumental in leading in-depth product discussions with customers, developing consultative and solution-based sales strategies, and building deep knowledge of the AI industry and its unique monetization challenges. You will collaborate closely with Product, Marketing, Product Marketing, and User Operations teams to develop and execute against our go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision for a growing AI GTM team and scale day-to-day operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage a team of Account Executives managing existing AI accounts (driving revenue expansion, product attach, and retention) and looking for new business opportunities. Establish strategic plans and objectives to drive growth across the AI GTM business line, guiding execution to KPIs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a high-performing team, fostering a strong culture of energized and engaged Stripes while investing in the growth and development of your team. Coach and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based sales skills throughout the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for driving revenue, increasing product attach rates, and growing existing clients at high rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product, Marketing, and User Operations teams to influence our product roadmap (you are on the frontier!) and accelerate our growth trajectory for our AI industry users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as both an internal and customer-facing expert on Stripe&#39;s products, particularly as they apply to AI-native business models (usage-based billing, marketplace payments, embedded finance, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with customer executives (CEO, CFO, CTO) and serve as a trusted advisor on how Stripe can support their growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create best practices and improve the business and customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales leader: &lt;/strong&gt;You are an adept sales leader, capable of engaging in business-level and technical conversations at multiple levels of the organization. You see value in competitive situations and enjoy working on products that require both deep product understanding and technical knowledge, especially for AI industry users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People developer: &lt;/strong&gt;You are a strong people leader who builds high-performing teams through coaching, accountability, and culture. You&#39;re as comfortable working with clients as with internal stakeholders (including executives) and are excited to become an expert and share your knowledge. You possess an organized, self-starter mindset and excellent communication skills, with a track record for improving the processes and organizations around you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI enthusiast:&lt;/strong&gt; You have deep context in the AI industry and are energized by keeping up with new developments in the space. You bring a user-first mindset— you approach every customer interaction as a consultative partner rather than a transactional seller.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technically curious:&lt;/strong&gt; You understand APIs, webhooks, and modern developer tools—and you can hold credible conversations with engineering leaders about how Stripe&#39;s infrastructure fits into their stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales leadership experience, launching and growing high-functioning sales teams/products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in hyper-growth SaaS or technology environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing existing/growth customer portfolios and driving revenue expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to be a self-starter, capable of driving business results without significant supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex technical requirements and craft solutions across multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of AI industry dynamics, business models, and monetization strategies (usage-based pricing, API-first distribution, agentic commerce).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product acumen—ability to learn and articulate complex product capabilities, understand how they work technically, and connect them to user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including strong presentation skills for in-person meetings with multiple stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead complex negotiations involving bespoke agreements with commercial and enterprise businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Industry experience in payments, financial infrastructure, developer tools, or AI/ML platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships within the AI ecosystem (AI labs, AI-native SaaS companies, developer platforms).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling complex platform solutions involving multiple products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth-stage software company or a leading payments/fintech company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe&#39;s product suite and how AI companies leverage financial infrastructure to scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to start their business, accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The AMER Startups team is responsible for Stripe&#39;s fastest-growing and highest-potential customer segment. Within this organization, the &lt;strong&gt;AI Sales team&lt;/strong&gt; focuses specifically on the breakthrough ecosystem of AI - spanning foundation model builders, AI infrastructure platforms, agentic workflows, and AI-native SaaS applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI startups represent an unprecedented paradigm shift: they achieve hyper-growth at velocities previously unseen in software, operate complex token- or consumption-based monetization models, and face unique infrastructure and scaling demands from day one. You will tackle the challenge of building dedicated coverage, specialized technical go-to-market motions, and intelligent automation systems to support thousands of AI companies as they scale from seed stage to market dominance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of AMER Startups (AI Sales), you will lead the dedicated organization responsible for acquiring, expanding, and partnering with high-growth AI startups across North America. This role acts as both an expansion engine and a strategic acquisition vector for the most transformational segment in tech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be a second-line leader managing frontline managers across specialized Account Executives who grow distinct AI stages (e.g., early-stage AI labs, scaling AI infra, and enterprise-grade AI native apps). You will partner cross-functionally with product managers, solutions architects, risk specialists, and AI ecosystem venture partners to build GTM motions around usage billing, multi-product platform adoption, and AI-native monetization patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the Head of AMER Startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vision &amp;amp; Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop the overarching GTM vision, sub-team structure, and operating model for Stripe’s AI Startup organization across North America.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Specialized AI Coverage:&lt;/strong&gt; Design coverage models optimized for non-linear, hyper-growth trajectories—balancing high-touch high-velocity sales engineering for breakout AI labs with signal-driven, automated coverage for emerging AI developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monetization &amp;amp; Product Attach:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive adoption of core Stripe financial infrastructure—including Metered/Usage-Based Billing, Connect, Financial Connections, and Global Payouts—tailored specifically to consumption and token-based pricing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Breakout Detection Systems:&lt;/strong&gt; Create data-driven systems and signals to identify early breakout AI companies (e.g., sudden compute expansion, API usage spikes) and rapidly deploy specialized resources to capture and retain market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ecosystem Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with leading AI venture funds, incubators, AI compute providers, and cloud marketplaces to position Stripe as the default financial stack for AI startups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Building &amp;amp; Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Recruit, hire, and develop top-tier frontline managers and Account Executives, defining specialized AI sales profiles and fostering an environment of deep domain expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Feedback Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as the strategic voice of AI founders to Stripe’s Product and Engineering teams, shaping roadmap priorities for billing engine scalability, usage metering, and AI agent payment capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Forecasting &amp;amp; Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Own pipeline health and revenue forecasting for a volatile, hyper-growth segment using specialized leading metrics (usage volumes, API calls, compute commit signals).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience leading high-growth technology sales or GTM organizations, with 3+ years as a second-line manager leading multiple specialized sales sub-teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with usage-based, consumption, or complex SaaS billing and monetization models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving multi-product platform adoption and cross-sell growth in fast-moving technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong quantitative, analytical, and systems thinking skills to model portfolio economics, coverage ratios, and signal-driven investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, and retain high-performing frontline leaders and Account Executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain knowledge of the AI landscape, including LLMs, generative media, AI agent frameworks, and AI cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active connections within the startup and venture capital ecosystem (AI founders, investors, and startup communities).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior sales leadership experience at a high-growth developer-focused, infrastructure, or fintech platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing incentive and compensation structures aligned with consumption and usage-driven revenue models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of leveraging AI and automated signal workflows internally to scale sales productivity and coverage beyond linear headcount growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership Style&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a &quot;player-coach&quot; who can dive deep into the technical architecture of a generative AI startup&#39;s billing stack while stepping back to execute long-term strategic plans for the overall AMER market. You thrive in rapid, dynamic environments, embrace ambiguity, and lead through cross-functional influence across Product, Marketing, Risk, and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will embody Stripe’s core operating principles in your day-to-day leadership:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;User First:&lt;/strong&gt; You advocate relentlessly for the AI founder, ensuring our products solve the unique payment and monetization friction points of AI-native software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay Curious:&lt;/strong&gt; You continuously study emerging AI architecture patterns, new business models, and founder needs to keep Stripe ahead of market shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate Egolessly:&lt;/strong&gt; You work seamlessly across Stripe, prioritizing the overarching success of the Startups mission and the broader AI ecosystem over individual or team-specific metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services (GBS) primary goal is to ensure operational excellence across deal cycles, increase revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs, and drive closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as User feedback and market insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Global Business Services team is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Commercial Solutions&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the Commercial Solutions team. This involves managing and supporting the Commercial Solutions Program Managers, developing and implementing commercial strategies, and overseeing portfolio and resource management of commercial construct launches and product commercialization processes. Additionally, it includes establishing and maintaining program management standards and best practices to ensure consistency and quality across programs and projects. This is a large and diverse scope, including being accountable for all deliverables across the team&#39;s functional areas, setting a 12-24 month vision and growth trajectory plans for the organization, working with senior leadership to set/align to Stripe’s commercial evolution and strategies, and acting as a change agent across Stripe. This role requires a background in program management, deal policies and processes, a strong understanding of commercial frameworks and complex sales motions, experience developing a team through high-growth phases, and managing to the needs of the Enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will have experience with SaaS products, commercial &amp;amp; contracting strategies, and a strong background in program management. The candidate will have exceptional communication skills and executive presence to effectively communicate with Stripe and User senior leadership. You will love this job if you are a natural relationship, mechanism, and team builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and scale the Commercial Solutions team, focusing on developing, implementing, and evolving Enterprise-ready commercial programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a strategic vision while balancing program management office (PMO) maturity, capacity management, and stakeholder needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide reporting and progress updates to senior leadership on status of key initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with key internal teams—including Accounting, Commercial Legal, Engineering, Billing, Business Practices, Deal Strategy, and Deal Pricing—to drive commercial construct initiatives and NPI processes, serving as the Global Business Services’ Commercial Program PMO supporting the Go-To-Market (GTM) organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to create and drive the development of global mechanisms for efficient deal making processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal customers, including senior leadership and Stripe C-Suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strong leadership, communication, program management skills, and coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate and sponsor radical change of the commercial construct space, including evolving commercial program management, expanding commercial variant and approval standardization, driving policy and process enablement, and implementing broad system/process changes to streamline deal cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in program management/deal management/pricing strategy/financial consulting/legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with managing and developing a team, including defining respective roles/team scope, organizational priorities, and team strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a team of experienced Commercial Solutions Program Managers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills, each catered through an executive lens&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the Payment or SaaS domains, with a track record of program managing commercial initiatives and scaling to enhance quote-to-cash processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate business strategy at the C-Suite level, gaining credibility while advising organizations on how best to achieve business goals through the use of technology and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling cross-organizational programs including: commercial construct launches, policy development and process implementation, system deployments, and inter-team process design (pre- to post-execution)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated business sense with a high sense of ownership and ability to scale large scale mechanisms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building teams from the ground up, defining the functional space will setting the strategy and pace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conversant in all emerging trends in IT and Business and experience supporting complex transactions such as M&amp;amp;A, IP Acquisition, Revenue Share Models, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has deep understanding of the Payments or SaaS domain and experience scaling a business practices or commercial structuring function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JD degree with experience in either Corporate or International Law&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our users are the heart of our business. Stripe’s Global Customer Success Team is responsible for managing our largest and most strategic relationships, such as Bytedance, Canva, and Shopify. In this manager role you’ll be responsible for a high-performing team of Customer Success Managers covering the China Region. You’ll lead and coach the team, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, as well as roll up your sleeves to work directly with executives at existing enterprise Stripe customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a self-starter who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology sales or account management team, superior communication skills, and a knack for understanding unique customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Manager to lead a team of high-performing Customer Success Managers to build and grow the relationships with our most complex users from the China region.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, train, and lead a team of Customer Success Managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help drive an engagement model focused on high growth accounts in the China region.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop both the long-term vision and strategy for the team and drive progress toward key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for increasing revenue,&amp;nbsp; managing day-to-day operations, and scaling the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, mentor, and guide the team in developing consultative and solution-based customer success and sales skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Stripe’s solutions to meet client needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate, and enable individual development to promote career growth of direct reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to China to build interactions and relationships with our users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of customer success management or account management or sales experience with 3-5 years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to hire, train, and coach a high-performance Customer Success team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support the Customer Success Managers’ efforts through strategic advice on account strategies, and serving as executive sponsor with key relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal command of English and Mandarin as the position will require you to primarily work with China-based merchants&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for Stripe’s mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise East Sales team engages with some of the largest and fastest-growing businesses in the world to take advantage of Stripe’s solutions. You&#39;ll lead and coach high-performing sales executives dispersed along the East Coast, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, as well as roll up your sleeves to work directly with prospective Stripe customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, mentor, develop, and lead a team of sales professionals while scaling our New York GTM presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train the team in up-leveling professional skills such as collaborative pipeline generation, consultative and solution-based selling, closing tactics, adoption of MEDDIIC, and serving as a Trust Advisor to Stripe Users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop both the long-term vision and strategy for the team and manage day-to-day operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for operating net revenue and activation targets to grow Stripe’s revenue profitably.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively work cross-functionally across the organization to shape Stripe’s solutions to meet client needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire, motivate and enable individual development to promote career growth of direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a self-starting leader who is a builder and has demonstrated a track record of target attainment and success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, and solving complicated problems with limited oversight. Ideal candidates will have management and leadership experience scaling a technology sales team, superior communication skills, and a knack for understanding unique customer needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience as a proven account executive and/or 5+ years of front line sales management experience within technology, SaaS, banking or payments spaces. Second line management experience is preferred&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training, coaching, and scaling a high-performance sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build relationships with strategic clients, industry thought leaders and alliances &amp;amp; channel partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in an early stage, high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated passion for Stripe’s mission.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to clearly communicate technical concepts and build great relationships with highly technical customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Works in Progress is Stripe&#39;s magazine of new and underrated ideas to improve the world. We publish an eclectic mix of articles on policy, economics, business, technology, science, history, arts and culture, published online and in print. We have a fast-growing global audience, primarily in tech, finance and politics, and we are building out the team across editorial, design, operations and commercial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and run a commercial Works in Progress events program, focusing on the US. You will design events that people want to attend and that you can sell and grow sponsorship for. You will identify sponsors and partners, approach and pitch to them, and be responsible for meeting pre-agreed revenue and audience targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We currently offer infrequent events as one of the perks of being a subscriber to the magazine. Our existing community events program includes subscriber events in cities all over the world, particularly San Francisco; New York; Washington, DC; London; Dublin; and Brussels.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will assess where there are opportunities to raise revenue from our existing pipeline of events or by repeating existing formats, identify which events should be retired, and design new formats of events with commercial potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have the freedom to design your own events program, which may include a flagship annual summit, salons, themed dinners and lectures. Our events should appeal to ambitious people who are curious about the world. The Works in Progress editorial and operations teams will support you on programming: you will recommend speakers and formats, and we will sign them off. You do not need to arrive already knowing our taste — we will give you clear guidelines to work with. What matters most is commercial drive, energy and excellent production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll have the budget to add two more people to your team, plus contractors and agencies where needed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a model for US events, including sponsorship, ticketing, partnerships and invites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set events strategy and build an events calendar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the events P&amp;amp;L and set and hit revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell and manage sponsorships, and build relationships with sponsors across energy, housing, science, culture, economics and other core Works in Progress topics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead events end to end from concept to on-site delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the editorial and operations teams to identify the right ideas and people for live events, and build guest lists with genuine influence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage budgets, vendors, venues, production partners and timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching or substantially expanding a commercial events program, including developing its commercial model, operating plan, and performance measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven record selling and closing event sponsorship and hitting revenue targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Based in, or able to be based in, New York or San Francisco, with regular travel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Events experience at a media company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building commercially successful events for a high-value audience, not just a large one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing relationships with sponsors and brands, and with the kind of people we want on our guest lists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an existing fan of Works in Progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Finance Operations (FinOps) organisation delivers elegant financial services that are efficient, precise, and resilient—yielding a consistent, delightful experience grounded in controllership. Our service pillars span Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Travel &amp;amp; Expense, Payroll, and Monetisation Operations, with a sixth function—FinOps Strategic Enablement—driving AI adoption, process excellence, and scalable infrastructure across all pillars.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s &lt;strong&gt;Bangalore Finance (BFin) hub&lt;/strong&gt; is the largest concentration of FinOps and Controllership talent at Stripe and is central to our strategy of scaling financial services 10x without a proportional increase in cost or complexity. BFin houses teams responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounts Payable &amp;amp; Vendor Onboarding&lt;/strong&gt; — end-to-end supplier invoice processing, payments, and vendor lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel &amp;amp; Expense&lt;/strong&gt; — T&amp;amp;E policy compliance, employee reimbursements, and corporate card management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll&lt;/strong&gt; — accurate, timely compensation for Stripe employees across APAC and EMEA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monetisation Operations&lt;/strong&gt; — operationalising custom pricing and billing for Stripe&#39;s largest enterprise users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Controllership — BLR&lt;/strong&gt; — accounts receivable support, bank account management, and entity-level financial controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As &lt;strong&gt;Head of Finance Operations, Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the strategic and operational leadership of the entire BFin organisation. You will manage a team of team leads and managers—each running a distinct FinOps pillar—and will be the senior operational voice for Stripe&#39;s finance hub in India.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a builder and operator role. You&#39;ll set direction, elevate your managers, improve processes, and build trust with global Finance leadership—all simultaneously. You&#39;ll have a direct line to the global Head of Finance Operations and be a key contributor to decisions that shape how Stripe&#39;s financial services scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and Grow the Bangalore FinOps Organisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full people leadership of BFin: manage 4–6 team leads and managers across AP, T&amp;amp;E, Payroll, MonOps, and Controllership, with a combined org of 60–100+ Stripes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a clear performance bar, develop your managers&#39; leadership capabilities, and build a culture of ownership, precision, and psychological safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively manage talent density—attract strong candidates, address underperformance decisively, and retain top performers through meaningful development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate Global Strategy into Bangalore Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global Head of Finance Operations to translate Stripe&#39;s FinOps strategy into clear BFin operating plans and Stripe OKRs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure every manager in Bangalore understands what they&#39;re building toward, how their work connects to company outcomes, and where they have autonomy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent BFin&#39;s capacity, capabilities, and constraints in global planning; advocate credibly for resourcing decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive Operational Excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own BFin&#39;s key service metrics: accuracy rates, processing cycle times, SLA adherence, cost per transaction, and employee satisfaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a continuous improvement cadence—regularly auditing processes, identifying root causes of friction, and driving structured remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion Lean, Six Sigma, or equivalent methodologies as a discipline embedded in culture, not just process documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with FinOps Strategic Enablement to identify AI and automation opportunities; fix the process before automating it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build Scalable Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and maintain the organisational model and operating cadences that will support 2x–10x volume growth without proportional headcount growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve BFin&#39;s service catalogue, tiering, and SLAs in coordination with global FinOps leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure finance systems, controls, and data quality standards in Bangalore are fit for a public-company-ready financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Steward Risk and Controllership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed strong internal controls into every BFin process; partner with Accounting, SOX, and Internal Audit to maintain a robust controls environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify control risks, escalate with appropriate urgency, and own remediation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain compliance with regulatory, tax, and entity-specific reporting requirements across Stripe&#39;s India-based legal entities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence Stakeholders at Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships with global Finance Operations leads, Accounting, Legal, HR, and Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate BFin&#39;s roadmap, achievements, and blockers with clarity and data—this is Stripe, so you need to write well&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity, manage competing priorities, and drive alignment across time zones without escalating unnecessarily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;18+ years of relevant experience in Finance Operations, Accounting Operations, Shared Services, or Business Finance—including meaningful experience in a GCC, Captive, or SDC environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven manager of managers: you&#39;ve led teams-of-teams with 40+ total staff across multiple functional domains; your direct reports are themselves people managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational builder: you&#39;ve moved a Finance Operations org from one level of maturity to the next, with concrete, measurable outcomes (reduced error rates, faster cycle times, scaled volume without proportional cost growth)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep domain expertise in: Accounts Payable, Payroll, Travel &amp;amp; Expense, Accounts Receivable / Billing, Monetisation / Revenue Operations, or Corporate Controllership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured improvement methodology: direct, hands-on experience with Lean, Six Sigma, or formal process redesign—not just conceptual familiarity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving AI and automation adoption within Finance Operations or Shared Services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication; comfortable presenting to senior leadership and reconciling multiple stakeholder perspectives in writing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Business, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth technology company or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with enterprise finance systems: Oracle Fusion, Workday, Anaplan, or equivalents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading distributed teams across multiple time zones with US/global counterparts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of India-specific regulatory requirements (TDS, GST, FEMA, labour law) as they intersect with Finance Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes This Role Exciting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build at real scale&lt;/strong&gt; — Run Stripe&#39;s largest Finance Operations hub, with broad ownership and real resources to shape the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior visibility&lt;/strong&gt; — Direct line to the global Head of Finance Operations, with regular presence in global Finance leadership forums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Transformational moment&lt;/strong&gt; — BFin is moving from a cost-effective execution hub to a strategic centre of excellence; you&#39;ll define what that looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-forward environment&lt;/strong&gt; — Dedicated Enablement resources (FinOps Strategic Enablement team) sit alongside your org to accelerate automation and AI initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global career platform&lt;/strong&gt; — BFin operates as an integrated part of a global team, providing cross-domain exposure and a clear path for further growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Key Accounts Customer Success team is responsible for the growth, optimization, stakeholder engagement, and cross‑functional program delivery of Stripe’s most important users. Key Accounts often have complex multi-layered relationships, and are among our most important co-innovation partners. The team partners closely with Sales, Paid Support, Solutions Architecture, Product, and Payments Performance to drive critical outcomes for the users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a leader who will manage teams of CSMs focused on a portfolio of our largest Key Accounts at Stripe, driving strategic account planning, product distribution, executive engagement, and payments optimization to maximize retention, expansion, and customer lifetime value. You will hire, mentor, and scale the team, codify playbooks for platform engagement, and embed repeatable processes that balance bespoke customer needs with operational rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of senior CSMs focused on Key Accounts: hire, coach, set goals, run calibration and performance reviews, and develop playbooks and operating rhythms for a high-performing strategic CSM organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own strategic account planning and executive engagement for Key Accounts: define multi‑quarter account roadmaps, support executive business reviews, and ensure broad sponsorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals focused on product distribution and share of wallet gains that tie directly to business impact. Measure and report on performance metrics at an executive level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and scale programmatic account management processes: implement repeatable adoption, churn-risk, optimization, and renewal playbooks that balance scalability with bespoke engagement for strategic accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross‑functional delivery and escalation management in support of annual growth initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own account health, volume forecasting, and growth goals; align Stripe and customer leadership on success metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale learnings from Key Accounts to other GTM and product teams across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years in customer-facing roles with at least 8+ years leading Strategic Customer Success, Account Management, or related teams in a SaaS consumption environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, or fintech required; familiarity with Stripe products is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing a small portfolio of strategic large customers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independent, energetic leader with a proven track record of driving organizational change across cross-functional stakeholders and whole-team environments to deliver strong outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programmatic and strategic skills: account planning, project management, stakeholder mapping, and executive engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM/CSM tooling and data platforms (Salesforce, Gainsight, Looker or other BI tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a high‑growth, matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Japan Marketing team’s mission is to engage priority audiences through impactful and relevant marketing campaigns and events, to drive growth in adoption of Stripe’s solution offerings. Japan Marketing is a sales-aligned team, partnering closely with the Japan GTM organization, including Sales, Sales Development, Solutions Architects, Partnerships, and others. Our team works across all customer segments, and at each stage of the customer lifecycle journey. As a member of the Japan team, this is a great opportunity to build and have an impact on the Japan business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be part of the Japan team, setting and executing our Japan marketing strategy while working hands-on and developing a trusted relationship with Sales to drive successful user outcomes. The Head of Japan Marketing will lead the field marketing function and deliver high-quality leads, pipeline, and revenue. You will build, lead, and grow a small team of marketing leaders and professionals, and establish how the team responsibly uses AI to sharpen customer insight, accelerate execution, and improve performance. As an early member of the team, you will have an opportunity to build the Japan marketing function at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead marketing for Japan across all customer segments, with strong coordination with Sales leadership; customer segments include enterprise, digital native, software platforms, small businesses, and startups&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own key business and revenue metrics across the sales funnel (pipeline) and customer growth and retention.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a strong trusted relationship with the Japanese sales team, working closely with the sales leadership and sales development to jointly grow pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Asia Pacific demand generation and product marketing to refine our targeting and segmentation, and to identify, scope, and produce or localize compelling content, marketing assets and programs to drive demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute full funnel Japan marketing plans including digital marketing, demand generation campaigns, sales prospecting programs and ABM, virtual and in-person field events, and third party tradeshows and conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track, measure, and communicate program results, continually optimize for efficiency and scale, and seek to generate new global best practices through experimental efforts&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be creative in finding new ways of advising a diverse range of personas about the value Stripe brings to businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the Japan marketing team’s AI-enabled operating model, identifying high-value use cases across research, segmentation, localization, content development, campaign execution, measurement, and experimentation while maintaining strong judgment on quality, customer context, and responsible use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the team to adopt AI effectively, building repeatable workflows and raising the bar for strategic thinking, speed, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience leading a Japan marketing function across multiple customer segments including specific experience with content localisation and content marketing, event management, partnership marketing, and multi-touch campaigns to generate demand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years managing teams, with a track record of setting a clear strategy, developing talent, and leading through change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of defining and executing Japan B2B marketing strategies that deliver against funnel metrics and KPIs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills (both Japanese and English), including being able to convey complex topics with simplicity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven leadership capability and effectiveness working collaboratively and cross functionally:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Sales teams, including joint planning and execution, driving disciplined lead follow up, and earning trust as a strategic business partner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working as a Japanese leader partnering with global marketing teams, and leveraging central APAC capabilities and resources to lead growth in field marketing programs and events, executive programs and partner programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling through/and or leveraging agency and contractor resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding and/or experience with CRM, account-based marketing, email marketing tactics, and marketing technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated AI fluency in a B2B marketing context: hands-on experience using AI to improve insight, planning, content, execution, or measurement; ability to evaluate output quality and risk; and experience helping a team adopt new tools and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced industry and work environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing cloud services and/or software solutions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superb organization and project management skills and the capacity to manage multiple complex projects at once&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical skills and the ability to craft actionable insights from complex data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resourceful, creative and dedicated to achieving operational and creative excellence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering tailored marketing content and experiences for customer segments spanning from early stage startups to the largest enterprise companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the payments, financial technology, and/or ecommerce industries and partner ecosystems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success delivering marketing programs with and through consulting and technology partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High AI usage competencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Private Equity and Advisory Partnerships (PEP) team manages Stripe’s relationships with growth equity, private equity, and advisory firms. The team works with investors and advisors to help portfolio companies use Stripe to grow revenue and improve profitability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of Partnerships Managers and shape the strategy for expanding Stripe product use across private equity-backed companies. You will build relationships with investors, advisors, and portfolio company leaders, then work with Stripe’s sales, product, marketing, and operations teams to identify and develop long-term business opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of Partnerships Managers with experience in sales and private equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the team’s long-term vision and strategy, manage day-to-day operations, and deliver against key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain partner-level relationships with private equity firms and their portfolio companies through strategic planning and collaboration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Americas and global go-to-market leadership to communicate the team’s strategy, results, performance metrics, and industry insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally across sales, marketing, communications, business operations, people operations, finance, and product management to deliver the program’s goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in the financial sponsor ecosystem, including through relevant industry events and speaking opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise private equity firms on prospective investment opportunities and payments monetization across their portfolios, and educate financial sponsors on Stripe’s products, roadmap, and vision for financial technology and money movement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in business development, sales, private equity, investment banking, or management consulting, including 5+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience working with senior executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience using data and metrics to drive commercial outcomes for a business and its customers or partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a technology or payments company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and implementing a strategic plan for a growing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building skills and attention to detail, with the ability to cultivate partnerships and oversee programs at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage cross-functional projects and multiple priorities, with strong organizational skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of investment terminology and relevant industry performance metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Financial modeling experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is investing in building out its Payouts product sales team to help prospects and customers move money globally with greater speed, flexibility, and control. Our growing footprint of Payouts products (Instant, Next day, Global payouts) and Currency Management Solutions (FX, MCS ) enable businesses to send funds to sellers, service providers, contractors, creators, claimants, customers, and other third-party recipients around the world, as well as better manager their cash flow and treasury operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will represent Stripe across our global markets externally while helping develop and strengthen our culture internally. You know what it takes to build and scale a business structurally and methodically. You have a strong understanding of technical and financial concepts and enjoy working closely with Product and Engineering teams, as well as broader Sales and go-to-market organizations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Head of Product Sales, Payouts, you will be a critical member of the go-to-market leadership team. You will drive the strategy and execution of Stripe’s Payouts GTM, accelerating adoption and revenue growth across Payouts, platform and marketplace payout capabilities, cross-border payouts, FX/MCS solutions, payout methods, and recipient experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and drive the global go-to-market strategy for Payouts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, inspire, and lead a high-performing global team responsible for delivering ambitious adoption and revenue targets across Stripe’s Payouts portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Engineering, Sales, Product Marketing, Finance, and other cross-functional teams to align the Payouts GTM strategy and product roadmap with customer needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish Stripe as a strategic partner to businesses seeking to modernize how they move money to customers, sellers, service providers, and other recipients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate effectively at the highest levels of a matrixed organization, bringing together multiple functions to deliver against shared customer and revenue goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the voice of the customer, translating market feedback into actionable insights that inform product strategy, prioritization, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale Payouts business to fastest growing part of Money Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage the most up to date AI capability&#39;s to build and launch AI tools that improve processes, empower the team, and serve as a growth engine to the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a seasoned leader with a proven track record of building teams, delivering outstanding results, and maintaining a long-term, user-first mindset. This leader will thrive amid ambiguity, operate effectively in a high-growth environment, and bring structure to complex problems. Ideal candidates will have deep sales management and leadership experience, domain experience in payments, solid product knowledge, including bringing new products to market, developing go-to-market strategies, scaling technology sales teams, and building trusted relationships with senior customers and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, develop, and lead a global team focused on the Payouts business across AMER, EMEA, APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach the team in developing consultative, solution-oriented sales skills across every stage of the sales cycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create structure and focus for new GTM ideas, use cases, and product sales campaigns. Drive execution, measure results, and make timely recommendations based on performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage day-to-day operations, with a focus on performance against key adoption, pipeline, and revenue metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive revenue growth, increase product adoption and attach rates, and acquire new users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional and account sales leaders to embed Payouts into Stripe’s broader customer strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly in the largest and most strategic opportunities, developing executive relationships and helping the team win and grow complex customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of customers’ funds flows, operational requirements, and regulatory considerations, and translate those needs into compelling Stripe solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with clarity and context, developing a compelling plan aligned with Stripe’s overall direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable sales motions that address the needs of platforms, marketplaces, enterprises, fintechs, and other businesses moving money to third parties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve programs and operating mechanisms by introducing new ideas, sharing best practices, and strengthening Stripe’s customer engagement model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of technology sales experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of people leadership experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in payments, financial services, or money movement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building and scaling global teams that consistently deliver against ambitious goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience bringing new products to market and building repeatable go-to-market motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder’s mindset, with the ability to drive immediate results while establishing the foundations for long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of payments, payouts, treasury, or financial infrastructure and the complex funds flows that support global businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent relationship-building skills, with experience engaging senior executives and customers at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain complex technical, operational, and financial concepts in clear, accessible language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional leadership skills and experience influencing Product, Engineering, Marketing, Finance, and regional Sales organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a deep understanding of how to use data to guide decisions and improve the performance of revenue teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detail-oriented and willing to help a growing team navigate the operational aspects of scaling a global business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think globally, act regionally, and thrive in a multicultural, fast-moving environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience representing an organization publicly and communicating effectively with customers, partners, regulators, the press, and internal employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High energy, a strong work ethic, disciplined execution skills, and a willingness to do what it takes to deliver results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A true team player who puts Stripe and its users first.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Renewals Team partners with account teams to deliver successful contract renewals, protect margins, and grow Stripe’s existing revenue base. We bring commercial expertise to renewal planning and execution, including understanding historical consumption and pricing, positioning customer value, identifying risk, and surfacing upsell and cross-sell opportunities. Our focus is on building a proactive, consistent renewal motion that delivers strong outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the head of EMEA &amp;amp; APAC Renewals, you will lead a distributed team of Renewals Specialists and build regional refinement on a globally consistent model, including driving a proactive renewal motion across the two regions. You will partner with global and regional Sales leaders, Customer Success, Sales Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, and other internal partners to translate global priorities into regional plans, strengthen account-team engagement, and scale how we support renewals across markets and customer segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a commercial leader who combines strong renewal and negotiation judgment with the ability to build high-performing teams and durable operating processes. You will bring clarity in an ambiguous, high-growth environment, turn commercial insights into action, and build trusted partnerships with field leaders at every level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the EMEA and APAC renewals strategy, translating global priorities into regional and segment-specific plans that improve retention, support expansion, and protect sustainable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a proactive renewal motion with Sales and Customer Success, establishing early account planning, clear responsibilities, and consistent specialist partnerships. Enable engagement 12–18 months ahead of renewal where appropriate to the customer segment and deal complexity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted partnerships across account executives and front-line, second-line, and regional sales leaders, ensuring renewal insights inform account and territory plans and translate into clear action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a rigorous regional operating cadence for renewal forecasting, risk inspection, deal strategy, and escalation. Turn portfolio insights into actionable recommendations for field leaders and track follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design team coverage and capacity plans that balance strategic deal support with scalable engagement across the renewal portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, coach, and develop a high-performing team of Renewals Specialists, strengthening negotiation skills, commercial judgment, and strategic account-team partnership while supporting individual career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide strategic guidance on complex renewals and serve as an executive sponsor or senior escalation partner for key customer relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale shared playbooks, systems, and AI-enabled workflows, with clear quality standards, human review, and accountability for adoption and delivery. Maintain a consistent global baseline while adapting execution to regional and segment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface recurring customer and commercial insights to inform improvements to renewal playbooks, tooling, and cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in renewals, customer success, account management, or technology sales, including 5+ years of people leadership, with a demonstrated track record of delivering retention and growth outcomes for existing customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading geographically distributed commercial teams across multiple markets and cultures, with the ability to adapt engagement models to regional and customer-segment needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex renewal or existing-customer negotiations, balancing customer value, retention, expansion, pricing, and sustainable commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build trusted partnerships with senior Sales and Customer Success leaders, align teams around shared priorities, and establish clear responsibilities in a matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building proactive renewal engagement models that bring account teams together early to identify risks, establish account strategies, and uncover expansion opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and operational judgment, including renewal forecasting, performance inspection, and translating customer consumption, pricing, and commercial data into clear recommendations and action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and scaling team coverage, capacity plans, and repeatable operating processes in a high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to recruit, develop, coach, and retain high-performing teams, strengthening both commercial judgment and strategic account-team partnership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate long-term strategy into clear priorities, delivery commitments, and measurable execution, while operating effectively through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills, with the ability to advise senior stakeholders and engage directly in strategic customer negotiations and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a dedicated renewals organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across both EMEA and APAC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments, financial infrastructure, or consumption-based commercial models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying automation and AI to improve commercial workflows, with clear standards for adoption, quality, and human review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk Program Management Office is a global team that leads complex, cross-functional programs across Operations, Product, Engineering, GTM, Partnerships, and Risk teams. We are a team of program management allstars who work to make it as seamless as possible for our users to navigate an evolving regulatory environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are expanding our scope into one of Stripe&#39;s most consequential strategic priorities and launching in new markets. This work is new, fast-moving, and highly ambiguous — and we&#39;re looking for a leader who thrives in exactly that environment. In APAC, our portfolio spans established operations and GTM priorities as well as new licensing, market expansion, and product launches. The work ranges from strengthening and scaling existing programs to building entirely new capabilities from 0→1.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role with the responsibility for defining the vision and scaling the portfolio of Risk Programs across APAC. You will develop and lead a high-performing team, determine where it should focus, and lead a broad mix of work from initial problem framing through implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working as part of the global Risk Programs team, you will represent our team in regional and global forums. You will serve as a trusted partner to senior leaders, build alignment across cross-functional teams, and establish the operating models, playbooks, and programs needed to deliver durable outcomes at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Build and inspire an exceptional team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, lead, and retain a senior program managers, helping them grow into strategic leaders who can shape decisions and mobilize organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a compelling vision for the APAC Risk Programs team and connect its work to Stripe’s topline priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Build from 0&amp;gt;1 a broad and consequential APAC portfolio&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on the region’s most important and ambiguous Risk challenges—developing a point of view, defining the path forward, and leading the work from strategy through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify emerging needs, make thoughtful tradeoffs, and focus the team on the opportunities and problems that matter most&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Deliver Operational and GTM programs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage an existing suite of programs and partner with Operations to forecast demand, manage capacity, and prepare teams to support users as requirements, products, and volumes change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable GTM teams to guide users through complex and evolving compliance programs with clear guidance, effective tools, and strong escalation paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Mobilize Stripe and model execution excellence&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor to senior regional and global leaders, bringing clarity, judgment, and a strong understanding of APAC to important decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build durable partnerships across cross-functional teams to resolve tradeoffs and deliver shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an inspiring people leader and strategic operator who builds trusted relationships and brings out the best in others. You develop a clear point of view amid ambiguity, influence without authority, and turn complex challenges into action.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in strategy and operations, business operations, program management, management consulting, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of people leadership, with a track record of developing and retaining high-performing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a broad portfolio of complex, cross-functional programs from strategy through execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building from 0→1 and strengthening established programs at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication and presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading across cultures, geographies, and time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI tools and examples of using them to improve your own or your team’s effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a leading technology company or consulting firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience working in Singapore and across APAC markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments, fintech, or financial-services experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with licensing, market entry, or global expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s SMB and Commercial Sales organization helps ambitious businesses adopt Stripe’s financial infrastructure and accelerate their growth. The team is responsible for acquiring new users, expanding Stripe’s relationships with existing users, and building durable partnerships across a diverse and fast-moving market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced second-line sales leader to lead our SMB and Commercial business across Southern Europe. You will manage a team of sales managers and Account Executives, set the regional strategy, and be accountable for delivering sustainable growth across multiple countries, customer segments, and sales motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible leadership role requiring strong commercial judgment, operational discipline, and the ability to develop leaders. You will work closely with regional and global Sales leadership and cross-functional partners across Marketing, Partnerships, Product, Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Deal Pricing, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Southern Europe, SMB &amp;amp; Commercial, you will own the strategy, performance, and development of a complex, multi-market sales organization. You will build and lead a high-performing leadership team, translate Stripe’s broader strategy into clear regional priorities, and create the operating environment required to deliver consistent results at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will combine strategic leadership with hands-on involvement in the business. You’ll help your managers raise the performance of their teams, engage directly in the region’s most important opportunities, and represent Southern Europe in regional and global planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the overall strategy and commercial performance of Stripe’s SMB and Commercial business across Southern Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of sales managers and Account Executives across multiple countries, segments, and sales motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build a strong leadership bench by hiring exceptional managers, setting clear expectations, and creating development and succession plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish a clear regional vision and translate it into country, segment, and team-level plans with measurable outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliver ambitious revenue, acquisition, expansion, and activation goals while building a healthy and sustainable long-term business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Create a rigorous operating cadence across forecasting, pipeline generation, territory planning, performance management, and business reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hold managers accountable for team performance while coaching them to diagnose challenges, make sound decisions, and lead independently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify differences across Southern European markets and adapt coverage, capacity, and go-to-market strategies accordingly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build executive relationships with strategic customers and prospects, stepping into critical opportunities and negotiations when leadership involvement can materially improve the outcome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Improve sales productivity and effectiveness by identifying systemic opportunities across process, tooling, enablement, segmentation, and coverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner closely with Marketing, SDR, Product Sales, Solutions Architecture, Customer Success, Partnerships, Deal Pricing, and Operations to deliver an integrated regional strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Represent the needs of Southern European users and sales teams to Stripe’s regional and global leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide clear, evidence-based forecasts and communicate business performance, risks, and opportunities to senior stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Foster an inclusive, high-accountability culture in which managers and sellers can do the best work of their careers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as a senior leader for Stripe in Southern Europe, contributing beyond the immediate sales organization to the health and growth of the broader regional business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an experienced second-line sales leader who has successfully grown a complex business across multiple markets, teams, or customer segments. You know how to lead through managers rather than relying on direct intervention, while remaining close enough to customers and the field to make high-quality decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You can move comfortably between long-term strategy and operational execution. You bring structure to ambiguity, communicate clearly with senior stakeholders, and build organizations that deliver both near-term results and durable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12+ years of relevant sales or commercial experience in technology, financial services, payments, or another fast-growing industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A proven track record as a second-line manager, with meaningful experience leading and developing sales managers as well as Account Executives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated success growing a complex business across multiple countries, customer segments, products, or sales motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience owning a significant regional or multi-market revenue target and delivering sustained performance against ambitious growth goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong record of building high-performing organizations, including hiring and developing leaders, managing performance, and creating succession plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate company strategy into clear regional priorities, operating plans, and measurable team goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience running a disciplined sales organization, including forecasting, pipeline management, capacity planning, territory design, and performance reviews.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong executive presence and a track record of building trusted relationships with senior customer and internal stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Excellent commercial judgment, including the ability to evaluate complex opportunities, allocate resources, and balance short-term execution with long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading through periods of rapid growth, organizational change, or significant ambiguity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to influence across a highly cross-functional and matrixed organization without relying solely on formal authority.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong analytical skills and the ability to use data to identify patterns, challenge assumptions, and make informed decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A commitment to building inclusive teams and creating a culture of high standards, continuous improvement, and shared accountability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience leading SMB and Commercial sales teams with distinct coverage models, sales cycles, and customer needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience managing a geographically distributed organization across several Southern European markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience scaling a business through multiple phases of growth rather than inheriting a mature and stable organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A track record of successfully leading both new-business acquisition and existing-customer expansion motions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, financial infrastructure, SaaS, or another technically complex industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with platform, marketplace, subscription, or usage-based business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working in a global organization and influencing regional and global go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Professional fluency in one or more Southern European languages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience engaging with founders, CEOs, CFOs, and other C-level decision-makers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A strong understanding of the economic, regulatory, and competitive dynamics affecting businesses across Southern Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Specialist Solutions Architects (SSAs) are domain experts aligned to Stripe’s solutions and the customer buying centers they serve. We combine deep product and industry expertise with an understanding of our customers’ most complex business and technical challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The SSA team partners with specialist sellers and the broader pre-sales organization to shape strategic opportunities, develop pipeline, improve revenue attainment, and turn Stripe’s product capabilities into measurable customer outcomes. We also bring field insights to Product and Engineering, helping influence Stripe’s roadmap and go-to-market strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Specialist Solutions Architecture for Revenue in the Americas, you will lead the regional strategy, execution, and growth of the SSA organization supporting Stripe’s Revenue Suite. You will define how Stripe engages customers around billing, monetization, and revenue management—from initial business and technical discovery through solution design, adoption, value realization, and expansion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build and develop a high-performing team of specialist architects and create the operating model, playbooks, and cross-functional partnerships needed to scale the organization. Working closely with Sales, Marketing, Alliances, Professional Services, Support, Product, and Engineering, you will help customers modernize their revenue infrastructure while accelerating adoption and growth for Stripe’s Revenue Suite across the United States, Canada, and Latin America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to shape a growing regional function at an important point in Stripe’s expansion beyond payments. You will connect deep technical expertise to customer value and commercial outcomes while ensuring that the needs of AMER customers influence Stripe’s global product and go-to-market direction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and execute the AMER technical sales strategy for Stripe’s Revenue Suite, aligning specialist coverage, priorities, and investments with regional growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, lead, and develop a high-performing team of specialist solutions architects, establishing clear expectations for technical excellence, customer impact, and commercial contribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales leadership to prioritize resources, shape territory and account strategies, and improve the progression and conversion of complex opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish repeatable engagement models, playbooks, reference architectures, and execution standards for Stripe Billing, Revenue Recognition, and related revenue management solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise executives, developers, architects, finance leaders, and other decision-makers on modernizing their monetization and revenue-management architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide strategic customers from business and technical discovery through solution design, validation, adoption, value realization, and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate recurring customer needs, market signals, and deal friction into actionable insights that influence Product and Engineering priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the Revenue SSA organization in regional and global leadership forums, providing clear perspectives on performance, capacity, risks, customer needs, and growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the Revenue Suite go-to-market approach across AMER, accounting for regional regulatory requirements, business models, and market-specific billing practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong collaboration and knowledge-sharing mechanisms across AMER and global teams to improve consistency, reuse, and execution quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance Stripe’s external thought leadership through executive briefings, industry events, white papers, and reference architectures focused on billing, monetization, and revenue management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in technical sales, solutions architecture, solution consulting, or another customer-facing technical role in enterprise technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and scaling pre-sales or solutions architecture teams, including hiring, managing, coaching, and developing senior individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success partnering with sales leaders on complex, multi-stakeholder enterprise opportunities and connecting technical strategy to commercial outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of enterprise monetization models, including subscription, consumption-based, marketplace, platform, and hybrid models, and how they shape billing and revenue-management requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or advising on complex enterprise architectures and integrations involving financial or revenue-management systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across the United States, Canada, and Latin America, with an ability to adapt leadership and go-to-market approaches across different markets and cultures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication, relationship-building, and cross-functional leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate complex business and technical concepts clearly to audiences ranging from developers and architects to finance leaders and C-level executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel up to 30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, implementing, or advising on enterprise billing and financial transformation programs involving configure-price-quote, order-to-cash, revenue recognition, and ERP systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a regional technical go-to-market function during a period of rapid product or organizational growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of translating field insights into meaningful product, engineering, or go-to-market changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing executive-facing thought leadership, reference architectures, or industry-specific solution strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the regulatory and commercial considerations that affect billing and revenue management across AMER&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solutions Architecture team partners with Stripe’s users to design and build transformative solutions that unlock growth, modernize business models, and shape the future of commerce. We work with executives, product leaders, and engineering teams at the world’s largest and most innovative companies, helping them translate ambitious strategies into scalable solutions on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strategic Accounts Solutions Architecture serves Stripe’s most complex and consequential users. The team combines deep technical expertise, commercial judgment, and customer empathy to solve problems that often have no established playbook. Its work not only helps individual users grow; it also surfaces emerging needs and opportunities that can inform Stripe’s product strategy and create value for users at global scale. These Solution Architects are deeply embedded in these users and are working along as their technical co-founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Head of Strategic Accounts, Solutions Architecture will lead a team of senior architects who are trusted partners to strategic, key, and major accounts. This leader will set the vision for the team, develop exceptional technical talent, and work closely with account leadership to deepen and grow Stripe’s most important relationships. They will also build a strong partnership with Product and Engineering, turning insights from leading-edge customer engagements into the next wave of innovation across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly technical, hands-on leadership role. The successful candidate will be comfortable moving between executive conversations, account strategy, architecture reviews, product discussions, and direct support for the team’s most complex engagements. They will be AI-enabled in how they lead and operate, highly curious about new technologies and business models, and committed to helping their team and Stripe continuously raise the bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision, strategy, and operating model for Strategic Accounts Solutions Architecture, aligning the team’s priorities with Stripe’s user, product, and business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, lead, coach, and retain a world-class team of senior Solutions Architects supporting Stripe’s strategic, key, and major accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account leaders to develop and execute technical account strategies that deepen customer relationships, unlock new use cases, and drive durable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead from the front in the team’s most complex and high-impact engagements, including architecture workshops, executive briefings, solution design, technical evaluations, and critical escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor to senior executives, product leaders, and engineering leaders at the world’s largest and most innovative companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a close, durable partnership with Stripe Product and Engineering teams; synthesize patterns from strategic accounts, influence product priorities, and help translate customer needs into scalable capabilities for all Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create mechanisms for senior architects to share technical insights, reusable patterns, and field learnings across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a culture of technical excellence, curiosity, accountability, experimentation, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion AI-enabled ways of working across the team, using AI to improve insight generation, solution development, team productivity, and the quality and speed of customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop talent through clear expectations, thoughtful coaching, meaningful feedback, and opportunities for architects to expand their technical, commercial, and leadership impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Sales, Customer Success, Professional Services, Technical Account Management, Partnerships, Marketing, Product, and Engineering to deliver cohesive outcomes for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build processes and metrics that measure the team’s impact on customer outcomes, account growth, product influence, and organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate changes in technology, customer needs, competitive dynamics, and industry structure, and translate those signals into action for the team and Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in executive forums, customer business reviews, industry events, and other strategic engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience leading technical pre-sales, solutions architecture, sales engineering, or comparable customer-facing architecture teams aligned to strategic, key, or major accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of hiring, developing, and leading senior technical talent in a complex, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep technical fluency and the ability to remain hands-on—quickly understanding architectures, APIs, data flows, integration patterns, security and reliability considerations, and emerging technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering directly with senior customer executives, product leaders, and engineering leaders on complex, business-critical initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success connecting technical strategy to account growth, customer outcomes, and long-term partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience partnering with Product and Engineering teams to influence roadmaps, shape requirements, and turn customer insights into scalable product innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI-enabled approach to leadership and problem-solving, with practical experience using AI tools to increase the quality, speed, or scale of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional curiosity and learning agility, including a strong desire to explore new technologies, business models, and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence and communication skills, with the ability to make complex technical and business topics clear to audiences at every level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and the ability to lead through ambiguity, balance competing priorities, and make high-quality decisions in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative leadership style and a demonstrated ability to align stakeholders across Sales, Product, Engineering, and other cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel as needed to engage with strategic customers and collaborate with internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, financial infrastructure, fintech space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Management, Support and Services (TAMSS) supports Stripe’s largest, fastest-growing, and most strategically important users through our paid support offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Account Managers serve as trusted advisers to users and account teams. They combine an understanding of a user’s business, Stripe integration, technical architecture, and strategic priorities to improve integration performance and resilience, lead complex engagements, and coordinate Stripe’s response to critical issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The EMEA organization supports direct merchants and platforms across a diverse set of markets, industries, and technical environments. The team partners closely with Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, Support, Professional Services, and Solutions Architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Head of Technical Account Management for Europe, the Middle East, and Africa (EMEA), you will own the regional direction and performance of TAMSS, including teams supporting Stripe’s largest direct merchants and platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll translate Stripe’s global priorities into regional plans that reflect EMEA’s markets, users, and commercial opportunities. Your remit will include user outcomes, service quality, paid support growth, organizational health, and the effective allocation of TAM capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll also serve as an executive partner for strategically important users and represent EMEA on the global TAMSS leadership team. Insights from the region will inform how Stripe develops its products, services, and approach to supporting complex users around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the multi-year strategy and operating model for EMEA TAMSS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and scale a substantial, distributed EMEA Technical Account Management organization, developing a strong management layer across multiple markets, user segments, and technical domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own regional outcomes across paid support growth, service delivery, strategic-user health, technical impact, and organizational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the regional organization and coverage model, including leadership structure, market coverage, capacity allocation, and investment priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with senior leaders across Sales, Customer Success, Product, Engineering, Support, Professional Services, and Solutions Architecture to deliver coordinated outcomes for users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with go-to-market leaders on paid support adoption, renewals, account strategy, staffing, and the sustainable growth of Stripe’s services business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with executive technical and business leaders at Stripe’s largest users, serving as a senior escalation point when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide executive oversight for high-impact user escalations and critical support incidents, ensuring clear ownership, rapid coordination, timely communication, and effective resolution, translating learnings into support experience improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use user feedback, commercial insights, and operational data to identify risks, improve performance, and inform investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn patterns from complex user engagements into improvements to Stripe’s products, services, and operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire and develop managers, set clear expectations, and build a strong succession pipeline for critical leadership roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent EMEA in global TAMSS planning and develop approaches that can be adopted across other regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in technical account management, solutions architecture, customer success, or related user-facing technical functions, including 6+ years managing people and experience managing managers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading substantial, distributed organizations through multiple organizational layers, developing managers, and retaining strong management and technical talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting multi-year strategy and translating it into organizational plans, investment decisions, and measurable user and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building trusted relationships with executive business and technical leaders at large and strategically important users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical and commercial judgment, including the ability to understand complex integrations, assess user and service-delivery risks, and work effectively with Product and Engineering leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success aligning senior leaders with different priorities around a shared strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with P&amp;amp;L management, budget ownership, or operating in a General Manager (GM) capacity for a regional services organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a technical services organization across multiple EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing and delivering paid technical services, support plans, or another recurring services offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial technology, payments, Software as a Service, or API-based products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting global enterprises or platforms with complex technical and operational environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is intended for current high school students graduating in 2027 or later.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier, from solo founders to established enterprises, united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.6% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Though people at Stripe do not tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many, especially the new and innovative ones, we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a small, selective internship for exceptional high school students and recent graduates whose technical work already stands out well beyond what we typically see at this stage. We are not looking for potential or credentials alone. We are looking for students who can show, through what they have built, researched, or contributed, that they are ready to do substantive engineering work with a Stripe team.&lt;br&gt;You will spend 12 consecutive weeks between May and August working in person from Stripe’s San Francisco or Seattle office on a scoped engineering project. You will own a problem end to end with support from your manager and teammates, contribute to Stripe’s codebase, and learn how engineers build reliable systems used by millions of businesses. Recent Stripe intern projects include expanding Payments Foundation Model capabilities to improve generalized anomaly detection, building more approachable fraud controls, creating safer payouts, and developing user-facing solutions that prevent costly pricing mistakes and make merchant checkout setup easier.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work alongside Stripe’s collegiate interns and full-time employees. That means participating in the same team environment, learning how engineers at different stages approach technical decisions, and building relationships across the broader Stripe community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a trainee or classroom-based program. You will receive support from your manager and teammates, but you will be expected to contribute to your team’s work, learn quickly, communicate clearly, ask strong questions, and produce work that holds up under technical review.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As with Stripe’s collegiate internships, strong performance may lead to consideration for future opportunities at Stripe, including full-time employment for interns who meet the relevant eligibility and hiring requirements. Future opportunities are not guaranteed and will depend on individual performance and Stripe’s hiring needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Participate fully in the team you join, including team discussions, decisions, and the technical design process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Write, test, and document software intended for production use by Stripe teams and users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Give and receive technical feedback through code reviews and design discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with engineers and cross-functional partners to seek and incorporate feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Learn unfamiliar systems through independent research and close work with your manager, mentor, teammates, and subject matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Communicate the status of your work clearly, including progress, risks, open questions, and where you need help.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Use current AI development tools thoughtfully while applying rigorous judgment to review, refine, test, and validate outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Look For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t have a test score threshold. We look for people who have already started acting like the engineers and operators we most admire.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ambitious builder: Y&lt;/strong&gt;ou are energized by building solutions without a clear precedent and working through difficult technical problems. You can point to technical work that shows unusual initiative, depth, or originality for someone at your stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rigorous thinker:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;You care about whether your work is correct, not just whether it runs. You test your assumptions, examine edge cases, and can explain the choices you made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Adaptable problem solver:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;You learn quickly, respond well to feedback, and keep making progress when the path is unclear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative teammate:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;You communicate clearly, treat others with kindness, and know when to work independently and when to ask for help.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Currently enrolled in high school, or graduating from high school before the internship begins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Available to work full-time and in person from Stripe’s San Francisco or Seattle office for 12 consecutive weeks during a mutually agreed period between May and August 2027. We cannot accommodate remote participation, a shorter internship, or breaks within the 12-week period.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience programming through independent projects, research, coursework, competitions, open source contributions, a startup, or another setting. We work mostly in Ruby, Java, JavaScript, Go, and Scala. We believe new programming languages can be learned when the fundamentals are strong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Evidence of exceptional technical achievement for your stage. This could include a product or system you built, a substantial open source contribution, original research, meaningful work at a startup, advanced competition performance, or another body of work that demonstrates comparable depth and ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to explain your individual contribution to the work you submit, including the problem, technical decisions, tradeoffs, testing, feedback, and what you would improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience working with others on a technical project and incorporating feedback from peers, mentors, teachers, users, or collaborators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar systems through independent research and work with a mentor or subject matter expert.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Clear written and verbal communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to meet the employment eligibility, minimum age, and documentation requirements for the role’s location by the internship start date. Final contract language is subject to Legal review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;One or more areas of deeper technical knowledge, such as frontend, backend, infrastructure, data, machine learning, security, or developer tools, balanced with strong general programming fundamentals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience writing high-quality pull requests, tests, technical documentation, or design notes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity navigating an unfamiliar codebase or contributing to a multi-person project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A record of sustained technical work over time, not only one-time awards or credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Curiosity about how businesses operate and how software can improve the conditions for economic growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What to submit&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A resume or short summary of your technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;In that summary please include one or two examples of your strongest work, such as a repository, live product, technical paper, research abstract, competition submission, or project write-up. Private work may be described without sharing confidential material.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;For each example, a short explanation of the problem, what you personally contributed, the hardest technical decision, how you tested the work, and what you learned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Optional: High school transcript, standardized test scores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Please note that this is an hourly position with a pay rate of $60 per hour.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’d be joining the Professional Services team. Our team’s mission is to empower every Stripe user to achieve maximum value from their investment quickly and confidently. Our team helps Stripe increase the GDP of the internet by supporting the success of our large, intricate Stripe implementations. This involves guiding users through their integration process, project planning, coordinating with stakeholders, handling deliverables, meeting key timelines, and educating our users about the maximum potential they can achieve with Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Implementation Consultant at Stripe, you are the driving force behind these strategic implementations. Your role is key in leading them through the integration process, turning them into long-term transacting Stripe users. Our team’s core objective is to provide an efficient, seamless transition for our clients, assuring top-notch user satisfaction and relationship management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Implementation Consultant, you will be managing the full onboarding cycle for mid-market and enterprise companies from contract signing through launch. You will proactively develop and manage integration architecture, change management strategy, and timelines. You will be expected to collaborate across departments, including Sales, Technical Services, Product, and Engineering, to ensure a successful transition for our clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full onboarding cycle for mid-market and enterprise companies from contract signing through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, manage, and implement a customer’s integration architecture, change management strategy, and timeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with other Sales and Technical Services teams to improve the overall Stripe user journey.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to help drive product strategy for large users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teammates on strategic projects that improve and scale our implementation process and team operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp; The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience working with strategic customers on technology solutions, with a track record of top performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex business requirements and craft tailored solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quick learner with the ability to explain technical concepts to Stripe’s largest customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven project management skills and strong critical thinking abilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying and solving internal process inefficiencies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of APIs&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

