&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Press publishes ideas for progress in technology, science, and economics because we believe that for many of the most significant breakthroughs in each of these categories, the key ingredient is ideas. The Stripe Press team is effectively a startup within Stripe; we have an unusual amount of autonomy and the trust of Stripe’s leadership team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our bar for publishing is high, and our list is small—by design. We’d rather publish fewer books than publish books we’re not passionate about and that we don’t think will challenge and galvanize our audience, which is global, fiercely curious, and shares our exacting standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Press is seeking a Managing Editor to own the editorial development and execution of its publishing program. You will guide intellectually ambitious nonfiction from acquisition through final proofs and production-ready handoff, upholding Press’s standards for rigor, clarity, accuracy, and editorial distinction.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role calls for exceptional editorial judgment and project management skills. You will work closely with Stripe Press’s editors, production manager, designers, authors, agents, and external specialists. You will also help build the systems and contributor network needed to support a growing list without compromising quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the editorial path of every Stripe Press book from acquisition through final proofs and handoff to production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage editorial schedules spanning manuscript delivery, editorial review, revision, copyediting, fact-checking, permissions, indexing, proofreading, and final approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate manuscripts for structure, argument, clarity, pacing, voice, evidence, and accessibility, ensuring that complex ideas remain accurate and intellectually substantive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish clear expectations with authors and provide candid, actionable guidance throughout development. Provide direct developmental or line-editing support when a project requires senior intervention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the appropriate editorial and verification process for each book, including when to commission technical, legal, or other specialist review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, commission, and supervise a trusted network of developmental editors, line editors, copyeditors, fact-checkers, proofreaders, indexers, typesetters, and specialist reviewers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give final editorial approval before manuscripts enter production, and remain responsible for editorial decisions and author review through the proof stages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the Stripe Press house style and create clear, repeatable workflows and handoffs across editorial and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have significant experience managing complex nonfiction books at a trade, academic, journalistic, or ideas-focused publishing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate exceptional editorial judgment across structure, argument, prose, evidence, and authorial voice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with technical, scientific, economic, historical, or otherwise research-intensive nonfiction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have deep knowledge of developmental editing, line editing, copyediting, fact-checking, permissions, proofreading, and editorial-production workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are an exceptional project manager, capable of coordinating multiple complex projects and timelines with a high degree of precision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy operating in a small, ambitious organization where systems are still being built, and you share Stripe Press’s appetite for ideas that can improve how people understand and shape the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have helped launch or materially scale a publishing program, list, or imprint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have developed editorial standards, tools, or workflows that improved quality and execution in a growing organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our EMEA Marketing team is a dynamic, fast-growing group that loves turning customers into enthusiastic Stripe advocates. We work hand-in-hand with our Sales team to build demand, help users get the most out of our products, and craft marketing plans that truly resonate with local audiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the DACH region, our team partners with some of the most ambitious innovators across Germany, Austria, and Switzerland—brands like DeepL, refurbed, N26, and Nestlé. We help them use Stripe’s financial infrastructure to unlock new revenue, navigate local complexities, and scale globally. What we learn from these relationships directly influences how Stripe builds its products. The opportunity in this region is massive. We’re tackling it as a diverse, international team that thrives on collaboration, bold innovation, and genuine curiosity. If you love to learn and want to make a meaningful impact, we&#39;d love to have you join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll lead marketing strategy and plan execution for the DACH region and serve as the primary Marketing partner on the DACH Leadership Team. You’ll set the regional strategy and investment plan, with Germany as the main market, and shape priorities across Austria and Switzerland. You’ll be accountable for demand, pipeline, customer advocacy, and Stripe’s long-term market position in the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior individual contributor, you will align regional and global cross-functional teams around shared priorities, secure the necessary resources, and navigate trade-offs between global strategies and local market needs. You will directly lead high-priority initiatives across the region.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leveraging deep market and account insights, you will identify key growth opportunities across target industries and audiences. In close partnership with Sales, you will build tailored programs for strategic accounts and high-potential prospects aligned with their business models, technical environments, and commercial objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the integrated DACH marketing strategy, turning business goals, market dynamics, and competitive context into clear priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with DACH GTM leadership, Sales, Sales Development, and Partnerships to set shared priorities, join business and pipeline reviews, and focus investment on the highest-value opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and oversee a full-funnel DACH marketing plan across brand, demand generation, account-based marketing, pipeline acceleration, executive engagement, and customer advocacy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop industry and account programs for strategic customers and high-potential prospects, helping Sales engage the right stakeholders with relevant messages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring together EMEA and global teams, including Demand Generation and Product Marketing, to deliver the DACH plan, working with Sales, Product, Solutions Engineering, Partnerships, and Communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build Stripe’s brand and local presence in DACH through regional customer stories, partner programs, and executive, industry, and ecosystem engagement, including activation around Stripe flagship and third-party events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own metrics across demand, pipeline, opportunity progression, priority-account engagement, and return on investment. Use results to improve programs and stop or change those that aren’t delivering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent DACH across EMEA and global marketing teams, bringing market insight into planning and sharing successful programs across markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re an experienced B2B marketer who has owned a country, regional, or similarly broad marketing strategy. You can set direction, make investment trade-offs, and work credibly with senior Sales and GTM leaders. You stay close enough to execution to turn the strategy into commercial results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. If you meet them, we encourage you to apply. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of B2B marketing experience, including ownership of planning and investment for a country, region, or comparably broad portfolio in enterprise technology or another complex B2B environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the German and wider DACH business and technology markets, including enterprise buying dynamics and local ecosystems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven record of partnering with senior Sales and GTM leaders and aligning cross-functional teams without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading integrated programs across several marketing disciplines, drawing on regional and global specialist teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership of annual budgets and multi-program portfolios, with evidence of using commercial results to prioritize investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in German and English, with the ability to explain technical concepts and present complex strategies to executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and comfort making decisions when priorities compete or information is incomplete.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, commerce, B2B cloud services, or another complex and highly competitive technology category.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging enterprise executives and buying groups across Finance, Treasury, Technology, Product, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of building local brand relevance, thought leadership, customer advocacy, or influence strategies—not only demand-generation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a marketing approach where the playbook, resources, or route to impact was still taking shape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Stripe user base and global footprint grow dramatically, we have distinctly unique support problems resulting from both our type of scale and the type of businesses we partner with. The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand the Stripe portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an independent business, startup, SMB, or enterprise, and our mission is to provide all Stripe users with the best support experience possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll recruit, manage, and develop a group of Marketing Operations Associates and team leads that are focused on delivering repeatable, measurable programs and campaigns targeted on spend optimization, producing highly qualified leads, improving the customer experience, and increasing retention. You&#39;ll lead the team supporting the Stripe Marketing Operations and are comfortable jumping in to perform production duties, especially in times of need. You&#39;ll cultivate the happiness of your team members while guiding them to excel, through feedback, coaching, mentoring, and advocacy within the organization. This means helping to set team goals and using metrics to efficiently measure and guide team performance in pursuit of those goals. You&#39;ll have a strong operations mindset, move quickly, and be passionate about delivering an incredible user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, lead, develop, and coach a high-performing team of Marketing Operations Associates and Campaign Producers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global counterparts in EMEA and AMER, necessitating flexible scheduling for cross-regional alignment on email marketing success, best practices, process, workflows, policies, execution, and enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project manage marketing campaign production across the globe, including managing handoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Marketo workflows, performance marketing operations, and event analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure reportability of core operations cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Marketing Operations processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years relevant work experience in Marketing Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in leading teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of hands-on experience in Marketo (or similar) with a deep understanding of campaign architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading, mentoring, managing, and developing a team of Marketing Operations Campaign Producers responsible for delivering high-quality work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building strong cross-functional partnerships with Marketing and internal technical support teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading end-to-end execution of projects and programs that have significantly improved operations and delivered quantifiable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with a precise talent for articulating challenges, generating insights, and translating them into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid analytical skills and a strong understanding of technical concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A startup mentality with a bias to action and the ability to flex in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience and desire for contributing to developing business infrastructure and aggressively scaling a high-growth business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at highly dynamic, high-growth tech companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great service mentality and track record of building positive relationships with peers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

