&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consumer Support team partners closely with Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Regulatory, Localisation, Operations Technology, and other Operations teams to build and scale support for Link and Crypto Onramp products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Consumer Support team, you will develop a deep understanding of Stripe’s consumer product suite and identify opportunities to resolve consumer pain points at scale. You will influence Product and Engineering roadmaps, shape support strategies, and build scalable operations for new and existing consumer products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a highly visible, senior individual contributor (IC) role. While you will influence senior leadership and set strategic direction, you are also the primary driver of execution. You will need to zoom out to design the long-term vision, and zoom in to manage the details—building templates, tracking deliverables, writing documentation, and directly unblocking cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or partner with cross-functional teams, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Support, Operations Technology, and Vendor Management, to define operational requirements for new Link, Stripe Managed Payment, and Crypto Onramp products, features, and experiments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to build the infrastructure and tooling required to launch and scale consumer operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the voice of the consumer and advocate for product improvements that address recurring pain points and their root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop support strategies that improve the consumer experience and increase adoption of effective self-service tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and deliver operational improvements that enable Consumer Support to scale efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to surface insights, prioritize opportunities, and measure the impact of operational and product changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a high-quality consumer experience while meeting applicable local, consumer-protection, and regulatory requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s degree in business, management, economics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategy and operations, consulting, program management, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in highly cross-functional roles spanning strategy, analysis, and operations in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program management skills, including experience leading complex programs from strategy through execution and delivering measurable business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and critical-thinking skills, with the ability to derive insights from data and translate them into action&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain complex topics clearly to leaders and partners across Product, Engineering, and Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience aligning stakeholders with different priorities and driving commitment toward shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to bring structure to complex, ambiguous problems and solve them using first-principles thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to execute independently with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in SQL, including writing queries and analysing large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI tools to improve analysis, automate workflows, or increase team efficiency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe’s user base and global footprint grows dramatically, we have distinctly unique support problems resulting from both our type of scale and the type of businesses we partner with. The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) strategy will provide operational leverage and expand Stripe’s portfolio of operational capabilities to support the scaled needs for external users and internal Stripe teams. We strive to deliver frictionless experiences for all of our users, whether they are an Independent Business, Startup, SMB, or Enterprise and our mission is to provide all Stripe Users with the best support experience possible.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will manage a team of Seller Systems Operations Associates in a player-coach capacity. You’ll be accountable for your team’s operational performance, development, and engagement, while working closely with global operations specialists, business process owners, and cross-functional partners to improve workflows and user experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the day-to-day operational performance of a team of Associates, including quality, productivity, service-level, and other team goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear expectations, priorities, and performance goals for individuals and the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage team capacity, scheduling, and work allocation to ensure critical workflows are covered and work is completed accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Associates on troubleshooting, process knowledge, communication, and sound judgment in resolving user issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold regular development conversations and provide timely, constructive feedback that supports growth and career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete performance reviews and address performance concerns in partnership with your manager and People team partners, as appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a collaborative, inclusive team environment where Associates can raise risks, share ideas, and learn from one another.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an escalation point for complex operational or user issues, using sound judgment to resolve issues or route them to the right partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with global operations specialists and business process owners to run critical Internal Systems workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring issues, process gaps, and manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead or contribute to improvements that increase quality, reduce effort, and improve the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use operational data and team insights to surface trends, risks, and opportunities to relevant stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with cross-functional teams to improve product offerings, processes, tools, and user-facing communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support hiring, onboarding, training, and ramping of new team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help build the operating culture, team practices, and capabilities of Stripe Delivery Centers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience leading, supervising, or formally mentoring an operations, support, or user-facing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9+ years of experience in customer support, technical support, operations, or another internal or external user-facing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing operational work against defined quality, productivity, or service-level goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to give clear, constructive feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching others and supporting their professional development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL skills and experience working with API integrations, including diagnosing implementation issues, interpreting technical documentation, and guiding teams through ambiguous customer or system problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical thinking and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify root causes and make practical improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to prioritize effectively and make sound decisions in a fast-moving, structured environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A process-oriented mindset and a track record of improving workflows, reducing manual effort, or improving user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working effectively with cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first mindset and interest in learning technical products, systems, and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work from the Bengaluru office in night shift&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational data to manage performance, identify trends, and prioritize improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hiring, onboarding, workforce planning, or scheduling for an operations team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with global teams across time zones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead&lt;/strong&gt; based in Singapore to own Stripe’s Global Partnerships strategy and execution across SE Asia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the regional Global Partnerships Lead, you will own Stripe’s most important in-market relationships across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners. You will set the partnership strategy for the region; identify, prioritize, and develop new opportunities; lead complex negotiations; and ensure partnerships deliver durable commercial, product, and expansion outcomes for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a leadership role at the intersection of product strategy, market expansion, and commercial execution. You will serve as Stripe’s senior partnership representative for the region, build trusted executive relationships with ecosystem partners, and lead alignment across Product, Engineering, Go-to-Market, Legal, Risk, Compliance, Finance, Treasury, and Operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Stripe’s &lt;strong&gt;Global Partnerships Lead for SE Asia Expansion&lt;/strong&gt;, with end-to-end accountability for the regional partnership portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and execute the regional strategy across local payment methods, financial partners, card networks, banks, and expansion partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead Stripe’s senior external relationships in the region, building alignment and representing Stripe’s strategic priorities with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own partnership opportunities from market assessment and strategy through negotiation, contracting, onboarding, launch, governance, and performance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional expansion-partnership strategy and execution, coordinating the partnerships required to establish, operate, and scale Stripe in-market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate market intelligence, partner priorities, and ecosystem developments into clear recommendations for Stripe’s product and business strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional decision-making on commercial, product, operational, regulatory, and technical dependencies related to regional partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and manage partner-performance metrics, including commercial outcomes, product adoption, operational health, and strategic progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate and manage partnership risks, escalations, and trade-offs, ensuring sustained executive alignment internally and externally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, strategy, financial services, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in payments, fintech, e-commerce, banking, card networks, local payment methods, or adjacent financial-services sectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading complex, strategic commercial negotiations with senior external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of the payments and financial-partnership landscape in SE Asia, including relevant market dynamics and business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and English executive communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to develop a clear point of view amid ambiguity, influence without authority, and drive decisions across complex internal and external stakeholder groups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with product and engineering organizations on partnerships with meaningful technical, operational, and regulatory dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate autonomously while balancing multiple high-priority initiatives and long-term strategic relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a regional or multi-market portfolio of payments or financial-infrastructure partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting market-entry, expansion, licensing, or ecosystem-development initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Existing senior relationships across banks, networks, payment-method providers, fintechs, or other relevant ecosystem partners in the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced, global technology company with cross-functional product, commercial, and regulatory stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Alliances and Channels (A&amp;amp;C) team builds and scales the partner ecosystem that powers Stripe&#39;s growth. We work with SaaS platforms, technology partners, and services partners to drive merchant acquisition and expand Stripe&#39;s reach across markets. In LATAM, partners are a the primary growth engine — and this role sits at the center of that motion.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of partner development and channel sales. You&#39;ll own the full lifecycle of SaaS platform partnerships across LATAM — recruiting and developing vertical platforms that embed Stripe into their products, then activating and growing those relationships into meaningful contributors to regional revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working closely with Stripe Account Executives, you&#39;ll drive joint go-to-market motions, identify high-value opportunities within your partner portfolio, and own the co-sell pipeline from sourcing through to close. Expect a mix of partner engagement (enablement, solution development, business reviews), sales engagement (opportunity qualification and pipeline progression), and direct user engagement (prospecting, activation).This role requires a high level of dynamism and the ability to adapt to evolving business strategies and changing conditions. We are looking for someone who feels comfortable working in ambiguity and who can quickly adjust to new priorities, changes, and strategic shifts as the business evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, recruit, and develop a portfolio of SaaS platform partners and community services partners across LATAM, with a primary focus on Mexico and support for Brazilian partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full partner lifecycle — from first contact through onboarding, enablement, activation, and long-term growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive joint go-to-market and co-selling initiatives with your partner portfolio; own forecasting across Partner Sourced Opportunities, Co-Sell, and Product Live metrics&lt;/li&gt;
