&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Partnerships team sits within the Global Partnerships organization and is a key component of our success. Our team is responsible for developing and managing relationships with the global and regional banks that enable the Stripe product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional product partnership initiatives across existing products and early-stage &quot;up the stack&quot; financial products. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and are essential for us to offer products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Note: This is not a commercial sales position - for those opportunities, see our Business Development roles&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager to help manage out portfolio of international banks. You&#39;ll be responsible for developing and executing the multi-year, global strategies for building our relationships across many of our most important banking partners. You&#39;ll focus on designing, scaling, and continuously improving mechanisms to deepen relationships with our partners, as well as highly impactful programs key to differentiating Stripe. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders (including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, etc.), and with the banking partners&#39; executive teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The successful candidate will have a demonstrated ability to manage and develop partners, think strategically and apply diagnostic thinking to business, product, and technical challenges, and earn trust with and influence others. A high-agency attitude, the ability to raise expectations in changing environments, and a drive to create impact through ownership are all important in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the go-to-partner strategy and execute on our most ambitious company-bending, bank-network-driven projects that are global and cross-border in nature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the banking partner plans, the overall economics, day-to-day operational excellence, and be responsible for driving the partnerships to successful outcomes for Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage banking, treasury, and payments industry knowledge to craft thoughtful partnership and product strategies with transaction banks, lenders, capital markets, central banks, and schemes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate, in partnership with Product, to execute deals supporting that strategy and help ensure a proper execution plan is in place&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage significant industry experience to educate and help internal teams compose our holistic bank-led strategy and to advance that strategy with banking partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;9+ years of relevant experience in banking or fintech, including direct ownership of banking partnerships supporting collections, payouts, stored value, or embedded financial products. This is a specialised banking-infrastructure partnerships role, rather than a general fintech business-development role. The strongest candidates will combine commercial bank-partner ownership with evidence that they have taken a payments capability into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced knowledge of the banking and clearing landscape across multiple geographies with specific focus on transaction banking, e-money, safeguarding, multi-currency, and cross-border payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience building proprietary global collection and payout networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of working in a product-centric environment with significant internal and external dependencies across product, engineering, legal, sales, risk, and compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad and deep experience executing industry-wide partnership strategies to build innovative product experiences and go-to-market models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link Partnerships team sources, develops, and manages relationships with the payments ecosystem partners that power Link, Stripe&#39;s consumer wallet. Our team drives the growth and utility of Link by building partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, crypto providers, and emerging commerce platforms. We execute on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives that expand Link&#39;s acceptance, improve performance, and enable new payment experiences—including agentic commerce. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Partner Development Manager who builds and manages Link&#39;s payments partnerships with card networks, card issuers, local payment method providers, and crypto and stablecoin providers. You&#39;ll own the strategy and execution of partnerships that expand Link&#39;s payment capabilities, improve transaction performance, and position Link as the default payments layer for agentic commerce. You&#39;ll negotiate commercial agreements, drive technical integrations, and shape Link&#39;s payments roadmap in collaboration with these partners. As part of these efforts, you&#39;ll collaborate closely with cross-functional stakeholders, including Product, Engineering, Legal, Finance, Risk, and others. You&#39;ll also lead relationship management and partner closely with external partners&#39; executive leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and execute Link&#39;s payments partnership strategy across card networks, card issuers, local payment methods, and crypto and stablecoins&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Negotiate and manage commercial agreements with payment partners that expand Link&#39;s acceptance footprint, improve authorization rates, and unlock new payment capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the card network and issuer landscape—including scheme rules, tokenization frameworks, authentication protocols, and competitive dynamics—to inform partnership strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive partnerships that enable Link to serve as the payments layer for agentic commerce, working with networks and issuers to establish rules, liability frameworks, and technical standards for agent-initiated transactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather inputs from and coordinate with internal cross-functional stakeholders (including product, risk, compliance, engineering, and security) to drive creation and execution of partner strategy including our global LPM roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Product and Engineering to define requirements and shape Link&#39;s payments product roadmap based on partner capabilities and market opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify partner stakeholders who will champion Stripe, educate them about Link&#39;s value proposition, and build alignment between Stripe and our partners&#39; executive teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and effectively analyze new partnership opportunities, ultimately making recommendations to relevant decision makers and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exhibit an operationally focused mindset, with an ability to lead teams through complex relationship management activities by setting a clear vision and running tight processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You&#39;re a skilled dealmaker and a strategist by nature. You understand how to work closely with Product and Engineering teams and can formulate partner strategies that drive tangible and measurable results. You&#39;re energized by the intersection of payments infrastructure and emerging commerce models, and you see the opportunity to define how payments work in an agentic world.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in partnerships, business development, corporate development, or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in or working closely with card networks, card issuers, digital wallets, or payments infrastructure providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with partners, including scaling such deals across multiple partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills, in both verbal and written form, and ability to influence stakeholders across a wide variety of functions, including at executive levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, especially an ability to understand product strategy and use this understanding to define requirements for scaling products through partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing partnership strategies and identifying, sourcing, and analyzing new partnership opportunities in greenfield segments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong agency, can handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrives on a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with card scheme rules, tokenization (network tokens, device tokens), authentication frameworks (3DS, SCA), and issuer-side authorization optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with emerging payment models such as agentic commerce, embedded payments, or programmable payment flows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new partnership category or vertical from zero—defining the strategy, establishing first partnerships, and scaling the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Payments Partnerships team develops and manages relationships with large payment method and ecosystem partners that enable Stripe’s product strategy and deliver new capabilities to Stripe users. Our team executes on high-impact, cross-functional initiatives across new products, geographic expansion, user advocacy, and policy. These partnerships have a significant impact on Stripe and the products used by millions of our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow priority payment-method partnerships, with a focus on strategic wallets, buy now, pay later (BNPL) providers, and related payment partners. You will manage day-to-day partner relationships, lead defined commercial and product initiatives, and work across Stripe to increase payment-method adoption and deliver better experiences for users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires sound commercial judgment, a structured approach to execution, and the ability to bring together internal and external stakeholders with different priorities. You will develop deep expertise in your partners and the payment-method ecosystem, using that context to identify opportunities, inform Stripe’s decisions, and execute initiatives that support Stripe’s product and business goals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage one or more priority payment-method partnerships, driving the execution of joint initiatives and launching new offerings that benefit Stripe users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage internal and external stakeholders with varying priorities, driving alignment on shared goals and ensuring structured partner and deal management rooted in clear milestones, performance metrics, and opportunities of mutual interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow Stripe’s relationships with partners, including their senior executives and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather input from and coordinate with cross-functional stakeholders, including Risk, Legal, Product, and Engineering, to execute deals and related partner product initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring an operationally focused mindset to relationship management, setting clear goals, running tight processes, and proactively identifying opportunities to improve execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in strategic partnerships or business development, including 3+ years working in payments, fintech, or financial institutions, and 3+ years of experience negotiating commercial deals with financial and technology institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading commercial discussions or negotiations using established deal strategies and frameworks, with sound judgment about trade-offs and when to escalate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning partner relationships, channel or distribution initiatives, and/or cross-functional commercial programs from planning through execution, and working in a product-centric environment with meaningful internal and external dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take initiative, handle ambiguity in a fast-moving organization, and thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility; strong verbal and written communication skills; and the ability to influence internal and external stakeholders across a wide variety of functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical acumen, including the ability to understand Stripe’s product portfolio and strategy and use this understanding to define requirements with partners and evaluate new partnership opportunities, along with interest in and intellectual curiosity about payments, economic infrastructure, and Stripe’s partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, payment methods, wallets, BNPL, or financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Worldwide Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team is responsible for developing and managing a global community of partners that helps ambitious businesses with industry-leading payments and financial infrastructure solutions and services. These partnerships provide Stripe with the opportunity to unlock our market opportunity, supporting us in accelerating our users growth across all market segments from Startup to Enterprise companies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Partner Development Manager to own and grow existing, mature, strategic systems integrator (SI) partnerships across EMEA. The focus is on deepening established relationships and improving joint commercial outcomes, rather than incubating or building new partnerships.&amp;nbsp;You’ll manage a defined portfolio of large SI organizations, owning each partnership end to end. You’ll engage senior commercial and technical stakeholders, align on shared priorities, and turn joint partner plans into measurable pipeline and revenue.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a partner relationship and revenue-generating role. You’ll work closely with regional sales teams and partner stakeholders on joint account planning and customer engagements. You’ll also coordinate with partner solution engineering, marketing, and program teams to strengthen partner capabilities and grow their Stripe practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a defined portfolio of existing, mature, strategic SI partnerships end to end, from joint planning and stakeholder alignment through execution and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain relationships with senior commercial and technical stakeholders across large partner organizations, including alliance, sales, practice, and delivery leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute joint partner plans with clear commercial priorities, owners, and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Stripe’s enterprise sales teams and partner account teams on account mapping, opportunity identification, and co-selling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow partner-sourced and partner-influenced pipeline, track progress, and coordinate the teams needed to move joint opportunities forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Partner Solution Engineering to deepen partners’ technical capabilities, support training and certification, and strengthen their ability to deliver Stripe solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate targeted campaigns, events, and enablement with marketing and program teams to support joint commercial priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular partner business reviews, agree on actions with senior stakeholders, and follow through on delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to expand established partnerships across accounts, practices, and EMEA markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report clearly on partnership performance, pipeline, risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8 years+ Experience in partnerships, sales, or business development within a technology or financial services organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing established SI or consulting partnerships, with an understanding of how these organizations sell and deliver services to enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing existing partnerships and progressing commercial opportunities against defined goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to own partner relationships end to end, coordinating internal and partner teams to deliver agreed outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging senior commercial and technical stakeholders within large, complex organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in joint account planning, pipeline development, or enterprise sales engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand customer needs and explain how a joint solution addresses them, working with technical specialists when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organization and follow-through, with the ability to manage multiple partner initiatives and work through ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to travel for partner and customer engagements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience in payments, financial infrastructure, or enterprise technology transformation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Partner Marketing team extends Stripe’s marketing reach to customers and prospects by educating, engaging and enabling partners, globally, to build market awareness and generate demand for their Stripe solutions and services. We recruit prospective partners and support the on-boarding and growth of existing partners as they build, launch, market, and scale business through the Stripe Partner Ecosystem and the Stripe platform. We partner closely with our global partnerships, GTM partners, marketing, and product teams and serve many different partner types.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced, strategic, and results-oriented marketing leader to own Stripe’s global partner marketing strategy for Services partners—including GSIs—and Technology/ISV partners. You’ll lead a global team, define the multi-year operating and investment model, build influential relationships with partner and Stripe leaders, and scale programs that drive partner-sourced and partner-attached pipeline, customer activation, and product adoption. This role requires setting a clear long-term direction while leading through others and using performance insights to focus the organization on its highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the multi-year vision and global strategy for Services, GSI, and Technology/ISV partner marketing, translating Stripe’s company, marketing, and partnerships priorities into an operating model, investment strategy, and measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing global team of four Partner Marketing professionals across APAC, AMER, and EMEA. Establish clear accountability, build organizational capability, evolve the team as business needs change, and ensure agencies and vendors extend the team effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with partner CMOs and senior Stripe leaders. Develop joint strategies with priority partners and align global and regional teams around shared priorities, investments, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a portfolio of differentiated programs for strategic partners and scalable programs for the broader ecosystem. Integrate partners into Stripe campaigns, regional initiatives, co-sell motions, events, content, and enablement to drive pipeline, activation, and product adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape joint value propositions, messaging, and customer evidence, and turn successful programs into reusable playbooks that can scale across partners and regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish governance for market development funds and other investments, alongside the performance framework, dashboards, and business-review cadence. Use data and financial insight to assess impact, address underperformance, and reallocate resources toward the strongest opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of relevant B2B marketing experience, including substantial experience in partner, ecosystem, channel, or alliances marketing and a strong understanding of partner business models and indirect GTM motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting and leading global marketing strategy across regions, translating company priorities into long-term plans, scalable operating models, and measurable business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building, leading, and developing a distributed team of experienced marketers, including setting direction and accountability, coaching talent, and evolving organizational capabilities through change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead complex cross-functional initiatives with a high degree of autonomy, build trusted relationships with partner and internal executives, and align senior stakeholders without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success delivering measurable partner-marketing outcomes and using analytical and financial judgment to manage significant budgets or market development funds, evaluate ROI, and make portfolio trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the judgment to simplify complex issues, articulate a compelling vision, and turn strategy and performance insights into clear executive recommendations and action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing marketing strategies for Services, GSI, Technology, or ISV partners in a global, high-growth technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, enterprise software, or an adjacent industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Breadth across partner marketing and adjacent disciplines such as demand generation, product marketing, field marketing, or integrated campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing agencies or vendors across markets and holding them accountable for quality and results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;As a member of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team, you will be responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe’s partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education and enablement with our partner organization. The right candidate will be a critical technical liaison to the Stripe Partner Development Manager. This will involve creating comprehensive technical business plans for Partners, including identifying, incubating and bringing to market service/solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solution Architect is someone who is intellectually curious, motivated to win, open and entrepreneurial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, PSAs build highly consultative trusted relationships with executives and technical decision makers in the customer’s organisation to provide business and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges. We architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with key partners to build out their Stripe capabilities and solutions to grow their business and drive non-linear growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute enablement plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be at the forefront of technical discussions &amp;amp; solution deep-dives with partners on the value Stripe can provide to their clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with CTOs, engineering &amp;amp; other technical leads at key partners to share technology roadmaps, demonstrate the latest innovations, and define a solution strategy to expand the partnership revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate success internally through QBRs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight, guidance, and assistance during the partners sales process to ensure mutual success in joint opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate the Stripe sales team on key partner solutions and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for key partners within specific sales regions and identify areas for sales partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on technical content (sample code, demos, etc.) to show partners how to implement specific use cases or best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Partner-focused guidance on Stripe’s product through feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role such as solution consultant, solutions architect, sales engineer, for a global software enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical acumen in API integrations, SaaS platforms, and enterprise architectures, with particular emphasis on order-to-cash processes and billing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience with subscription, billing, and payment solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of financial infrastructure industry trends and emerging technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience co-selling and co-solutioning with go-to-market partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer meetings to gain strategic footing and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle and API architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills, presentation skills, and confidence in explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn Stripe solutions such as Payments, Billing, Connect, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand how a wide variety of applications such as ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax and legacy systems interact with each other in an enterprise technology ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple strategic opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and creative thinker who can proactively identify challenges and maintain a positive approach when facing difficult obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team, you will be responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe’s partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education and enablement with our partner organisation. The right candidate will be a critical technical liaison to the Stripe Partner Development Manager. This will involve creating comprehensive technical business plans for Partners, including identifying, incubating and bringing to market service/solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solution Architect is someone who is intellectually curious, motivated to win, open and entrepreneurial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of the team, PSAs build highly consultative trusted relationships with executives and technical decision makers in the customer’s organisation to provide business and technical thought leadership, and become a trusted advisor in solving mission-critical business challenges. We architect business models with them so they can drive new monetization opportunities and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with key partners in Japan to build out their Stripe capabilities and solutions to grow their business and drive non-linear growth in Stripe’s Japan business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute enablement plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be at the forefront of technical discussions &amp;amp; solution deep-dives with partners on the value Stripe can provide to their clients&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with CTOs, engineering &amp;amp; other technical leads at key partners to share technology roadmaps, demonstrate the latest innovations, and define a solution strategy to expand the partnership revenue&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate success internally through QBRs, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide oversight, guidance, and assistance during the partners sales process to ensure mutual success in joint opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educate the Stripe sales team on key partner solutions and capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as an advocate for key partners within specific sales regions and identify areas for sales partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide thought leadership via webinars and conferences across the financial and AI industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate on technical content (sample code, demos, etc.) to show partners how to implement specific use cases or best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Partner-focused guidance on Stripe’s product through feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in a similar customer-facing engineering role such as solution consultant, solutions architect, sales engineer, for a global software enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent English and Japanese proficiency and the position would require you to communication with both English speaking and Japanese speaking stakeholders&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customers and partners such as GSI and SI’s in the Japan region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive engagement skills and presence, with an ability to establish strong relationships with key decision makers and build credibility at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective group-facilitation skills and confidence in proposing and leading customer meetings to gain strategic footing and pursue opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an advanced level of AI Fluency, including but not limited to Agentic commerce and Agents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of the software development lifecycle and API architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding spoken and written communication skills, presentation skills, and confidence in explaining complex concepts to both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn Stripe solutions such as Payments, Billing, Connect, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand how a wide variety of applications such as ERP, CRM, Billing, Tax and legacy systems interact with each other in an enterprise technology ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organisational and time management skills and the ability to juggle competing priorities while working with multiple strategic opportunities and customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic and creative thinker who can proactively identify challenges and maintain a positive approach when facing difficult obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Members of the Partner Solutions Architecture (PSA) team are responsible for providing technical guidance to Stripe’s key strategic partners. Our goal is to drive growth through co-solutioning, education and enablement with our partner organization. PSAs are a critical technical liaison to the Stripe Partner Development Manager and Partners. This involves creating comprehensive technical business plans for Partners, including identifying, incubating and bringing to market service/solution offerings built on or with Stripe. A Partner Solutions Architect is someone who is intellectually curious, motivated to win, open and entrepreneurial.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a dynamic and experienced Partner Solutions Lead, SA (Americas), you will lead our growing team of talented SAs working closely with our Alliances &amp;amp; Channels team. This role will focus on building robust alliances with Independent Software Vendors (ISVs) such as Salesforce, Commerce tools, and AWS, as well as Global System Integrators (GSIs) like Accenture and PWC, on top of other strategic regional partnerships. The ideal candidate will possess a blend of technical leadership and managerial prowess, driving the development and execution of strategic initiatives that foster collaboration and growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a team of Partner Solutions Architects (PSA), providing guidance on best practices for engaging with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute strategic plans to enhance the capability of the PSA team in supporting ISV and SI partners across AMER.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal stakeholders, including sales, product, and engineering teams, to ensure alignment in partner strategies and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with key partner accounts, understanding their needs and translating them into action for the PSA team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze market trends and partner feedback to identify opportunities for improvement and direct the team in addressing these areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of continuous improvement, innovation, and knowledge sharing within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and grow talent on a scale across AMER.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and lead efforts to develop Centers of Excellence within partners, driving solutions-orientated go-to-market services, products and strategies with Stripe as a key pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in technical Pre-Sales / Solutions Architecture, including 8+ years in a pre-sales leadership position. Ideal candidate will have experience in a similar role leading a partner solution architects org across geos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years experience building and developing teams across multiple regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of cloud computing, APIs, software architecture, and integration technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent leadership skills with the ability to inspire and develop high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills, capable of liaising effectively with technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven project management skills with the ability to lead multiple initiatives simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A results-oriented mindset with strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in an environment that featured Billing, Payments, fraud solutions, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note - for candidates living within 35 miles of a Stripe office (San Francisco, Seattle, New York, Chicago or Georgia) we operate a hybrid work policy where 50% office attendance per month is expected. For candidates more than 35 miles from an office, fully remote work can be approved.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner Solutions Engineering sits within Global Partnerships at the intersection of Stripe’s Product and Engineering teams and the partners that extend Stripe’s platform. We own the partner-side technical outcome for selected partnership work, from architecture and implementation through testing, launch readiness, and production support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem Partner Solutions Engineering team helps partners build high-quality integrations across Stripe’s app and developer-platform ecosystem. We work across areas such as developer tools, commerce, billing, automation, and data, while helping Stripe turn recurring partner needs into stronger products and reusable integration paths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work has two forms. We deliver priority partner implementations, and we turn the lessons from those implementations into Product feedback, reference architectures, testing and certification paths, and reusable guidance. This allows Stripe to support more partners without treating every implementation as a bespoke project.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Partner Solutions Engineer, Ecosystem, you will own the technical outcome for a portfolio of ecosystem areas and priority partner integrations. You will work directly with partners, Partner Development Managers, Product Managers, and Engineers to move opportunities from technical discovery through implementation and launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also develop deep expertise in selected parts of Stripe’s app and developer platform. You will identify recurring technical barriers, help Product teams distinguish isolated partner requests from broader platform needs, and create reusable paths that improve the next partner’s experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, partner-facing engineering role. The strongest candidates can move comfortably between partner architecture, API and code-level debugging, Product feedback, delivery planning, and executive communication.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own partner technical delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical planning, architecture, implementation support, testing, and launch readiness for selected partner integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate partner goals into clear technical requirements, dependencies, milestones, and success criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain one accountable technical plan across the partner, Global Partnerships, Product, and Engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify delivery risks early and drive technical decisions through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead critical partner escalations and help resolve complex production integration failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage an ecosystem portfolio&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own a technical portfolio across multiple ecosystem areas, based on team priorities and your expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with partnership leads to prioritize integrations and determine where dedicated technical support will create the most value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect partner technical delivery to adoption, commercial, and user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize technical engagements based on partner impact, strategic value, implementation readiness, and team commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop platform expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop deep expertise in Stripe’s app, developer-platform, and extensibility capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise partners and other Partner Solutions Engineers on embedded experiences, workflow automation, application distribution, permissions, and monetization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain reference architectures, implementation guidance, testing standards, and certification paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track emerging platform capabilities and help priority partners adopt them successfully.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence Stripe’s Product roadmap&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring friction and unmet partner needs through direct implementation work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distinguish partner-specific requirements from platform gaps that affect multiple integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate implementation evidence into clear Product requirements and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product and Engineering teams to reach clear decisions on requirements, workarounds, ownership, and sequencing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close the feedback loop with partners when Stripe makes or declines a Product investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create reusable technical leverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn initial partner builds into repeatable implementation and enablement paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build prototypes, examples, scripts, or lightweight tooling when they accelerate partner delivery or validate a Product direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define launch-readiness standards across permissions, authorization, testing, observability, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Transition mature integration patterns to scalable support models when they no longer require dedicated engineering ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shared team standards for custom partner applications, incidents, escalations, and partner handoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Measure outcomes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track technical milestones, launch outcomes, adoption signals, and implementation quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure the commercial, user, or Product outcomes that your work enables, accelerates, or protects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use portfolio data to identify repeated blockers, improve prioritization, and guide future investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. Preferred qualifications are useful but not required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in solutions engineering, partner engineering, software engineering, technical consulting, developer relations engineering, or another hands-on technical role supporting external users or partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and delivering production integrations using APIs, webhooks, authentication and authorization, event-driven systems, or developer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, write, and debug code in at least one general-purpose programming language such as JavaScript or TypeScript, Python, Ruby, Java, or Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience diagnosing complex integration failures across partner systems, APIs, and product surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading external partners from technical discovery through implementation, testing, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous partner goals into a clear architecture, delivery plan, and set of technical decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify patterns across multiple implementations and turn them into reusable guidance or Product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication with technical, business, and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working across Product, Engineering, Partnerships, Sales, or other cross-functional teams without relying on direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment when balancing partner urgency, Product constraints, implementation quality, and long-term platform leverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with developer platforms, platform ecosystems, marketplaces, or partner-distributed products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with application extensibility, embedded applications, workflow automation, OAuth, or delegated API access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, fintech, commerce, billing, monetization, or financial operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating partner certification, integration-quality, or launch-readiness programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building prototypes, examples, or developer tooling that influenced a Product roadmap or accelerated partner adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Launch priority partner integrations that produce measurable user, adoption, commercial, or Product outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give partners one accountable technical owner through implementation and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve Stripe’s Products by bringing clear, repeated partner evidence into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce repeated partner blockers through reusable architecture, guidance, testing, and certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop recognized expertise across your assigned ecosystem areas and Stripe’s app and developer-platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increase the number of partner integrations that can move to scalable support models without sacrificing quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Stripe&#39;s user base and global footprint grows dramatically, we face uniquely complex operational challenges at the intersection of payments infrastructure, financial data integrity, and global scale. The Stripe Delivery Center (SDC) provides operational leverage across Stripe&#39;s portfolio supporting external users and internal teams with precision and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Technical Operations Analyst on the Payments team, you will own the reliability and accuracy of some of the world&#39;s most critical payment flows, a platform processing hundreds of billions of dollars annually. You will sit at the intersection of engineering, finance, and operations: triaging live payment failures, driving reconciliation accuracy, and partnering with financial institutions globally to resolve issues fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a passive monitoring role. You will be expected to independently own investigations end-to-end, identify systemic issues before they escalate, and drive process improvements that scale with Stripe&#39;s growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own reconciliation and payments-related investigations, ensuring accurate ledgering of funds and resolving discrepancies with banking partners swiftly and precisely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively monitor payment performance across users and payment methods; triage degradation alerts, diagnose root causes, and communicate findings clearly to technical and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the escalation point for complex support inquiries from Technical Account Managers, Product Support, and internal Stripe teams providing fast, well-reasoned resolutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface directly with Stripe&#39;s global financial partners (card networks, banks, payment processors) to manage operational incidents and drive resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validate the accuracy of Stripe&#39;s financial data through rigorous analysis and cross-functional collaboration with finance and infrastructure engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify process inefficiencies and lead automation initiatives to reduce manual workload and improve operational throughput at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain high-quality SOPs, runbooks, and process documentation to ensure institutional knowledge is captured and transferable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3-7 years&lt;/strong&gt; of experience in a technical operations, payments operations, or financial technology role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advanced SQL proficiency&lt;/strong&gt; - you write complex queries (joins, window functions, aggregations) independently and use them as a primary tool for investigation and root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of &lt;strong&gt;end-to-end payment flows &lt;/strong&gt;- including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience investigating and resolving &lt;strong&gt;high-severity operational incidents&lt;/strong&gt; in a payments or financial systems environment with minimal oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with &lt;strong&gt;large-scale financial datasets&lt;/strong&gt; - validating accuracy, identifying anomalies, and reconciling discrepancies across systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage &lt;strong&gt;complex, cross-functional workflows&lt;/strong&gt; - coordinating simultaneously with engineering, finance, banking partners, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of &lt;strong&gt;identifying process gaps and driving automation or efficiency improvements&lt;/strong&gt; that meaningfully reduced manual workload.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing and maintaining &lt;strong&gt;SOPs, runbooks, and technical documentation&lt;/strong&gt; to a high standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent &lt;strong&gt;written and verbal communication in English&lt;/strong&gt; - able to translate complex technical issues into clear, concise updates for both technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with &lt;strong&gt;high autonomy&lt;/strong&gt; in a fast-paced environment, managing competing priorities and time-sensitive deadlines without close supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience working directly with &lt;strong&gt;card networks, acquiring banks, or payment processors,&lt;/strong&gt; including managing operational escalations and SLA-driven communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;payment cost optimization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of &lt;strong&gt;end-to-end payment flows &lt;/strong&gt;- including authorization, clearing, settlement, reconciliation, and exception handling across multiple payment methods and geographies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with &lt;strong&gt;accounting and financial reconciliation principles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in a &lt;strong&gt;high-growth fintech or global payments company&lt;/strong&gt; operating at significant transaction scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or improving &lt;strong&gt;monitoring and alerting frameworks&lt;/strong&gt; for payment systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical history of&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;developing AI-driven solutions&lt;/strong&gt; designed to automate and optimize high-volume operational workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Payments Fraud Investigator, you’ll play a critical role in safeguarding our financial ecosystem by investigating high-risk accounts and identifying various forms of fraud. You’ll conduct deep-dive analyses of merchant accounts, lead cross-functional projects, and collaborate with stakeholders to enhance our fraud detection and prevention strategies at scale. Your expertise in fraud patterns and typologies will be essential to developing and enhancing investigative processes and programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze high-risk accounts to identify fraudulent merchants, card testing, account takeovers, and other fraud vectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead root-cause analyses to identify gaps in current systems, policies, and strategies, and determine enhancements and process improvements to address emerging fraud risks in collaboration with key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional projects aimed at refining operational processes and tools and enhancing the detection and management of fraudulent accounts across our global analyst network&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate, mitigate, and remediate urgent fraud incidents, such as card testing and account takeover, and manage user responses to high-urgency, distributed fraud attacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regular updates during team and organization-wide business reviews, summarize the outcomes of complex investigations for executives, and deliver clear case determinations to users and partner financial institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to vendor locations to conduct analyst training sessions and knowledge-sharing initiatives, identify challenges, and enhance analyst performance to improve overall outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience conducting complex investigations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ year of experience leading risk-related projects and initiatives and collaborating effectively with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to leverage data to propose solutions to both tactical and strategic challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive approach to challenging the status quo, with a willingness to question existing processes and advocate for improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-centric perspective when addressing challenges, balanced with a pragmatic and solutions-oriented mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to vendor locations for up to 10% of the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mitigating digital or card-not-present fraud in payments, e-commerce, social media, or fintech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience investigating and mitigating card-testing and account-takeover attacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing fraud and risk workflows, analyst tooling, processes, and procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in using SQL to analyze data, generate insights, and create dashboards and visualizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

