&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe&#39;s products. Product Designers work directly with Engineers, Product Managers, Data Scientists, and Marketers, as strategic partners, in each product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global design team crafts product experiences that make cross-border selling as simple, performant, and scalable as domestic sales. Experiences empower businesses to easily expand into new markets worldwide without the friction of complex global operations, ranging from localized checkout experiences and comprehensive payment method coverage to handling global tax compliance and cross-border money management. Because of its global reach, this team&#39;s efforts drive significant impact for our users and business and navigate the unique challenges of designing for regions with dozens of currencies, languages, and regulatory frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product designer, you&#39;ll work closely with product managers and engineering teams to envision features in the Stripe Dashboard and checkout surfaces and partner with go-to-market teams to bring them to users. That includes new feature development, localization for priority geographies across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, and setting vision for our products to meet new user expectations in an increasingly globally connected and AI-driven world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user workflows and pain points, and produce, test, and iterate on high-quality designs to solve user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, engineering, marketing, and strategy partners to define a north star and product experience for new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype user experiences for user research testing and internal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to craft a seamless dashboard user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct UXR to test design decisions before shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our design systems teams to leverage and improve templates and components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of relevant design experience at a product-driven tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong craft demonstrated through a portfolio of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skills in prototyping at high fidelity using the latest AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills through design deliverables, videos, and written artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a growth team driving user activation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excited about building collaborative relationships with many partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for turning complexity into usable, beautiful experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong design leader comfortable bringing your point of view to a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with several teams of engineers and PMs to shape products used by Stripe employees across engineering, operations, finance, and beyond. This is a high-impact role for a designer who finds as much satisfaction in untangling complex workflows and dense information architectures as in crafting polished interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll take ownership of two spaces within our internal tooling portfolio—Developer Productivity, focused on ensuring every engineer at Stripe has the tools to be productive, and Collaboration, focused on knowledge discovery and communication at scale. You&#39;ll pair with an existing designer on the team to bring design quality and consistency to surfaces that are critical to how Stripe operates internally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end design for a portfolio of internal tools—from discovery and problem framing through interaction design, prototyping, and implementation support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and product managers to define product requirements and translate them into clear, usable, and well-considered design solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct lightweight research and usability sessions with internal users to validate decisions and surface unmet needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a consistent design language across our internal tools suite, working in close coordination with the Sail Design team and the Stripe design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make design trade-offs confidently, knowing when to go deep on craft and when to ship a pragmatic solution that moves the product forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help raise the bar for internal product design at Stripe, advocating for users who are often underserved compared to customer-facing surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product design experience, with a portfolio that demonstrates strong UX thinking, clear visual craft, and an ability to navigate ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing tools for complex or data-heavy workflows—internal tools, developer tools, ops platforms, or similar are a strong plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across the full design process—you can lead discovery, write a problem brief, design and prototype, and ship without needing every step handed to you&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinker—you naturally look for patterns, reusable components, and structural solutions rather than one-off fixes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and direct communicator. You share work early, give and receive feedback well, and know how to align cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Figma and comfortable working within or alongside a design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing for internal-facing or enterprise tooling environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve contributed to a design system, or worked closely to a design systems team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to information architecture challenges—navigation, search, and content modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in or interest in developer tooling, ops platforms, or workflow automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link team builds the global, consumer network for next-generation commerce, using our base of 300M+ registered consumers to pioneer the future of Identity, Consumer Finance, and AI-driven transactions. While our foundation was built on high-conversion merchant payments and a flexible digital wallet, we are expanding far beyond. We are building the infrastructure for a world where AI agents transact on your behalf, stablecoins go mainstream, and identity dictates how money moves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We think of Link as the wallet for the internet — and we&#39;re building for what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with your product and engineering partners and design teammates to craft the future of Link. You&#39;ll help us build the fastest, most convenient and powerful checkout experience. You&#39;ll explore new features and products that expand Link&#39;s reach and consumer value beyond checkout. And through close partnership with our brand team, you&#39;ll ensure Link&#39;s visual identity and end-to-end experience is unmistakably distinct and raises the bar for what a great consumer experience looks and feels like online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design delightful, high-quality consumer checkout experiences across mobile and desktop&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and solve user problems by translating research insights and product goals into clear, well-crafted design solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and product to design, build, and ship user-facing experiences at high quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Brand Studio to maintain a cohesive visual identity across Link&#39;s surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Link&#39;s design system and help evolve patterns that scale across the product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and share your work regularly in design reviews, building a feedback loop with design and cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years relevant design experience at a consumer tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong craft across visual design, interaction design, and prototyping, demonstrated through a portfolio spanning desktop and mobile&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with engineering and product teams through the full product development cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to a design system—proposing, refining, or documenting reusable components and patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to design and prototype in code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong independence and an ability to advocate for a larger design vision with cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to reduce complex problems down to the right balance of flexibility, power, and ease of use&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in explaining your work, process, and decisions to cross-functional stakeholders and crave feedback to help you produce your best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;About the team&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team defines and delivers user-facing experiences across Stripe. Product Designers work closely with engineers, product managers, researchers, strategists, operations, data scientists, and marketers to shape products from early strategy through launch and iteration. You’ll be joining the Risk team, which shapes how businesses get started on Stripe, build trust, stay compliant, and grow with confidence. The work spans businesses of every size and helps keep both our users and Stripe’s ecosystem safe. Risk is a high-impact design space where the problems are both strategic and complex. As a designer on the team, you’ll help bring clarity to critical user moments, reduce friction for legitimate businesses, and raise the craft bar where trust, ease, and confidence matter most. This role is a strong fit for a designer who is energized by complexity, motivated by impact, and excited to turn difficult systems into simple, intuitive experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll design experiences that help businesses start and grow successfully on Stripe. You’ll work closely with cross-functional partners to define problems, shape direction, and ship high-quality experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex systems, policies, and operational constraints into clear, thoughtful product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-leverage opportunities that improve coherence across journeys, touchpoints, and surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with PMs, engineers, researchers, operations, and strategists to shape product direction and drive user and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop both long-term strategy and pragmatic short-term solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, prototype, and communicate ideas with creative storytelling and demos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use qualitative and quantitative signals to inform decisions and evaluate impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering to ensure a high bar for craft and implementation quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shared patterns and systems that help the broader Risk organization build with coherence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant product design experience at a product-driven technology company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating strong visual craft, interaction design, and systems thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on complex product areas with multiple stakeholders, constraints, and interconnected workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product thinking and the ability to shape direction, not just execute against requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to prototype and design across multiple touchpoints and surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence through clear design rationale and artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You’ll likely thrive in this role if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think in systems and design solutions that scale across users, workflows, and surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong product judgment and influence beyond the UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Care deeply about quality from concept through implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable operating in fast-moving environments where priorities may shift in response to policy, operational, or regulatory needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Product Design team is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe’s brand and product. Product Designers are strategic partners to Engineering and Product Management within their product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Terminal design team crafts product experiences that empower users to configure and manage in person payments. This team transforms the intricate world of payments into intuitive solutions, letting users focus on growing their businesses. The team spans hardware and software, focusing on many types of users: end users who pay at the point of sale, cashiers and operations managers who set up and run the devices, and merchants who manage a fleet of devices and need to monitor performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product designer, you’ll work closely with the product manager and engineering team to envision payments features in the Stripe Dashboard and our end-user-facing surfaces and partner with go-to-market teams to bring them to users. That includes new feature development, product quality improvements to our most frequently used workflows, and setting vision for our products to meet new user expectations in an increasingly data and AI-driven world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand user workflows and pain points, and produce, test, and iterate on high-quality designs to solve user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with product, engineering, marketing, and strategy partners to define a north star and product experience for new features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype user experiences for user research testing and internal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to craft a seamless dashboard user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct user research to test design decisions before shipping&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with our design systems teams to leverage and improve page templates and components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has 4+ years relevant design experience at a product-driven tech company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has strong craft demonstrated through a portfolio of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has demonstrated skills in prototyping at a high fidelity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience collaborating closely with engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has excellent written and verbal communication skills, demonstrated through design deliverables, videos, and written artifacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited about building collaborative relationships with many partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate for turning complexity into usable, beautiful experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are a strong design leader comfortable with bringing your point of view to a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product Designers at Stripe are strategic partners to Engineering and Product Management. Together, we define user-facing experiences, then translate that thinking into complete products that can be tested, shipped, and refined. We’re responsible for creating powerful, well-crafted, beautiful products that users love and are eager to recommend to others.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/treasury&quot;&gt;Treasury&lt;/a&gt; brings business banking and payments together on Stripe. We help businesses receive, store, send, and spend their money in one place — with faster access to funds, global money movement, and cards for everyday spending. Instead of stitching together banks, payment processors, and financial tools, businesses can manage their money where they already run their payments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ambition is to make managing business finances feel as intuitive and thoughtfully designed as the best consumer products. That means making sophisticated capabilities accessible, bringing clarity to complex workflows, and paying close attention to the details that help people feel confident and in control of their money.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Designer on the Treasury team, you’ll help rethink an essential part of running a business. Your work could help businesses access their earnings sooner, understand their cash flow, move money across currencies and borders, or manage everyday spending — all within a connected experience on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work across new and existing products, shaping zero-to-one experiences and refining the details of what’s already in users’ hands. You’ll partner closely with Product and Engineering to define problems, explore possibilities, and bring high-quality experiences to life. This work involves substantial ambiguity and technical and regulatory complexity; your role is to make the experience feel simple without losing the rigor that financial products demand.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end product design process, from understanding user needs and defining problems through prototyping, detailed design, launch, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design intuitive, cohesive experiences that help businesses receive, store, send, and spend money with confidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring clarity to ambiguous problems, using research, exploration, and prototypes to establish direction and turn early ideas into products people can use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver exceptional interaction and visual design, bringing a consumer-grade standard of usability, polish, and care to complex financial tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Engineering to shape the roadmap around meaningful, measurable user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Legal, Compliance, Risk, and other stakeholders to understand constraints and find thoughtful solutions that protect users without introducing unnecessary friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with user researchers, content designers, and other product designers to validate ideas and create a consistent experience across Treasury and the broader Stripe Dashboard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineers through implementation, refining interactions and details so the shipped experience meets the intended quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share work regularly in design reviews, explain your decisions clearly, and use feedback to strengthen your work.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 6+ years of relevant product design experience at a technology, product-driven company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong visual design, interaction design, and prototyping skills, demonstrated through shipped experiences with a high bar for craft and usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can make complex products feel simple and approachable, with thoughtful information hierarchy, clear interactions, and meticulous attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are comfortable working through substantial ambiguity: defining problems, exploring alternatives, and making progress when requirements are incomplete or evolving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can engage deeply with technical and regulatory requirements, working with cross-functional partners to translate constraints into clear, trustworthy user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have worked autonomously on substantial product initiatives, partnering with Product and Engineering to shape both direction and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working with and contributing to an established design system, balancing consistency with the needs of new experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience collaborating closely with engineers to deliver high-quality interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate your thinking clearly through prototypes, user flows, and design rationale, and actively seek feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can prioritize effectively across projects at different stages, balancing speed, scope, and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping zero-to-one products, from early exploration through launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing financial products, particularly business accounts, money management, payments, or spending tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing consumer products, or bringing a comparable standard of simplicity and craft to complex business software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience connecting fragmented tools or workflows into a cohesive product experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enjoy collaborating with other designers, sharing feedback, and helping one another grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier—from solo founders to established enterprises—united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.7% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches. Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinopenstandard.com/&quot;&gt;infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Though people at Stripe don’t tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many (especially the new and innovative ones), we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Our internship program is structured to provide interns with the opportunity to work on real projects that our customers urgently need. In this role you will be part of the Product Design team, which is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe’s product. Product Designers are strategic partners to Engineering and Product Management within their product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;As a Product Design Intern, you will focus on designing and building experiences that will be shipped to our users in production. You will contribute design iterations to ongoing project workstreams, tackling important projects to increase global commerce, and help shape brand new experiences. Our internship program is competitive and the expectations are high.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Work on a product design project with a product team, translating business ideas into real experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Help craft thoughtful experiences that enable startups and large businesses to establish and manage their businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Apply problem-solving skills and human-centered approaches to address complex and ambiguous business and user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Develop and refine design solutions by partnering closely with other designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Craft and prototype visually polished experiences to get user feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with engineering to implement a feature/product from design to implementation, and get it in the hands of our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Engage in group design critiques and collaborative design sessions to improve and receive feedback on your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders, including engineers, product managers, data scientists, and researchers, proactively seeking and incorporating feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Understand and advocate for our users, participating in the design process from early concepts to final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Ambitious builder: You’re energized by building solutions without clear precedent and solving problems with far-reaching consequences. Successful Stripes are deeply curious, and prefer the joy of discovery to the comfort of certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Rigorous thinker: You appreciate that things worth doing are rarely simple. You enjoy working on problems that have never been tackled before.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Adaptable problem solver: You adapt quickly and treat obstacles as opportunities. At Stripe we embrace kindness while encouraging Stripes to take measured risks and act boldly, even in the absence of consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a design-related field, such as UX/UI, Interaction Design, Human Interface, Computer Science,&amp;nbsp; HCI, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Some experience using computer programs to design, such as Figma/Canva.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience designing experiences and user flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of user-centered design principles and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar systems, form an understanding through independent research, and effectively work with a mentor and teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Are a self-motivated problem solver committed to personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Proven ability to leverage AI tools to accelerate work while applying rigorous critical thinking and professional judgement to review, refine, and validate all outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to participate in a paid full-time internship between May–August, 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (A bonus, not a requirement)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Previous project, internship, or work experience in UX/UI design or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Experience working with or conducting your own research, presenting results, and acting on those results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Experience with AI tools like Cursor, Lovable, V0, or any others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge in design craft and visual design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Intent to return to the degree program after the completion of the internship/co-op.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;

&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a technology company focused on improving the conditions for economic growth and prosperity. We build programmable financial infrastructure, rethinking from first principles how financial services should work, to make it easier and cheaper for any business to start and scale. More than 10 million &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers&quot;&gt;businesses&lt;/a&gt; build on Stripe, spanning the economic frontier—from solo founders to established enterprises—united by a practical focus on growth. The most ambitious companies in the world use Stripe as core infrastructure to grow faster. They process trillions of dollars a year on Stripe, equivalent to around 1.7% of global GDP. While economic growth makes everyone better off, open markets also enable greater variety. When any business can easily serve a global customer base, the quality and diversity of products in the world increase, and craft and creativity are unleashed into the smallest niches. Our own growth is wholly contingent on the success of the businesses building on Stripe. We therefore invest back into our technology at an unusual rate. We make &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/roadmap&quot;&gt;upgrades to our products&lt;/a&gt; every single day to deliver compounding gains to our customers. We maintain some of the most &lt;a href=&quot;https://status.stripe.com/&quot;&gt;reliable APIs&lt;/a&gt; on the internet. We build entirely new &lt;a href=&quot;https://tempo.xyz/&quot;&gt;pieces&lt;/a&gt; of &lt;a href=&quot;https://mpp.dev/&quot;&gt;financial&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&quot;https://joinopenstandard.com/&quot;&gt;infrastructure&lt;/a&gt; to enable new ideas. And our significant advances in &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/radar&quot;&gt;risk and fraud&lt;/a&gt; infrastructure over many years are making the internet economy safer and more accessible.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Though people at Stripe don’t tend to take themselves seriously, Stripe is a fairly serious place: our customers are depending on us for their livelihoods. We admire ambition, intensity, curiosity, humility, and rigor. The most effective people become knowledgeable about many domains besides their own. Any company is an applied exercise in understanding some aspect of society or the market. In working with so many (especially the new and innovative ones), we think that Stripe is one of the very best places to learn about how the world works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Our internship program is structured to provide interns with the opportunity to work on real projects that our customers urgently need. In this role you will be part of the Product Design team, which is made up of several groups that define, create, and deliver all user-facing aspects of Stripe’s product. Product Designers are strategic partners to Engineering and Product Management within their product area. In close collaboration with product teams, they shape user experiences, then translate them into high-quality designs that can be tested, shipped, and refined. Designers are responsible for building elegant, functional products that users love—and want to tell others about.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;As a Product Design Intern, you will focus on designing and building experiences that will be shipped to our users in production. You will contribute design iterations to ongoing project workstreams, tackling important projects to increase global commerce, and help shape brand new experiences. Our internship program is competitive and the expectations are high.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Key responsibilities include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Work on a product design project with a product team, translating business ideas into real experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Help craft thoughtful experiences that enable startups and large businesses to establish and manage their businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Apply problem-solving skills and human-centered approaches to address complex and ambiguous business and user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Develop and refine design solutions by partnering closely with other designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Craft and prototype visually polished experiences to get user feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with engineering to implement a feature/product from design to implementation, and get it in the hands of our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Engage in group design critiques and collaborative design sessions to improve and receive feedback on your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders, including engineers, product managers, data scientists, and researchers, proactively seeking and incorporating feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Understand and advocate for our users, participating in the design process from early concepts to final delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Ambitious builder: You’re energized by building solutions without clear precedent and solving problems with far-reaching consequences. Successful Stripes are deeply curious, and prefer the joy of discovery to the comfort of certainty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Rigorous thinker: You appreciate that things worth doing are rarely simple. You enjoy working on problems that have never been tackled before.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Adaptable problem solver: You adapt quickly and treat obstacles as opportunities. At Stripe we embrace kindness while encouraging Stripes to take measured risks and act boldly, even in the absence of consensus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Currently pursuing a Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in a design-related field, such as UX/UI, Interaction Design, Human Interface, Computer Science,&amp;nbsp; HCI, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Some experience using computer programs to design, such as Figma/Canva.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience designing experiences and user flows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of user-centered design principles and best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar systems, form an understanding through independent research, and effectively work with a mentor and teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Are a self-motivated problem solver committed to personal growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Strong interpersonal and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.5;&quot;&gt;Proven ability to leverage AI tools to accelerate work while applying rigorous critical thinking and professional judgement to review, refine, and validate all outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to participate in a paid full-time internship between May–August, 2027.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications (A bonus, not a requirement)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Previous project, internship, or work experience in UX/UI design or related fields.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Experience working with or conducting your own research, presenting results, and acting on those results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Experience with AI tools like Cursor, Lovable, V0, or any others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge in design craft and visual design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;line-height: 1.4;&quot;&gt;Intent to return to the degree program after the completion of the internship/co-op.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/treasury&quot;&gt;Treasury&lt;/a&gt; brings business banking and payments together on Stripe. We help businesses receive, store, send, and spend their money in one place — with faster access to funds, global money movement, and cards for everyday spending. Instead of stitching together banks, payment processors, and financial tools, businesses can manage their money where they already run their payments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For design, this is an opportunity to rethink money management- an essential part of running a business. How might we make managing money feel effortless, help businesses operate across currencies and borders with confidence, and turn complex financial operations into intuitive, powerful experiences that give people more time to focus on building their businesses?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a design leader to help shape those answers. Our ambition is to build products that are powerful, well-crafted, and beautiful—bringing the quality and care of the best consumer experiences to business financial tools. You’ll lead a team defining new experiences from the ground up, navigating substantial ambiguity and regulatory complexity without losing sight of what makes a product exceptional.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a design team focused on Treasury, shaping a compelling vision for a unified experience across business banking, payments, money movement, and spending&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex financial capabilities into intuitive experiences that help businesses access their funds faster, manage cash flow, and operate globally with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide zero-to-one work from early exploration through launch, helping the team turn open-ended problems into clear product direction and cohesive experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high bar for craft and beauty, coaching designers to deliver exceptional interaction design, visual design, and thoughtful details that build confidence and trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Engineering, Legal, Compliance, Risk, and other stakeholders to find ambitious solutions within financial and regulatory constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and develop a team of designers, growing their skills, judgment, and careers while fostering a high-performance, customer-obsessed team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire the team and align cross-functional leaders around a clear design vision, balancing long-term ambition with pragmatic progress and world-class excellence in what we ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 5+ years of people management experience and are confident in building and developing design teams in fast-paced, evolving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading design teams tackling complex products with technical or financial systems, including shaping zero-to-one products from understanding user needs and defining the problem to establishing a product direction and bringing it to market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong design judgment and a track record of helping teams deliver world-class, consumer-grade experiences. Ability to make sophisticated products feel simple, coach designers toward outstanding interaction and visual craft, and balance detail-oriented design with big-picture strategy, combining a deep understanding of users with business goals to drive meaningful outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable designing within regulatory constraints and partnering with legal, compliance, and risk teams. You can distinguish firm requirements from assumptions and find creative solutions without compromising user trust or regulatory obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have demonstrated the ability to drive progress through substantial ambiguity. You bring structure to unclear problems, make sound decisions with incomplete information, and help teams move forward as requirements evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excel at balancing detail-oriented design with big-picture strategy, combining a deep understanding of users with business goals to drive meaningful outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, using storytelling and clear reasoning to align teams and influence senior stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing financial products, particularly banking or bank-like experiences, money management, cards, or treasury tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering products across global markets with differing regulatory, operational, and user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience bringing fragmented tools and workflows together into a cohesive product experience with a consistently high standard of craft.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The recruiting team seeks to build the culture of Stripe by aligning the strongest global talent to our highest impact business needs. They focus on bringing Stripe’s operating principles to life in their recruiting processes, providing the highest-quality candidate experience, and leveraging data driven storytelling to influence the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are looking for a driven and collaborative Product &amp;amp; Design Recruiter to grow and scale our global product management and design organizations. You can expect high-impact and wide-ranging responsibility: owning full-cycle recruiting for specialized product and design searches, contributing to our geographic strategy through talent market insights, and delivering an exceptional candidate experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This person must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment—unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, navigate ambiguity, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner with senior leaders across product management and design to understand hiring objectives and develop recruiting strategies tailored to each organization’s needs.&lt;br&gt;- Own full-cycle recruiting across product management and design disciplines, including product design, brand design, content design, design engineering, web presence design, and UX research.&lt;br&gt;- Build a deep understanding of the skills, experience, and craft required for product and design roles, partnering with hiring teams to define profiles and align on evaluation criteria.&lt;br&gt;- Develop strategic sourcing and engagement plans to attract product and design talent across different geographies, including passive senior candidates.&lt;br&gt;- Use talent market insights to advise hiring leaders on candidate availability, search strategy, and geographic opportunities.&lt;br&gt;- Track and analyze recruiting metrics, share hiring progress with product and design leadership, and use insights to improve search outcomes.&lt;br&gt;- Initiate creative and scalable improvements to recruiting processes while maintaining a high-quality candidate experience.&lt;br&gt;- Work closely with Finance, People Ops, Benefits, Onboarding, and Legal to deliver a high-quality and holistic candidate experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 7+ years of full-cycle recruiting experience, including 4+ years recruiting across product management and design in a fast-paced, high-growth environment, with in-house experience.&lt;br&gt;- Experience supporting hiring across both product management and design, with a track record of building high-performing teams and delivering an exceptional candidate experience.&lt;br&gt;- Ability to understand distinct product and design profiles and translate business needs into effective search strategies.&lt;br&gt;- A growth mindset and flexibility to shift tasks and priorities as business needs change.&lt;br&gt;- An active, data-driven approach to problem-solving, using recruiting trends and market insights to improve processes and outcomes.&lt;br&gt;- Proven ability to attract passive senior candidates and build diverse pipelines across different hiring locations.&lt;br&gt;- Strong stakeholder management skills, including the ability to advise hiring leaders and navigate competing priorities across product and design searches.&lt;br&gt;- Strong operational rigor and the ability to stay organized amid change.&lt;br&gt;- Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with an appropriate blend of professionalism and friendliness.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Connect Platform&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It helps platforms onboard and verify participants, manage accounts, accept payments, and pay out funds without building payments, compliance, or financial services infrastructure themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Risk team builds the risk management capabilities that help platforms operate safely from day one, including onboarding, Know Your Customer (KYC) verification, fraud and credit risk management, and tax reporting. As AI-native platforms and marketplaces emerge, this work helps Stripe support increasingly dynamic global ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own Connected Account Onboarding Experiences, the products and journeys that help platforms onboard their users safely, compliantly, and with minimal friction. You will shape experiences from sign-up and authentication through readiness to use Stripe products, across application programming interfaces (APIs) and hosted or embedded user interfaces (UI).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will use funnel data, user research, and experimentation to improve conversion while meeting Stripe’s commitments to regulators and financial partners. You will set the strategy for what should be standardized or configurable across platform business models, products, and geographies, including opportunities to use artificial intelligence (AI) and agentic interfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the vision, strategy, goals, and roadmap for Connected Account Onboarding Experiences globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional execution across Connect, Risk, engineering, design, data science, and partner-facing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use funnel metrics, user research, and experimentation to identify friction and improve onboarding conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate risk, regulatory, and partner requirements into intuitive experiences across APIs, platform tools, and connected-account UI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable onboarding foundations that support different platform models, geographies, and evolving AI-enabled experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex, multi-quarter product roadmaps and aligning internal teams and external partners around shared goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience partnering with engineering, design, and data teams to build products and systems at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including defining success metrics, running experiments, and using data to improve business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate user problems and product decisions clearly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on complex platform, ecosystem, or regulated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate with autonomy in a dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in high growth companies and products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building user onboarding solutions in enterprise or business-to-business (B2B) industries through APIs or user interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience redesigning traditional user journeys through AI and building agentic interfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Connect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While accepting payments on the internet has become easier over the past several years, due in large part to the advent of modern payments APIs, the internet infrastructure for routing these same payments—to suppliers, sellers, partners, service providers, and recipients—remains outdated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s leading product for marketplaces, on-demand services, ecommerce site builders, invoicing platforms, professional SaaS products, fundraising platforms, rental management platforms, and more. By using Connect, users in each of these categories can link multiple parties to exchange goods or services. These users rely on Connect for the crucial function of routing payments reliably between these parties.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By powering fast, flexible, compliant, and cost-efficient payment routing on the internet, Connect not only spurs the creation of innovative business models but also enables organizations—whether businesses, nonprofits, or government agencies—to bring previously offline payments online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to define a foundational product area at Stripe. You will turn a fast-changing set of user and product needs into durable platform primitives that work across products, industries, and geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines high-leverage strategy with hands-on product execution. You will work through ambiguous, consequential questions like: what should a platform be able to model? What should be simple by default but flexible when needed? How can Stripe make complex financial infrastructure feel effortless for a platform and its users?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The outcome of your work will compound. The abstractions you help create will be reused across Connect and Stripe, shaping what new products platforms can build and how quickly they can bring them to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager on Stripe’s Connect team, you will shape the strategy and oversee the execution of high-impact initiatives serving modern marketplaces and software platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Product development at Stripe is highly collaborative. You will work closely with engineering, design, analytics, marketing, sales, and customer-facing teams. You will also engage directly with customers and present your plans to Stripe’s leadership team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and advance a compelling product vision for Connect&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Devise the strategy for high-impact initiatives serving modern marketplaces and software platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product strategy and customer needs into clear product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee execution across the teams involved in delivering these initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineering, design, analytics, marketing, sales, and customer-facing teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet with customers to understand their needs and gather feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present product plans to Stripe’s leadership team and incorporate feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;More than three years of product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A computer science background or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to lead products that require coordination across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence and resourcefulness in driving successful outcomes for products and teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consumer Bank Network team helps people do more with their bank accounts. We build consumer experiences for connecting financial accounts and making payments across Stripe, spanning &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/financial-connections&quot;&gt;Financial Connections&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://link.com/&quot;&gt;Link&lt;/a&gt;. We make these experiences simple, secure, and trustworthy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team owns the user experience for one of the highest-traffic products at Stripe. Our work spans onboarding, authentication, checkout, and returning user experiences. We combine product design, experimentation, and personalization to reduce friction, improve conversion, and help consumers discover and adopt payment methods that meet their needs. For businesses, this means easier customer onboarding and better payment experiences. This is both an application and platform team: in addition to the thousands of merchants integrating the Financial Connections UX, more than a dozen teams across Stripe also rely on Financial Connections to serve their users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Link is used by &lt;a href=&quot;https://link.com/&quot;&gt;more than 300 million consumers&lt;/a&gt;. You’ll build consumer experiences within that ecosystem, where small improvements in conversion can help more people connect accounts, make purchases, and get paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the strategy and roadmap for consumer growth, conversion, and payment method adoption across Financial Connections and Link. You’ll work across the consumer journey, from connecting a financial account to completing a purchase, setting up a subscription, managing your finances with your agent of choice, or receiving a payout.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines a high bar for consumer product craft with a disciplined approach to growth. You’ll turn user research and funnel analysis into ideas, work closely with Engineering, Design, and Data Science to test them, and scale what works. You’ll shape both the everyday details of the experience and larger changes to how people discover and use financial products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the product strategy and priorities for consumer conversion, growth, and payment method adoption across Financial Connections and Link.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a steady pipeline of experiments, from targeted UX improvements to new growth opportunities. Define hypotheses, success measures, and guardrails, then use results to decide what to ship, change, or stop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Design and User Research to understand consumer behavior and create clear, intuitive experiences across consent, authentication, bank selection, and error recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering and Data Science to build personalized consumer experiences using machine learning and adaptive experimentation, improving conversion and payment method adoption while balancing user value, business outcomes, and consumer trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own measurement of conversion, activation, and payment method adoption. Understand differences across consumer cohorts and use cases, and distinguish product impact from changes in traffic mix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering to improve reliability and experience quality, resolve friction, and make it easier to deliver and evaluate product changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead work across Link, Payments, Financial Connections, and cross-functional teams such as Partnerships, Risk, and Legal. Address important merchant needs while keeping the team focused on its highest-impact opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the face of the product for Stripe’s users and external partners, showcasing and building demos and prototypes in collaboration with Engineering, Design, and Go-to-Market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of growing consumer products, with direct ownership of measurable improvements in activation, conversion, adoption, or repeat use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading an experimentation program, including forming hypotheses, interpreting results, and adapting your approach when the evidence challenges your assumptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong consumer product judgment and UX instincts. You work closely with designers, care about the details, and can make complex or unfamiliar tasks feel simple and trustworthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and a practical understanding of statistics. You can design and interpret experiments, reason about statistical power and confidence intervals, and use funnel and cohort analysis to make sound product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineers and data scientists on technically complex products, with the judgment to balance growth, quality, and implementation cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The autonomy and persistence to turn an ambiguous problem into shipped improvements, align teams around clear priorities, and communicate your reasoning in writing and conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, wallets, consumer fintech, marketplaces, or subscription products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with personalization, recommendation systems, or incentive programs, including evaluating their long-term impact and economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer and B2B2C products, where consumer needs, merchant requirements, and platform constraints all shape the user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Product team to build the systems that make global, programmable money trustworthy at scale. At Bridge, we’re not just improving global payments — we’re reinventing how money moves across borders using stablecoins and modern financial infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager for Developer Experience, you&#39;ll own the end-to-end developer experience from their first encounter with Bridge to transacting billions of dollars in volume on our platform. You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, engineering, data, and go-to-market to build the self-serve onboarding, developer Dashboard, and activation systems that help any developer build a scaled and successful business with Bridge.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is about enabling a developer of any size and stage to build and scale their business successfully on Bridge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end developer lifecycle and key products, spanning self-serve sign-up, KYB and onboarding, the developer Dashboard, and activation and retention programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product features from ideation to launch in close collaboration with engineering, design, data, and go-to-market teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve data-driven signals and systems that recognize what a developer needs at each stage and respond automatically with the right nudges, support, and interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the product roadmap that creates a scalable and intuitive experience for every developer to use Bridge’s full suite products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own key developer metrics (e.g. activation rate, time-to-first-transaction, developer retention) to drive business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with go-to-market and support teams to understand developer feedback and ship improvements rapidly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathy for users&lt;/strong&gt;: You’re passionate about uncovering and solving pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: You never stop asking “why” and dig into both qualitative and quantitative data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owner’s mentality&lt;/strong&gt;: You tackle challenges head-on and drive solutions with conviction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative spirit&lt;/strong&gt;: You work seamlessly with team members but aren’t afraid to make the call when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity and simplicity&lt;/strong&gt;: You translate complex systems into intuitive, straightforward user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for learning&lt;/strong&gt;: You embrace mistakes as opportunities to grow and improve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6–10+ years of product management experience, with exposure to developer platforms, onboarding, and product-led growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or owning systems related to onboarding, activation, retention, or self-serve growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across multiple customer segments or go-to-market motions, from self-serve to enterprise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working with APIs, dashboards, or developer-facing platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, payments, or crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to shape the future of how money moves, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments Intelligence organization builds the systems that optimize payments across Stripe’s global network. We develop data-driven products that help businesses maximize revenue while minimizing fraud, disputes, and payment costs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Disputes team builds products that help businesses prevent, manage, and resolve payment disputes. We are creating an increasingly automated, end-to-end experience from helping cardholders recognize purchases and resolving issues before they become disputes, to recovering revenue when disputes do occur. Our products help businesses reduce operational effort, maintain healthy dispute rates, and stay in good standing with payment networks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Dispute Prevention is a fast-growing product area with an ambitious vision: make Stripe’s intelligence and network capabilities available to businesses of every size, including large platforms and businesses that process payments across multiple providers. We work across Stripe and with external partners to turn a complex, fragmented ecosystem into products that are simple to adopt, easy to operate, and capable of delivering measurable value at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Dispute Prevention team, you’ll shape the next generation of products that help businesses prevent and resolve disputes. You’ll define the vision and strategy for a fast-growing product area, expanding our capabilities across customer segments, platforms, and payment-processing environments. You’ll help users reduce purchase confusion, maintain healthy dispute rates, and recover more revenue by combining network technologies with Stripe’s data and intelligence. Your work will move businesses toward an automated, hands-off approach to dispute management and help connect prevention with the broader end-to-end disputes experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of customer needs and commercial opportunities to shape what we build and how we bring it to market. Working closely with engineering, data science, design, and go-to-market teams, you’ll build products and relationships that deliver lasting value to customers and partners. You’ll connect technical decisions to commercial outcomes while maintaining a high bar for reliability, craft, and the details that make complex products feel simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the payments and disputes landscape, including how businesses prevent and manage disputes, how payment networks and ecosystem partners operate, and where new technologies can improve outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with businesses, developers, platforms, and partners to uncover unmet needs, understand integration and operational challenges, and identify opportunities to build broadly useful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a clear product vision, strategy, and roadmap that advances Stripe’s goal of making dispute management increasingly automated and effortless.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape products that serve businesses of different sizes and business models, including platforms and businesses operating across multiple payment processors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering and data science to translate Stripe’s data and intelligence into understandable, actionable products that automate workflows and optimize for user-defined outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product development from ideation through launch and scale, setting clear goals, prioritizing thoughtfully, navigating technical and ecosystem dependencies, and executing with rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with payment networks, vendors, and technology partners to bring new capabilities to market, improve existing solutions, and translate customer needs into shared priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product’s business performance, including P&amp;amp;L, pricing, commercial terms, and long-term growth. Use market research and competitive analysis to inform product and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate deeply with sales, marketing, partnerships, and other go-to-market teams to validate demand, develop positioning, support strategic customers, and grow adoption and market share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with internal and external stakeholders about priorities, trade-offs, progress, and results, building alignment across teams you don’t directly manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product management experience, ideally in B2B software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a rigorous approach to quantitative and qualitative evidence. You’re comfortable digging into data, writing SQL when needed, and connecting product decisions to user and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful, with experience taking products from zero to one. You thrive in early-stage environments, test ideas quickly, and turn what you learn into products that scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and business acumen. You understand how customer needs, market dynamics, and product differentiation translate into adoption and durable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional leadership, including experience partnering with B2B sales teams on customer discovery, technical evaluation, and commercialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping Dashboard and API products, with empathy for end users and developers alike.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing pricing and monetization models for B2B products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on APIs, system architecture, and integration trade-offs, and to explain those decisions clearly to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling complex user problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and a high bar for product quality. You do what it takes to solve user problems and care deeply about the details of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building fraud prevention, risk, or banking products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer platforms and working with integration partners, including navigating technical dependencies and high-stakes external relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow revenue, and create new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s ecosystem enables third-party developers and technology partners to extend products such as Payments, Billing, Tax, Checkout, and Workflows. The Ecosystem team builds the Stripe Apps Marketplace and the distribution, platform, and incentive systems that connect businesses with valuable third-party solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to create a compounding ecosystem: better distribution generates merchant demand and stronger partner returns; those returns attract more high-quality apps; and those apps broaden Stripe’s product fit and value to users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Ecosystem Product Lead to own the strategy, roadmap, and outcomes for Stripe’s third-party app ecosystem, including the Stripe Apps Marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead both sides of the ecosystem: helping businesses discover and adopt trusted solutions, while enabling developers and partners to build successful products on Stripe. You will determine where Stripe should expand ecosystem coverage, improve the merchant journey from discovery through ongoing usage, and establish the product and operating foundations for a high-quality marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for Stripe’s third-party app ecosystem and Marketplace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the highest-value merchant needs and ecosystem gaps by product, segment, industry, and geography; determine when Stripe should build, partner, or enable third parties to address them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the merchant funnel from discovery and evaluation through installation, activation, usage, and retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand distribution beyond the Marketplace by surfacing relevant apps across Stripe’s product workflows, onboarding, Dashboard, support, and other high-intent experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve discovery through search, taxonomy, recommendations, personalization, and merchandising.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish marketplace standards for app quality, reliability, security, permissions, support, and data-use transparency so businesses can adopt third-party solutions confidently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the incentives, analytics, growth tools, and monetization capabilities that help developers build sustainable businesses and continue investing in Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor ecosystem health, including app coverage and quality, merchant conversion and retention, partner success, and incremental value to Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Engineering, Design, Data Science, Partnerships, Developer Relations, Marketing, Sales, Support, Risk, and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe’s ecosystem strategy with developers, technology partners, and users, using their feedback and quantitative evidence to guide product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders around priorities and trade-offs, and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements below. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product-management, engineering, product-focused founder, or equivalent experience, including ownership of a complex product area at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting strategy and driving execution for a platform, marketplace, ecosystem, developer product, or other multi-sided business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success improving acquisition, discovery, conversion, activation, or retention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment across user-facing products, technical platforms, partner economics, and marketplace trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading ambiguous initiatives across multiple product, engineering, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency with APIs, integrations, developer tooling, and platform products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define metrics and use qualitative and quantitative evidence to prioritize investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with external developers, technology partners, or enterprise users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including influencing senior stakeholders and leading across organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling an app marketplace, developer ecosystem, or two-sided platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketplace search, recommendations, ranking, personalization, or contextual distribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing partner monetization, incentives, or revenue-sharing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise SaaS workflows such as CRM, ERP, ecommerce, support, reporting, or quote-to-cash.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or another regulated technology environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience taking a platform or marketplace from 0→1 and scaling its adoption and operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Ecosystem Risk Product Management team sits at the intersection of growth and protection. Our focus is twofold. We enable online businesses—including those in emerging and regulated industries—to start and grow on Stripe, while protecting consumers, merchants, and partners from financial crimes. We build financial infrastructure at scale that powers every transaction on Stripe, deliver merchant-facing UI and API experiences, and develop AI-driven solutions to some of the hardest and most exciting challenges in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision and multi-year roadmap for AI-powered financial crimes controls—spanning detection, investigation, information collection, and the UI and API surfaces that tie them together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build core infrastructure that underpins Stripe&#39;s growing suite of products and services. • Develop investigator tools that power accurate case reviews using the best of AI and human expertise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional execution by partnering closely with engineering, operations, design, data science, go-to-market, legal, and product teams across Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own success metrics, navigate complex trade-offs, drive prioritization, and measure outcomes with rigor to demonstrate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align leadership and stakeholders by synthesizing input from across the organization and external sources, and communicating a clear point of view to peers and executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor the external landscape—regulatory trends, emerging technologies, and competitive offerings—to inform strategy and identify opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Product Management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building infrastructure and user experiences at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of operating effectively in highly cross-functional environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial crimes or fraud prevention within financial services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to grow the GDP of the internet, and we won&#39;t stop until we&#39;ve made it easy for any business anywhere to participate in the digital economy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Governments around the world are fundamentally changing how businesses report and exchange transactions. Continuous Transaction Controls (CTC) and e-invoicing mandates — now active or imminent in France, Germany, Spain, Poland, and across Latin America — require businesses to transmit structured invoice data through certified government networks in real time. For Stripe&#39;s global user base, compliant e-invoicing is rapidly becoming a prerequisite for conducting commerce, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re building the e-invoicing infrastructure that makes this invisible for Stripe users. That means embedding compliant invoice generation, validation, and transmission directly into Stripe Billing and Invoicing — abstracting the full complexity of regional mandates and network certification behind a seamless product experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact, greenfield role. You&#39;ll own Stripe&#39;s e-invoicing product end-to-end: setting the strategy, driving execution, and making Stripe the go-to solution for businesses navigating the global shift to real-time invoicing compliance. You&#39;ll work at the intersection of product, engineering, partnerships, and go-to-market — and you&#39;ll be laying the foundation for a capability that will matter to every Stripe user operating in a mandated market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the e-invoicing product vision and roadmap, translating complex and evolving regulatory requirements into a coherent multi-year strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive Stripe&#39;s expansion across mandated global markets (France, Germany, Spain, Poland) and into Latin America, sequencing coverage pragmatically against enforcement timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead build, buy, and partner decisions — evaluating the right combination of internal investment and external capabilities to meet compliance deadlines without sacrificing long-term product quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own the end-to-end user journey: from onboarding (including business identity verification) to live invoice transmission via certified networks like Peppol&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Billing, Invoicing, Tax, and Connect teams to embed e-invoicing as a native part of Stripe&#39;s financial infrastructure — not a bolted-on feature&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish quality, reliability, and activation metrics that hold every component of the e-invoicing stack accountable, and use those metrics to drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM, Sales, and Solutions Engineering to position Stripe as the leading e-invoicing solution for upmarket and enterprise customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe credibly with regulators, certification bodies, and industry partners as we build direct relationships with key tax authorities and networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with at least 2 years in a B2B fintech, payments, tax, or compliance-adjacent product domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with the e-invoicing landscape — you understand CTC frameworks, structured invoice formats (Factur-X, XRechnung, PEPPOL BIS), and the regulatory dynamics driving mandates in Europe and Latin America&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency: you can credibly partner with engineers on API design, data schemas, and network integration architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to run a build/buy/partner analysis and translate the output into concrete roadmap decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience launching products across multiple markets simultaneously, including navigating localization, regulatory compliance, and differing user needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional leadership — you get things done across Engineering, Legal, Finance, and GTM without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, direct communication: you can distill a complex compliance landscape into a compelling product narrative for both internal stakeholders and external audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating third-party technology providers or acquisitions into a core product platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Stripe Billing, Invoicing, or Tax products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience building toward Peppol access point certification or direct integrations with national tax authority platforms (e.g., Chorus Pro, KSeF)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to B2B invoicing workflows in mid-market or enterprise contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role, why now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;E-invoicing is one of the most consequential shifts in global business compliance in a decade, and Stripe is early in building the infrastructure to make it effortless. You&#39;ll have the mandate, the resources, and the cross-functional backing to build something significant — and the chance to make Stripe synonymous with world-class e-invoicing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is an equal opportunity employer. We look for people with exceptional abilities, who are excited by hard problems and big opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, manage their businesses, and grow their revenue. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a significant amount of work ahead. You’ll have an opportunity to help put the global economy within everyone’s reach.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Foreign Exchange team builds the products and infrastructure that help Stripe users operate across currencies. Businesses increasingly operate globally from the moment they launch, collecting revenue, holding balances, paying suppliers, and managing expenses across multiple currencies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Managing those currencies remains fragmented. Finance teams must decide what to hold, when to convert, how to manage currency exposure, and how to reconcile the results. Today, these workflows often span banks, spreadsheets, treasury systems, and specialist FX providers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is uniquely positioned to simplify this. We sit at the center of the payments, Billing, balances, payouts, and settlement flows that create a business’s currency needs. Our vision is to make Stripe the financial home for businesses operating internationally, with a unified offering for holding, converting, and managing currencies and FX risk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A core part of this vision is making currency management agentic. We believe software agents will increasingly help businesses understand their FX position, recommend actions, and manage currencies within defined policies and controls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This could include Stripe-native agents that monitor exposure and take approved actions. It could also mean enabling customers’ own agents to use Stripe’s infrastructure to understand balances and exposures, obtain pricing, execute conversions or hedges, and reconcile the results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make Stripe the currency-management layer that both people and agents can build on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will build these capabilities both for globally operating businesses and for the platforms and marketplaces that use Connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Product Manager to build a new area of Stripe’s FX and currency-management offering. This is a zero-to-one product role at the intersection of FX, treasury, and agentic AI. You will help define what agentic currency management should look like. That could mean Stripe-native agents that understand exposure, recommend actions, and execute within customer-defined policies. It could also mean enabling customers’ own agents to use Stripe’s FX infrastructure to understand balances, obtain pricing, manage risk, execute transactions, and reconcile the results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work directly with globally operating businesses to understand their most important currency-management problems. You will identify the right initial product wedge and take it from discovery through launch and iteration. Today, treasury teams assemble exposures from multiple systems, determine hedge requirements, monitor changing positions, request pricing, execute trades, and reconcile the results. We believe much of this workflow can become continuous, intelligent, and increasingly automated.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You might build products that combine Stripe’s real-time view of payments, balances, and settlement activity with customer forecasts and policies to identify exposures and recommend actions. You might also define the APIs, permissions, controls, and financial primitives that allow customer or third-party agents to safely take those actions through Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, these systems could move from surfacing insights to requesting quotes, executing conversions or hedges, rebalancing positions, and escalating exceptions within clearly defined permissions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will determine which intelligence Stripe should provide directly, which capabilities we should expose for others to build on, where humans should remain in the decision loop, and how we evaluate whether agents are making good decisions. Your product area could also include automated conversion and balance policies, recurring currency-management workflows, or capabilities distributed through Connect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The opportunity is broad. Your job will be to make it focused. You will determine where Stripe can create differentiated value, build the first product, measure whether it works, and use those learnings to shape the roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Engineering and Design on product experiences, APIs, data models, agent behavior, controls, and system reliability. You will also partner with Treasury, Risk, Legal, Finance, Sales, and Product Marketing to ensure the products are economically sound, operationally scalable, and ready for customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand how global businesses and platforms manage currencies, including holding, converting, forecasting, hedging, and reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for a focused area of Stripe’s FX and currency-management offering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-value customer problems and take new products from discovery through launch, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Stripe’s approach to agentic currency management, including Stripe-native experiences, agent-ready APIs, permissions, controls, and evaluation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering and Design to build simple, reliable products across user experiences, APIs, data models, and financial infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Treasury, Risk, Legal, Finance, Sales, and Product Marketing to ensure products are economically sound, operationally scalable, and successful with customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer insights and product results to shape Stripe’s broader FX and currency-management strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. Preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, including taking technically complex products from problem definition through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to turn ambiguous customer problems into clear product strategies and focused roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building financial infrastructure, enterprise software, APIs, regulated products, AI-native products, or similarly complex systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and experience partnering with engineers on APIs, data flows, reliability, and system behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer instincts and experience translating complex financial or operational workflows into simple, scalable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical judgment and ability to make decisions with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, including the ability to explain product decisions, risks, and tradeoffs across technical and nontechnical teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with foreign exchange, multi-currency products, treasury, cross-border money movement, hedging, or financial risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-native or agentic products, especially systems that can recommend or take actions within defined controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for finance or treasury teams at globally operating businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with API-first, configurable, or automated financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the economics, accounting, liquidity, regulatory, or operational considerations involved in FX products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is open to remote candidates located anywhere within the Eastern Time Zone.&amp;nbsp; Global Payouts empowers Stripe users to move money effortlessly, quickly, and securely to anyone, anywhere. Businesses rely on us to distribute billions of dollars to employees, contractors, sellers, and claimants across our Dashboard, APIs, and platform integrations via Financial Accounts.We are gaining rapid momentum across both self-serve and enterprise segments. Our demand spans high-growth fintechs, leading AI platforms, and some of the world&#39;s largest marketplaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are now entering a decisive phase of expansion. Over the next 12–18 months, the capabilities we build robust cross-border infrastructure, advanced enterprise controls, and tailored vertical-specific features will determine whether Global Payouts becomes the definitive default for businesses distributing money at scale. This role sits at the absolute center of that mission.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager to spearhead our cross-border expansion and enterprise capabilities. This is a high-impact, broad-scope role where you will set the strategic vision and drive execution across two pillars essential to our hyper-growth:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-border: You will expand the reach and competitive edge of our cross-border infrastructure by building out rate locking, local bank account coverage, and cross-border card rails. Crucially, you will lead the productization of fee passthrough—translating a bespoke solution originally built for a major AI platform into a broadly available, highly scalable capability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enterprise: You will define and deliver the advanced controls, reporting, and billing features required by sophisticated, high-volume operators. This includes recipient tax reporting, two-step confirmation workflows, enterprise billing models (e.g., IC+, platform fees), and robust security access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Across both domains, you will partner directly with Sales, Partnerships, and Go-to-Market (GTM) teams to convert active enterprise demand into durable product investments, developing industry-specific capabilities for key verticals like remittance and fintech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Border Expansion&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap for global payout infrastructure, prioritizing rate locking, local bank coverage, and cross-border card rails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Productize fee passthrough, transforming a custom integration into a scalable, self-serve offering to drive rapid adoption among new users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design industry-specific solutions for high-value verticals (e.g., remittance, fintech) rooted in deep user research and strategic GTM alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Enterprise Capabilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship enterprise-grade controls and reporting tools, including recipient tax reporting, two-step confirmation workflows, and advanced security access controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect enterprise billing primitives—such as Interchange Plus (IC+) and platform fees—to enable flexible, scalable commercial models for large payout operators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and Partnerships to support active enterprise deals and PUA requests, distilling bespoke client requirements into scalable, prioritized product investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate seamlessly across Financial Accounts, Connect, and the broader money movement platform to ensure new capabilities integrate cleanly and compound in value over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track success metrics, holding yourself accountable to measurable adoption targets across both self-serve and enterprise segments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Who you are&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is open to remote candidates located anywhere within the Eastern Time Zone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end-to-end—defining strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping products that serve multiple user segments or operate across significant technical or regulatory complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work with Sales, GTM, or enterprise customers and translate their needs into scalable product investments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts: comfort with data, metrics, and building the measurement framework before you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication: crisp specs, clear PRDs, and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, financial infrastructure, or other regulated industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working on enterprise or B2B products with complex commercial or compliance requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Product Manager, Global Self-Serve Product&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the team&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Self-Serve Product team&#39;s goal is to make Stripe the #1 self-serve financial infrastructure provider for users outside the U.S. We drive product-led growth for the millions of users who adopt Stripe without a sales relationship, and we own self-serve activation goals across our ex-US business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a cross-functional team of Engineers, Data Scientists, Growth Marketing Managers, Designers, and Product Managers, organized around three focus areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing our self-serve domestic business across a portfolio of our core, mature markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growing cross-border self-serve business across the next wave of emerging markets and launching bespoke registration, onboarding and upsell pathways for new markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raising the bar on the quality of the localized experience of our international users by building and improving our localization platform at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Most of Stripe&#39;s future users outside the US will never speak to a salesperson—they&#39;ll discover, sign up, and scale on Stripe entirely on their own. Getting that self-serve journey right, in every market and language, is one of the biggest growth opportunities ahead of us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Product Manager to own self-serve activation and growth across our ex-US business. You&#39;ll set the strategy for how we win self-serve users in international markets and then make it real—turning funnel data and customer insight into a sequenced roadmap, and shipping the experiments and features that move the metrics.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The right person for this role thinks like a growth PM and a founder: you&#39;re fluent in funnels and experimentation, you have genuine taste for 0-to-1 product, and you move fast under ambiguity. You bring deep user empathy to localizing Stripe with contextual relevance, and you think in systems and platforms—turning experimental features into scaled growth levers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the self-serve growth roadmap: identify the highest-leverage opportunities to grow activation across our ex-US markets, and build the case for investment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of our customers—from bootstrapped solopreneurs to well-funded founders—synthesizing funnel metrics, experiment results, and time in the product into sharp hypotheses about what will drive growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to ship—you&#39;ll drive specs, prioritization, and execution with a high degree of hands-on involvement, and run experiments to build conviction in your roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale what works: take wins proven in small samples and roll them out through our localization and recommendation platforms, so the right experience reaches each market and use case&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Stripe&#39;s global product teams to ensure regional needs are reflected in platform decisions, and advocate for regional investment at the right moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have 7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time spent shipping 0-to-1 products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You reason from first principles—breaking ambiguous growth problems down to fundamentals, forming a sharp point of view, and moving fast under uncertainty with the ownership of a founder&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re data-savvy: fluent in funnels, metrics, and experimentation, you let the numbers sharpen your instincts, and you know when a test earns conviction and when it only adds noise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong product taste and are technically comfortable—you sweat the details of a localized experience (message clarity, contextual guidance) and can engage credibly with engineers on API design and system tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re an exceptional communicator—verbal and written—who can influence without authority across a matrixed organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re based in Singapore or have a strong reason to be&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why Stripe&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is still early in its presence outside the US, which means the person in this role will have genuine influence over how we show up in some of the world&#39;s most important emerging markets. You&#39;ll have the scope of a startup with the resources of a company that processes hundreds of billions of dollars a year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Bridge&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re creating an entirely new payments platform, built with stablecoins, to simplify global money movement. Bridge enables faster, cheaper payments and borderless access to dollars via stablecoins. Through our APIs, businesses can send and receive funds across borders faster and cheaper vs. SWIFT and other fiat-only rails. Our virtual accounts enable international consumers and businesses to easily access, store, and spend US dollars. Our payouts infrastructure enables platforms to disburse USD to anyone globally. We believe many trillions of dollars will move and settle through stablecoin payment rails. Bridge is pulling this future forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a small team of people who have previously built financial infrastructure at some of the world&#39;s leading companies (Coinbase, Stripe, Square, Brex, Upstart, DoorDash, Airbnb), and each and every one of them chose Bridge because they fundamentally believe that stablecoins will be a critical piece of financial infrastructure that allows for the improvement of global money movement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join our Issuance Product team to shape the future of financial access and infrastructure. We&#39;re not just improving global payments, we&#39;re reinventing them with modern rails that allow for fast, cheap transactions at any size. You will build a platform that powers issuing compliant stablecoins in US/EU and beyond. We work with some of the largest fintechs, crypto companies, blockchains and more. This is your chance to lead meaningful innovation from day one, redefining the way businesses and people exchange value globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a world class issuance platform that has the scale to power billions of dollars of transactions and issued stablecoins. Product areas include liquidity delivery, reserves management, mint/burn infrastructure, rewards, on-chain/crypto smart contracts, and launching custom stablecoins.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product features from ideation to launch, collaborating with designers, engineers, and cross-functional partners such as legal and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of our users’ needs, operational landscape, and competitive environment&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;across international markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own outcomes end-to-end, using data, feedback, and rapid iteration to refine your approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make tough prioritization calls, balancing user needs, technical feasibility, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-traffic features at scale, ensuring security, speed, and reliability for millions of users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Need to Thrive&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empathy for users&lt;/strong&gt;: You’re passionate about uncovering and solving pain points.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: You never stop asking “why” and dig into both qualitative and quantitative data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Owner’s mentality&lt;/strong&gt;: You tackle challenges head-on and drive solutions with conviction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative spirit&lt;/strong&gt;: You work seamlessly with team members but aren’t afraid to make the call when needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Clarity and simplicity&lt;/strong&gt;: You translate complex systems into intuitive, straightforward user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bias for learning&lt;/strong&gt;: You embrace mistakes as opportunities to grow and improve quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in product management or a related role, with a proven record of delivering impactful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success working with engineers, designers, and external partners to build complex systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and comfort navigating ecosystem and platform-level challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating APIs, managing developer platforms, or building ecosystem-driven products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building regulated infrastructure in fintech, payments, or crypto.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re ready to shape the future of how money moves, we want to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link team builds the premier consumer network for next-generation commerce, leveraging our base of 300M+ registered consumers to pioneer the future of Identity, Consumer Finance, and AI-driven transactions. While our foundation was built on high-conversion merchant payments and a flexible digital wallet, we are expanding far beyond. We are building the infrastructure for a world where AI agents transact on your behalf, stablecoins go mainstream, and identity dictates how money moves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We think of Link as the wallet for the internet — and we&#39;re building for what&#39;s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build the Link App experience across web and native — building the wallet product consumers need to feel confident, excited, and inspired by the new ways payments and identity are changing online.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;That means being a true champion of the consumer: end-to-end owner of core features, a cross-functional partner to Engineering, Design, and GTM, and an active voice in shaping Link&#39;s consumer strategy alongside Link leadership. You&#39;ll define, build, and scale new and existing products — informed by consumer insights and data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technical PM who operates with a high degree of autonomy and drive. You care deeply about craft and impact — the only thing that really matters to you is getting well-built products into users&#39; hands. You&#39;re probably already exploring how AI is changing how products get built and what it means for the PM role; you might even have a few half-finished side projects that prove it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the consumer perspective — spend time with users, partner closely with Engineering, GTM, and Operations, and synthesize feedback and market signals into clear product direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the voice of the Link consumer, both within the team and across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive an ambitious roadmap, from expanding core capabilities to leading nascent initiatives through to maturity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish team pace, clear prioritization, and rigorous execution standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with Engineering, Design, Data Science, Marketing, Sales, and Operations to ship cohesive, frictionless experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in a product or technical role, with experience shipping world-class consumer products at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High taste, design empathy, and sharp judgment — can put yourself in the shoes of consumers and be a steward of crafting great experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous with data — comfortable digging into metrics, writing SQL when needed, and thinking from first principles to deliver the right results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire for continuous product improvement; able to optimize for shipping a portfolio of small, medium, and large releases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership mindset — works on whatever it takes to solve problems and delight consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, with a talent for distilling user problems into precise, actionable framing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing high-stakes external partnerships — aligning on milestones and executing integrations end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives with a high level of autonomy and responsibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on consumer financial products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building brand new products or working in a startup environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with GTM teams to bring a new product to market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is looking for AI-enabled builders. If you are looking to apply your skills at a company that deeply cares about quality with global scale, we&#39;d love to hear from you. We&#39;re looking for early career engineers who can solve problems, write code, ship features, and iterate quickly, all with a core focus on elevating Stripe’s craft and quality. This is a 12-month intensive training program where you will be paired with a host team within Stripe, given a broad mandate, and ideally placed full time in a Product Manager role after completion of the program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Embed yourself deeply with Stripe’s users&lt;/strong&gt;. Our users expect Stripe to provide the best financial technology that is also enabled with deep insights, automations and features that only AI can solve. You will work with users on a daily basis to understand their needs and forge new solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the entire lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll take a user problem from initial discovery through design, implementation, deployment, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build on a home team, learn across Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll start on one team (e.g., Dashboard, Docs, Crypto, Payment Methods) and eventually land a full time role as a Product Manager.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ownership mindset&lt;/strong&gt;. When you hit technical constraints, unclear requirements, or process friction, you&#39;ll figure it out. You&#39;ll navigate codebases, track down answers, and push through obstacles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Optimize how you work, not just what you build&lt;/strong&gt;. You&#39;ll constantly refine your workflows and tooling to increase your leverage. Every bottleneck is an opportunity to automate or improve; and then show others how to achieve our end goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What success looks like&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Users win&lt;/strong&gt;: You deliver meaningful features and improvements week after week. Users see real impact from your work.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality and speed&lt;/strong&gt;: You maintain Stripe&#39;s quality bar while moving faster than traditional team-based development.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence&lt;/strong&gt;: Your approaches to AI-enabled development spread to the rest of the team. You help others level up their AI skills.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Logistics&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: In-person at Stripe offices in San Francisco, Seattle, or New York. You&#39;ll benefit from direct collaboration and a strong support network as we figure this out together.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience level&lt;/strong&gt;: New grad or 0-2 years of professional experience, with a CS or engineering degree. We care more about what you&#39;ve built (through internships, personal projects, or school) than years of specific experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radar helps businesses prevent fraud and abuse without getting in the way of legitimate customers. We combine machine learning powered by Stripe’s global network with intuitive dashboard experiences and developer APIs, to give our users comprehensive controls and insights to protect their business against threats ranging from payment fraud and card testing to bot and free trial abuse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud doesn’t stand still, and it isn’t limited to checkout. As businesses launch new products and business models, attackers find new ways to exploit them. We obsess about understanding those attacks, identifying defenses that work, and making sophisticated fraud prevention simple for the businesses that depend on us to help them protect and grow their revenue with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Radar team, you’ll help customers, developers, and partners bring fraud prevention naturally into the systems and workflows they rely on. You’ll shape products that make fraud management feel effortless, connecting Radar’s capabilities to the tools and experiences our users build and run.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of customer needs and commercial opportunities to shape what we build and how we bring it to market. Working closely with engineering, data science, design, and go-to-market teams, you’ll build products and relationships that deliver lasting value to customers and partners. You’ll connect technical decisions to commercial outcomes while maintaining a high bar for reliability, craft, and the details that make complex products feel simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the payments and fraud landscape, how businesses manage risk, and the systems and workflows they rely on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with customers, developers, and partners to uncover unmet needs, understand integration challenges, and identify opportunities to build broadly useful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a clear product strategy and roadmap, prioritizing opportunities based on user impact, technical feasibility, and business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering and data science to turn sophisticated fraud control and monitoring capabilities into reliable APIs, intuitive tools, and well-crafted developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product development from ideation through launch, setting the pace, scoping thoughtfully, prioritizing ruthlessly, and executing with rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate deeply with sales, marketing, and partnerships teams to identify opportunities, validate demand, and drive the adoption of new experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with customers and partners through early implementations, using hands-on feedback to improve documentation, onboarding, and the path from initial evaluation to production use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own metrics for integration success, adoption, retention, revenue, and user value; use results to guide product and commercial decisions and communicate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly with internal and external stakeholders about priorities, trade-offs, progress, and results, building alignment across teams you don’t directly manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a rigorous approach to quantitative and qualitative evidence. You’re comfortable digging into data, writing SQL when needed, and connecting product decisions to user and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful, with experience taking products from zero to one. You thrive in early-stage environments, test ideas quickly, and turn what you learn into products that scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and business acumen. You understand how customer needs, market dynamics, and product differentiation translate into adoption and durable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional leadership, including experience partnering with B2B sales teams on customer discovery, technical evaluation, and commercialization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping Dashboard and API products, with empathy for end users and developers alike.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing pricing and monetization models for B2B products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineers on APIs, system architecture, and integration trade-offs, and to explain those decisions clearly to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling complex user problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and a high bar for product quality. You do what it takes to solve user problems and care deeply about the details of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building fraud prevention, risk, security, or ML powered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building developer platforms and working with integration partners, including navigating technical dependencies and high-stakes external relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Radar helps businesses prevent fraud and abuse without getting in the way of legitimate customers. We combine machine learning powered by Stripe’s global network with intuitive dashboard experiences and developer APIs, to give our users comprehensive controls and insights to protect their business against threats ranging from payment fraud and card testing to bot and free trial abuse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fraud doesn’t stand still, and it isn’t limited to checkout. As businesses launch new products and business models, attackers find new ways to exploit them. We obsess about understanding those attacks, identifying defenses that work, and making sophisticated fraud prevention simple for the businesses that depend on us to help them protect and grow their revenue with confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Radar team, you’ll work directly with customers to understand the novel fraud and abuse attacks they face, identify the most important problems to solve, and turn those insights into product strategy and a roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work at the intersection of customers, engineering, data science, design, and commercial teams to shape what we build and bring it to market. Your work will span the fraud and abuse detection and control capabilities at the heart of Radar and the user and developer experiences that put those capabilities into our customers’ hands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires both urgency and taste. You’ll move quickly as threats evolve, without compromising on reliability, craft, or the details that make complex products feel beautifully simple.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the fraud and abuse landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigate emerging attacks with customers, assess their financial and operational impact, and distinguish isolated incidents from opportunities to build broadly useful defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate findings into a product strategy and roadmap, prioritizing the defenses that deliver the greatest customer and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, data science, and design to explore signals, shape solutions, and rapidly turn effective defenses into scalable, reliable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the pace for the team by scoping the product thoughtfully, prioritizing ruthlessly, and executing with high rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with sales, marketing, and customer-facing teams to validate demand, coordinate launches, and help customers adopt and maximize the value they get from new capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own product performance, user experience, and business metrics to guide iteration and communicate progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly analytical, with a rigorous approach to quantitative and qualitative evidence. You’re comfortable digging into data, writing SQL when needed, and defining metrics that connect product decisions to user outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrappy and resourceful, with experience taking products from zero to one. You find ways to test ideas quickly, learn from real users, and turn early solutions into products that scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial and business acumen. You understand how customer problems translate into willingness to pay, adoption, and durable business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven cross-functional leadership, including experience partnering with B2B sales teams on customer discovery, product positioning, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping Dashboard and API products, with empathy for both end users and developers and an understanding of their different workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with substantial ambiguity. You can set direction with incomplete information, make thoughtful trade-offs, and adapt as new evidence emerges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency to go deep with engineering and data teams on complex systems, understand constraints, and evaluate alternative approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling complex customer problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and a high bar for product quality. You do what it takes to solve user problems and care deeply about the details of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building fraud prevention, risk, security, or ML powered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing machine learning powered products and evaluating trade-offs between detection effectiveness and customer friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building tools for fraud analysts or risk teams, or developer products that support real-time decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering, data science, or similar technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI agents are increasingly building Stripe integrations alongside professional developers and vibe coders. To build and test these integrations safely, without affecting live accounts or moving real funds, agents require isolated sandbox environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own the end-to-end product experience for Stripe Sandboxes and the broader testing platform, guiding the journey from a developer&#39;s first sandbox creation to an agent validating complex payment flows at scale. Because this role touches the testing workflow of every Stripe product, your work will have company-wide impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with external developers and internal Stripe teams to translate user feedback into intuitive developer experiences and platform capabilities. Partnering with engineering, design, and user research, you will deliver features that enable every developer on Stripe to build faster and with greater confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be responsible for product management of Stripe Sandboxes and the testing platform that every developer building on Stripe depends on. You&#39;ll deliver platform features that give developers the isolation, simulation, and observability they need to test their integrations with confidence. You&#39;ll define the vision and roadmap for how the testing platform evolves to support new use cases, including agentic tooling and new Stripe products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact daily with users, Stripe developers, and internal product teams to validate product ideas, requirements, and prototypes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and design to ship functionality that delights developers testing their Stripe integrations, balances impact with engineering cost, and delivers measurable results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the vision, strategy, and roadmap for Stripe Sandboxes and the testing platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define key success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with user researchers to test hypotheses and understand user pain points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape how testing and developer experiences adapt with agentic tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience, with a track record of shipping products that solve real user problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise gained through building and owning technical, developer-facing products or tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to define strategy, set goals, and drive execution across cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to structure ambiguous concepts clearly and from first principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a collaborative environment involving different functions, stakeholders, and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy using social media to interact directly with customers for feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;ve founded a business or startup, taking a product from 0 to 1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You only ship functionality after you&#39;ve personally test-driven it and made substantial edits to the documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Apps connect Stripe with the tools businesses already use, bringing relevant data and workflows into the Stripe Dashboard and third-party systems. The Strategic Apps team owns a portfolio of integrations with enterprise systems that are critical to our users’ workflows—from quote-to-cash and support to reporting. We help users embed Stripe more deeply into the way they run their businesses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Staff Product Manager to set the strategy and lead execution for Strategic Apps. You will own a portfolio of existing and new integrations, including those with systems such as Salesforce, and determine where Stripe should invest based on user needs, Stripe’s product and industry priorities, and market signals. You will work across Stripe and directly with external partners to deliver reliable, high-quality integrations that drive adoption and business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the vision, product strategy, roadmap, and success metrics for a portfolio of strategic apps, making and communicating clear trade-offs amid significant ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, prioritize, and validate the highest-value user problems and integration opportunities through direct user research, ecosystem analysis, and quantitative evidence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams across Engineering, Design, Data Science, Finance, Sales, User Support, Marketing, Partner Management, and other product teams to deliver and evolve integrations end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering to define product requirements, technical approach, and quality standards for integrations, including APIs, documentation, edge cases, reliability, security, compliance, and ongoing maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish feedback loops and measurement plans before launch; use product, business, and user metrics to assess efficacy, diagnose changes in performance, and continuously improve adoption, retention, and revenue outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe’s product strategy with strategic technology partners and enterprise users, building productive relationships with product and technical counterparts and incorporating their feedback into roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive launches, beta programs, user acceptance testing, and go-to-market readiness in partnership with Marketing, Sales, Partner Management, and Support; ensure teams have the materials and operating model needed to support adoption at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make and drive important cross-functional decisions, align senior stakeholders around a shared strategy, and communicate progress, risks, and outcomes clearly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance new feature development with investment in quality, reliability, technical debt, and foundational platform capabilities across the app portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how Stripe builds and operates strategic integrations by turning user, partner, and performance signals into scalable product and process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant product-management, engineering, or equivalent experience, including ownership of a high-quality product or feature area at scale or a major evolution of an existing product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting product strategy and driving execution across multiple cross-functional teams or a complex product area, from ambiguous problem definition through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to use qualitative and quantitative evidence to define success metrics, evaluate product performance, and make prioritization decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and fluency working with engineers on API-based products, integrations, technical constraints, and product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging directly with enterprise users and external technology partners, and translating their needs into clear product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a track record of influencing senior stakeholders and leading through organizational boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with enterprise business systems and workflows, such as CRM, ERP, quote-to-cash, support, or reporting platforms; familiarity with Salesforce, Oracle, SAP, or Microsoft Dynamics is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling platform, ecosystem, marketplace, or partner-integrated products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience growing product adoption, usage, or revenue through product-led and go-to-market initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, financial technology, or other regulated technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in computer science, engineering, or another technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Technologies builds the products, platforms, and capabilities behind Stripe’s support experiences. The team helps users resolve issues quickly, supports internal teams, and creates reusable technology that improves support across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role focuses on the complex support needs of Platforms and Connect. Platforms, connected accounts, and their customers each have different relationships with Stripe, access levels, and responsibilities. Resolving an issue often requires understanding who owns the account, which permissions apply, how products are configured, and which party should provide support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is building the foundations for more contextual support across this multi-party ecosystem. A key part of the work is improving Stripe’s customer-facing AI agent so it can understand these relationships, handle complex cases, and provide accurate, personalized resolutions at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;As a Product Manager for Support Experience, you will be responsible for improving the outcomes of Stripe’s user-facing&amp;nbsp;AI agent that holds 100k+ conversations per week.&amp;nbsp;You’ll be at the forefront of applied AI, solving problems for businesses and consumers, and redefining what great can look&amp;nbsp;like.&amp;nbsp;You’ll directly build agent capabilities to solve real-world user problems. That means getting hands-on with prompts,&amp;nbsp;evals, skills, tools and the machinery that lets you introspect and identify opportunities within the conversational&amp;nbsp;experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the product strategy and roadmap for Support Technologies serving Platform and Connect use cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a deep understanding of the needs of platform operators, connected accounts, Stripe support teams, and platform support teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the capabilities and effectiveness of Stripe’s user-facing AI agent for Platform and Connect support experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring support problems and translate them into reusable product, platform, and AI agent capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, ship, and iterate on the prompts, skills, tools, and evaluations that enable the AI agent to solve real-world user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve how account relationships, roles, permissions, product configurations, and support history inform routing and resolution across AI and human-assisted support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tools that help the AI agent and support teams understand complex Platform and Connect issues and take the right next action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enable platforms to support their connected accounts more effectively through appropriate tooling, visibility, automation, and contextual guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help clarify whether Stripe, the platform, or another party is responsible for resolving a user’s issue, and route the issue accordingly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create continuous improvement loops that turn insights from AI agent conversations and support interactions into scaled solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Platform, Connect, and conversational AI product teams to incorporate support capabilities into critical product journeys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, excluding internships and co-ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep user empathy and a high bar for user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-team initiatives from ideation through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading technical products or a background in computer science or a similar field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps our users extend their online presence to the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has made it to accept online payments. Whether a user is building a superb retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling mobile point-of-sale payments at their next event, Terminal gives them the building blocks to do it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Almost every Terminal experience starts with a developer building the integration. The Developer Experiences team owns that work: the SDKs, APIs, integration primitives, documentation, and example apps that developers—and, increasingly, AI agents—use to build on Terminal. In this role, you’ll own how developers and agents integrate in-person payments with Stripe, from making their first test charge to running their integrations at scale in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own the roadmap and execution for Terminal’s developer-facing surface: the client SDKs (JavaScript, iOS, Android, React Native, .NET, and Java), the integration primitives developers depend on, and the documentation and example apps that help them make their first successful charge. You’ll work with engineering to ship capabilities that make Terminal faster to integrate and more reliable to run while supporting newer patterns such as server-driven integration and agent-built integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and execution for Terminal’s developer experience within the team’s strategy: break the roadmap into milestones, define requirements, prioritize work, and drive delivery through sprint planning while making the tradeoffs required by a broad surface area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk regularly with external developers, platforms, and internal Stripe teams to validate ideas, requirements, and prototypes and turn what you learn into better developer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and design to ship functionality that delights developers building on Terminal, balancing impact against engineering cost and delivering measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the integration primitives developers depend on—including connection tokens, integration authentication, device attestation, and connectivity—to ensure that developers can build secure, reliable in-person payment experiences consistently across every SDK and platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the direction for integrations at scale, from server-driven integration and reusable example apps to agentic tooling that allows AI agents to build and test safely, and maintain a high bar for Terminal’s documentation and accessibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data to form a point of view, set success metrics, and determine whether changes are working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate decisions and status to stakeholders and use your technical judgment to help the team make tradeoff decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience or equivalent experience, with a track record of shipping products that solve real user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical expertise gained by building and owning developer-facing products such as APIs, SDKs, or developer tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of driving execution across cross-functional teams within an established product vision and strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to make complex concepts accessible and structure ambiguous problems from first principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working across many functions, stakeholders, and subject-matter experts and engaging in healthy, respectful debate in pursuit of shared goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mobile SDKs, including iOS or Android, or cross-platform frameworks such as React Native.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with payments, in-person commerce, or hardware-adjacent products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building for AI agents or developing agentic tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and launching zero-to-one products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on approach: you test-drive integrations yourself and improve the documentation before shipping functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps our users extend their online presence to the physical world. The Terminal team’s mission is to make accepting in-person payments as easy as accepting online payments with the Stripe API. With Terminal, businesses can unlock in-person payment use cases that fit their business model, whether that’s creating a superb retail experience, extending their website to a pop-up store, or enabling a mobile point of sale at their next event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Terminal is one of the fastest-growing products at Stripe, and we are building a uniquely powerful unified commerce platform for global enterprises. The platform offers a single integration for in-person payments, fast and low-cost cross-border money movement, AI-powered optimizations and fraud protection, reporting, and differentiated ways to pay.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the product manager responsible for enterprise success within Terminal Payments, you’ll deliver an end-to-end payments and commerce platform for enterprise users. You’ll work directly with users and partners to understand their needs, identify investments that serve multiple businesses, and turn those opportunities into products and integrations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a multi-year strategy for Terminal’s enterprise payments capabilities, build alignment, and translate that strategy into roadmaps and measurable objectives and key results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead product discovery and roadmapping conversations with enterprise users, balancing their specific requirements with investments that benefit Stripe’s broader platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build integrations that expand Terminal’s enterprise capabilities, including gift cards, private-label credit cards, tax refunds, and third-party point-of-sale systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate opportunities to meet enterprise loyalty and customer relationship management needs through Stripe-built offerings, and scale host-to-host capabilities for users that operate their own payment gateways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and product teams, including Core Payments, Optimized Checkout Suite, and Agentic Commerce, to deliver integrated experiences and resolve technical and product trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with partnerships, marketing, legal, and industry teams on user and partner needs, go-to-market activities, and representing Terminal at trade shows and partner conferences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product Strategy and Operations to deliver in-person support and installation services for enterprise users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of product management experience or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on business-to-business products, ideally with a track record of building for enterprise scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical proficiency and systems-thinking skills, ideally with a degree in engineering or computer science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills, including the ability to make complex concepts accessible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Demonstrated success and strong execution track record in building payment products&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Treasury for Platforms sits at the center of Stripe&#39;s evolution from a payments processor to a complete financial infrastructure provider. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and Treasury extends that mission by enabling marketplaces, software-as-a-service platforms, and fintechs to embed fully featured financial services directly into their own products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By handling bank partnerships, compliance, and regulatory requirements, we allow platforms to launch quickly while focusing on the core parts of their business. We pair this with embedded user interfaces, managed support, and rich treasury features so our users can build great financial experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, our platforms serve a highly diverse set of use cases, from payout cards for on-demand workers and operational accounts for in-field purchases to financial accounts for small businesses. We proudly power industry-leading products like Shopify Balance and Ambrook Wallet, serving a rapidly growing roster of users across the United States.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Product Manager to own and drive critical Treasury for Platforms infrastructure and features, including new account types, checkbooks, and accounting integrations. You will take these products from alpha to general availability across consumer and commercial Treasury. You will work directly with platforms by joining sales calls, running product demos, and shaping integration paths. You will be the most technically fluent person in the room with the user and the most user-fluent person in the room with engineering. Ultimately, you’ll turn every platform into a financial hub for its users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the financial management needs of our diverse user base and how they can benefit from strong treasury features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a clear product strategy and roadmap that aligns with Stripe’s broader vision and market demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product development from ideation to launch, ensuring the delivery of high-value experiences for our users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with engineering, design, legal, and other teams to ensure cohesive execution and alignment across all phases of product development and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate for the Treasury for Platforms vision internally and externally, ensuring key stakeholders are informed and engaged.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of product management experience, with a strong track record of launching impactful products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mindset and willingness to do what it takes to solve problems and delight consumers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to handle and prioritize work in a fast-paced, dynamic environment while managing multiple projects and deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, with a talent for distilling user problems into precise, actionable framing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigorous approach to data, including comfort digging into metrics, writing SQL when needed, and thinking from first principles to deliver the right result.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in treasury services and financial account management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platforms with multiparty transaction capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing high-stakes external partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of international payments, foreign exchange, and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team&#39;s mission is to generate customer insights that inform Stripe&#39;s product strategy, and lead go-to-market for our suite of products. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation and Campaigns to name a few. Different from many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle, from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption post-launch.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking to hire a Product Marketing Manager to own go-to-market strategy and drive adoption for Stripe&#39;s data products — including Sigma, Data Pipeline, Database, and new products we’re incubating. As monetization grows more complex — from AI companies hyperscaling globally to enterprises integrating Stripe deeply into their operations — data has become a critical lever that helps businesses make better decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key owner of our GTM strategy for Stripe&#39;s data products, you&#39;ll need to quickly build a deep understanding of our products, the data analytics buyer, and our competitive differentiation. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the expert on our data analytics buyers — understand how data analysts, analytics engineers, and BI practitioners evaluate and adopt tools, and translate those insights into product roadmap recommendations and GTM strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own positioning and messaging for Stripe&#39;s data products, building a clear and differentiated point of view in a competitive market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end go-to-market for data product launches — from defining the narrative and target audience to developing the assets and programs that drive adoption across sold and self-serve motions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with demand generation and campaigns to design and execute programs that reach the data analytics buyer and accelerate product adoption at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build sales enablement — develop the messaging frameworks, competitive battlecards, and assets that help sales teams clearly articulate the value of Stripe&#39;s data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own competitive intelligence for the analytics and BI landscape, tracking competitors and turning that intelligence into differentiated positioning and sales tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define program KPIs and maintain accountability to measurable business outcomes across the data products portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product marketing experience, preferably in B2B tech.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A builder mentality with a strong bias to action. Comfortable with ambiguity, able to experiment and adapt at pace.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and presentation abilities, with a proven track record of distilling complex technical concepts into compelling narratives for executive and external audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional cross-functional leadership and ability to influence across all levels and functions, from senior leadership to project teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort toggling between strategy and execution — big picture to fine detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to translate customer and market insights into differentiated positioning and measurable GTM programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep familiarity with the data analytics ecosystem — BI tools, cloud data warehouses, and analytics workflows — and a proven ability to market to the data analyst or analytics engineer buyer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience marketing to technical audiences such as data engineers, analytics engineers, or developers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Power user (and builder) of AI-powered tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Product Marketing team&#39;s mission is to generate customer insights that inform Stripe&#39;s product strategy, and lead go-to-market for our suite of products. Product Marketing is a highly cross-functional role at Stripe, partnering closely with Product and Engineering, Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation and Campaigns to name a few. Different from many other Product Marketing teams, our team works across the entire product lifecycle, from helping shape the product, to driving launch and commercialization, to growing product adoption post-launch. We also drive both self-serve and sales-sold marketing efforts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an experienced product marketing leader to own our go-to-market strategy and grow adoption for Stripe Billing—which includes Subscriptions, Invoicing, and Metronome.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and lead the go-to-market strategy for all Billing products, including segmentation, target audiences, positioning, launches, and post-launch adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead, and develop a high-performing team of product marketers, setting clear priorities and raising the bar for strategic thinking, customer insight, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize customer, market, and competitive insights to inform product strategy, roadmap prioritization, and differentiated commercialization plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear, compelling positioning and messaging that translates complex revenue-management capabilities into value for executive and technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales, Partnerships, Demand Generation, and Campaigns to equip go-to-market teams with the narratives, enablement, and programs needed to engage enterprise customers effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional teams through high-stakes launches and growth initiatives, aligning senior stakeholders around decisions, sequencing, and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish success metrics and use customer, sales, and product data to assess performance, identify growth opportunities, and improve go-to-market strategy over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the product area in executive narratives, customer conversations, and key industry moments, building credibility with enterprise audiences and internal leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of product marketing experience, preferably in B2B technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience managing teams, with a proven record of building and leading high-performing, highly cross-functional teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience marketing to enterprise audiences, with a demonstrated ability to understand complex buying committees, long sales cycles, and sophisticated business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High comfort toggling between big-picture strategy and detailed execution, with a strong bias to action.&lt;/li&gt;
