&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Tax team helps ensure that Stripe’s products comply with applicable tax requirements. We partner with product teams to understand Stripe’s products, evolving product strategy, and desired business outcomes. We develop tax approaches that support those goals while maintaining tax integrity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We provide tax requirements to cross-functional partners and help ensure they’re implemented. We also identify process gaps and support finance operations across several functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced tax professional to focus on products developed by Stripe. You’ll help scale Stripe’s tax processes as we grow in a fast-paced environment. You’ll assess the tax implications of Stripe’s products and initiatives, then partner with cross-functional teams to develop and implement effective solutions that meet Stripe’s tax obligations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary tax contact for end-to-end product launch readiness, partnering with cross-functional teams on tax issues related to Stripe products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and assess tax issues associated with product launches, including indirect tax, information reporting, transfer pricing, and income tax, and work with tax subject matter experts to provide clear requirements to product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help draft and implement tax policies and procedures that affect product operations, keeping them current as tax laws change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal user-facing teams, including Account Management, Sales, and User Operations, in addressing product needs and user questions related to tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review internal processes and external user communications drafted by Marketing or User Operations to help ensure that tax-related documentation is clear and useful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with other tax projects as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 or more years of cross-border tax experience at an accounting or law firm, in-house, or in the financial services or payments industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An advanced degree or professional qualification in tax or law, such as a Certified Public Accountant certification, Juris Doctor, master’s degree in tax, or Master of Laws degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of tax subject areas such as indirect tax, information reporting, withholding, transfer pricing, and income tax reporting, with experience applying these rules in scalable operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing time, projects, and competing priorities in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to adapt your communication to different audiences and translate tax laws into requirements for product and engineering teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in both an accounting or law firm and an in-house tax role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in technology, payments, financial services, or another high-growth multinational business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience addressing the tax implications of cross-border product launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable tax processes and controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Professional Services Sales team works with our most strategic users; You will help customers accelerate their growth and adoption on Stripe. This role is responsible for leading strategic conversations during pre-sales that will transform the payments and financial infrastructure for leading enterprises, ultimately driving revenue growth through our professional service offerings.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Enterprise Services Manager, you will sell Professional Services engagements to strategic clients and drive Stripe’s future growth engine by building relationships with prospective users and turning them into happy Stripe users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the entire Professional Services sales cycle for enterprise companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Executives on named account lists to develop account plans aimed at winning and expanding Professional Services business with enterprise clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the success of Professional Services by managing and forecasting bookings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft custom proposals that align with clients&#39; business outcomes, utilizing services across Professional Services and partner offerings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise senior leadership in customer organizations on building business cases for digital transformation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead pre-sales workshops with customers, focusing on strategy, vision, discovery, and assessment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Professional Services deals, and build and negotiate contracts/Statements of Work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Product and Engineering teams to influence product strategy for large clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with GTM partners to integrate complementary strategies and drive mutual growth objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the delivery team with user insights to ensure that the delivery aligns with the desired business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional services sales experience, preferably at a technology company or a consulting firm, with a track record of top performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in pre-sales and sales of sizable service engagements, as well as in contract and Statement of Work (SOW) development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead large transformational engagements using disruptive technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives on the urgency and importance of working with our largest customers, achieving set objectives while balancing competing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand complex business requirements and develop tailored solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to navigate ambiguity to produce strategic insights and identify opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of the sales cycles associated with a SaaS product or technology platform for strategic enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An in-depth understanding of the buyer journey and the ability to lead complex, multi-party sales in a highly consultative manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with upper middle market and enterprise companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of driving cross-functional alignment among a broad set of stakeholders, including engineering, sales, support, product, marketing, data science, and senior leadership, to achieve growth targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in building and scaling a go-to-market (GTM) growth discipline, including the development of strategy, processes, and operating models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to create a strong growth culture within a team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in a growth-stage internet/software company and/or the payments industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs and their role in digital solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio builds and evolves the systems, experiences, and programs that shape how Stripe shows up in the world. We create high-quality, versatile, and forward-looking brand systems and help teams across Stripe use them clearly and consistently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an individual contributor role embedded directly within the Stripe Brand team and reporting to the Head of Brand Operations. As a Brand Program Manager, you will lead programs that make Stripe’s brand easier to use, apply consistently, and scale across teams, tools, and assets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In partnership with Brand producers and designers, you will identify gaps and opportunities in Stripe’s brand system, help the team enhance and evolve it, and translate decisions into clear rationale and guidance. Your portfolio will include Stripe’s brand consultation program, AI-enabled brand operations, the Identity team’s migration to a new digital asset management system, and the merchandise program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Lead the Identity team’s workstream for Stripe’s new digital asset management (DAM) system, partnering with the Marketing teams to migrate and organize assets in a clear and usable way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve Stripe’s brand consultation program, identifying recurring needs that can be addressed through clearer guidance, reusable templates, automation, or AI-enabled self-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help scale and evolve Stripe’s brand system in partnership with Brand Producers and designers, improving how guidance is documented, shared, and applied.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Brand Producers to develop a connected brand operating system and home base for Brand Studio’s internal AI tools; prototype workflows, evaluate their reliability, and support adoption across design teams and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a portfolio of brand systems and operations programs, including roadmap development, budgets, resourcing, project scoping, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage Stripe’s merchandise program operations, including budgets, invoices, vendor relationships, warehouse inventory, product testing and launches, and RFPs for new vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional design, marketing, technical, and operational teams to support the consistent application of Stripe’s brand across surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clarity through documentation, tooling, operating rhythms, and updates; connect teams, anticipate risks, and proactively resolve blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold and advocate for design quality while helping creatives establish practices that make high-quality work easier to produce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Program Managers at Stripe are operators first. They find the work in the process: the right framework, the workback schedule that holds, and the system that scales without breaking. They measure success by how well the creative team around them can do its best work. They have strong design sense and apply it to the operational decisions that protect quality, reduce friction, and keep programs moving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate excels at operating complex, evolving programs while maintaining and raising the bar on craft. They are curious and experimental with AI, offer thoughtful options and tradeoffs, articulate decisions clearly, and collaborate effectively with leadership, creatives, cross-functional partners, and vendors. Most importantly, they are meticulous about details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in program management, creative operations, design operations, brand operations, or related roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think users first: understand their needs, find thoughtful solutions, and continuously improve how they access and use brand guidance, tools, assets, and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong strategic acumen for developing complex program roadmaps and cross-functional processes in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience managing program budgets, tracking spend, and anticipating costs to keep work within budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate strong design sense and production fluency across multiple asset types and surfaces, including brand systems, web, digital, motion, email, reusable templates, and design asset management (DAM) systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively use AI tools in day-to-day work and have experience prototyping, building, or implementing AI-enabled workflows or systems that others can adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience operating in an in-house brand or creative environment with shared cross-functional resources and a lean production bench.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring strong information architecture and knowledge management skills, with experience organizing documentation, tools, assets, metadata, or sources of truth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience managing vendors; experience with procurement, inventory, physical goods, or merchandise is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong track record of influencing outcomes and building alignment across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are highly detail-oriented, can balance speed and quality, and communicate clearly in writing and conversation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about Stripe&#39;s mission to grow the internet economy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global Partner Engineering and Operations (PE&amp;amp;O) team is a vital part of Stripe’s Global Partnerships organization, playing a key role in our overall success. We manage the technical and operational dimensions of new and existing strategic product partnerships and programs. Positioned at the nexus of product development, engineering, and partnerships, we facilitate seamless collaboration essential for supporting Stripe’s rapid growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our team is a diverse mix of technical and business professionals dedicated to executing operations with financial ecosystem partners. We ensure efficient technical onboarding and implementation, while also overseeing ongoing KTLO (Keep-The-Lights-On) activities and achieving strict quality and performance benchmarks. Additionally, the PE&amp;amp;O team initiates partner-agnostic programs and solutions to tackle broad ecosystem challenges, developing tools that enhance operational efficiency and scalability.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In This Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is establishing a new function to oversee Card Network Compliance. In this position, you will be responsible for developing programs and processes to address Stripe’s card network changes and their implications for both Stripe and its users. This role is crucial for ensuring we stay informed about ongoing card network announcements, enhancing our strategic position, and driving operational efficiency in response to changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an exciting opportunity to contribute significantly to building a function from the ground up and to help formulate strategies that align with the best interests of Stripe and its users!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Implement Release Management Process: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish a release management process for Stripe in accordance with Card Network mandates, advising all cross-functional partners on the impacts, changes, and timelines associated with network updates. Conduct comprehensive analyses of how these mandates affect existing processes and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Review Card Network Releases: &lt;/strong&gt;Review, analyze, and assess biannual card network releases to identify key initiatives that will significantly impact Stripe’s business. Collaborate cross-functionally with various teams to ensure proper visibility and prioritization of these initiatives. Facilitate communication between engineering teams and the card networks&#39; Technical Partner Managers (TPaMs) to streamline clarifications and negotiations regarding complex mandates and programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Monitor Compliance: &lt;/strong&gt;Establish a framework and process for monitoring compliance with card network requirements and internal policies. Ensure regular audits and assessments are conducted to identify gaps and drive continuous improvement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Metrics and Dashboards: &lt;/strong&gt;Create and implement comprehensive metrics and JIRA dashboards to effectively monitor, review, and analyze mandates for each release cycle. Regularly update and refine the dashboards to reflect current business priorities and challenges, enabling teams to make informed decisions and proactively address potential issues related to card network mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage Mandate Intake Process: &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee the network mandate intake process, ensuring timely review, assessment, and prioritization of mandates. Lead the proactive management of waiver requests, liaising between compliance and operational teams for resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engage with External Partners: &lt;/strong&gt;Actively engage with external network partners by participating in councils, forums, and regular strategic meetings. Establish and nurture relationships that facilitate mutual understanding of goals and objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advocate for Stripe: &lt;/strong&gt;Serve as a dedicated advocate for Stripe within the card network ecosystem, ensuring that the unique perspectives, challenges, and opportunities faced by Stripe are considered by network stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the payments industry, with significant expertise in working with card networks and understanding card network rules and compliance activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of acquiring platforms and systems, and their interactions with card network products and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in navigating and using JIRA for project management and tracking. Familiarity with card network portals for managing and monitoring compliance activities. Comfortable utilizing Google Workspace tools (such as Sheets, Docs, and Slides) for collaboration and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of effectively collaborating with product and engineering teams to develop new processes and strategies in partnership with them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program and project management abilities, with the capacity to engage and influence stakeholders outside of direct control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills to effectively engage with both internal and external partners and drive change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive with minimal guidance, navigating uncertainty and ambiguity while shaping a new program and function at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker adept at identifying cross-functional issues, providing innovative solutions, and communicating the implications of these solutions across existing processes, systems, and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a payment service provider (PSP), card network, or high-growth technology company&amp;nbsp; is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a relevant field (e.g., Finance, Technology) is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) Commercial Solutions team ensures operational and programmatic excellence across deal cycles, increases revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs, and drives closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users, and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as User feedback and market insights. This role sits within Global Business Practices’ Commercial Solutions team, responsible for developing, launching, and maintaining commercial constructs and programs to drive revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Global Business Services’ Commercial Solutions team is looking for a Commercial Solutions Program Manager to own the end-to-end programmatic development of commercial and GBS launch readiness programs that drive revenue for Stripe. Programs have a large scope and/or impact in nature, including owning the development and support of first-of-its-kind commercialization efforts, ongoing program support (pre to post-launch), custom deal support related to the program, ownership of related enablement and communications, as well as acting as a change agent across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the end-to-end management of commercial and/or GBS launch readiness programs, driving cross-organizational alignment through the delivery of related outputs. This role requires a background in program management and commercial program experience, change management, a strong understanding of and experience in scaling global, cross-organizational mechanisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will have experience in program ownership and management, custom pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. The candidate will have strong communication skills and executive presence to effectively communicate with Stripes from sellers and Deal Strategies through to senior leadership. You will love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead large-scale, cross-functional commercial or GBS launch readiness programs that have Stripe-wide impact, often first-of-their-kind programs and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and lead highly complex programs that require considerable resources and high levels of functional and technical integration and knowledge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the commercial program deal motion, partnering with Deal Pricing and/or Deal Strategy Strategists, sellers, and internal stakeholders to create custom commercial approaches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with sales teams, sales leaders, services and support teams, product teams, and other cross-functional teams to develop, launch, and scale commercial programs, continuously evolving the ways Stripe goes to market to support commercialization efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, surface, and address systemic, broad issues and gaps, proposing holistic solutions to address root causes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work through complex programmatic problems at scale across go-to-market and Stripe, proposing creative solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams such as Legal, Finance, Accounting, service teams, and product teams to resolve and remove internal blockers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a liaison among Sales, Deal Pricing and Deal Strategy Strategists, and other stakeholders for custom elements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run meetings, working sessions, and exercises that help the leadership team improve effectiveness among themselves and across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate on behalf of a position and quickly gain cross-functional alignment on that position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead projects to solve existing commercialization issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in program management, commercial strategy, economics, deal management, or pricing, including ownership of program strategy or business operations and direct experience in commercial pricing model program management, deal management, and/or oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving cross-team mechanism development end to end, including ideation, planning, execution, launch, and post-launch support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, with a high degree of agency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with senior executives on high-priority initiatives, as well as the ability to work effectively across internal and external organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to articulate and understand business strategy at the C-suite level to gain credibility and advise organizations on how best to achieve their business goals through commercial programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to establish credibility and maintain working relationships with internal stakeholders involved with commercial constructs, including Legal, Finance, and Accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting data and metrics to senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to advocate for a position, even in the face of pushback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct commercial construct launch oversight and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess PgMP or PMP certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) Commercial Solutions team ensures operational and programmatic excellence across deal cycles, increases revenue through the development of transformative commercial constructs and/or operationalizing commercial readiness, and drives closure of Stripe’s sold portfolio. The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users, and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations, as well as User feedback and market insights. This role sits within Global Business Practices’ Commercial Solutions team, responsible for developing, launching, and maintaining commercial constructs and operationalizing products for GBS readiness to drive revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Global Business Services’ Commercial Solutions team is looking for a Commercial Solutions Program Manager to own the end-to-end programmatic development of commercial and GBS launch readiness programs that drive revenue for Stripe. Programs have a large scope and/or impact in nature, including program managing first-of-its-kind commercialization efforts of acquired company product offerings, ongoing program support (pre to post-launch), custom deal support related to the program, ownership of related enablement and communications, as well as acting as a change agent across the business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for the end-to-end management of commercial and/or GBS launch readiness programs, driving cross-organizational alignment through the delivery of related outputs. This role requires a background in program management and commercial program experience, change management, a strong understanding of and experience in scaling global, cross-organizational mechanisms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The candidate will have experience in program ownership and management, custom pricing strategies, and a background in supporting selling motions. The candidate will have strong communication skills and executive presence to effectively communicate with Stripes from sellers, and Deal Strategies and Deal Pricing through to senior leadership. You will love this job if you are a natural relationship and mechanism builder.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently lead large scale, cross-functional commercial or GBS launch readiness programs that have Stripe-wide impact, often first-of-their-kind programs and initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and lead a highly complex program/s which require considerable resources and high levels of complex functional and technical integration and knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the commercial program deal motion, partnering with Deal Pricing and/or Deal Strategy Strategists, sellers, and internal stakeholders to create custom commercial approaches&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with sales teams, sales leaders, services/support teams, product teams, and cross-functional teams to develop, launch, and scale the commercial program (continuously evolving the ways Stripe goes to market) to support commercialization efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, surface, and action systemic, broad issues and gaps, proposing holistic solutions to address root causes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate, and propose creative solutions, through complex programmatic problems at scale across Go-To-Market and Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross-functional teams such as Legal, Finance, Accounting, Service Teams, Product Teams, etc to resolve and remove internal blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as liaison within Sales, Deal Pricing and Deal Strategy Strategists, and other stakeholders for custom elements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate meetings, working sessions, and exercises that assist the leadership team in optimizing effectiveness amongst themselves and across the organization in general&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advocate on behalf of a position and quickly gain cross-functional alignment on the position&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly build credibility and trust with internal stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead projects to solve existing commercialization issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in program management/commercial strategy/economics/deal management/pricing with experience owning program strategy or business operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of direct commercial pricing model program management skills/knowledge/experience/deal management, and/or oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving cross-team mechanism development end to end (ideation, planning, execution, launch, post-launch support)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in ambiguous, quickly scaling environments, comfortable with high-agency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience engaging with senior executives on high priority initiatives, as well as the ability to work effectively across internal and external organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be able to articulate and understand business strategy at the C-Suite level to gain credibility and advise organizations on how best to achieve their business goals through the use of commercial programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication, presentation, negotiation, and project management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish credibility and maintain working relationships with internal stakeholders involved with commercial constructs (Legal, Finance, Accounting, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting data and metrics to senior leadership to report on metrics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to advocate for a position even in the face of pushback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct commercial construct launch oversight and experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments industry experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA degree in Business, Technology, Finance, or Economics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Possess PgMP or PMP certification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Competitive Programs team, which is part of the Go-to-Market (GTM) Strategic Programs team, is a new team dedicated to establishing and scaling Stripe’s Competitive Programs capability. Stripe operates in a dynamic and evolving competitive landscape. This role will help Stripe understand market developments and translate competitive insights into actionable guidance for teams and users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Competitive Programs team works alongside Market Intelligence to help Stripe identify meaningful threats and opportunities early, mobilize coordinated action across the company in priority situations, and turn market and deal signals into better Product, Marketing, and GTM decisions. We build the competitive operating system—program design, cross-functional coordination, deal-routing mechanisms, visibility, and accountability—while Product, Sales, PMM, Pricing, and other functions retain ownership for decisions and delivery in their domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-stack program manager role. While the initial assignment is Competitive Programs, we are looking for a versatile program manager who can apply the same skills to other high-priority GTM initiatives as the team’s mandate and Stripe’s needs evolve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead complex, C-suite level high-priority programs that require Stripe to move quickly and cohesively across functions. Initially, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the foundations and operating mechanisms to turn ad hoc competitive programs into a repeatable, scalable playbook&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run one or more named competitive programs to protect strategic business, close recurring gaps, and pursue opportunities to take share&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Stripe’s leadership to execute on initiatives to drive a strategic shift in company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be successful in this role if you can turn an ambiguous problem into a clear program with the right objectives, owners, decisions, operating cadence, and measures of success. You will be a trusted partner to executive leaders across Sales, Product, Product Operations, Marketing, Market Intelligence, Pricing, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, and GTM Operations. You will not be expected to make Product roadmap, commercial-policy, or account-strategy decisions yourself; instead, you will ensure the right functional owners are engaged, accountable, and able to make decisions at the pace required.&amp;nbsp; You will need (1) superior communication skills to work across senior stakeholders from different functions and (2) are someone who thrives when solving complex problems with limited oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable Competitive Programs infrastructure that can scale beyond individual competitors—for example, playbooks for deal escalation, commercial guidance, incentives, user-base analysis, regional teardowns, and cross-functional feedback loops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead named P0 and P1 competitive programs end-to-end, including defining the program charter, objectives, workplan, milestones, decision forums, and success measures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and run the cross-functional operating cadence for each program; this may include delivery of critical program workstreams including product and regional teardowns, seller enablement, product-gap reviews, GTM plays and executive engagement plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate competitive deal-triage and swarm mechanisms for priority opportunities, ensuring each deal has a clear commercial owner, response plan, and access to the required Product, Pricing, Legal, Risk, or executive support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Market Intelligence to translate competitor, customer, and deal signals into concrete actions for Product, PMM, Sales, and GTM leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clear, decision-oriented reporting for executive leadership on program health, competitive pipeline, risks, progress against commitments, and recommendations to continue, adjust, elevate, or graduate a program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and operationalize company-wide competitive cultural initiatives to shift Stripe’s behavior to be focused on competing fiercely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong, trusted working relationships across functions and levels, while maintaining clear accountability boundaries between central program coordination and functional ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply the same program-design and execution skills to other strategic GTM priorities over time, as business needs and the team’s mandate evolve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You are a strategic, hands-on program leader who is comfortable working in ambiguity and accountable for creating clarity. You can move between executive-level strategy and operational detail, bring disparate groups to a decision, and build mechanisms that outlast the initial program. You are energized by the intersection of market dynamics, competitors, strategy, product, marketing, commercials and deals, and how they all bridge together in a competitive situation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in program management, business operations, GTM strategy, management consulting, or a related discipline. Experience working in a Sales, Marketing, Product, GTM Operations, or other commercial organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong record of leading complex and ambiguous cross-functional programs from problem definition through implementation, adoption, and operational handoff. Experience managing global programs across regions, segments, and product lines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience navigating multiple senior stakeholders with differing incentives, priorities, and decision rights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to structure ambiguous problems, synthesize qualitative and quantitative inputs, make recommendations, and drive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive communication skills, including the ability to produce well-structured written updates, facilitate senior working sessions, and communicate risks or trade-offs directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build and maintain an operating cadence across multiple teams, including tracking milestones, dependencies, actions, and escalations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A high degree of ownership, sound judgment, adaptability, and comfort working in a fast-paced and changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and comfort using data to diagnose issues, assess program health, and guide prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves mentality” paired with a collaborative working style that builds trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Someone who demonstrates leadership qualities throughout their work – taking ownership of challenges, selflessly supporting their colleagues, and setting the standard for quality in their deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading competitive programs, strategic account programs, product-launch programs, commercial transformation, or other high-stakes GTM initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working at a B2B technology, enterprise software, fintech, payments, or platform company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with competitive intelligence, win/loss analysis, sales enablement, pricing, commercial strategy, or product-feedback mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a new operating model, program-management function, or repeatable playbook from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product, Product Operations, PMM, Sales, Pricing, Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, and GTM Systems teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL, BI tools, or other methods of analyzing pipeline, adoption, revenue, and operational data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Global Business Services’ (GBS) Business Practices team establishes and manages policies and processes for the GTM motion, including deal policy, approval and revenue contracting processes, and other deal related operations (e.g. misbilling, deal support models, etc). The team&#39;s reach is widespread across Stripe, not exclusive to one sales segment or geographical region; GBS drives change across go-to-market, positively impacting Stripe users, and cross-functional teams. GBS’s priorities are set through the direction of Stripe leadership and executive vision, partnership with sales and cross-functional organizations. This role sits within Global Business Practices’ Business Practices team, responsible for establishing, managing, and improving policies and processes to improve deal quality and velocity for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Program Managers are focused on solving GTM’s deal lifecycle challenges to create scalable and efficient deal policies and processes in support of commercial activities. We are looking for a self-starter who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguous global-scale programs, with multi-layered stakeholder management and significant cross-functional team engagement. &amp;nbsp;The ideal candidate will: (1) have deal policy and process background working at a hypergrowth technology/GTM org, (2) have superior communication skills to work across senior stakeholders across different functions, and (3) thrive when solving complex problems with limited oversight &amp;amp; incomplete data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for building and driving large-scale deal lifecycle transformation program changes end-to-end, and be directly responsible for marshaling the cross-functional support and resources needed to accomplish your goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Business Practices’ CPQ governance across the deal lifecycle by coordinating UAT for new features, ensuring all GA products are available in the CPQ, and establishing scalable best practices for evaluating and prioritizing new CPQ requests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage directly (or coordinate) the ‘full-stack’ of change management activities across stakeholder engagement and creating champions, messaging/communication planning, support and enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong collaborative relationships with key stakeholders across Stripe across levels and functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to proactively identify deal lifecycle improvement opportunities for the GTM teams spanning strategy, people, policy, process, and/or technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seamlessly prioritize among various projects and synthesize data to guide/support strategy and decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make exec level recommendations and drive decisions, where necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of delivering global, complex enterprise deal lifecycle/commercial transformation programs with multiple constituents in a changing, ambiguous environment end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deal management processes, deal process related root cause analysis, and commercial agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in program management, business operations, management consulting or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to diagnose, simplify and structure problems and solutions while having command of “the details”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enthusiastic “roll up your sleeves” mentality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, presentation, and communication experience, influencing across all levels from front lines to executive stakeholders. You set a high-bar in terms of communication effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with Excel and/or Google Sheet for analyzing large datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with Salesforce, CPQ, Deal Approval, Contract Lifecycle Management tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with incomplete data and adapting / re-prioritizing activities as business needs change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep problem solving and analysis experience (solving business problems - commercial, operational, financial) in a sales-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset and innate curiosity where every interaction is an opportunity to learn and improve (yourself, and those around you)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You demonstrate leadership qualities throughout your work – taking ownership of challenges, selflessly supporting your colleagues, and setting the standard for quality in your deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with payments and/or SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Seller Experience &amp;amp; Insights team is responsible for ensuring Stripe’s Go-to-Market teams have the tools, systems, processes and policies they need to sell effectively. We identify friction in how sellers get work done, translate seller needs into scalable solutions and partner across Product, Engineering, Data Science, Sales Operations and Enablement to improve productivity and the quality of Stripe’s customer engagement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is evolving how Sales Development Representatives identify, engage and qualify prospective users. Agentic workflows can remove repetitive work and help SDRs focus their time on judgement-rich customer conversations. Realising that value requires more than introducing new tools: it requires a coherent end-to-end experience across targeting, outreach, task execution, lead handoff, follow-up, qualification and reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the business experience and improvement roadmap for Stripe’s SDR workflows. You will work closely with SDRs and their leaders to understand how work happens today, identify the highest-value sources of friction and shape tools, processes and policies that make the organisation more effective. Your initial coverage will be &lt;strong&gt;Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage&lt;/strong&gt;, including how these capabilities interact with Salesforce, Orum, Gmail, LinkedIn and supporting routing and data services. Over time, the remit may expand to other parts of the SDR tooling and workflow ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will act as the connective tissue between frontline sellers and the teams that build and operate these capabilities. You will turn ambiguous problems into clear requirements, prioritised roadmaps, measurable launches and continuously improving workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end SDR experience roadmap across account and contact sourcing, targeting, outreach, task execution, handraiser management, meeting disposition and qualification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the business product and operational strategy for Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage within Sales Development, ensuring agentic and seller-led workflows solve meaningful seller problems and fit coherently into the broader SDR operating model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the experience across the hand-offs between Stripe’s agentic outreach solution and Gong Engage, including cadence creation, SDR task execution, prospect responses, meeting hand-offs and downstream activity capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map current workflows and redesign them to reduce manual work, duplicate actions, context switching and avoidable failure points across SDR tools and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish scalable mechanisms to capture, synthesise and prioritise SDR and manager feedback, combining qualitative insight with product usage, workflow, support and pipeline data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate frontline needs into clear business requirements, user journeys, success criteria and prioritised recommendations for Product, Engineering, Data Science, Sales Systems and Operations partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and monitor the metrics that matter across productivity, adoption, workflow health, data quality, follow-up speed, pipeline quality and prospect experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales Development leadership, Sales Operations and policy owners to ensure tooling and workflow design reflects routing, territory, rules-of-engagement and qualification requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build launch and change-management plans with Enablement and Communications so that new capabilities are understood, adopted and embedded in daily SDR work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create governance and operating rhythms for agentic workflows, including release readiness, feedback triage, incident escalation, experiment review and post-launch iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to simplify or consolidate the SDR tooling landscape and develop evidence-based business cases for investment, deprecation or process change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the SDR experience in cross-functional planning and communicate trade-offs, progress, risks and results clearly to frontline teams and senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of experience in program management, product operations, revenue operations, sales operations, product management or process improvement in a technology or high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience building, improving or supporting Sales Development or broader GTM workflows, data and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success leading complex, global and cross-functional initiatives from problem definition through launch, adoption and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of how modern prospecting and sales-development workflows operate, including targeting, contact sourcing, outreach, lead routing, qualification and CRM activity capture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to map complex user journeys, identify root causes and translate ambiguous seller problems into clear requirements and prioritised solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, including the ability to define success metrics, interpret workflow and funnel data and use evidence to make trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering effectively with technical teams and communicating across frontline, operational, product and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, low-ego and hands-on working style, with comfort moving between strategy and detailed execution in a rapidly changing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong change-management skills and a track record of driving adoption, not just delivering a launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience in Sales Development, SDR Operations or the design of SDR productivity programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Salesforce and sales-engagement, conversation-intelligence, dialing, enrichment or routing platforms such as Gong, Orum, Salesloft, LinkedIn Sales Navigator or comparable tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating AI-assisted or agentic workflows, including human-in-the-loop controls, quality measurement and responsible-use guardrails.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with experimentation, funnel analysis, SQL or business-intelligence tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong understanding of data quality, routing, rules of engagement and the downstream effects of workflow changes on reporting and seller incentives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing enablement, documentation or operating mechanisms for global sales teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for understanding seller behaviour and improving both employee and prospective-user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Go-to-Market (GTM) Strategic Programs team supports Stripe&#39;s mission (to &quot;Increase the GDP of the internet&quot;) by building GTM strategy, bringing it to life through incubation programs, and providing program management expertise across global, cross-functional programs. We bring a desire to chart the unknown, rigorous thinking, and a user-first approach to problem-solving, while helping to build connections between Stripe go-to-market teams and the business overall.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we rapidly grow our company and customer base, we need &quot;full stack&quot; program management experts with global program experience who easily flex between:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PMO responsibilities coordinating across a number of cross-functional team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running the full breadth of building and operationalizing incubation programs from diagnosis, design, implementation, and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving a successful transition and handover to operational counterparts across GTM and Product Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Program Managers are focused on solving GTM&#39;s most pressing challenges. We&#39;re looking for a self-starter who has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguous global-scale programs, with multi-layered stakeholder management and significant cross-functional team engagement. You have worked in a hypergrowth technology or GTM org or come from a strategic consulting background, have superior communication skills to work across the most senior stakeholders across different functions, and thrive when solving complex problems with limited oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for building and driving large-scale programs end-to-end, and be directly responsible for marshaling the cross-functional support and resources needed to accomplish your goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage directly (or coordinate) the &quot;full-stack&quot; of change management activities across stakeholder engagement and creating champions, messaging and communication planning, and support and enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop strong collaborative relationships with key stakeholders across Stripe across levels and functions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to identify improvement opportunities for the Revenue teams spanning strategy, people, process, and technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a Programs Center of Excellence, providing guidance, consulting, and coaching to peers and others on partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Seamlessly prioritize among various projects and synthesize data to guide and support strategy and decision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make C-suite-level recommendations and drive decisions, where necessary&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a sales and marketing organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in program management, business operations, management consulting, or a related discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of delivering global, complex programs with multiple constituents in a changing, ambiguous environment end-to-end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast-paced, rapidly changing environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to diagnose, simplify, and structure problems and solutions while having command of &quot;the details&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent analytical, presentation, and communication experience, influencing across all levels from front lines to C-suite. You set a high bar in terms of communication effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated leadership qualities throughout their work—taking ownership of challenges, selflessly supporting their colleagues, and setting the standard for quality in their deliverables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort operating with incomplete data and adapting and reprioritizing activities as business needs change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep problem-solving and analysis experience (solving business problems—commercial, operational, financial) in a sales-oriented environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A growth mindset and innate curiosity where every interaction is an opportunity to learn and improve (yourself and those around you)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience with payments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with SQL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe&#39;s Professional Services (ProServ) team helps businesses around the world design, implement, and optimise their Stripe integrations. As we scale our global delivery capability, we are building a structured portfolio of service offerings that define the scope, methodology, resourcing, and commercial terms of how we engage with our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Product Manager (&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Services)&lt;/strong&gt; to own the portfolio of offerings end-to-end. The role sits at the intersection of services strategy, commercial design, and delivery operations. You will be the person who determines whether our offerings are well-designed, effectively sold, and profitably delivered and you will take action to refine the portfolio as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a traditional Product Manager role, but it demands the same rigour. Your &quot;product&quot; is the service itself: its scope, its pricing, its methodology, and its performance. You will work closely with Sales, Delivery, Finance, and Stripe&#39;s Product organisation to ensure that every offering in our portfolio is fit for purpose and continuously improving.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the offering portfolio for Professional Services&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and govern ProServ’s offering portfolio including scope, hours, pricing, and resource plans for each offering. Our portfolio includes offerings designed&amp;nbsp; for all user segments from start-ups to enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the full offering lifecycle: design, build, launch, iterate, and deprecate offerings based on market need, delivery performance, and product roadmap changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the portfolio stays current as Stripe launches new products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement a governance framework for the portfolio of offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive offering performance analytics&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track the offering KPIs: attach rate, average scope deviation, planned vs. actual burn rate, gross margin per offering, and customer satisfaction&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run regular performance reviews and present findings to ProServ leadership with clear recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Refine and Improve Offering Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse delivery burn data to identify offerings that are systematically over- or under-scoped, and propose refinements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct structured retrospectives with Delivery Leads after engagement close to capture insights and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the structured feedback loop between Delivery (what is hard to deliver), Sales (what is hard to sell), and Finance (what is margin-accretive), synthesising those inputs into offering design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of Professional Services or consulting delivery experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrable experience shaping or owning a service offering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial literacy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Management training or experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to apply product thinking (hypothesis, prototype, measure, iterate) to service design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Certinia and/or Salesforce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to partner and SI ecosystem dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk PMO team protects Stripe’s revenue and drives cross-functional strategy for company-level and org-level priorities. As Stripe operates across an increasingly complex and fast-moving global regulatory environment, one of our most important functions is ensuring that our largest, most strategic users can grow with us—compliantly, confidently, and at speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We sit at the intersection of Legal, Compliance, Engineering, Product, Data Science, and GTM—serving as the bridge between teams coordinating massive programs with global, wide-reaching impact. We build durable systems that enable strong collaboration across functions and seamless experiences for our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re energized by high-stakes, ambiguous problems and thrive on building programs from scratch in environments where the rules are still being written—we want to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will define, own, and execute program strategies for large-scale regulatory initiatives, operating with significant autonomy across a portfolio of global projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly visible, senior individual contributor (IC) role. While you will influence senior leadership and set strategic direction, you are also the primary driver of execution. You will need to zoom out to design the long-term vision, and zoom in to manage the details—building templates, tracking deliverables, writing documentation, and directly unblocking cross-functional teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and execute high-stakes global programs end-to-end,&lt;/strong&gt; from initial strategy and scoping to project planning, day-to-day tracking, and change management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive step-change improvements&lt;/strong&gt; in our operational processes, rolling up your sleeves to build systems and workflows that directly improve business outcomes and top-line metrics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge compliance and commercial strategy&lt;/strong&gt; by partnering with GTM and account leadership to turn complex regulatory requirements into a competitive advantage that builds deep user trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and run operating models&lt;/strong&gt; across diverse cross-functional teams (including Product, Engineering, Legal, Risk, and Compliance), keeping highly distributed workstreams aligned and accountable&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as a trusted advisor&lt;/strong&gt; by preparing strategic reviews for senior stakeholders and managing critical escalations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate user friction into program evolution&lt;/strong&gt; by establishing structured, data-driven approaches to gather user feedback and turning those insights into actionable product and operational improvements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diagnose and resolve systemic operational gaps&lt;/strong&gt; before they impact our users, building self-healing processes and scalable internal infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion Stripe’s Operating Principles&lt;/strong&gt; by fostering a high-performance culture that values rigorous thinking, rapid execution, and putting users first&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a highly strategic operator, a masterful communicator, and a systems thinker with operational grit. You thrive in the gray area, possessing the ability to translate ambiguous global challenges into elegant, structured, and highly actionable operational frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a natural leader who leads by influence and by example. You have a deep empathy for the user, an unyielding bias toward action, and you take pride in the craft of execution. No problem is too complex for you to deconstruct, and no detail is too small if it impacts the user experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in Program Management, Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, Management Consulting, or Go-to-Market (GTM) Strategy in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on execution track record: Proven ability to work independently as an individual contributor, managing complex, multi-stakeholder project plans and deliverables from inception to completion&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication &amp;amp; storytelling: Excellent written and verbal communication skills; a proven ability to distill highly complex, technical, or regulatory topics into clear, succinct, and persuasive narratives to external and senior audiences&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems and infrastructure builder: Deep experience designing, launching, and scaling complex cross-functional operating models, feedback loops, and PMO frameworks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset: A high willingness to learn, adapt quickly to changing environments, and actively seek and act on feedback to continuously improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in high-growth technology or fintech environments&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep cross-functional partnership: Prior experience working alongside Engineering, Product, Legal, Compliance, and GTM/Sales&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data fluency: Experience leveraging data visualization tools and analytical frameworks to back up strategic decisions and measure program success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

