&lt;li&gt;Recruit, lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing team of Account Executives spanning Startups, SMB’s, Platforms and Large Enterprises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish the team’s long-term vision, go-to-market strategy, and operating rhythm for LATAM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own team-level revenue, activation, pipeline, and other sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach Account Executives across the full sales cycle, including prospecting, discovery, business-case development, solution design, negotiation, close, and long-term account growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the team’s capabilities in collaborative pipeline generation, consultative and solution-based selling, closing strategy, and MEDDIIC.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team create and execute territory and account strategies that generate new business and expand Stripe’s footprint within existing users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on coaching for complex opportunities, including executive engagement, deal strategy, commercial structuring, and negotiation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with strategic customers, industry leaders, partners, and senior stakeholders across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with Solutions Architecture, Product, Risk, Legal, Marketing, and other teams to develop solutions that address users’ business and technical needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain high standards for account planning, stakeholder mapping, pipeline management, and forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a deep understanding of the payments landscape and the priorities of enterprise businesses across Brazil and&amp;nbsp; LATAM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire and motivate the team while supporting each team member’s performance, professional development, and long-term career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the needs of Brazil users internally and contribute to Stripe’s evolving enterprise sales strategy, processes, and culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a strategic, hands-on sales leader with experience building and coaching enterprise technology sales teams. You have a record of delivering strong commercial results, developing talent, and helping sellers navigate complex customer environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a self-starting builder who is comfortable operating in an ambitious, fast-changing environment. You can move between setting regional strategy, coaching an individual seller, engaging an executive customer, and collaborating with technical and product teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant enterprise sales experience, including experience as a successful quota-carrying Account Executive, and/or 5+ years of frontline sales-management experience in technology, SaaS, fintech, banking, payments, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading, coaching, and scaling a high-performing enterprise sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A consistent record of meeting or exceeding individual or team sales targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and executing regional, territory, and account strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience coaching sellers through complex, end-to-end sales cycles involving technical, commercial, product, risk, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build trusted relationships with strategic customers, senior executives, industry leaders, and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
