&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with engineering, product, and Stripe’s security org to move fast without compromising safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have 8+ years of experience in Security GRC, ideally with time spent in fast-paced startup environments where you’ve built security practices from the ground up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a startup mindset: you’re scrappy, pragmatic, and move quickly to solve the most critical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re proficient with NIST CSF, OCC’s Cybersecurity Supervision Work Program and/or FFIEC IT Examination Handbook or other similar global frameworks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven prior experience with regulatory audits from Global auditors across Security domains.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in ambiguity and know how to ruthlessly prioritize.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can balance security rigor with speed, especially in fast-moving environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated history converting complex policy, audit, and regulatory mandates into actionable operational and engineering controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Broad technical depth across cloud architecture, identity management, appsec, data protection, and incident response operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of evaluating control environments, uncovering underlying risks, and executing sensible, long-term solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong program execution skills: crafting strategic roadmaps, setting milestones, navigating cross-team blockers, and driving remediation projects to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach to partnering across engineering, product, compliance, legal, and audit teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience building or scaling security programs through execution, either at a startup or in an embedded role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are excited about the potential of crypto and stablecoins to power global financial infrastructure (you don’t need deep prior knowledge—just curiosity and openness to learn).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Security team is dedicated to improving the security of Stripe and its users. Our users trust us with some of their most sensitive information, and we make security a first-class consideration in everything we do. Security concerns are ever-evolving, creating an extremely dynamic environment for the Security team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Security Governance, Risk, and Compliance (SGRC) team helps Stripe make informed security decisions, understand its risk and control posture, and represent its security program to internal and external stakeholders. The team also manages security risk arising from Stripe’s relationships with third parties by assessing their security controls, identifying and mitigating risk, and supporting informed onboarding and risk-acceptance decisions. Our work helps Stripe move quickly while maintaining clear and consistent security expectations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage a portfolio of Third Party Security Risk Assessments (TPSRAs) for new engagements, renewals / reassessments, and material changes in relationship scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review security questionnaires, independent assurance reports, certifications, penetration-test results, and other evidence to evaluate third-party control effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify security gaps, determine proportionate remediation requirements, and clearly communicate findings to Stripe DRIs and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply Stripe’s third-party security standards consistently, documenting assessment results, decisions, and supporting evidence in Zip, Aravo, and other program systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate novel, complex, or high-risk findings and support Enhanced Due Diligence and risk-acceptance processes when a third party cannot meet Stripe’s security requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Procurement, Legal, Privacy, Business Continuity, Security, and business stakeholders to resolve assessment issues and support timely third-party onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical guidance to Stripe teams on TPSRA requirements, timelines, and their responsibilities throughout the assessment process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track assessment volume, aging, service levels, remediation status, and other program-health indicators; use the data to identify trends and recommend improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in program processes, documentation, or tooling and contribute to implementing improvements that increase consistency, scalability, and stakeholder experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to third-party security risk policies, standards, procedures, and guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Need:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of relevant experience in third-party security risk, security assessments, information security, or a related risk-management function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting end-to-end third-party security assessments, including reviewing security documentation, identifying control gaps, determining risk, and defining remediation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of common security and assurance frameworks, such as SOC 2, ISO 27001, PCI DSS, NIST, and CSA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment and analytical skills, including the ability to distinguish material security risks from lower-priority findings and recommend a proportionate response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently manage multiple assessments, priorities, and stakeholder relationships while meeting defined timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical security findings to non-security stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational data and reporting to identify trends, communicate program health, and improve processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach and experience working with cross-functional partners such as Procurement, Legal, Privacy, and business teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with third-party risk management platforms or procurement workflow tools such as Aravo, Zip, or similar systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Enhanced Due Diligence, security risk acceptance, or third-party incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving or scaling a third-party risk assessment program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio lays the foundations that help Stripe accelerate. We do this by creating, evolving, and maintaining Stripe&#39;s high-quality, versatile, and forward-looking brand design systems, experiences, and advertising campaigns. We sweat the details. We make it seem effortless. The Experiential team is responsible for bringing Stripe&#39;s brand to life in the real world, from flagship events and industry conferences to internal summits and curated partner experiences. This team operates at the intersection of creativity, strategy, technology, and production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Brand Designers at Stripe demonstrate a passion for the craft of design and a deep understanding of how design communicates brand essence. You will be responsible for defining and advancing Stripe&#39;s experiential design systems across physical experiences, digital surfaces, and mainstage creative content. You work at the intersection of design systems, concepting, and storytelling, creating design frameworks that scale while still feeling intentional and human. The ideal candidate is technically fluent, conceptually strong, crisply articulates design decisions, and collaborates seamlessly with creative directors, producers, marketers, communications, and engineering partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Lead the end-to-end design of experiential programs, from early concepts and storytelling through detailed design, production, and launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate Stripe’s brand and product strategy into compelling physical, digital, and hybrid experiences for global audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create scalable visual identities, design systems, and toolkits for events and environments that extend Stripe’s evolving brand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with producers, marketers, product teams, and senior stakeholders to define goals, make tradeoffs, and deliver work on time and at a high bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Art direct agencies, fabricators, contractors, and other external partners; provide clear feedback and uphold quality through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design keynote and presentation systems that make complex ideas feel clear, cohesive, and engaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help evolve the Experiential Design discipline by sharing craft knowledge, improving team practices, and mentoring other designers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experiential, environmental, brand, or integrated design experience, ideally for technology or product-led companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in art, design, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating concept-to-production work across events, environments, installations, keynotes, or other immersive brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading large-scale conferences, trade shows, executive or customer events, or comparable IRL and hybrid experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong visual design, art direction, and storytelling skills across physical and digital media.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently lead complex work while influencing designers, agencies, contractors, and cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment in incorporating stakeholder feedback while protecting the core creative idea and quality bar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with motion design systems and how to apply them consistently across contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of design principles: layout, grid systems, typography, color, iconography, and photo art direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to designing for live event environments: LED walls, stage visuals, real-time rendering, and large-format displays&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with design collaboration tools, including Figma and Keynote, and a systems-thinking approach to extending design systems across shared patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of emerging AI tools and how they fit into a professional creative production workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record delivering high quality work independently, and in close collaboration with cross-functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Find a meaningful balance between optimizing for speed, quality, and doing challenging, interesting, frame-perfect work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions and crave feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and have them help you learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, with a drive for perfection down to the last pixel or inch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about Stripe&#39;s mission, are dedicated to a user-first mindset, and have experience working with data and insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience designing within real-world production constraints, including materials, fabrication, installation, wayfinding, accessibility, and on-site iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building scalable experiential identity systems across multiple locations, audiences, or event formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort experimenting with emerging technologies where they improve storytelling or audience participation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written, verbal, and presentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, low-ego approach to critique, mentoring, and learning across disciplines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe &amp;amp; Link&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, we’ve spent the last 15 years building financial infrastructure for the internet, serving millions of people and businesses worldwide. Our flagship consumer product, Link, makes online payments and digital transactions effortless and secure—the digital wallet for what’s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a unique opportunity to continue building a standalone brand and introduce it to new global audiences. You’ll play a key role in making payments more personal and convenient while doing some of the most impactful work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sitting within Brand Studio, the Link team is building Stripe’s first consumer brand. We build, evolve, and maintain a versatile, forward-looking visual identity system and find clear, fresh ways to apply it across surfaces. The brand designers on our team are multidisciplinary: they design robust visual systems, lead art direction, and craft surfaces that prioritize brand and product storytelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working with cross-functional teams across Stripe and external partners, we set the vision and execute to a high quality bar. Our work shows up IRL, online, and everywhere between.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining a highly creative team that spans anywhere from developing storytelling to creating digital tools, brand systems to rapid ideation. The work is highly experimental, idea driven, and very collaborative and cross-functional.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Be an adamant maker that is genuinely curious, experimental, and loves to tinker, iterate quickly, and innovate on ideas, narrative, and making beautiful things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to raising the team&#39;s standards and culture of craft through the quality, clarity, and consistency of your own work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Elevate and shape a brand system that is flexible enough to work across various surfaces and exemplifies Stripe’s commitment to craft &amp;amp; beauty&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with like-minded creative people who have radically different skill sets and together create ideas that envision an optimistic, progressive future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner widely with cross-functional teams to build upon great ideas through making things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give and solicit feedback from wide range of teammates and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant design and art direction experience for technical and product-driven companies&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating high-quality visual design work, with strong typography and a hands-on approach to making and iterating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record of independently delivering work as well as influencing the work of other designers, contractors, and agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying and evolving a brand in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Figma, Adobe Creative Cloud, Keynote, and Google slides&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experimentation with AI tools to both generate ideas, get stakeholders to see where an idea is headed, and to scale design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Curiosity, ambition, and a distinct point of view on design, with strong typography skills and an appreciation for creative process, technology, and design engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow—and invite them to help you learn and grow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative coding or creative technologist background is a nice to have&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Design team works across most projects at Stripe—from our brand standards to campaigns, events, digital products, and even printed publications. And since Stripe’s main audience is other people who build products, we agonize over and take pride in crafting user-friendly and user-focused experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Brand Design team lays the foundations that help Stripe accelerate. We do this by creating, evolving, and maintaining Stripe’s high-quality, versatile, and forward-looking visual identity design system. We sweat the details. We make it seem effortless.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team—and our design efforts—are multipliers for Stripe and Stripes. Our focus on principles, systems, and standards makes it easier for all Stripes to get work done—at a high quality bar, while still creating space for evolution and innovation. Collaborating with other teams at Stripe, as well as select external partners, we raise the quality and consistency of interactions with the Stripe brand.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Designers at Stripe demonstrate passion for great design and for expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible design systems that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency for the brand at scale. They are user focused, have a strong understanding of the business, and are empathetic and inspiring team leaders. The ideal candidate excels across a variety of styles, crisply articulates design decisions, iterates quickly, and collaborates seamlessly with marketers, producers, leaders, other designers, and agency partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building one of the world&#39;s most important companies, and the way we show up creatively in the world matters. As a Senior Designer, Brand Advertising, you&#39;ll sit at the center of that work, concepting and crafting campaigns that earn attention, build brand equity, and reflect Stripe&#39;s ambition. You&#39;ll work day-to-day within the Advertising team while staying in close partnership with the Stripe Identity team, making sure every campaign is rooted in who Stripe is and where the brand is going.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who thinks in campaigns and executes with craft, equally comfortable generating a big idea and sweating the details of how it comes to life across every channel. This is a high-impact, high-ownership position where you will help define what advertising and campaigns can be and feel like, with craft and beauty.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Concept, develop, and execute integrated campaigns across digital, film, print, OOH, and live activations, from early brief through final delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the Advertising team to build a strong, consistent creative pipeline that connects brand to business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Stripe Identity team to ensure campaign work is grounded in and advances Stripe&#39;s visual and verbal identity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate briefs, user insights, and business objectives into campaign ideas that are both strategically sharp and creatively distinctive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present and champion ambitious creative work to stakeholders and senior leadership, building the case without diluting the idea&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Art direct external agencies, contractors, and collaborators, maintaining quality and brand alignment throughout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with producer leads to drive program success, managing timelines, quality, and alignment across workstreams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to raising the team&#39;s standards and culture of craft through the quality, clarity, and consistency of your own work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of design and art direction experience, ideally at technical or product-driven companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong track record of independently delivering work while also influencing the output of other designers, contractors, and agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep cross-functional collaboration skills, comfortable working across creative, product, marketing, and strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic instincts for building ambitious, globally facing brands in fast-moving environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong instincts across film, digital, print, OOH, and activations, with a genuine pulse on culture and the ability to translate that into concepts that earn attention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven ability to sell ambitious creative work: concepting ideas and presenting them in a way that earns buy-in from senior leadership without flattening them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong partnership mindset, particularly with producer leads, to drive programs forward with quality, clarity, and momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident stakeholder management skills: able to navigate ambiguity, align competing priorities, and bring people in on the creative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, and the latest AI workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional craft and impeccable taste&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuinely curious, ambitious, and creative, with a sharp eye for typography, a deep appreciation for craft and the creative process, and a digitally native sensibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persuasive and considered in presenting your work and process; skilled at facilitating stakeholder conversations without losing creative integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Active experimentation with AI tools in the creative process, with an honest point of view on how they can shape the way work gets made&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication; strong organization and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in sports marketing, sponsorship activations, or brand-in-culture work, with a perspective on how brands earn credibility in spaces they don&#39;t own&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Created work that generated genuine cultural traction, beyond media spend alone&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to art direct at a high level and think through how a design system or campaign idea can evolve and deepen over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in environments where product and brand both had to pull their weight, and where the product itself was central to the creative story&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A history of award-caliber work, and the perspective to know that awards aren&#39;t always the goal, but that they have a real place in raising ambition, sharpening craft, and setting a team&#39;s creative standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a technology company that builds economic infrastructure for the internet. Businesses of all sizes—from new startups to public companies like Amazon and Salesforce—use our software to accept online payments and run technically sophisticated financial operations in more than 100 countries. By helping businesses accept payments from anywhere in the world and accelerating the economic shift from offline to online, we aim to increase the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Leadership Recruiting Team (LRT) is a high-performing group of strategic and creative problem solvers. We are passionate about finding and hiring the very best leaders and experts from around the globe to help drive the next arc of Stripe’s growth.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be directly responsible for partnering with senior stakeholders to identify, attract, assess, and hire individuals for leadership roles across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategically partner with executives to hire top talent for Stripe’s highest priority leadership roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define, design, and implement recruiting processes and search engagements for a variety of senior leadership roles. This includes understanding and mapping the talent landscape, internal calibration and referrals, and matching those data points with the external talent supply&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage end-to-end leadership-level searches from inception of candidate contact to onboarding, including research, outreach strategies, candidate experience, negotiations, partnering with HR for successful onboarding, and communicating with stakeholders along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional partners, such as People Partners, Compensation, and Business Leads, to align hiring goals with business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop competency-based interviews that surface a candidate’s full range of capabilities, explore their aspirations, and gain insight into how their experience will apply to a leadership role at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster trust-based relationships with candidates, gaining a close understanding of their requirements and concerns. Serve as a skilled problem solver, facilitator and coach in final negotiations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize team-wide systems and tools to capture current market, client, and candidate information to facilitate both the search process and market intelligence initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a team that values creative ideas and constant improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a contributing member of the recruiting team that effectively embodies and promotes the culture and values of Stripe. A quick guide to Stripe’s culture is located&lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/jobs/life-at-stripe&quot;&gt; here&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years proven executive search experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in identifying, engaging, and closing senior-level passive candidates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding sourcing skills and ability to think ‘outside the box.’&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with team and hiring managers, including the executive team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior use of talent market insights and data to influence decisions within the leadership groups and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of building working relationships with leaders and cross-functional partners - we value a Users First approach to executive search, ensuring a positive experience for candidates and hiring managers alike.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of creating and maintaining positive candidate experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to distill complex information into a consumable and organized format with a focus on content, tone, and structure - we value Craft and Beauty across all of our outputs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to take ownership and effectively manage time and process across roles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in both search firms and in-house&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who We Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior SD Manager, you will drive Stripe’s future growth engine by leading a team of SDRs supporting our Startup and Velocity Users. You will be working with the Stripe’s Sales teams to build Sales people and pipeline for the business. As a Senior SD Manager, you’ll lead and coach a group of high-performing Managers and SDRs, helping them deliver on ambitious targets, as well as roll up your sleeves to work directly with the team. We are looking for a self-starter who has demonstrated what it means to take an AI-supported approach to sales, success dealing with ambiguity, operating in a high-growth environment, working with cross-functional partners to lead charge change management initiatives.&amp;nbsp; As a cross-functional leader, you will also work closely with cross-functional partners on an evolving AI-supported sales development model that accelerates the impact that we have for our Users. Ideal candidates will have management experience scaling a technology Sales Development team and superior communication skills.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We take an AI-forward yet people focused approach to Sales Development, and are looking for someone who enjoys building – who will actively participate in the development of sales processes, the articulation of Stripe’s value proposition, and the creation of key tools and assets to measure success. Stripe is not a typical company, and this is not a typical sales development function. If you’re hungry, smart, persistent, and a great teammate, we want to hear from you!&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role requires a blend of long-range strategic vision and high-leverage execution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You Will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help craft and execute an AI-powered strategic vision for our Startup, SMB, Commercial segments that includes both inbound and outbound workflows.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence and execute an interactive approach to AI-powered, human in the loop workflows that evolve over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a growing team including 5 Managers and 50+ SDRS, reporting to the Head of AMER.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be accountable for Sales Development qualified pipeline and business outcomes, owning the volume and quality of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive a high sense of accountability, setting a consistent operating cadence that delivers high impact results using data and strong operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and mentor managers who in turn build healthy, high-performing teams, while ensuring succession plans and resources are in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a trusted partner to regional segment leadership, consistently bringing market knowledge, insights, and credibility that shape future growth strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver accurate and reliable forecasting, proactively identifying trends, risks, and opportunities while driving cross-functional changes to sustain multi-quarter growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion operational excellence, ensuring Salesforce hygiene, data integrity, and innovative metrics that optimize business performance and enable scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and deepen cross-functional partnerships with Marketing, Sales Ops, Enablement, and Product Marketing to influence and execute regional campaigns and strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Play an active role in attracting and retaining top talent, while coaching and mentoring managers and SDRs to develop consultative, solution-oriented skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire career growth for team members by identifying transformational development opportunities and preparing future leaders for broader impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead with innovation, curiosity, and discipline, piloting new processes, tools, and playbooks that refine how SDR teams forecast, execute, and deliver business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re Looking for Someone Who Has:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience leading high-performance Sales Development, Inside Sales, or lead qualification teams, including second line leadership, with a proven record of consistently exceeding targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success designing and scaling organizations in high-growth, ambiguous environments, ideally within technology or SaaS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for building AI-enabled processes and cultures, with curiosity to pilot new technologies that enhance SDR productivity and pipeline generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to hire, coach, and develop managers and SDRs into future leaders, fostering a culture of growth and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional cross-functional influence, with a track record of driving alignment and results across Sales, Marketing, Product, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in operational excellence, including Salesforce discipline, data integrity, accurate forecasting, and performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong analytical mindset with the ability to leverage data to inform decisions, optimize processes, and track impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for building AI-enabled processes and cultures, with curiosity to pilot new technologies that enhance SDR productivity and pipeline generation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to hire, coach, and develop managers and SDRs into future leaders, fostering a culture of growth and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine passion for innovation, start-ups, and technology, with a bias toward experimentation and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Trust is central to Stripe’s mission to grow the GDP of the internet and the Risk team advances that mission by building products and infrastructure that Stripe businesses, Stripe product teams, and Stripe’s network of regulators and financial partners rely on. From helping businesses onboard to Stripe to managing regulatory compliance at scale, Risk is at the center of what makes Stripe run. The Technical Program Manager team is responsible for delivering the cross-Stripe programs that help businesses grow on Stripe, enable products to launch safely at scale, and Stripe to maintain its position as the most trusted network in the financial ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead a team of TPMs and PGMs to deliver on Stripe’s most complex, cross-cutting, and critical programs. As a manager, you will support your team in leading programs that advance Stripe and Risk’s mission. You’ll hire, coach, and grow a team of excellent TPMs that support Stripe’s growing needs and the individuals’ careers. You will also act as a TPM yourself on the most complex initiatives that uniquely need your hands-on leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, lead and manage high-performing teams, managers, and individuals, across multiple locations, including providing performance reviews, continual feedback, and career growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and deliver on long-term vision and multi-year strategy for company-wide programs collaborating with product management and engineering leadership/executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success criteria, delivery plans, track risks, and ensure successful execution of Risk’s most complex programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make substantial improvements to how the teams you work with communicate and operate to significantly increase the productivity and efficiency of the teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of management experience of varying seniority, including managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of software engineering, systems engineering or technical product/program management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in finding and growing talent through coaching, mentoring, and career development conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving technical programs from ideation to delivery at scale and leading teams of Technical Program Managers who have done the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating autonomously and leading across multiple teams, with stakeholders in different disciplines across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to demonstrate critical thinking and thought leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable working with geographically distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve managed teams that designed and operated critical infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are empathetic to customer needs but visionary enough to not just deliver a faster horse&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are excited about collaborating with teammates across Stripe’s organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience as an engineer or similar technical role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Terminal helps businesses extend their online presence into the physical world. Our mission is to make it as easy for businesses to accept in-person payments as the Stripe API has made it for online payments. With Terminal, businesses can create flagship retail experiences, extend their websites to pop-up stores, or enable mobile point-of-sale payments at their next event. All of this is built on the Stripe Payments Platform, so businesses can maintain a single view of customers and sales across online and offline channels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our hardware engineering team in Taiwan designs and builds the physical payment devices at the heart of that experience, including products such as the Stripe Reader S700 and Stripe Reader M2. We are expanding the team and seeking an experienced Senior Mechanical and Industrial Design Engineer who can own both the structural engineering and aesthetic form language of our next generation of payment terminals. This is a blended role. You will be equally comfortable driving design for manufacturability (DFM) for a plastic enclosure and sketching form concepts that express Stripe&#39;s design identity in hardware.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the industrial and mechanical design of next-generation Stripe Terminal payment devices, shaping their form, feel, usability, and structural performance from early concepts through mass production. You will partner with cross-functional teams and suppliers to deliver manufacturable, high-quality hardware, including enclosure design, color, material, and finish specifications, packaging, validation, and production readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industrial design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead ideation and concept development through rapid hand sketching, digital sketching, and physical foam or 3D-printed models to explore form factors early in the product lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the visual and tactile design language of Terminal hardware, including proportion, form, surface transitions, button feel, and overall product character.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce photorealistic product renders using KeyShot or similar tools to communicate design intent to cross-functional teams and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage color, material, and finish (CMF) specifications. Work directly with suppliers to qualify target surfaces, textures, and coatings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage packaging design, working directly with suppliers to qualify final deliverables and the unboxing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply ergonomics and human factors principles to ensure products are intuitive and comfortable for a diverse range of users and environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain visual consistency and brand coherence across the Terminal hardware product family, in alignment with Stripe&#39;s design identity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mechanical engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design mechanical components and assemblies using SolidWorks or Creo, following professional engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience in mechanical designs and drawings, assess manufacturability, and resolve technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and plan problem-solving activities using scientific approaches, such as tolerance analysis, computer-aided engineering (CAE) and finite element method (FEM) simulations, design of experiments (DOE), and physical prototyping.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently analyze and verify mechanical designs, identify risks, and propose mitigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage bill of materials (BOM) cost and design schedules from a mechanical engineering perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare mechanical engineering deliverables, including BOMs, component specifications, and support for failure mode and effects analysis (FMEA) activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review Design fixtures and calibration processes for high-precision mechanical assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify and qualify components in first-article builds from suppliers, and participate in pilot production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce and maintain engineering documents, including specifications, design-for-excellence (DFx) guidelines, technical reports, and gate-review packages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Quality and Reliability teams to support successful validation outcomes and improve hardware durability standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support product compliance and certification activities, including Payment Card Industry (PCI) and regulatory certifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements listed below. If you meet these requirements, we strongly encourage you to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Industrial Design, or a closely related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of hands-on product design experience spanning mechanical engineering and industrial design, with a portfolio of consumer or commercial hardware products. This includes experience designing consumer-grade plastic enclosures for handheld products, such as smartphones, tablets, or payment terminals, from concept through mass production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to communicate design concepts through hand or digital sketching at the pace of a design conversation, and experience defining CMF specifications with suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of manufacturing and mechanical production processes, with direct experience taking industrial design concepts through DFM, tooling, and production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in mechanical CAD software. Creo is required, and SolidWorks is a plus. Expertise in creating detailed 2D drawings and performing geometric dimensioning and tolerancing (GD&amp;amp;T) and tolerance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with mold design, first-article inspection (FAI) processes, and process capability (Cpk) analysis, along with experience managing supplier and factory relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and spoken English and Mandarin communication skills to collaborate directly with suppliers in Taiwan, Hong Kong, and mainland China throughout product development and production. Willingness to travel internationally, including to Hong Kong and mainland China, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in rendering software, with KeyShot strongly preferred. VRED or Blender experience is also valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience maintaining a coherent design language across a multi-SKU hardware product family or accessory ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ergonomics methodologies, including grip studies, anthropometric data, and usability evaluations, applied to handheld device design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with point-of-sale hardware, payment terminals, or consumer electronics peripherals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PCI hardware requirements, material properties, and associated manufacturing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in thermal calculations and an understanding of plastic material properties.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mechanical simulation tools and metal-part design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to create compelling design presentations for cross-functional and executive audiences, clearly articulating the rationale behind design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are passionate about startups’ success, and building a strong community among founders and investors is core to Stripe’s mission of increasing the GDP of the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Europe, Middle East, and Africa Head of New Business for Startups, you’ll lead an organization of more than 30 account executives, including three direct-report managers, focused on new business acquisition across the region. You’ll oversee high-value deals, develop systematic approaches to acquiring new business, and establish Stripe as the strategic financial infrastructure partner for high-potential startups.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead an organization of more than 30 account executives through three regional managers, establishing consistent processes for user acquisition, growth, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Startups New Business revenue targets across Europe, the Middle East, and Africa, with personal involvement in strategic deals, deal analysis, complex negotiations, and pricing discussions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a long-term growth strategy focused on winning new users, increasing product adoption, and improving activation across the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement sales methodologies that identify high-potential startups while supporting acquisition across a broader user base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build executive-level relationships with key prospects and represent Stripe in strategic deals and at industry events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tailor regional sales approaches for local markets, with a focus on increasing product adoption at the point of acquisition and improving sales cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product, Marketing, Solutions Architecture, and Sales Finance to develop value propositions, metrics, and accountability frameworks that support consistent performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of sales experience, including at least four years in second-line management, and experience working with startups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing and scaling a sales organization of more than 30 people across multiple managers, geographies, and European markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of managing and growing multimillion-euro portfolios, meeting revenue targets, and coaching managers and individual contributors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with senior leaders during high-stakes negotiations and complex pricing discussions, and aligning large cross-functional groups around a shared strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify long-term opportunities beyond immediate targets, along with an understanding of how artificial intelligence companies operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’d be joining the Big Data Infrastructure team. Our team builds and maintains the platforms that power data work across Stripe, managing three core layers:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Orchestration (Airflow)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Batch Compute (Spark, Celeborn)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Lake (Iceberg, Hive, S3, Azure Blob Storage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support over 2,000 engineers and 600+ internal teams, processing workloads that organically grow more than 30% year over year.&amp;nbsp;Our infrastructure handles massive scale, managing over 800 PB of data, running 325,000 applications a day, and accounting for hundreds of millions of dollars in annual spend, directly powering critical pipelines like inbound payments, network reconciliation, and capital underwriting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the technical leader for the Big Data Infrastructure organization, you will guide a 40+ person engineering team to scale our foundational data systems. You will partner closely with major internal customers like Data Foundations, Payins Engineering, and AI/ML Foundations to modernize our tech stack and execute Stripe&#39;s transition to the &quot;Agentic Era&quot; - building &quot;invisible infrastructure&quot; where AI agents operate data pipelines end-to-end.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical leader for the Big Data Infrastructure organization, overseeing distributed systems that manage 20% of Stripe&#39;s total AWS spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute Stripe&#39;s transition to the &quot;Agentic Era&quot; by building invisible infrastructure that empowers AI agents to author, validate, ship, and operate data pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the architecture and delivery of critical modernization bets, including YARN to Kubernetes migrations, native vectorization (Gluten/Velox), and Airflow and Data Catalog modernization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the implementation of a multi-region and multi-cloud data strategy for high availability, disaster recovery, and Azure Blob Storage compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce operational burden and maintenance overhead (KTLO) from over 40% to under 10% by shifting fixes into the platform instead of relying on runbooks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of operational excellence and mentor engineers at various stages in their careers, up to Staff+&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Computer Science or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a Senior Staff role, so ideally 12+ years of professional experience in a software development role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong engineering background in distributed infrastructure and/or platform services, including one or more of the following: storage, databases, or compute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading projects on a cross-team and company-wide scale, including scaling and migrating systems with little to no downtime&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing, maintaining, and debugging distributed systems while optimizing their reliability and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving a culture of operational excellence, with a deep understanding of metrics, alerts, and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving AI-led architectural transformations and integrating agentic workflows into large-scale data systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a development team at AWS, Azure, OCI, or Google&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with big data infrastructure at scale, such as Spark, Iceberg, S3, Airflow, YARN, and Celeborn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with database internals and/or with Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and create new business models. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing some of the most important work of your career. You can read more about the business we’re building and what we’re looking forward to in our annual letter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk team builds trust, an essential ingredient for Stripe’s mission to increase the GDP of the internet. We make it possible for millions of businesses to access and use Stripe’s financial infrastructure while protecting our users, financial partners, and the broader ecosystem from harm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk sits at the center of our users’ and Stripe’s ability to grow safely. We help legitimate businesses access Stripe’s financial services, provide credit to creditworthy businesses, and increasingly help users manage their own risk. We also prevent fraud and financial crime, manage Stripe’s credit exposure, meet our obligations to regulators and financial partners, and enable Stripe’s product teams to launch and grow products safely. To do this, we set the policies and standards that guide how Stripe manages risk and develop the advanced AI, infrastructure, and product experiences that put them into practice for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe’s scale—$1.9T in annual payment volume, equivalent to 1.6% of global GDP, across millions of businesses—we face risk problems no other company has encountered. The opportunities and complexities are only growing as AI reshapes what is possible, Stripe expands its product suite, regulators raise their expectations, and we support more businesses in more countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Staff Product Manager for Risk, you will lead cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives that fundamentally change how Stripe and our users manage risk. You will identify the most important opportunities that cut across Risk’s infrastructure and products, define solutions to our most ambiguous problems, and drive execution from early technical shaping through delivery and adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate as a product counterpart to Risk’s senior technical leaders. You will shape infrastructure and product direction across Risk, connect work that would otherwise remain fragmented, and help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities. You will remain deeply engaged in the work, helping teams navigate difficult technical and product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will partner closely with Risk leadership to shape the organization’s strategy, vision, and most important investments. As a senior member of Stripe’s product community, you will also coach other PMs, raise the quality of product thinking across Risk, and advance the product management discipline across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-leverage problems that cut across teams, turn ambiguity into clear product and technical direction, and establish measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives from initial shaping through delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead changes to Risk’s approach to leveraging data and AI to accurately identify and mitigate risk at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering, data science, and ML leaders to shape architecture, data foundations, models, APIs, and product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities quickly and effectively, while guiding Risk teams toward coherent, reusable infrastructure and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Risk leadership to define multi-year strategy, identify the organization’s most important bets, and make clear investment and sequencing decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment among teams with different goals and constraints, resolving difficult tradeoffs and driving progress without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and mentor PMs across Risk, helping them strengthen their product judgment, technical depth, strategic thinking, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advance the product management discipline across Stripe by raising the bar for how we define problems, develop strategy, partner with technical teams, and deliver complex cross-organizational work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an exceptional product leader who combines strong technical judgment with product insight, strategic range, and executional rigor. You identify important problems before they become obvious, bring clarity to deeply ambiguous spaces, and mobilize teams around solutions that work across products, organizations, and time horizons. You are deeply curious and stay at the forefront of advances in AI and technology, finding practical ways to apply them to our most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You move fluently from defining multi-year strategy to driving the details of execution. You build alignment and lead transformational work across teams without direct management authority. You earn trust through the clarity of your thinking, your focus on users, and your hands-on engagement in the work. You raise the ambition and effectiveness of the teams and PMs around you without needing to manage them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of identifying and delivering high-impact, transformational product or technical initiatives that span multiple teams and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to bring clarity to deeply ambiguous problems, set a compelling direction, and drive work through execution and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment across data, machine learning, AI, APIs, platforms, and system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering deeply with senior engineering, data science, and product leaders to shape both technical direction and product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment across foundational infrastructure and user-facing experiences, with a focus on building capabilities that solve real user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep quantitative fluency and the ability to use data and causal reasoning to understand problems, evaluate tradeoffs, and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior leaders, build alignment across organizational boundaries, and drive execution without direct management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring and developing PMs and raising the quality of product thinking and execution across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication, with the ability to articulate compelling strategies, influence technical and executive audiences, and make complex topics clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency, intellectual honesty, curiosity, and a low-ego, hands-on working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering and preferably ML-based technical background.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI and machine learning to complex, high-stakes problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fraud, credit, payments, financial services, trust and safety, or another domain involving complex decisions and asymmetric consequences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with globally distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

