&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for people with an interest in building the tools to improve the day to day experience of Engineers in Stripe. The ideal candidate will have a passion for solving developer experience problems, and a pragmatic ability to ship results iteratively—powered by a mix of technical expertise across some or all of: language processing tools; version control systems; build systems; and distributed systems engineering. You’ll be working on a mix of engineer-facing systems, CI infrastructure platforms, and big-data engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a ton of important work to do, which is why we’re hiring! Our active projects change all the time, but here are a few examples of recent projects so you can get an idea of the types of work we do:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle CI at massive scale—including batching, speculative stacking, merge-race inhibition, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage systems to handle our enormous CI test suite–identifying and managing flaky tests, assessing and reproducing flakiness, and optimizing for test effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhance our CI systems for reliability, including adaptive response to available capacity, resilience and self-recovery from outages, and highly-leveraged observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Detect and isolate code breakages to minimize their blast radius.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with product engineers to understand and deliver their productivity needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope and lead large technical projects with enormous impact for engineers within Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain the core CI systems used by all of Stripe’s engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrutinize and reason clearly about the technology and architecture choices we make in building these products. In many cases, you will be the owner of these decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly contribute to core interface design and write code. Serve as a role model for how great software should be written for Stripe as a whole.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrate critical decisions correctly that fully consider software best practices, Stripe system realities, and numerous stakeholders’ preferences and concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Teach and mentor the next generation of technical leaders at Stripe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the effective and highly-leveraged use of AI-assisted implementation, ops, and delivery within the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional hands-on software development experience&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience designing and building large scale distributed systems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of technically mentoring junior and senior engineers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer obsession, ability to articulate and represent customer experience in various forums to drive the right outcome&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability of defining &amp;amp; driving complex initiatives/projects across multiple teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success with cross-discipline and cross-team collaborations, possess strong conviction and courage skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have the ability to thrive on a high level of autonomy, responsibility, and think of yourself as entrepreneurial&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Related experience in the area of Developer Tooling, CI/CD or DevOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies, from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups, use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Supportability sits at the vital intersection of platform safety, regulatory trust and merchant growth. Our mission is to ensure legitimate businesses can seamlessly onboard and thrive on Stripe, while proactively safeguarding the financial ecosystem from bad actors and high-risk activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Supportability Decisions team is a newly forming pillar anchored in our Dublin office. In this role, you will be the foundational technical lead establishing this capability in Dublin. Our mission is to accelerate Stripe’s global expansion by building the canonical Supportability Decision Layer; a stateful distributed platform that provides unified, real-time, and explainable risk determinations to unlock fast, compliant merchant onboarding and payment method expansion worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doing this at scale requires solving high-stakes risk challenges with precision. Deceptive merchant activity, such as transaction laundering, introduces significant threats as bad actors actively adapt to mask illicit and unsupported activities behind legitimate storefronts. Rather than relying on rigid, fragmented controls that create unnecessary friction for good users, our team builds the intelligent decision systems that systematically separate legitimate businesses from adversarial behavior, enabling Stripe to grow safely and aggressively.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Backend Engineer and Technical Lead for Supportability Decisions, you will take ownership of defining and building this new space from the ground up. You will build systems that operate at the intersection of AI/ML, distributed data processing and real-time risk decisioning. You will tackle high-ambiguity technical challenges in an adversarial threat landscape, turning broad risk policies and operational needs into resilient, high-throughput backend services and stateful decision engines. As the technical anchor in Dublin, you will set architectural patterns, mentor engineers as the team scales from its initial members to ~7 ICs, and drive technical alignment with distributed partner teams globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical vision, system architecture and delivery of the canonical Supportability Decision Layer, establishing stateful, explainable decision APIs consumed across automated systems and human operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect decision aggregation and AI/ML orchestration pipelines, synthesizing upstream machine learning outputs, website intelligence, backsite detection, and agentic AI evaluations into unified, low-latency determinations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design high-throughput, low-latency distributed backend services that balance platform safety, regulatory compliance, and minimal friction for legitimate merchants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguous, zero-to-one problem spaces to define clean domain models, contracts and interfaces across transaction laundering detection, web-presence screening and Local Payment Method (LPM) support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build resilient, AI-assisted decision engines designed to withstand circumvention, ensuring systems maintain integrity against sophisticated bad actors who actively evolve their tactics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the technical lead and mentor for the Dublin engineering team, setting architectural patterns, conducting design reviews, and raising the technical bar as the team expands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Engineering Managers, Product Managers, Risk Operations, and Data Science to translate strategic risk policy into scalable technical roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive technical alignment and system integrations across global partner teams, leveraging strong written design artifacts and asynchronous collaboration to ensure cohesive platform architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a technical leader who thrives in ambiguity, has deep distributed systems instincts, and is energized by building a critical platform that enables global merchant growth while safeguarding the financial ecosystem. If that sounds like you, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional backend software engineering experience building and maintaining complex distributed systems in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record as a technical lead or staff engineer driving multi-quarter technical initiatives from ambiguous requirements to production delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience designing durable, scalable APIs, data models, and backend architectures capable of processing mission-critical data with high reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and leadership skills with experience mentoring engineers, aligning cross-functional stakeholders, and driving technical consensus across distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in a modern backend language (such as Ruby, Java, Go, Python, or C++).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building systems in trust, safety, or risk domains where external bad actors actively evolve their tactics (e.g., transaction laundering, fraud, deceptive practices, or platform abuse).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience architecting workflow orchestration, policy evaluation, or decision platforms that balance robust risk evaluation with frictionless merchant onboarding and product access.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with global payment ecosystems, Local Payment Methods (LPMs), financial partner dynamics, or card network standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in AI/ML systems, agentic workflows, orchestrators, or integrating machine learning models into high-throughput, real-time backend decision pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience serving as an anchor or founding engineer establishing a new team or technical domain in a regional engineering hub.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio team works on a variety of brand-centric projects for Stripe, from our brand standards to campaigns, events, IRL experiences, packaging, digital products, and even printed publications. The brand designers on this team are multidisciplinary in nature, able to design robust visual systems, art direction, and craft surfaces that focus on brand and product storytelling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborating with other teams at Stripe, as well as external partners, we raise the quality and consistency of experiences with the Stripe brand IRL, virtually, and everywhere in between. We craft the creative vision and strategy for different types of projects and audiences, and amplify them across various mediums, channels, objects to environments, and digital and physical experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe Creative Lab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Creative Lab aims to create breakthrough, culturally resonant, and exquisitely crafted projects that reveal Stripe’s magic in surprising ways. We dedicate ourselves to meticulously crafting the work to ensure the highest possible creative quality. The work is experimental, often starts with ambiguous briefs and requires finding a way where others might deem it impossible. We are making it up as we go, and that’s the way we love to work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll be joining a highly creative team that spans the gamut of creative execution, from digital experiences (like interactive games or live-streaming a handbuilt, miniature city) to physical activations (like retrofitting CRT monitors or retired MTA ticketing machines) and beyond. The work is highly experimental, idea-driven, and very collaborative.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The work starts with ideas. Your ability to generate original and interesting concepts is foundational, as is your ability to find the right form for them and bring them to life, both with your own hands and through close collaboration with people across a wide range of disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an adamant maker that is genuinely curious, experimental, and loves to tinker, iterate quickly, and innovate on ideas, narrative, and making beautiful things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative vision: Design execution and quality of ideas work in equal partnership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with like-minded creative people who have radically different skill sets and together create ideas that envision an optimistic, progressive future&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help shape the strategic vision for design that pushes the boundaries of the brand and build awareness for what we do and why it’s important to Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner widely with cross-functional teams to build upon great ideas through making things&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Give and solicit feedback from wide range of teammates, agency partners, and stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate original, conceptually strong ideas from ambiguous briefs, strategic problems, cultural observations, and emerging opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine the right form for an idea, then direct multidisciplinary collaborators to bring it to life across a wide range of mediums&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop clear creative narratives, pitches, references, treatments, and prototypes that make an idea compelling before its final execution is known&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant creative experience in concepting and delivering ideas&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and directing experimental work across a variety of mediums, disciplines, and collaborators&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record independently delivering work as well as influencing the work of other designers, contractors, and agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong strategic acumen for building leading brands in a fast paced, global facing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A portfolio demonstrating exceptional conceptual thinking and art direction across a range of formats and disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional visual and cultural taste, with a broad frame of reference extending beyond design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are genuinely curious, ambitious and creative with a refreshing sense of design, art, technology, and culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive and humble in explaining your work, process, and decisions and experienced at facilitating stakeholders to advance the project as well as design quality&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Love working with other designers to help them learn and grow (and invite them to help you do the same)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience working in or alongside highly conceptual advertising, design, or cultural studios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cross functional partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in the latest AI and creative tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative coding or creative technologist background is a nice to have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Compute Foundation group builds and operates the core systems that enable every Stripe engineer to ship code, configuration, and infrastructure changes safely and at high velocity. Embedded on the Imaging team, you will design, build, and distribute Linux machine images; manage host bootstrapping and OS-configuration systems; oversee OS packages and security-patching infrastructure; and provide platforms that empower service teams to safely run workloads across cloud providers and regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own the foundation of Stripe’s compute fleet: Stripe’s services rely on host infrastructure that boots reliably, receives accurate configurations, and operates safely. Your decisions will directly shape the base operating system, package ecosystems, security posture, and bootstrap behavior of Stripe’s fleet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead active architectural transformations: The team is driving key platform evolutions, including modernizing the OS configuration layer, containerizing workloads, scaling machine image distribution across multi-cloud regions, and streamlining OS upgrades and critical security patching.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Drive broad, end-to-end host lifecycle ownership: Work across the entire host lifecycle - from image construction, package distribution, kernel and OS configuration, early boot/systemd, storage, networking initialization, and workload readiness. You will tackle complex engineering challenges that balance reliability, security, compliance, developer experience, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your judgment prevents fleetwide incidents: Changes to machine images, packages, kernels, bootstrap systems, and host configuration can have broad consequences. You will design validation, canarying, rollout, health-evaluation, and rollback mechanisms that contain blast radius and make foundational infrastructure changes safer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agency to shape technical strategy: As a Staff engineer, you will set technical direction for the team’s systems, author designs that span multiple teams, mentor engineers and be the person engineering managers and engineers rely on for the technical north-star.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead large, ambiguous infrastructure projects from initial design through production launch, broad adoption, and long-term operation. Define the architecture and success criteria, sequence the work, resolve technical ambiguity, coordinate cross-team dependencies, and shepherd projects to measurable impact.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for the evolution of Stripe’s host infrastructure, including how machine images are built, validated, distributed, and operated. Guide thoughtful decisions about when to containerize workloads and when host-based approaches remain appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems and practices that make broad infrastructure changes safe and predictable. Establish strong validation, staged rollout, observability, and rollback capabilities. Build guardrails that prevent unhealthy changes from progressing and give operators clear, actionable information when failures occur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead incident response for the systems the team owns. Systematically reduce operational toil and make reliability, security, debuggability, and maintainability first-class properties of the platform.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with technical leaders across infrastructure, security, compliance, and service teams to represent the Imaging team’s perspective and align on shared technical direction. Build strong relationships with partner teams and lead work that crosses organizational and system boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead critical design reviews and establish standards for the safety, reliability, operability, and usability of Stripe’s host infrastructure. Mentor senior engineers through high-stakes architectural decisions. Raise the quality of designs and implementations through hands-on coding, code review, debugging, and operational leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of professional software engineering experience, with a demonstrated track record of designing and shipping production infrastructure systems of significant scale and complexity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead large, ambiguous infrastructure projects end-to-end - from technical design through delivery - including managing cross-team dependencies and coordinating migrations across many consuming teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in Linux systems, including boot and initialization, systems, processes, networking, filesystems, storage, packages, and production debugging.&lt;br&gt;Strong foundations in cloud compute infrastructure, including machine images, virtual machines, autoscaling fleets, launch configuration, block storage, IAM, health evaluation, and multi-region operation in AWS, Azure, or an equivalent environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating fleet-scale image, host-management, configuration-management, or infrastructure-provisioning systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with safe infrastructure rollout practices, including automated validation, canarying, progressive rollout, health evaluation, rollback, and blast-radius containment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background in service reliability and operational excellence: demonstrated ability to lead incident response, reduce toil, and build systems that are reliable, debuggable, and maintainable by a team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of broad technical impact across multiple large systems: fluency across a complex codebase, force- multiplier effect through code review and mentorship, and the ability to set technical direction for a team rather than just execute within it.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience building modern image-based, immutable, or declarative infrastructure platforms.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Expertise with containers, Kubernetes, and migrating VM-based workloads to managed platforms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience operating large-scale Linux fleets across AWS, Azure, or multiple regions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with progressive delivery, automated validation, fleet health signals, and rollback systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience modernizing legacy configuration-management or host-provisioning systems.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Knowledge of OS security patching, software supply-chain security, and artifact provenance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong developer-platform instincts, with experience building safe abstractions and self-service workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies — from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups — use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Organization&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Core Infrastructure organization operates the foundational systems that power Stripe globally — including databases (MongoDB, PostgreSQL), high availability and disaster recovery (HADR), AWS cloud infrastructure, Linux servers, container orchestration, mesh networking, service discovery, and network edge infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within Core Infra, the &lt;strong&gt;Regional Enablement Platform (REP)&lt;/strong&gt; team helps Stripe launch and operate new regions without learning about broken dependencies from users. REP builds the regionalization, validation, deploy-safety, and operator tooling needed to answer practical launch-readiness questions: can critical payment paths run from the new region, which services still depend on a remote control plane, what breaks under packet loss or failover, and what must be fixed before deploys, launches, traffic shifts, or failovers proceed. The team uses traffic replay, synthetics, failover drills, dependency analysis, CI/CD gates, and incident data to turn those findings into platform fixes, service-owner asks, and reusable readiness checks across networking, HADR, and service teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in &lt;strong&gt;Bangalore&lt;/strong&gt; and serves as a senior technical anchor for Core Infrastructure in India, with direct cross-region influence across AMER, EU, and APAC.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on REP, you will play a key leadership role in enabling Stripe&#39;s infrastructure to power all of our products, globally and at scale. You will decide how Stripe validates that a new region can safely take traffic and continue working through network loss, failover, and deploy changes. You will define the checks that must pass before launch or failover, build validation systems that replay real production paths against regional infrastructure, and turn those checks into CI/CD gates, operator workflows, and concrete fixes for service or platform owners. You will also help build Core Infrastructure&#39;s senior technical bench in Bangalore through design review, mentoring, and cross-region technical leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define evidence-based readiness criteria for regional launches, traffic migrations, and failovers — replacing manual checklists with repeatable, globally consistent patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and mitigate risks on critical payment paths; use system data to drive ownership and validate that platform mitigations measurably reduce impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead end-to-end cross-functional delivery for new-region infrastructure, including safe service behaviors for remote control planes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build reusable validation tooling that accelerates infrastructure integration for new acquisitions and reduces high-priority blockers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert recurring operational friction into scalable platform capabilities used across teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead technical conversations and define decision mechanisms across Core Infrastructure and product teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and communicate a multi-year technical strategy for REP with clearly defined quarterly milestones and success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debug production issues across services and levels of the stack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and grow senior engineers, elevating technical planning, design standards, and cross-region execution from Bangalore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively in a global, distributed environment with asynchronous decision-making across AMER, EU, and APAC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Computer Science or equivalent field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of professional experience in software or infrastructure engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading complex, cross-team or company-wide infrastructure projects with high reliability and scale requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering background in distributed systems, platform engineering, or backend infrastructure, with a focus on operational safety and correctness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing the reliability and security of distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling and migrating systems with little to no downtime&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and written communication skills, including design docs and trade-off analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring engineers at various stages of their careers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with one or more major cloud providers — AWS, Azure, OCI, or GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with ops culture and a solid understanding of metrics, alarms, and dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience validating large-scale migrations, failovers, regional launches, regionalization, or control-plane behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or operating infrastructure with strict reliability, correctness, latency, or availability requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong observability judgment across metrics, logs, tracing, alerting, and incident analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with networking, service discovery, traffic routing, databases, Kubernetes, Terraform, or cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reducing packet loss, network latency, cross-region dependency risk, or other infrastructure failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making infrastructure validation or readiness evidence usable by service owners, operators, or partner teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience turning repeated operational problems into reusable tools, standards, or platform mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience with Go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Revenue Experiences Engineering team is part of the Commerce Systems organization at Stripe. We focus on ensuring that our users, both internal and external, have a best-in-class experience with billing at Stripe. This includes working on the systems and processes needed to bill our largest and most complex customers, as well as designing and delivering experiences to help guide users through their billing, from fee explainability to deep diving on product usage optimization. We are a cross-functional technical team that seeks to bring clarity to a complex space. The team is at the crux of all Stripe products and builds user-facing as well as internal infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build platforms and services to define and manage pricing, calculate and collect Stripe&#39;s revenue, and empower Stripe and our users to understand and manage revenue and costs. We work on customer-facing experiences, internal platforms, and data pipelines to empower Accounting, Finance, Strategy, Sales, and Stripe&#39;s Products to drive business value across the entire user and product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced technical leader to join our India-based team and drive the technical roadmap for Revenue Experiences Engineering, collaborating deeply with partner teams across Commerce Systems in the US, EMEA, and India. In this role, you will work closely with engineering managers, senior engineers, and cross-functional partners to help design architecture, ensure technical excellence, and break down complex problems to make them more tractable with engineering teams. You will be involved in the building of the technical bench, mentoring and growing the next senior engineers within the broader organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work cross-functionally to align on the business challenges in delivering excellent billing and accounting experiences to our users. Often this will include influencing across organizations and grounding your arguments in solid data and a technical roadmap. As such, you will have excellent technical leadership and communication skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also be hands-on in building key systems, while mentoring and leading other engineers. Join us in driving change in an area with tremendous opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the technical leadership, execution, and roadmap for Revenue Experiences Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally with business leaders across the company as well as partner engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering, product, and design leadership to define our product strategy and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure our platform solutions and user billing data are high quality, meet the needs of our internal users, and position us to meet Stripe&#39;s growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive interoperability across platforms in User Billing and integrations across Stripe with product, accounting, sales, finance, and data science teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scrutinize billing interfaces and data models, elevating our focus on correctness and ease of use within User Billing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish best practices, frameworks, and repeatable processes that enable the team to execute effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of learning and data-driven decision making on the team and to influence the broader organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and support the growth of engineers at different levels in their careers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of hands-on experience building large-scale, distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building large-scale, complex distributed systems; identifying shortcomings and optimization opportunities; and making data-driven cost performance tradeoffs to influence design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating infrastructure and tools that empower developers/product teams to deliver business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing company strategy at the intersection of business needs and technology (you measure your success in terms of business impact, not lines of code).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and creating strong technical teams that balance operational excellence, collaboration, and user needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills to work effectively across multiple teams and stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are effective in giving and receiving constructive feedback to/from peers and team members.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Past experience mentoring and investing in the development of engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Prior experience in the financial technology space, particularly in payment processing, accounting, or financial reporting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Support Experience engineering organization builds and improves Stripe’s user support&amp;nbsp;from end to end: how users get help within our products, how they get in touch with us when&amp;nbsp;they have questions, and how our teams use internal tools to answer those questions. We’re&amp;nbsp;accountable for the quality and reliability of this support stack and we use data and firsthand&amp;nbsp;experience to continuously improve it.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Providing great support to users of all sizes is culturally important to everyone at Stripe. We&amp;nbsp;partner closely with Stripe’s design, product, and operational teams across a wide surface&lt;br&gt;area: the external-facing support interfaces (https://support.stripe.com/), self-serve content,&amp;nbsp;entry points, internal tooling, case routing, and helping product teams across the company&lt;br&gt;reduce support volume by improving our products. We are also using the latest generative AI&amp;nbsp;technologies to re-imagine support experiences, and are developing AI assistants for Stripe’s&lt;br&gt;users and to help our operations teams be more productive.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Engineer on an established team, you will bring technical leadership and set the&amp;nbsp;technical strategy and architecture for Stripe’s support products. You will mentor and grow&lt;br&gt;senior engineers, build a culture of technical excellence, and serve as a role model for our high&amp;nbsp;engineering standards. As a technical leader, you will drive fast-paced, sustained product&lt;br&gt;delivery while upholding high standards for building reliable, scalable distributed systems that&amp;nbsp;delight our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Design, build, and operate production systems, with an emphasis on extensibility, reliability, and usability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Write and review code regularly, setting the pace and elevating standards for the team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build high-quality end-to-end product experiences, demonstrating deep care for users&#39;&amp;nbsp;needs and serving as a steward of crafting great experiences&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional stakeholders - navigating various types of&amp;nbsp;organizational complexity with the support of your own leadership team&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Partner with Engineering Management, Product Managers and key leaders across the&amp;nbsp;company to create and drive toward the longer term vision&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Unblock the team to execute against both short-term and long-term roadmaps, making&amp;nbsp;effective tradeoffs that consider business priorities, user experience, and a sustainable&lt;br&gt;technical foundation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Improve engineering standards, tooling, and processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Teach and mentor other engineers to become the next generation of leaders at Stripe&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;10+ years of professional backend or full-stack development experience, including&amp;nbsp;actively writing and reviewing code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience successfully setting and executing on long-term technical strategy for a&amp;nbsp;large product area.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to prioritize competing requirements and stakeholders to iteratively ship new&amp;nbsp;product features, drive alignment and proactive communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proven track record of technical leadership, including meaningfully contributing to the&amp;nbsp;growth of other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;User empathy and a customer-centric approach to problem solving and product&amp;nbsp;development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience building software systems for customer support or operations&amp;nbsp;organizations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience leading projects across multiple teams &amp;amp; timezones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proficient in JavaScript /TypeScript, Ruby, Java, and React.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience designing, deploying, and owning Agentic LLM solutions (e.g., multi-step&amp;nbsp;orchestrators, tool use/function calling) specifically for complex customer support or&lt;br&gt;internal workflow automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Link team builds the premier consumer network for next-generation commerce, leveraging our base of 300M+ registered consumers to pioneer the future of Identity, Consumer Finance, and AI-driven transactions. While our foundation was built on high-conversion merchant payments and a flexible digital wallet, we are expanding far beyond. We are building the infrastructure for a world where AI agents transact on your behalf, stablecoins go mainstream, and identity dictates how money moves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Consumer Preference team is building the Link experience across the web app and agents — building the wallet product consumers need to feel confident, excited, and inspired by the new ways payments and identity are changing online. As a senior member of the team, you will create new experiences such as financial insights powered by purchase history, rewards cards backed by a stablecoin balance, safe agentic purchase UX, automatic purchase protections, and subscription management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Full Stack Engineer to lead the design and delivery of new consumer capabilities in Link. The ideal candidate will combine technical depth across the stack with a strong product sense. In this role, you will take ambiguous product opportunities, create ways to validate them early, and ultimately ship complete products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on individual-contributor role with broad technical and organizational scope. You will own large, cross-functional projects from early product and technical definition through launch and iteration; lead teams of engineers through complex execution; and partner closely with the many Stripe systems and teams that provide new capabilities. You will work across the stack, building services and APIs as well as user interfaces. You will make the architectural decisions that balance a high quality bar with the need to move fast and iterate quickly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive technical strategy across Link Consumer, connecting near-term product delivery to a cohesive, durable engineering vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead large, ambiguous 0→1 initiatives from problem definition and architecture through implementation, safe launch, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain polished user experiences, reliable backend services, APIs, and systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks, dependencies, and foundational investments early, creating incremental plans that de-risk the roadmap and accelerate future work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering teams across Stripe, building alignment and influencing their roadmaps and priorities when Link Consumer depends on shared capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion pragmatic solutions and code patterns throughout our codebase, setting standards in React/JavaScript/CSS/GraphQL as well as Ruby APIs and LLM-powered systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure our UI and backend components are reliable, secure, extensible, and accessible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define operational processes and lead response to production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack, growing the learning and retrospective culture on our team and driving remediations that reduce risk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of backend and/or full-stack software development experience, with a track record of owning large, ambiguous systems end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated technical experience leading the design and delivery of large, complex software projects from early definition through production launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong full-stack engineering skills, including experience building reliable backend services and polished user-facing product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and unblocking a group of engineers on a substantial project as a senior individual contributor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in high-ambiguity environments: framing problems, making durable technical decisions, and creating an actionable path forward.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent cross-functional and cross-organizational collaboration skills, with the ability to align teams with different systems, priorities, and constraints.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering judgment around system reliability, operational excellence, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A product-minded approach to engineering, with a focus on delivering meaningful outcomes for users and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Java, Ruby, and/or TypeScript. We care more about strong engineering fundamentals and the ability to learn than expertise in a particular language or framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building payments, money-movement, fintech, or other regulated financial products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building consumer products at scale, particularly products that require a high degree of user trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on 0→1 products or taking new capabilities from concept through launch and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LLM-powered products, evals, or agentic assistants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appreciation for the importance of strong distribution and taking pride in seeing projects through to successful completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Financial Connections is Stripe&#39;s open banking platform, enabling businesses to securely access consumer-permissioned financial data. Our platform connects to thousands of financial institutions, powering use cases from account verification to risk assessment to personal financial management. Across the Financial Connections Engineering org, we focus on delivering high-quality, enriched bank data at scale — building the ML systems that transform raw financial data into actionable signals for both internal Stripe teams and external merchants.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our ML work spans transaction categorization, risk scoring, data enrichment, and the development of intelligent systems that improve data quality across our network. We operate at the intersection of fintech infrastructure and applied machine learning, solving problems that directly impact Stripe&#39;s ability to serve millions of businesses and consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for machine learning engineers who want to build intelligent systems that provide financial data at scale. You&#39;ll play a key role in designing, training, and deploying ML models that improve the quality, accuracy, and usefulness of financial data across Stripe&#39;s ecosystem.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, train, evaluate, deploy, and own ML models in production that improve transaction categorization, risk scoring, and data enrichment across Financial Connections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build large-scale ML systems that operate on diverse financial data from thousands of institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experiment and iterate on ML models (using tools such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, XGBoost) to achieve key business goals around data quality and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop pipelines and automated processes to train and evaluate models in offline and online environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate ML models into production systems and ensure their scalability and reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with product, data science, and engineering partners across Stripe to identify opportunities where ML can improve outcomes for merchants and consumers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with the latest ML/AI developments and take calculated risks in transforming innovative ideas into productionized solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers and contribute to a strong ML engineering culture within the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry experience building and shipping ML systems in production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient with ML libraries and frameworks such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, XGBoost, as well as Spark&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in designing, training, and evaluating machine learning models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in productionizing and deploying models at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in orchestrating data pipelines and efficiently leveraging large-scale datasets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration skills and the ability to work across teams and contribute to peers&#39; success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive with a high level of autonomy and responsibility and an entrepreneurial mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS or PhD degree in ML/AI or a related field (e.g., math, physics, statistics, computer science)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, open banking, or financial data domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NLP, LLMs, or text classification at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in adversarial or noisy-data domains such as fraud detection, risk modeling, or data quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of building and deploying ML systems that have effectively solved ambiguous business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deep learning architectures, including transformers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Radar ML team builds the machine learning systems that power Stripe’s Radar fraud and abuse product suite. Our models make real-time decisions across a significant share of internet commerce - helping businesses stop fraud, increase authorization, and grow safely. By turning economy-scale datasets into compelling ML products, the team directly improves customer outcomes and drives meaningful revenue for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The team is growing, and expanding into multiple new areas. We are building abuse protections across the full customer life-cycle, adaptive and customizable fraud systems for enterprises, and risk intelligence for 50+ global payment methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead the machine learning strategy for abuse prevention across the full customer lifecycle. Abuse doesn&#39;t stop at the payment. Bad actors create fake and duplicate accounts, take over legitimate ones, farm free trials and promotions, resell access they obtained below cost, use services they never intend to pay for, and file bad-faith refunds and disputes. For AI companies, every abusive account burns real compute, and the same actors keep moving from one account, product, and access path to the next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is uniquely positioned to solve this. Our network sees consumers across millions of businesses, so we can recognize a bad actor at signup, at login, at payment, and long after. Radar has already shipped the first building blocks: account evaluations at signup and login, customer-level abuse risk, and APIs that let businesses report their own abuse outcomes. You will turn these building blocks into a unified abuse prevention layer that understands the consumer behind every event and helps businesses act consistently across all of that consumer&#39;s accounts. This is a large growth opportunity for Radar, and a strategic priority for Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fast-moving 0→1 area, built alongside some of the world&#39;s leading AI companies, and the attacks are real today. Labels are sparse, delayed, and differ by business. Much of the customer journey is only partly visible to us. Adversaries adapt as soon as we ship. You will set the technical direction, make the hard architecture calls, and personally build the hardest pieces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical strategy and multi-quarter roadmap for lifecycle abuse ML, with product and engineering leadership: which abuse vectors to take on, in what order, and with what approach.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design a persistent, continuously updated consumer risk profile that combines signals from signups, logins, payments, product usage, refunds, and disputes. Evolve it from explainable composite scores toward model-driven risk scores for each type of abuse.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of models for abuse vectors such as multi-accounting, account takeover, bots, free-trial and promotion abuse, unauthorized resale, non-payment, refund abuse, and friendly fraud. Use graph, sequence, and LLM-based approaches over payment, account, and product-usage data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve the label problem by designing ways to learn from sparse, delayed, merchant-specific, and weak labels, including merchant-shared feedback, LLM-assisted labeling, and network-level signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how we measure success: evaluation frameworks, impact and ROI estimates, and operating-point guidance that help businesses trade off abuse losses against growth and conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn detection into action by shaping the risk controls, interventions, and recommendations businesses can turn on at each step of the customer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay deeply hands-on: write substantial production code, prototype quickly, and personally land the most technically difficult components, with the reliability and latency standards of systems in Stripe&#39;s critical path.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break ambiguous problems into parallel workstreams, unblock other engineers, and raise the team&#39;s bar through design review, code review, and mentorship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with leading Stripe users, fraud experts, product, and adjacent Stripe teams to ground the work in real user pain and change course quickly based on what you learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI-native tooling, agents, and workflows that let the team investigate attacks and build and operate models dramatically faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on technical leader who has built ML systems that matter, shipped them to production, and led others in doing the same. You thrive in ambiguity. You can take an open-ended problem with messy data and incomplete labels, find the highest-leverage path, get to user impact quickly, and change course when the data says so. You make the engineers around you better. You&#39;re as comfortable talking with a customer about the economics of their abuse problem as you are debugging a feature pipeline. You&#39;re excited to use frontier AI both in the systems you build and in how you build them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience developing, evaluating, and deploying machine learning models in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of technically leading large, ambiguous ML initiatives from problem definition to production, with measurable business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in machine learning, statistics, model evaluation, and experiment design, including where labels are noisy, delayed, or scarce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software-engineering skills, and you remain a hands-on contributor who regularly writes tested, maintainable production code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating production ML systems at scale, including data and feature pipelines, real-time inference, deployment, and monitoring, and making architecture tradeoffs across them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting technical direction across multiple engineers or teams, and mentoring engineers to grow their scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to explain complex tradeoffs clearly to engineers, product leaders, and customers, and to build alignment across functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying ML to fraud, abuse, integrity, trust and safety, identity, or security, where adversaries actively adapt to your defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with entity resolution, graph learning, or behavioral and sequence modeling of users, accounts, or devices (for example, detecting multi-accounting, account takeover, or bots).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productionizing modern deep learning or LLM-based approaches, including using LLMs for labeling, investigation, or detection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building 0→1 ML products and working directly with customers to define what to build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building shared ML platforms, representations, or foundation models used across multiple products or teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-assisted tooling or agents that measurably increased a team&#39;s velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe Checkout helps any business–from fast-growing startups to enterprises–accept payments without building their checkout from scratch. We have a suite of checkout surfaces that range from no- and low-code checkout pages to embedded payment forms and highly customized checkout flows. We’re expanding the suite to support emerging business models and continually optimizing so we can ensure Stripe has the most profitable, safest checkouts on the internet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Designer on Checkout, you&#39;ll lead the visual and interaction design direction for our most opinionated and optimized checkout surfaces. You’ll define how checkouts should flex to support emerging business models and underserved verticals, taking complex merchant needs and translating them to simple, conversion-optimized solutions. You’ll also contribute to and evolve the backing design system for our checkout surfaces.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the design direction for new features and checkout surfaces across the conversion funnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead design explorations from initial concept through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve and push boundaries on visual language, component patterns, and design systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape early product strategy through design exploration and rapid prototyping, making abstract opportunities tangible for product and engineering partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Checkout in senior reviews and establish the creative bar for new product directions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience at a tech, product-driven company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep fluency in visual design, interaction design, systems thinking, and prototyping with AI tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading complex work in close partnership with product management engineering, and design leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shaping ambiguous spaces and driving clarity through design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident presenting work to senior leaders and skilled at communicating design decisions through clear, compelling storytelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading changes to a design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in explaining your work, process, and decisions to cross-functional stakeholders and crave feedback to help you produce your best work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in SaaS, e-commerce, or fintech products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

