&lt;li&gt;Enjoy turning complex systems, policies, and edge cases into elegant product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are energized by ambiguous, strategic problem spaces—not just well-defined execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are an influential storyteller who can align partners around a clear point of view&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can move fluidly between big-picture thinking and interaction-level craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Know how to build trust through design, especially in high-stakes or sensitive user moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work well across disciplines and build credibility with technical, operational, and policy-oriented partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe’s Accounting Products team is building modern infrastructure for the Office of the CFO. Our vision is to give finance teams, and the agents that support them, one reconciled and explainable presentation of financial truth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today, the data and context required to make accounting decisions are fragmented across billing systems, contracts, spreadsheets, general ledgers, and the minds of the people doing the work. Finance teams spend significant time reconstructing what happened, determining the appropriate accounting treatment, reconciling results, and gathering evidence. Giving an agent access to the underlying data is not enough: it also needs the business context, accounting policies, approved judgments, and guardrails required to act reliably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue Recognition is our first major proof point. Stripe has a unique opportunity to help Billing and Metronome users turn complex revenue activity—including usage-based pricing, minimum commitments, credits, and contract modifications—into accurate, explainable journal entries. Our ambition is for agents to take on the investigation, configuration, and repetitive work while accountants retain control over consequential judgments and approvals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over time, we expect to expand into additional Office of the CFO workflows, and we are looking for a Staff Product Manager to help turn this vision into products that finance teams trust. This is a senior individual contributor role with significant ownership, autonomy, and influence across Product, Engineering, Design, Finance, Data Science, and Go-to-Market teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll own a significant product area within Accounting Products, setting its strategy, roadmap, and measures of success. You’ll translate the broader product vision into a focused plan, taking it from customer discovery and early prototypes through scaled adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll help build the future of agentic accounting: products that help finance teams automate work, understand financial results, and resolve exceptions while retaining control. Your work will connect Stripe’s Revenue Suite with the external systems customers rely on to manage their accounting workflows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define a focused product strategy, initial customer market, and roadmap, making explicit choices about where Stripe has an advantage, what to prioritize, and what not to build, and revising those choices as evidence changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with controllers, accountants, finance leaders, auditors, and implementation partners to understand accounting workflows, including month-end close, and translate customer problems into clear product requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define how humans and agents work together to configure accounting policies, explain results, investigate exceptions, and propose or execute resolutions, with appropriate review, approvals, controls, and audit trails&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape Revenue Recognition for Stripe Billing and Metronome users, supporting accurate journal entries and revenue schedules for usage-based pricing, credits, minimum commitments, contract modifications, and other complex business models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build products that are accurate, explainable, and operationally reliable, with results traceable to source activity, accounting treatment, and supporting evidence, and measure success through accurate closes, accepted outputs, time savings, reliable general-ledger handoffs, adoption, and retention&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take products from prototype to scale with design partners, deciding what to standardize, automate, or keep narrow, and define integrations with general ledgers, ERP, customer relationship management, and professional-services platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders and partner with Billing, Metronome, Tax, Payments, and other teams to make financial results consistent across products, raising the quality of product thinking through clear writing, sound judgment, and constructive challenge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management experience delivering complex, technically or domain-intensive products, including as a senior individual contributor who independently sets direction, aligns cross-functional teams, and drives decisions without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products for finance, accounting, or similarly demanding domains where accuracy, controls, traceability, and trust are essential, with a high bar for correctness, explainability, reliability, and operability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer instincts and experience working directly with specialized users to uncover underlying needs and translate domain complexity into coherent products, supported by an understanding of complex systems, data models, APIs, integrations, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgment and experience taking products from ambiguity to execution: identifying differentiated advantages, defining initial markets, sequencing multi-year opportunities, and connecting strategy to detailed requirements, data analysis, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and collaborative leadership across technical, business, and go-to-market teams, with the ability to clarify complex problems, align stakeholders, surface risks, and make or revise decisions as evidence changes in high-stakes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building accounting products for controllers, accounting teams, or other users in the Office of the CFO&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of revenue recognition under ASC 606 or IFRS 15, particularly for usage-based pricing, variable consideration, minimum commitments, credits, and contract modifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI or agent-powered products that investigate information, explain recommendations, or take action within defined controls and human review or approval workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with general ledgers and ERP systems, such as NetSuite, QuickBooks, or Xero, including the integrations and operational processes needed to transfer and reconcile financial results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An accounting background CPA qualification, or experience partnering closely with accounting policy, controllership, or audit teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Agentic payments is a team that’s building new API and integration experiences for agentic commerce online. We think that the proliferation of consumer-facing AI experiences will unlock new ways that consumers buy things online, and our existing payments experiences need to evolve to new commercial models that cutting-edge builders are starting. Our first launch, Instant Checkout in collaboration with OpenAI, took the industry by storm and we’re bringing experiences like that to the entire universe of AI agents, and sellers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on Agentic Commerce, you’ll own the vision and execution of transformative products that redefine how commerce works, making it more fluid, automated, and aligned with user intent. You’ll collaborate closely with engineering, design, data science, and marketing to unlock new opportunities for our customers and partners globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our north star provides a new integration shape for AI agents who are looking to build agent-powered online commerce experiences, via their Stripe integration. They will have access to our entire suite of connected sellers, and can focus on the experience with the end-user. Enabling an AI agent to do this requires new API primitives, new dashboard surfaces, and deep thought about what financial and e-commerce complexity Stripe can simplify on their behalf.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the product roadmap for agentic commerce solutions that empower users, from automated merchant tools to intelligent purchasing workflows and beyond.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full stack solutions across Stripe&#39;s ecosystem, including back end services, dashboard interfaces, money movement systems, and integrations with other Stripe primitives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering and design to ship high impact features that increase user autonomy and reduce friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills: comfort diving into data to test hypotheses and make informed trade-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally across Stripe’s broader platform and product teams to integrate agentic commerce capabilities seamlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage directly with users (particularly large enterprises) to understand their business needs and translate requirements into novel product shapes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of Product Management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Computer Science background or equivalent technical experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience of leading initiatives across large engineering organizations, spanning multiple teams to influence tech roadmap planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, structuring ambiguous concepts clearly and from first principles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrive in a collaborative environment involving different functions, stakeholders, and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep empathy for users balancing autonomy and guidance in digital commerce experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building APIs or new integration experiences for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy using social media to interact directly with customers for feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve founded a business / startup, taking a product from 0-1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building APIs or new integration experiences for users&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in eCommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Billing team builds software tools that accelerate the economic and technological growth of global businesses by helping them operationalize their commercial relationship with their customers. Our product offering is a robust set of building blocks which our customers combine in creative ways to support their ever-evolving business. Our Billing platform serves as the strong foundation to support different billing models, customer acquisition channels and ways of issuing bills and collecting payments. We also offer tools such as billing and SaaS analytics, revenue retention and recovery, designed to meet the full recurring revenue management needs of startups and large enterprises alike.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Manager on Stripe Billing, you will be responsible for understanding user needs, developing long-term product plans to solve categories of problems for our users and shaping specific product features to solve those user needs. You will also be responsible for the growth and usage of our products, to ensure we’re helping businesses get the most value from using Stripe Billing.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe, product development is an extremely collaborative effort between engineering, design, product marketing, data science and customer-facing teams. You’d be joining a team of experienced Product Managers who have a track record of successfully building large-scale business and consumer products that are collectively impacting millions of users around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On a day to day basis you will spend your time split between external meetings with customers and internal discussions with your engineering, design, marketing, analytics, and sales counterparts. You will identify the most important problems to solve, develop product solutions and work with engineering and design to scope the work. You will articulate the product vision, develop annual and quarterly plans, and collaborate with other functions to deliver these solutions to our users and make them successful.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years relevant product management experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical skills e.g., ability to gain an in-depth understanding of software systems, build a robust integration 1 with the Stripe API, make meaningful contributions to high-stakes discussions on API design, data modeling and software architecture&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer empathy across different segments and personas: from startups to large enterprises, across both engineering and finance functions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product sense: ability to understand user needs in-depth and build delightful product experiences to solve them and make our users successful&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills: ability to synthesize complex discussions, write succinctly and present to senior stakeholders both within and outside Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience managing technical software products from infancy to scale&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can internalize an entire cross-functional business and lead a comprehensive product vision You have experience designing and building a multi-product platform&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a creative product thinker who loves collaborating across the company with engineering, analytics, marketing, design and sales to experiment and build superior products&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong written and verbal communication skills with a talent for precise articulations of customer problems&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re motivated by the chance to improve the lives of your users&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve ever started or run a business before (not a requirement)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re scrappy, you do what it takes to get it done&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Product&amp;nbsp; - Connect Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect is Stripe’s platform for businesses that serve other businesses. It gives platforms the infrastructure to represent the people and companies in their ecosystem, onboard and verify them, manage their accounts, accept payments, and pay them out - without building payments, compliance, or financial-services systems themselves. This is how businesses like Shopify can help entrepreneurs run and grow their businesses. It is also the kind of infrastructure that marketplaces such as DoorDash need to coordinate money movement across large networks of restaurants, merchants, and dashers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Connect has impact across industries. &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/shopify&quot;&gt;Shopify&lt;/a&gt; uses Stripe to embed financial services for merchants; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/lugg&quot;&gt;Lugg&lt;/a&gt; streamlines worker onboarding and offers instant payouts; &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/doorloop&quot;&gt;DoorLoop&lt;/a&gt; reduces manual customer onboarding tasks by nearly 50% with Stripe; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://stripe.com/customers/sharetribe&quot;&gt;Sharetribe&lt;/a&gt; helps entrepreneurs launch and run marketplaces on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI is accelerating the emergence of entirely new business models: global networks of creators and experts, AI-native marketplaces, and agent-driven products that change how people discover, buy, sell, and deliver services. These businesses are more dynamic than traditional platforms: participants may operate across borders, take on different roles, and need new ways to establish trust, access financial capabilities, and get paid.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Connect Abstractions team owns the platform primitives that make these models possible. We are building the foundational abstractions for representing participants, onboarding them safely, configuring their capabilities, and managing their lifecycle on Stripe. Our work will determine how quickly the next generation of platforms can launch, how flexibly they can evolve, and how much of Stripe they can bring to the businesses and people they serve.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a chance to define a foundational product area at Stripe. You will turn a fast-changing set of user and product needs into durable platform primitives that work across products, industries, and geographies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines high-leverage strategy with hands-on product execution. You will work through ambiguous, consequential questions like: what should a platform be able to model? What should be simple by default but flexible when needed? How can Stripe make complex financial infrastructure feel effortless for a platform and its users?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The outcome of your work will compound. The abstractions you help create will be reused across Connect and Stripe, shaping what new products platforms can build and how quickly they can bring them to market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an entrepreneurial Product Manager to build the platform experiences behind Connect&#39;s next generation of users. You will own critical product primitives that platforms, including the fastest-growing AI companies, use to onboard, configure, and manage their users on Stripe. You will turn a clear strategic direction into products that solve hard user problems today while creating a coherent, extensible foundation for business models that are still being invented.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is for someone who enjoys the depth of platform work but is uncompromising about product craft and solving real user needs - both the ones users have today and will have in the future. The work is not building infra for its own sake; you will build capabilities that help our users launch a new marketplace, enable a global network to pay its contributors, or give a business entirely new ways for their end users to earn.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the next generation of Connect accounts to life. Own key product areas within the account platform, translating strategy into a focused roadmap, crisp product decisions, and high-quality launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build from use cases. Start with the real problems platforms face, such as onboarding a new seller, supporting a complex business model, or evolving a user&#39;s financial capabilities, and then work towards the primitives needed to solve them well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sophisticated infrastructure feel simple. Partner with engineering and design to create API and product experiences that are powerful and intuitive.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;See around corners. Develop a strong point of view on how AI will change platform economics, participant models, and financial workflows. Make focused foundational investments that unlock the next wave of demand.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn user signals into durable product investments. Work closely with users, Sales, Partnerships, and other Stripe teams to distinguish bespoke requests from patterns that should become scalable platform capabilities, connecting business needs, user needs, and platform evolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive high-velocity, high-craft execution and own outcomes. Lead cross-functional work from discovery through launch, and hold yourself accountable for developer experience, platform adoption, user value, and business impact, not simply features shipped.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a product builder who can move easily between a user’s hardest problem, the business opportunity behind it, and the product decisions needed to solve it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked on technically complex products - such as APIs, developer tools, shared platform capabilities, or core product experiences - but you do not build tech/platform for its own sake. You see strong platform design as a way to help users move faster, create better products, and unlock new business models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are opinionated, thoughtful, and execution-oriented. You can focus a team on the few decisions that matter most, create momentum in ambiguous situations, and ship products that raise the bar for both quality and impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience, with meaningful time owning platform, API, or developer-facing products end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own a product area end to end: setting strategy, driving execution, and measuring outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical instincts and comfort defining the measurement framework before you ship&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written communication and the ability to build alignment across functions and levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in payments, fintech, or financial infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience productizing bespoke or custom solutions into broadly available platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of making well-judged foundational investments ahead of user demand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.stripe.com/custom-objects&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Custom objects&lt;/a&gt; allow businesses to define custom data models in Stripe, ensuring Stripe reflects how their business operates. A business might have data that doesn’t fit standard Stripe objects, such as Shipments, Reservations, or InsurancePolicies. Once defined in Stripe, that custom data can be used with Stripe-native objects, such as Customers, Subscriptions, and Invoices. Companies can keep their existing system of record and bring over what their Stripe integration needs, or use custom objects as the system of record for that data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Custom objects are the data pillar of Stripe’s extensibility platform, which consists of Stripe Apps, Stripe Workflows, scripts, and extension points.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a product manager to lead our custom objects product, which will make it easy for anyone to model, ingest, and use data on Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a product management opportunity for an early-stage product (private preview!), and you’ll be responsible for the entire product line: identifying use cases, product design, iterating quickly by partnering with early adopters, pricing, and more. You’ll also work very closely with multiple teams at Stripe to enable their products to be “custom object-ready.”&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interact with customers and internal product teams daily so that you can validate product ideas, requirements, and prototypes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and design to ship functionality that delights users, strikes the right balance between impact and engineering cost, and makes a measurable impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the vision, strategy, and roadmap so that we can launch in public preview in early 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define key success metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with user researchers to test hypotheses and understand user pain points&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of product management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A computer science background or equivalent technical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Both passion for and experience building data platforms. For example, you’ve either built a custom data platform, such as Salesforce Custom Objects, Shopify Metaobjects, or HubSpot Custom Objects, or you’ve built a tool that consumes or modifies objects from those platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to structure ambiguous concepts clearly and from first principles, and the ability to thrive in a collaborative environment involving different functions, stakeholders, and subject matter experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading initiatives across large engineering organizations, spanning multiple teams to influence technical roadmap planning and execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy using social media to interact directly with customers for feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ve founded a business or startup, taking a product from zero to one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You only ship functionality after you’ve personally test-driven it and made heavy edits to the documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Product team is responsible for bridging the gap between Stripe&#39;s core capabilities and the bespoke needs of the world&#39;s largest organizations. We are hiring product managers who will be aligned to specific priority industries (e.g., insurance, healthcare, public sector), with each product manager acting as the &quot;CEO&quot; of their assigned vertical—identifying high-leverage opportunities, building 0-to-1 products to solve industry-specific blockers, and influencing our global product roadmap. You will be a critical partner to GTM leadership (Sales, Partnerships, Marketing) and a navigator across the broader Product organization. We are looking for high-agency builders who thrive in ambiguity and know how to move mountains through both direct execution and cross-functional influence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a product manager to own Stripe&#39;s product strategy and execution across our priority industry verticals, starting with complex, regulated industries like insurance, healthcare, and public sector. We are seeking a highly-entrepreneurial, data-driven product leader who will define where Stripe plays, build 0-to-1 products to unlock new revenue, and influence Stripe&#39;s broader Product organization to meet the unique needs of enterprise customers in your vertical. The products you build will directly shape how the world&#39;s largest companies use Stripe—and how Stripe grows within one of its most strategic segments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the industry product roadmap—Define and execute the multi-year product strategy for your priority vertical. Translate your &quot;where to play and how to win&quot; thesis into a concrete roadmap—deciding what Stripe builds natively, what we solve through platform extensibility, and where we partner. Own measurable outcomes tied to revenue, adoption, and merchant satisfaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship 0→1 products—Identify unmet needs through deep customer research, data analysis, and market intelligence. Lead the full product lifecycle for industry-relevant functionality—from problem definition and technical scoping with engineering, through PRD, API and UX design, build, launch, and post-launch iteration. You&#39;ll make hands-on trade-off decisions about scope, technical approach, and sequencing with your engineering team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a strategic partner to GTM and customers—Work deeply with our largest customers, partners, and GTM teams. Translate &quot;market noise&quot; into clear product signal—shaping feature requirements, and defining the data models and integration patterns that enterprise customers in your vertical need.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a force multiplier across Stripe&#39;s platform—Influence Stripe&#39;s core product teams (Payments, Billing, Connect, and beyond) to ensure their roadmaps reflect the requirements of enterprise customers in your vertical. To do this credibly, you&#39;ll need to go deep on Stripe&#39;s platform—understanding our APIs, infrastructure constraints, and extensibility model—so you can advocate for changes with technical specificity, not just business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of product management experience, with a track record of shipping successful products in complex, regulated environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency—You don&#39;t need to write code, but you&#39;re comfortable reading an API spec, reasoning about system design trade-offs, and holding your own in engineering discussions. You&#39;ve shipped products where the &quot;how we build it&quot; mattered as much as the &quot;what.&quot;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep customer obsession—A talent for getting close to customers—talking to merchants and partners—and distilling complex pain points into simple, elegant product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical rigor—You use data—not just intuition—to prioritize. You&#39;re comfortable defining metrics frameworks, digging into usage data, and making quantitative arguments for (or against) product investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A master communicator—Stripe is a writing-heavy culture. You must be able to articulate deep technical and strategic concepts through precise, persuasive prose—your narrative docs are things of beauty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency and influence—Adept at finding &quot;homes&quot; for initiatives, building consensus across disparate teams, and driving momentum without needing formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset and bias for action—Comfortable with ambiguity, skilled at prioritizing high-impact initiatives, and experienced operating with limited resources to unlock outsized outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience building products in Healthtech, Insurtech, Public Sector, or similarly complex, regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building platform, API, or developer-facing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with Enterprise Sales teams and C-suite stakeholders at Fortune 500 companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Billing Foundations team builds the core infrastructure and data foundations that power Stripe Billing and support products across Stripe’s revenue and finance suite, including Tax. We build the shared systems that help these products scale, from real-time infrastructure for usage-based billing to customer balance management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our product is the infrastructure itself: the building blocks that product teams depend on to deliver reliable experiences for businesses. As usage-based business models evolve, including those powering AI products and agents, we’re solving technical challenges around scale, low latency, and strong system guarantees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product management on this team combines long-term technical strategy with a deep understanding of internal users’ needs. You’ll work closely with principal engineers and product teams across Stripe to shape shared infrastructure, make thoughtful platform tradeoffs, and build foundations that support the next generation of billing products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with engineering leadership to set a long-term vision for how our product infrastructure best supports the agent-led workflows of the next million Stripe Billing customers. Because our users are engineers and their agents, your deep technical product understanding is uniquely important to ensure successful onboarding, retention, and growth of our customer base.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Additionally, you are the steward for the technical and security aspects of our entire revenue and finance suite. You will ensure that our product is the fastest, most secure, and most reliable monetization infrastructure on the planet.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the strategy, vision, and outcomes for the Foundations team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work directly with our most important clients to ensure that our product infrastructure and service-level agreements meet their needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering to make correct product and engineering tradeoffs as we build new products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce new infrastructure products that advance our mission, such as Low Latency Streaming Billing and Margin-aware Event Pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of product management experience, including experience owning and delivering complex products with substantial technical or domain depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating as a senior individual contributor: independently setting direction, aligning cross-functional teams, and driving important decisions without relying on formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong customer instincts and experience working directly with specialized users to uncover underlying needs and translate domain complexity into coherent products, supported by an understanding of complex systems, data models, application programming interfaces (APIs), integrations, and technical tradeoffs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong strategic judgment and experience taking products from ambiguity to execution: identifying differentiated advantages, defining initial markets, sequencing multi-year opportunities, and connecting strategy to detailed requirements, data analysis, and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication and collaborative leadership across technical, business, and go-to-market teams, with the ability to clarify complex problems, align stakeholders, surface risks, and make or revise decisions as evidence changes in high-stakes environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with streaming systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing infrastructure products with reliability of four nines or higher&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering background&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;Who we are&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Stripe Issuing team enables users–from the most promising startups and largest platforms in the world to Stripe itself—to build and launch successful card programs and financial features into their product using powerful programmatic APIs and intuitive UIs. The team creates the infrastructure, user facing experiences, and partner integrations needed to manage the lifecycle of a card and enable efficient money movement. This is a great opportunity to help build one of Stripe’s fastest growing businesses. Our top users span fintechs to large enterprises &amp;amp; cover a range of verticals including Buy Now Pay Later, vertical SaaS platforms, on-demand marketplaces, expense management platforms, fleet, travel &amp;amp; more across the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As EMEA Staff Product Manager for Stripe Issuing, you will lead our product development efforts for building the best-in-class card issuance systems, including designing user-facing APIs and interfaces and working directly with top global users in building and growing their card programs in EMEA. This is a highly complex and challenging role that will require you to deeply understand user needs and collaborate across internal and partner teams to build and launch a seamless product experience at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a strong Staff Product Manager that can run Stripe Issuing in EMEA like a standalone business, with expertise in partnering with go-to-market teams to scale our EMEA Issuing business. This Staff Product Manager will spend significant time with users to deeply understand their needs and experiences, Stripe leadership and go-to-market teams to build the EMEA Issuing strategy and roadmap, and cross-functional internal stakeholders to build compliant and scalable products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead our Stripe Issuing effort in UK and Europe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape the direction and product strategy for helping users manage their card programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering to bring new Stripe Issuing product solutions to the UK and European markets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other Stripe teams (design, legal, risk, compliance, engineering, etc.) early in the product development lifecycle and jointly shape product plans that lead with delightful and helpful user experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the roadmap and go-to-market, with product marketing, of EMEA Stripe Issuing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the user in product and API designs, gathering direct feedback from customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure we’re building in a scalable, performant way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brings 8+ years of experience in a product role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has domain knowledge in financial products, particularly card issuing, financial systems, and card networks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong focus on scaling products in close collaboration with go-to-market teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has experience building platform and/or API products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has strong written and verbal communication skills with a talent for precise articulations of customer problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can put themselves in the shoes of their users and be a steward of crafting great experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be joining Stripe’s ML Foundations and Gen AI team to incubate new ML applications and improve our ML capabilities across Stripe. Our team is responsible for unlocking novel ML and LLM techniques and applications across Stripe’s product suite to drive business outcomes, as well as providing infrastructure, tooling and support for ML teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a senior product leader, you will lead a cross-functional team to define, incubate and scale new ML/AI applications across Stripe’s product suite, and drive our strategy and roadmap for ML/AI infrastructure powering all of Stripe’s teams. You will work closely with product leaders across business units to define and deliver on an AI-centric product strategy, launching new applications that drive incremental business outcomes.&amp;nbsp; At the same time, you will be advancing our core AI technology stack to empower teams across Stripe to infuse their scenarios with Agents and agentic capabilities, with API support for agent quality and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute on the Stripe-wide strategy for new ML/AI applications across our product suite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and align on areas of investment for ML/AI applications in collaboration with product leaders across the company&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with cross-functional teams to execute on the roadmap and launch successful new ML/AI applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly and crisply with leadership stakeholders and drive alignment across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute on a strategy for advancing Stripe’s ML/AI infrastructure and tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the requirements below, and has a passion for AI to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience delivering highly successful and innovative software products which are ML powered&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of ML and applied AI tech stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to influence company level strategy and work with business leaders to execute on the transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You push the pace. You take blame and pass the praise. People love working with you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead teams and work cross-functionally in a highly collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze and use quantitative and qualitative data to inform decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding and empathy for consumer and business users — you love building products that make our customers feel joy, delight and trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relentlessly drives product quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capable of working on both 1P and 3P products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From having their phone buzz as their first payment comes in to quickly resolving customer issues on-the-go, the Stripe mobile app is a critical lifeline for founders and business owners around the world. Our team is responsible for both the app platform and user-facing experiences. We collaborate closely with every product team to represent, shape, and enhance what it means to be mobile. The next chapter of our mobile efforts will take the quality bar to even greater heights and redefine mobile money movement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a passionate product leader to shape the strategy, amplify its impact across the company, and accelerate Stripe’s mission to help internet businesses grow faster.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the product manager on the Mobile team, you will be accountable for making the mobile app indispensable for startup founders and business owners. How do we get every YC founder to use the app? How can we increase usage across different geographies? How can we get more product teams to contribute to the app? In other words, your role is to ensure founders and business owners are more successful when they use the mobile app.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;Deeply understand the needs of founders and business owners and identify the unique superpowers mobile can deliver for them&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Articulate the mobile strategy, prioritize the roadmap, and furiously execute to deliver user value&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Craft powerful product experiences with surprisingly great details &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Steer the broader organization to understand and build for mobile use cases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with the go-to-market team to ensure the mobile app is discoverable and compelling&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;8+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Persistence and a whatever-it-takes approach to ensure that your product is successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of user interface (UI) and user experience (UX) principles and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Technical familiarity with mobile development, cross-platform architectures, and machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability to collaborate with engineering and design across time zones (PST, EST, CET)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Founder background, or experience in a very early stage company environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Built award-winning mobile apps in the past&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Believe that fast software is the best software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Payments Intelligence organization optimizes each of the billions of dollars of transactions processed by Stripe annually on behalf of our users, maximizing successful transactions while minimizing payment costs and fraud. We own products like Radar, Authorization Boost, and Disputes, building fast and scalable services and creating intuitive user experiences. We serve real-time predictions as part of Stripe’s payment infrastructure and architect controls that leverage AI to optimally manage users’ business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Product Lead on the Payments Intelligence team, you’ll be responsible for scoping, designing, and building intuitive features that help users maximize their revenue while minimizing their cost while shaping our intelligence platform. You will partner with many functions at Stripe, with the opportunity to both work on infrastructure/platform systems, as well as produce direct user-facing business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day to day you’ll be working closely with a team of engineers and data scientists. You’ll collaborate with peers in Design, Product Marketing, Partnerships and many others to craft the vision for our Payments Intelligence products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop the long-term vision and strategy for our Payments Analytics product and our intelligence platform, prioritize accordingly, and create an execution roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand our users’ needs by spending time with developers, sales, and support, and by observing patterns/trends across their feedback, the market, and our data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and launch new capabilities and products that bring significant value to customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the pace, prioritization and execution for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with a wide range of systems, processes and technologies to own and solve technical and product problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with stakeholders across the organization such as Engineering, Design, Data Science, Marketing, Sales, Account Management, and Operations&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product Management experience: 10+ years of relevant experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen: You enjoy digging into the details of how a business works, identifying how to make it better, and building product/technical solutions to do so&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer and Partner facing experience: You’re comfortable in front of customers or third-party collaborators, and have experience navigating customer conversations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational savvy: You are strong operationally, capable of designing and driving a cross-functional team and process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical horsepower: You dig deep into the data, think from user first principles, and deliver the right results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Crisp communicator: High attention to detail including precise and effective communications, including with external customers/partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Results-oriented: You enjoy doing whatever it takes to execute on complex projects&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Risk team builds trust, an essential ingredient for Stripe’s mission to increase the GDP of the internet. We make it possible for millions of businesses to access and use Stripe’s financial infrastructure while protecting our users, financial partners, and the broader ecosystem from harm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Risk sits at the center of our users’ and Stripe’s ability to grow safely. We help legitimate businesses access Stripe’s financial services, provide credit to creditworthy businesses, and increasingly help users manage their own risk. We also prevent fraud and financial crime, manage Stripe’s credit exposure, meet our obligations to regulators and financial partners, and enable Stripe’s product teams to launch and grow products safely. To do this, we set the policies and standards that guide how Stripe manages risk and develop the advanced AI, infrastructure, and product experiences that put them into practice for Stripe and our users.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Stripe’s scale—$1.9 trillion in annual payment volume, equivalent to 1.6% of global GDP, processed across millions of businesses—we face risk problems no other company has encountered. The opportunities and complexities are only growing as AI reshapes what is possible, Stripe expands its product suite, regulators raise their expectations, and we support more businesses in more countries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on the Risk team, you will lead cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives that fundamentally change how Stripe and our users manage risk. You will identify the most important opportunities that cut across Risk’s infrastructure and products, define solutions to our most ambiguous problems, and drive execution from early technical shaping through delivery and adoption.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will operate as a product counterpart to Risk’s senior technical leaders. You will shape infrastructure and product direction across Risk, connect work that would otherwise remain fragmented, and help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities. You will remain deeply engaged in the work, helping teams navigate difficult technical and product decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify high-leverage problems that cut across teams, turn ambiguity into clear product and technical direction, and establish measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major cross-Risk and cross-Stripe initiatives from initial shaping through delivery, adoption, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead changes in Risk’s approach to using data and AI to accurately identify and mitigate risk at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner deeply with engineering, data science, and machine learning leaders to shape architecture, data foundations, models, APIs, and product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help product teams across Stripe build on Risk’s capabilities quickly and effectively while guiding Risk teams toward coherent, reusable infrastructure and product decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build alignment among teams with different goals and constraints, resolve difficult tradeoffs, and drive progress without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an exceptional product leader who combines strong technical judgment with product insight, strategic range, and executional rigor. You identify important problems before they become obvious, bring clarity to deeply ambiguous spaces, and mobilize teams around solutions that work across products, organizations, and time horizons. You are deeply curious and stay at the forefront of advances in AI and technology, finding practical ways to apply them to our most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You move fluently from defining multi-year strategy to driving the details of execution. You build alignment and lead transformational work across teams without direct management authority. You earn trust through the clarity of your thinking, your focus on users, and your hands-on engagement in the work. You raise the ambition and effectiveness of the teams and product managers around you without needing to manage them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of identifying and delivering high-impact, transformational product or technical initiatives that span multiple teams and organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to bring clarity to deeply ambiguous problems, set a compelling direction, and drive work through execution and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment across data, machine learning, AI, APIs, platforms, and system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering deeply with senior engineering, data science, and product leaders to shape both technical direction and product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment across foundational infrastructure and user-facing experiences, with a focus on building capabilities that solve real user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep quantitative fluency and the ability to use data and causal reasoning to understand problems, evaluate tradeoffs, and measure outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to influence senior leaders, build alignment across organizational boundaries, and drive execution without direct management authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to articulate compelling strategies, influence technical and executive audiences, and make complex topics clear.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High agency, intellectual honesty, curiosity, and a low-ego, hands-on working style.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineering background, preferably with a focus on machine learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying AI and machine learning to complex, high-stakes problems at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fraud, credit, payments, financial services, trust and safety, or another domain involving complex decisions and asymmetric consequences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with globally distributed teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world&#39;s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sail Core builds Stripe&#39;s frontend platform—the data layer, navigation, observability, and developer tooling that 50+ product teams use to ship web applications, with the Dashboard being the largest. We are responsible for enabling a stellar developer experience for frontend engineers at Stripe. We&#39;re hiring a deeply technical product manager to own the platform strategy, drive cross-company modernization initiatives, and set the standard for frontend excellence at Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;How should a platform team decide what to build when 50 teams depend on you and each one thinks their request is the most urgent? When do you invest in long-term architectural health versus shipping the migration that unblocks next quarter&#39;s goal? How do you make 9,000 files at initialization become a fast, traceable, joyful developer experience—without breaking production for millions of merchants along the way?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the product strategy and roadmap for Stripe&#39;s frontend platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the largest frontend modernization initiative at Stripe while holding the line on architectural quality&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Redefine frontend development with agentic tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and track key metrics such as latency, build times, and reliability SLOs to make difficult trade-off decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the product voice in deeply technical decisions such as API surface design, framework deprecation sequencing, extraction boundaries, and migration tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You think in systems, not features. You go deep on architecture, you don&#39;t delegate to engineering. You&#39;re the person who reads the RFC before the meeting, asks why the error response looks like that, and frames migrations in terms of user outcomes, not just engineering milestones. You treat developer experience as part of the product, not a byproduct.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product management experience, with at least 2 years on platform, infrastructure, or developer tools teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical fluency in frontend web development—you discuss JavaScript and TypeScript, React component models, build systems, and performance optimization with depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving large-scale migrations or platform transitions across multiple teams, including the sequencing, dependency management, and stakeholder alignment that make them succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated use of quantitative metrics to drive platform investment decisions—you&#39;ve defined the metrics, not just tracked them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of partnering with engineering to make architectural trade-offs grounded in user impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering background—you&#39;ve written frontend code professionally and it still shapes how you think about product decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led or significantly contributed to a legacy extraction or monolith decomposition effort and understand viscerally why they&#39;re hard and where they get stuck&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Believe that fast software is the best software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Naturally default to the platform solution over the one-off fix, but know when speed demands the opposite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explain what a cascading re-render is, why it matters, and what to do about it—to an engineer, a designer, and a VP, in three different ways&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup Products team builds Stripe Atlas and other products that help founders start and run a company, from anywhere in the world. We believe that startups are one of the most effective ways to solve the world&#39;s problems, and we want to give founders a running start — and keep them running. We help founders form their company, raise capital, execute critical legal agreements, access the internet&#39;s best tools, and automate operations while feeling ambitious, smart, and assured. Our goal is to create more startups that get to product-market fit, fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is composed of high-agency, high-ownership product thinkers, who genuinely care about helping founders and making it easier to start and run a startup. Every person on the team is responsible for making our product the best it can be, and for ensuring our roadmap contains the highest impact ships for founders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a product manager on the Startup Products team, you’ll gain a deep understanding of what early stage founders need to get their company off the ground, identify the most important pain points to solve, help set the product strategy, scope product features and technical infrastructure, collaborate with design, drive execution with engineering, craft product marketing, and plan for go-to-market.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply understand the needs of startup founders and learn how they use Atlas and other startup products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay at the front of the ever changing technology landscape, ensuring we are building where founders are and with tools they want to use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive product development in collaboration with engineering counterparts by setting the pace, prioritizing ruthlessly, and unblocking execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Craft product experiences that are both simple and powerful, with surprisingly great details.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to our product strategy and own delivery of product and business metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively with internal stakeholders and deliver clear communication on statuses, priorities, and landed impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Atlas externally with founders, venture capitalists, accelerators, and partners. Establish new external partnerships as needed to drive product development.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain metrics to help us understand product performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that every user has a great experience with Atlas, using any means at your disposal. Review feedback, unblock stuck users, collaborate with our support teams, and recommend and deliver product solutions to common user problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of product management or product-focused founder experience.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipped user-facing or API products, built on complex technical systems running at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An AI enthusiast and experimenter. Someone who is willing to upend their workflows for something that works 2x better.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for helping founders build their businesses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Persistence and a whatever-it-takes approach to ensure that your product is successful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills with a talent for precise articulations of customer problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept with data and confident in how best to measure user impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Founder background, or experience in a very early stage company environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software engineering experience, a computer science or engineering degree, or similar technical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Stripe is building the economic infrastructure for the internet. Millions of businesses use Stripe to accept payments, manage revenue, and grow globally. Stripe Tax helps businesses calculate, collect, and manage indirect taxes as they sell across products, markets, and business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring a Staff Product Manager to help shape the future of Stripe Tax. In this role, you will lead high-impact product strategy and execution across a broad portfolio, making it easier for businesses to understand, calculate, collect, and manage tax as they grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Staff Product Manager on Stripe Tax, you will identify the most important opportunities to improve our tax products and turn them into focused strategies, durable platforms, and exceptional user experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with Engineering, Design, Tax, Partnerships, Go-to-Market, and other product teams to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set strategy and lead product initiatives that help more businesses successfully adopt and use Stripe Tax.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the speed, accuracy, reliability, and usability of Stripe Tax calculations and related workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expand support for the geographies, tax requirements, industries, products, and business models that matter most to Stripe users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build capabilities for complex tax needs, such as registrations, exemptions, address and fulfillment logic, tax customization, and other business-specific requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable products and platform capabilities that work across Stripe’s ecosystem, including integrations, connector apps, marketplaces, and Connect platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Stripe to create coherent end-to-end experiences spanning calculation, collection, reporting, and tax management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use customer insight, market context, data, and technical understanding to prioritize investments and make clear tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders and cross-functional partners around a shared product direction, measurable outcomes, and an execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help make Stripe Tax a product businesses can rely on as they scale. Merchants should be able to confidently answer “yes” to questions such as:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can I use Stripe Tax for my business and the locations where I sell?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does Stripe Tax support the taxes and business models that apply to me?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can it calculate tax accurately for my registrations, exemptions, customers, products, and fulfillment model?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Is it fast, reliable, and easy for my team to operate?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Does it work with the other Stripe products, platforms, and integrations my business depends on?&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a product leader who is comfortable operating in ambiguous, high-stakes spaces where customer needs, regulatory complexity, technical constraints, and commercial opportunity intersect. You can translate a broad mission into a focused strategy, build alignment across teams, and deliver meaningful products over multiple horizons.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You likely have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant product management experience, including ownership of complex, platform-oriented, or technically deep products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of setting strategy and delivering multi-team initiatives with measurable business and customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in prioritizing across customer needs, market opportunities, operational complexity, and engineering investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with engineering and design partners to build reliable, scalable products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to communicate clearly with executive stakeholders and to align diverse partners around a shared direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about global commerce, financial infrastructure, tax, compliance, payments, marketplaces, or developer platforms. Direct domain experience is helpful but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset and the ability to turn complex requirements into simple, effective product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tax is a fundamental challenge for businesses that sell across borders, channels, and business models. Stripe Tax has the opportunity to remove that complexity, helping businesses launch faster, expand with confidence, and operate globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-leverage role at the intersection of global commerce, financial infrastructure, and product platform strategy. You will shape how Stripe Tax evolves to serve the next generation of internet businesses.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Brand Studio lays the foundations that help Stripe accelerate. We do this by creating, evolving, and maintaining Stripe’s high-quality, versatile, and forward-looking brand design systems, experiences, and advertising campaigns. We sweat the details. We make it seem effortless.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for leading brand design operations and creative production across all of Stripe’s internal and external events, in close partnership with the Experiential Creative Director. This role is a hybrid mix of program management, project management, and creative production depending on the project phase. During certain periods you’ll be focused on the 10,000 foot view of the program, and at other times you’ll be working side-by-side with the Design team overseeing execution of every design detail before an event.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead experiential program management across roadmap development, budget oversight, project scoping, timelines, resourcing, partner relationships, cross-functional communication, and scalable approaches that create clear paths forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a high volume of simultaneous projects, ranging from small to large scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Experiential Creative Director to further scale and evolve event design at Stripe; optimize processes to streamline how work is done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Corporate Events team to ensure smooth execution and integration of event brand design across all surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure smooth collaboration with leadership, creatives, cross-functional partners, and vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own project management through documentation, tooling, trackers, standing meetings, org-wide updates, and Slack&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Source, onboard, and oversee external creative agencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Connect silos, socialize changes, anticipate risks, and provide actionable solutions for escalation to Brand Studio leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate challenges and blockers with ease; proactive in finding solutions, and always looking ahead for the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uphold and advocate for design quality with cross-functional teams and vendors to exceed engagement and registration goals&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspire and sustain a culture of excellence by collaborating with creatives in best practices and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Staff Program Managers within Brand Studio at Stripe demonstrate passion for great design and have strong design sense. They’re experts in diving deep into details, expanding, evolving, defining, and documenting flexible systems and processes that achieve bar-raising quality and consistency at scale.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate excels at keeping the work on track while maintaining (and raising) the bar on craft. They offer options and tradeoffs, crisply articulate decisions, iterate quickly, and collaborate seamlessly with senior leadership, marketers, creatives, and agency partners. Most importantly, they are meticulous when it comes to details.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in similar roles and industries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think users first—understand their needs, find interesting and unique solutions, and strive to consistently optimize how to best engage with them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong strategic acumen for developing complex program roadmaps and cross-functional processes in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can demonstrate strong design sense, industry knowledge and best practices, have deep knowledge producing complex brand and event design systems, and bringing design assets to life across the creative production process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven excellence in producing creative systems that are optimized for scale and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail oriented and excel at simplifying complexity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record successfully influencing outcomes both internally and with agency partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can balance optimizing for speed and quality, with high craft and quality creative work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are persuasive in explaining your work, process, and decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organization and presentation skills, and excel in written and verbal communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about Stripe’s mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-we-are&quot;&gt;Who we are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-stripe&quot;&gt;About Stripe&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;about-the-team&quot;&gt;About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Abuse Control Engineering (ACE) is Stripe’s rapid-response technical defense and control incubator. When urgent abuse vectors emerge, ACE uses real-world attacker telemetry to prototype, test, and deploy software safeguards before vulnerabilities can be exploited at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We partner closely with Fraud, Risk, Abuse Research, and Product Engineering to run rigorous experiments that balance effective risk mitigation with legitimate user activity and conversion. Operating as both a strike team and an incubator, ACE builds automated regression suites to prevent threats from recurring and transfers mature controls to long-term product owners across Stripe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;what-youll-do&quot;&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Abuse Control Engineer on the ACE team, you will design, prototype, and incubate technical defenses that safeguard Stripe’s financial ecosystem against complex, cross-cutting abuse vectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When emerging threat patterns reveal weaknesses in Stripe products, ACE rapidly builds and experiments with technical safeguards. Guided by empirical evidence and Stripe’s Fraud Taxonomy 3.0 (FT3) framework, you will translate threat intelligence into precise technical control requirements, such as API rate limits, step-up challenges, parameter validation, and pre-debit holds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will run experiments to evaluate risk reduction against the impact on legitimate user conversion, carefully balancing security and product velocity. You will manage controls through a structured incubation lifecycle, build automated regression suites to prevent threats from recurring, and partner with product engineering teams to transfer mature, long-term defenses.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;responsibilities&quot;&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rapid control prototyping:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design, prototype, and deploy technical controls across API, protocol, and product boundaries to address high-impact abuse vectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evidence-based technical requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Translate empirical attacker evidence and FT3 threat research from Abuse Research, Fraud, and Security teams into precise technical abuse requirements and control specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Control co-design:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Collaborate with teams across Stripe to design resilient, secure controls across payments, onboarding, identity, and Connect surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Risk experimentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Run rigorous experiments and A/B tests to measure risk reduction against the impact on legitimate user conversion, optimizing controls to minimize friction while neutralizing threats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regression testing:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build comprehensive regression test suites and automated attack simulations with Abuse Research to ensure mitigated abuse vectors do not recur.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Execute ACE’s incubation model by defining handoff criteria, operational documentation, timelines, and target dates for transferring successful controls to product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&quot;who-you-are&quot;&gt;Who you are&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;minimum-requirements&quot;&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in security engineering, software engineering, application security, or anti-abuse engineering in a high-scale production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A bachelor’s or master’s degree in computer science, cybersecurity, software engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong software development background, with proficiency in Python, Go, Java, or a similar production programming language, as well as advanced SQL skills for analyzing system telemetry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using frontier AI models for software development, learning, and analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building API-level safeguards, rate-limiting frameworks, authentication or authorization checks, or input-validation controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated testing frameworks, including writing unit, integration, and regression tests for critical backend software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional collaboration and communication skills, with a track record of partnering across security, product, and platform teams to drive technical outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&quot;preferred-qualifications&quot;&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of designing and executing A/B tests, evaluating control efficacy, and balancing security safeguards against user conversion friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in threat modeling, secure systems architecture, and modern application-security design principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with established threat frameworks, such as FT3 or MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK, and experience applying adversary kill-chain analysis to build resilient defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial fraud vectors, threat-actor tactics, techniques, and procedures, and attacker infrastructure, including account takeover, card testing, and credential stuffing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with large-scale data-processing platforms, such as Databricks, Trino, or PySpark, to monitor and measure control performance across distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience incubating software features, establishing clear operational handoff criteria, and transitioning ownership to partner engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

