&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collecting and filing sales &amp;amp; indirect taxes is a classic area for technology disruption. Companies selling across countries, states, and even smaller jurisdictions have to navigate through a myriad of tax rates, product-level tax exemptions, filing requirements, and registration obligations. The rules are constantly changing, and not accurately calculating and filing tax can have legal ramifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It’s no surprise then that solving tax compliance is a top user request. We launched Stripe Tax as a new SaaS product in 2021 to make tax compliance as effortless as possible. The Stripe Tax team builds the systems and experiences that help businesses understand where they have obligations, calculate the right tax, and automate reporting and filing. We solve this at a global scale for users ranging from ambitious startups to the world’s largest enterprises, whose requirements demand exceptional correctness, extensibility, and operational rigor.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an experienced technical leader to shape the architecture and technical roadmap for Stripe Tax. You will work alongside leaders across engineering, product, design, operations, and go-to-market teams to turn complex and evolving tax requirements into simple, reliable experiences for millions of businesses. You will lead high-impact, multi-team efforts, make durable technical decisions, and raise the bar for how we build and operate Stripe Tax.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the technical strategy and execution for Stripe Tax’s most important and ambiguous product and platform investments, from early exploration through production adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work backwards from the needs of complex global businesses and evolving tax regulations to identify high-leverage opportunities and shape the product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, product, design, operations, legal, go-to-market, and infrastructure leaders to align teams and deliver cohesive tax experiences across Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve scalable, resilient systems and data models that meet the exceptionally high standards for correctness, auditability, security, and availability required in tax&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive interoperability across Stripe products and external tax ecosystems, scrutinizing service boundaries, interfaces, and data contracts to keep the platform extensible&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Raise the engineering bar through hands-on technical leadership, clear decision-making frameworks, operational excellence, and mentorship that accelerates other engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of industry software engineering experience building and operating large-scale, distributed systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep software engineering expertise, with a track record of making sound architectural decisions while remaining hands-on in the code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of leading complex, multi-team technical programs from ambiguous problem definition through successful delivery and adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to set long-term technical direction, identify the highest-leverage investments, and make progress amid uncertainty and competing constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and influence skills, with the ability to build alignment among senior technical, product, and business stakeholders without relying on authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A commitment to growing other engineers through mentorship, technical feedback, and a culture of rigorous, inclusive, and data-informed decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in tax, financial technology, payments, accounting, financial reporting, or another domain where correctness and regulatory complexity are central&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with large enterprise customers and translating their complex requirements into durable platform capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing robust integrations with external systems and APIs, or leading platform work that spans backend services, data, and user-facing experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe startups are the future. We work with many of the newest and most innovative companies to help them grow, and we need your help. We&#39;re looking for someone who knows their way around the early-stage startup ecosystem to represent Stripe and share what we&#39;re working on with a broad base of startups and accelerator partners. Our primary goal is to help early-stage founders succeed, and that comes in a variety of forms - mentorship, helping them set up their financial stack, connecting them with investors and mentors, being their internal advocate, and much more.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will oversee a portfolio of strategic early-stage accelerator partnerships, including Y Combinator, as we work to educate, attract and retain the most promising startups. You’re an energetic and organized self-starter; you understand the product well and can cultivate trusted partnerships with the right players in the ecosystem. You’re also able to succinctly communicate Stripe&#39;s mission and benefits to investors and startups. You will be on the front lines for evangelizing our product to prospective users and a key driver of our success with startups. You connect dots, constantly soliciting input from users and using that to improve product and GTM strategy. If you’re excited to spend your days interfacing with startup founders and early-stage investors, and find energy in tirelessly helping early-stage founders as they look to start and scale, then we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee our Y Combinator and other accelerator partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across the business to ensure that every founder&#39;s experience of Stripe is surprisingly delightful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build out and oversee the execution of key programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spin up new initiatives that add continuous value to the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a point of escalation for partners and top startups to grow Stripe’s brand within the Y Combinator ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a product feedback loop to internal teams to ensure that we continue to build for the highest potential businesses&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross functionally with key internal stakeholders to advance strategic Stripe initiatives for startup founders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collate startup ecosystem insights and prepare weekly / quarterly updates detailing business progress, market trends, and product feedback gathered from startup engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Stripe in the startup ecosystem and take up speaking opportunities at key startup events that bolster Stripe as the best platform for founders to start and scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage your data prowess (SQL, etc) to build out tools that enable us to better serve founders and demonstrate impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest and demonstrated ability to cultivate deep, trust-based partnerships with some of the most consequential venture capitalists&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in the startup ecosystem with startup or investing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced business or technical founder with a passion for helping other founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the startup ecosystem, founder empathy, and ability to build strong partnerships, particularly within the Y Combinator community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A user-first mindset, anything less than perfect is unacceptable to you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cross-functionally with internal and external stakeholders to get new programming off the ground.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re a builder by nature and are excited to launch new initiatives within Stripe that extend surprisingly delightful experiences to best in class founders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communications skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hunger and motivation to operate (and thrive) in a highly ambiguous and fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Humility, and who takes initiative with a “no task is too small” and “I’ll get it done” attitude.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Well-networked individual who is active in the early stage venture capital and startup ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alumni of Y Combinator&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand a technical buyer and key moments in their life-cycle where financial infrastructure decisions are made.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adept public speaker, presenter and moderator.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience, understands channel partnerships and the value this channel brings to a GTM org.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Data skills - conversant in SQL or Python - and willingness to build tools serve our users and measure business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Startup Products team builds Stripe Atlas and other products that help founders start and run a company, from anywhere in the world. We believe that startups are one of the most effective ways to solve the world&#39;s problems, and we want to give founders a running start — and keep them running. We help founders form their company, raise capital, execute critical legal agreements, access the internet&#39;s best tools, and automate operations while feeling ambitious, smart, and assured. Our goal is to create more startups that get to product-market fit, fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is composed of high-agency, high-ownership product thinkers, who genuinely care about helping founders and making it easier to start and run a startup. Every person on the team is responsible for making our product the best it can be, and for ensuring our roadmap contains the highest impact ships for founders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategy &amp;amp; Operations team member on the Startup Products team, you’ll help us understand and talk about the startups that use our products, turning data into clear internal and external narratives, and use analysis to shape strategy and product priorities. You’ll own high-signal metrics and dashboards while also leading deep dives that explain what is changing, why it matters, and what we should do next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delve into the data to glean new insights about how users use our products and how they are building their businesses on Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package insights into external-facing content, driving our public storytelling about our users and the startup market, in partnership with marketing and communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze product performance, identify trends and anomalies, diagnose drivers, and translate findings into concrete recommendations and synthesis to share with internal stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead analytical deep dives on strategic questions, new product opportunities, founder segments, growth drivers, and the impact of launches or operational changes.&lt;/li&gt;
